dc\nnn-NO -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\noc -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\npa-IN -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\npl -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\npt-BR -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\npt-PT -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\nrm -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\nro -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\nru -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\nsk -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\nsl -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\nson -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\nsq -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\nsr -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\nsv-SE -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\nta -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\nte -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\nth -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\ntl -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\ntr -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\ntrs -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\nuk -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\nur -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\nuz -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\nvi -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\nwo -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\nxh -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\nzam -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\nzh-CN -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\nzh-TW -\u003e f1a336f9ac0ac11e62d9dac6a140a1ee8b2d9adc\n", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": "743c56ca8c10e268fef6354bf8041d124045864f", "git_parents": ["6dbe77787095b9a75ba08dfa15a4b9a968669e5e"], "node": "7af15d037a6ab1417fe1f76d132d3d7a9e635d77", "parents": ["56a236152b2409f2d50b64bbe63995f726caf529"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063582 - Don't restore a stale expand-on-hover sidebar visibility, r=sfoster.\n\nSidebarManager only clears the visibility it saved on the way out of vertical\ntabs when a switch back consumes it, so a choice left behind by an earlier\nswitch stays latched and is applied to an unrelated later one.\n\nbrowser_resize_sidebar.js is where this surfaces. Once\nbrowser_launcher_splitter_expand_on_hover.js (bug 2051576) has run,\ntest_resize_after_toggling_revamp's orientation round trip lands on\nexpand-on-hover, which hides the launcher splitter while the launcher is\nexpanded, so every drag in the file silently does nothing. The added assertion\nnames that, instead of leaving the first failure as \"'NaN' is not a number\".\n\n#savedVisibility only lives as long as the process, so an expand-on-hover choice\nis still lost across a restart in horizontal tabs. Persisting it is a follow-up.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321914\n", "files": ["browser/components/sidebar/SidebarManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_resize_sidebar.js"], "git_node": "626911297b73efc0c9a634d72b43c5c9119bfca5", "git_parents": ["743c56ca8c10e268fef6354bf8041d124045864f"], "node": "78fdc605fd4ab9a866caaa9480d13b481a64ec93", "parents": ["7af15d037a6ab1417fe1f76d132d3d7a9e635d77"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063582 - Don't let a superseded expand-on-hover toggle finish its setup, r=sfoster.\n\ntoggleExpandOnHover() awaits twice while turning expand-on-hover on. A call that\nturns it back off in the meantime runs to completion first, and the suspended\ncall then re-registers MousePosTracker and the popup and uidensity listeners the\nnewer call had removed, and reinstates the root attribute over it. Nothing\ntouches either again.\n\nThe attribute is what browser_resize_sidebar.js's\ntest_pinned_tabs_height_reclamped_on_visibility_change ends up waiting on: the\npinned tabs grid rules are gated on the root not carrying it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321915\n", "files": ["browser/components/sidebar/browser-sidebar.js"], "git_node": "15823ef52a1607c2f865e88a4a24f616aaccc427", "git_parents": ["626911297b73efc0c9a634d72b43c5c9119bfca5"], "node": "86aadc221d5f23863cd0ee6bf71cbaa4534e3191", "parents": ["78fdc605fd4ab9a866caaa9480d13b481a64ec93"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2035383 - Wait for pref-driven styles in waitForTabstripOrientation, r=sfoster.\n\nThe helper returns as soon as the tabstrip's orient attribute is set, which a JS\npref observer does synchronously with the pref write; CSS keyed on the same pref\nthrough -moz-pref() only lands a refresh tick later, and no style flush brings\nthat forward. Callers could therefore assert on pref-driven layout before it\nexisted.\n\nbrowser_launcher_splitter_visibility.js is where this shows up: the launcher\nsplitter is display:none behind @media not -moz-pref(\"sidebar.verticalTabs\"),\nand its setup asserts the splitter is visible as soon as the helper returns. The\ntest has had that shape since bug 2016966 created it, a week before this bug was\nfiled. Fix the helper rather than the one assertion, because its ~20 callers all\nhave the same gap.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321916\n", "files": ["browser/components/sidebar/tests/SidebarTestUtils.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "66666c66deabd8e749db5a791896b9d891dfb7e0", "git_parents": ["15823ef52a1607c2f865e88a4a24f616aaccc427"], "node": "621ba8b2750423a0e085977bc899b92bf5b8840e", "parents": ["86aadc221d5f23863cd0ee6bf71cbaa4534e3191"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067146 - Measure the launcher when a splitter drag ends, r=sfoster.\n\n`launcherWidth` is only ever written by a ResizeObserver on #sidebar-container,\nwhich runs at the end of a rendering update, but the splitter's command event\narrives as soon as the button is released and consumed that value as if it were\nthe width the drag ended on. A release handled in the same turn as the last\nmovement therefore stored a width from before it, and the launcher settled\nnarrower than where the user let go \u2014 the faster the drag, the more of the final\nframe is lost. Taken to its extreme, a whole gesture in one turn from a\ncollapsed launcher stores the collapsed width, which is below\nLAUNCHER_MINIMUM_WIDTH, so the launcher snaps shut and the drag is discarded.\n\nMeasure the launcher instead, as the pinnedTabsDragActive and toolsDragActive\nsetters next door already do, and decide the expanded state from that\nmeasurement rather than relying on the observer having set it during the drag.\n\nReading the inline width the splitter itself writes, rather than measuring, was\nalso tried and is indistinguishable across all three new cases, including the\none written to catch a measurement that has gone stale.\n\nThe tests use plain synthesized mouse events with no test-only hooks in the\nsidebar code; the only thing they control is which movements share a turn with\nthe release. They run with the a11y checks' must-have-an-accessible rule off,\nbecause the launcher splitter exposes no accessible for any mouse event to land\non, as the other tests that drag it already do. That rule is the only one turned\noff, and the gap itself is worth its own bug.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321917\n", "files": ["browser/components/sidebar/SidebarState.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/SidebarTestUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_launcher_splitter_drag_release.js"], "git_node": "ee59e970cbd40a7a3d5c65f65cd4ae6f67356013", "git_parents": ["66666c66deabd8e749db5a791896b9d891dfb7e0"], "node": "6feb32b7ca48d219f2976e742974d30f4c8fb977", "parents": ["621ba8b2750423a0e085977bc899b92bf5b8840e"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787952073, "git_changesets": ["c7ef73fb502ec6f3bbcfbb632b4fcb019e962a3a", "549b72e2ad4afe1d235a83f4e8b654528669d0a6", "e01ca9802f4f5518a3780b50a79879312d4241b6", "9a1f4eb1674b77f2327ae186fc86e061ba6d7058", "ca7113a2eaf39971d471a4c02a058ac694c9519e", "baca6d1fcb19effff1f8a27b79f322ff66bcc380", "f81c88fd7436dc0ac8ee6a502f84a60fe2bc1733", "e8b222660197b43af9d4467d32f6c110890ca27b", "6dbe77787095b9a75ba08dfa15a4b9a968669e5e", "743c56ca8c10e268fef6354bf8041d124045864f", "626911297b73efc0c9a634d72b43c5c9119bfca5", "15823ef52a1607c2f865e88a4a24f616aaccc427", "66666c66deabd8e749db5a791896b9d891dfb7e0", "ee59e970cbd40a7a3d5c65f65cd4ae6f67356013"], "user": "agoloman@mozilla.com"}, "45205": {"changesets": [{"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067151 - Treat a missing drag service as no drag in the tooltip listener, r=layout-reviewers,emilio.\n\nnsXULTooltipListener::HandleEvent consults the drag service only to ask whether\na drag is in progress, but treated a missing service as a reason to stop. GTK\ndoes not instantiate one in headless mode (nsDragService::GetInstance, under\ngfxPlatform::IsHeadless), so every mousemove and mouseout was dropped before\nMouseMove() and no XUL tooltip could appear at all. No drag service means there\nis no drag.\n\nThis unblocks running XUL tooltip tests headless. They used to hang for the\nfull timeout without producing an assertion, which is indistinguishable from a\nreal failure and cost a false reproduction while investigating bug 2001695.\n\nnsContentUtils::GetDragSession already asks the question this way, so use it.\nOf the other callers that look the service up directly, none abandons unrelated\nwork when it is absent: they either guard with a null check or genuinely need\nthe service to do their job.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321923\n", "files": ["layout/xul/nsXULTooltipListener.cpp"], "git_node": "6ba803cc5c7c108b53b295d60da53dac43261d0f", "git_parents": ["ee59e970cbd40a7a3d5c65f65cd4ae6f67356013"], "node": "fd8a3e51d629c894f74910d2d00425a441046ae2", "parents": ["6feb32b7ca48d219f2976e742974d30f4c8fb977"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gopalarathnam Venkatesan \u003cgopal@g13n.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065468 - gBrowser.selectedTabs returns tabs in sorted order r=dao,tabbrowser-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322074\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_multiselect_tabs_using_Ctrl.js"], "git_node": "7e997e7f53776cf257d1ae5a75139aa7221a8f94", "git_parents": ["6ba803cc5c7c108b53b295d60da53dac43261d0f"], "node": "bfd37dce29b32dcfb89df2d8c083bf46c56e1f21", "parents": ["fd8a3e51d629c894f74910d2d00425a441046ae2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Mehic \u003cdmehic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061675 - Remove the Legacy Telemetry mirror of dom.parentprocess.private_window_used r=chutten\n\nDO NOT LAND until the clients_daily question below is answered. This is posted\nto get a data engineering verdict on that, not because it is ready to go.\n\nOnly the Legacy Telemetry mirror is removed. The Glean metric\ndom.parentprocess.private_window_used is left in place, so what Firefox collects\nis unchanged. The sole recording site, CanonicalBrowsingContext.cpp:103, already\nwrites exclusively through Glean, so the scalar was only ever fed by the mirror.\n\nBoth sides have to go in the same commit: test_mirrors.py asserts every\ntelemetry_mirror resolves to an existing probe, and separately that every scalar\nhas a mirroring metric, so removing either side alone fails. dom.parentprocess\nsurvives in both files because process_launch_errors follows the probe.\n\nNo test anywhere in the tree references the probe under any spelling, so there\nis nothing to convert.\n\nThe open question for data engineering\n--------------------------------------\n\ntelemetry_derived.clients_daily_v6 carries a column\ndom_parentprocess_private_window_used that is sourced from this legacy scalar,\nnot from the Glean metric. For 2026-08-06 at sample_id = 0, distinct clients\nwith the scalar true in telemetry.main and distinct clients with the\nclients_daily column true are both exactly 36232 - it is the same data.\nclients_last_seen, clients_first_seen and clients_daily_joined inherit the\ncolumn from clients_daily.\n\nThree scheduled Redash queries read it: 123355 \"[PBW] Monthly KPIs (28d)\",\n123356 \"[PBW] Daily users & share (90d)\" and 123357 \"[PBW] Frequency\ndistribution (28d)\", all last modified 2026-07-17. 123355 computes pbw_mau and\npbw_pct_of_mau from COALESCE(dom_parentprocess_private_window_used, FALSE).\n\nSo landing this as-is would leave Firefox collecting the data correctly while\nthose KPIs silently report zero.\n\nThe Glean metric is a viable replacement - 38095 of 706587 firefox_desktop\nmetrics rows at sample_id = 0, the same order as clients_daily's ~5.8%. One\nsemantic catch for whoever repoints the ETL: glean_true equals glean_present\nexactly, because the metric is only ever Set(true). Absence means false, not\nunknown, and a repoint treating NULL as missing would shift every PBM ratio.\n\nAlso note this removes the \"This metric was generated to correspond to the\nLegacy Telemetry scalar ...\" sentence from the Glean description, which bug\n2061675 comment 1 suggested keeping. Dropping it matches D317115, where Review\nHelper Bot asked for the stale reference to go once the legacy probe was\ndeleted.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317374\n", "files": ["dom/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/telemetry/Scalars.yaml"], "git_node": "775fd3d909e5f5d6de5d81d52cb9788eec46c6d5", "git_parents": ["7e997e7f53776cf257d1ae5a75139aa7221a8f94"], "node": "4f67bab19294fa1a9501ec520ff65fd075aa939b", "parents": ["bfd37dce29b32dcfb89df2d8c083bf46c56e1f21"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Mehic \u003cdmehic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1938232 - Check the Turnstile result when the shadow root observer is installed r=tjr\n\nCFTurnstileHandler is only constructed on DOMContentLoaded/pageshow, but the\ntest iframe posts \"ready\" from its inline script while the document is still\nparsing. The test replies immediately, so the fail/success div can be shown\nbefore the handler exists.\n\nA MutationObserver only reports mutations made after observe(), so when that\nhappens the callback never runs, CaptchaState:Update is never sent, and the\ntest waits for a metric that never arrives until it times out. The same\napplies outside of tests: a Turnstile widget that resolves before\nDOMContentLoaded is never recorded.\n\nCheck the current state once right after observe() so an already-visible\nresult is still reported, guarded by a flag so a later mutation cannot report\nit twice.\n\nWhile here, store the observer before calling observe(). The previous code\nassigned the result of observe(), which is undefined, so onActorDestroy()\nthrew a TypeError and the shadow root observer was never disconnected.\n\nThe regression test drives this deterministically: cf_turnstile.html now\naccepts ?state=success|fail to show the result while it is still parsing, so\nthe result is already visible when the observer is registered. Without the\npreceding fix the test hangs with the same signature as the intermittent.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317295\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/captchadetection/CaptchaDetectionChild.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/captchadetection/tests/mochitest/cf_turnstile.html", "toolkit/components/captchadetection/tests/mochitest/mochitest.toml", "toolkit/components/captchadetection/tests/mochitest/test_cf_turnstile_early_fail.html"], "git_node": "708c56bce73ce1a32e5552da21464fb0b6fd5e77", "git_parents": ["775fd3d909e5f5d6de5d81d52cb9788eec46c6d5"], "node": "8505f38840ae36b8b6aa31b1b8fae98289691978", "parents": ["4f67bab19294fa1a9501ec520ff65fd075aa939b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Mehic \u003cdmehic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1902300 - Remove queryStripping Nimbus feature r=emz\n\nThe last experiment using this feature ran in Fx128. All Experimenter\nrecipes referencing queryStripping are enrollment-paused with end dates in\n2024 (latest 2024-09-03), so nothing live depends on it.\n\nThe feature only mapped variables onto privacy.query_stripping.* prefs and\nhad no NimbusFeatures.queryStripping consumers. Those prefs keep their\ndefaults in StaticPrefList.yaml, so query stripping itself is unchanged;\nit just can no longer be controlled remotely.\n\nbrowser_urlQueryStringStripping_nimbus.js only exercised the Nimbus\nintegration, so it is removed along with the feature.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317294\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/antitracking/test/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/antitracking/test/browser/browser_urlQueryStringStripping_nimbus.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/FeatureManifest.yaml"], "git_node": "3ebe87649c082c831a94d18ce409f8e432150779", "git_parents": ["708c56bce73ce1a32e5552da21464fb0b6fd5e77"], "node": "d7a22a8c147b0ac9236fcfa2fa9ee411e3f48ac6", "parents": ["8505f38840ae36b8b6aa31b1b8fae98289691978"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Mehic \u003cdmehic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1885206 - Drop the unused about:preferences load from browser_sanitizeDialog_v2_dataSizes.js. r=emz\n\nclearAndValidateDataSizes() opened about:preferences before every dialog\ncheck, but ClearHistoryDialogHelper is constructed with the default\n\"browser\" mode, so open() goes through Sanitizer.showUI() and the browser\nwindow's gDialogBox. The preferences tab was never read from, only torn\ndown again at the end of the helper.\n\nThe file is a soft per-file timeout intermittent: recent CI runs take\n182-212s against a 180s limit on Windows debug, and the harness flags it\nafterwards because the test is slow rather than hung. Dropping the nine\nredundant about:preferences loads takes the file from 36.7s to 7.9s on a\nlocal debug build (mean of three alternating runs each), with the whole\nbrowser/base/content/test/sanitize/ directory still green.\n\nIt also stops the test leaking identity.fxaccounts.account.device.name,\nwhich about:preferences sets when it initialises the FxA pane.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317338\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/sanitize/browser_sanitizeDialog_v2_dataSizes.js"], "git_node": "ca65b5ff6cffc4ad0ecd0b9a76b100e32db20f8c", "git_parents": ["3ebe87649c082c831a94d18ce409f8e432150779"], "node": "b167d03a8318ef28d3c82e28975c25daa3b24bae", "parents": ["d7a22a8c147b0ac9236fcfa2fa9ee411e3f48ac6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-central repo-update HSTS HPKP - r=release-managers,diannaS\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322081\n", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc"], "git_node": "d94be005197ee0b09f6a82fc24c7c9d8d1917c30", "git_parents": ["ca65b5ff6cffc4ad0ecd0b9a76b100e32db20f8c"], "node": "2e1b89d09bb95523a866d97c22c6868c67b8611f", "parents": ["b167d03a8318ef28d3c82e28975c25daa3b24bae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mathew Hodson \u003cmathew.hodson@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067452 - Remove obsolete comment r=emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322080\n", "files": ["image/decoders/nsJPEGDecoder.cpp"], "git_node": "ab50be72f3fa1a53d841ed15b8c6f9abf3bb2521", "git_parents": ["d94be005197ee0b09f6a82fc24c7c9d8d1917c30"], "node": "3684b4f604add6ddc5aa4d685eba10527a6c5040", "parents": ["2e1b89d09bb95523a866d97c22c6868c67b8611f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Import translations from https://github.com/mozilla-l10n/android-l10n CLOSED TREE\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/addons/src/main/res/values-lv/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/downloads/src/main/res/values-lv/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/sitepermissions/src/main/res/values-lv/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/res/values-cak/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/res/values-hu/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/res/values-ka/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/res/values-lv/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/res/values-ro/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-cak/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-hu/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-ka/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-lv/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-ro/strings.xml"], "git_node": "1b0c8fac6e93715898d0c6b74ebbf18e4b8b0fe3", "git_parents": ["ab50be72f3fa1a53d841ed15b8c6f9abf3bb2521"], "node": "82cfe718c1fdade11a6775c97367ef4bfb44d1fc", "parents": ["3684b4f604add6ddc5aa4d685eba10527a6c5040"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787995920, "git_changesets": ["6ba803cc5c7c108b53b295d60da53dac43261d0f", "7e997e7f53776cf257d1ae5a75139aa7221a8f94", "775fd3d909e5f5d6de5d81d52cb9788eec46c6d5", "708c56bce73ce1a32e5552da21464fb0b6fd5e77", "3ebe87649c082c831a94d18ce409f8e432150779", "ca65b5ff6cffc4ad0ecd0b9a76b100e32db20f8c", "d94be005197ee0b09f6a82fc24c7c9d8d1917c30", "ab50be72f3fa1a53d841ed15b8c6f9abf3bb2521", "1b0c8fac6e93715898d0c6b74ebbf18e4b8b0fe3"], "user": "sstanca@mozilla.com"}, "45206": {"changesets": [{"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2022026 - Add automated test r=smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D287522\n", "files": ["layout/generic/test/mochitest.toml", "layout/generic/test/test_bug2022026.html"], "git_node": "a311ac37c550d7ccca4f811e8f392bd52dac3c55", "git_parents": ["1b0c8fac6e93715898d0c6b74ebbf18e4b8b0fe3"], "node": "31dcede4f177f01d98bb9cd178def2e8f7d612c4", "parents": ["82cfe718c1fdade11a6775c97367ef4bfb44d1fc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063890. Add patch files for rlbox_wasm2c_sandbox's local changes. r=tjr,shravanrn\n\nTwo changes in the vendored sources have no patch files behind them, so re-vendoring\nrlbox_wasm2c_sandbox reverts them, and the next update would too:\n\n  bug 2027312, better crash reporting messages, in include/rlbox_wasm2c_sandbox.hpp\n  bug 2048557, use macros for libc clock IDs, in src/wasm2c_rt_minwasi.c\n\nThe library has no patches list at all, so add one. Nothing checked that vendoring\nreproduced the tree until now, so there was no sign of this in either the tree or the\nbuild.\n\nBug 2027312 changed the rlbox library in the same way, so there is a companion patch\nadding patch files to third_party/rlbox.\n\nNeither change is upstream, and the upstream-wasm2c branch we vendor from has had no\ncommits since the revision we are pinned to, so these patches should be expected to stay.\n\nWith this, `./mach vendor config/external/rlbox_wasm2c_sandbox/moz.yaml -r\n5f2573e2203169b1a3e728a6d612fb78429e1cb8 --patch-mode check --force` reproduces the\ncommitted tree exactly.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318940\n", "files": ["config/external/rlbox_wasm2c_sandbox/clock-id-macros.patch", "config/external/rlbox_wasm2c_sandbox/crash-reporting-messages.patch", "config/external/rlbox_wasm2c_sandbox/moz.yaml", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/vendor-verify-expected-fail.yml"], "git_node": "7af3513db13dd2d2d49e15e0090a33f0d9f1fac7", "git_parents": ["a311ac37c550d7ccca4f811e8f392bd52dac3c55"], "node": "6b37b4a0f3a732c592a3cddbb8163e1645b2d29b", "parents": ["31dcede4f177f01d98bb9cd178def2e8f7d612c4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063890. Add patch files for rlbox's local changes. r=tjr\n\nTwo changes in the vendored rlbox headers have no patch files behind them, so\nre-vendoring rlbox reverts them, and the next update would too:\n\n  bug 2027312, better crash reporting messages, in rlbox.hpp and rlbox_sandbox.hpp\n  bug 2045149, don't reject unaligned transfer buffers, in rlbox_stdlib.hpp\n\nNothing checked that vendoring reproduced the tree until now, so there was no sign of\nthis in either the tree or the build.\n\nThe second change matters beyond reproducibility: upstream at our pinned revision\nchecks unconditionally that the source range does not cross the sandbox boundary,\nwhich rejects legitimate unaligned buffers, and re-vendoring brings that back.\n\nCapture each as a patch file and add them to the patches list, after fix-includes.patch\nsince that also touches rlbox_sandbox.hpp.\n\nUpstream 67c6c7b1cd8b limits those boundary checks the same way bug 2045149 does, so that\npatch can be dropped whenever rlbox is updated past it, at which point patch will refuse\nto apply it anyway. I did not find an upstream equivalent of the crash reporting change.\n\nWith this, `./mach vendor third_party/rlbox/moz.yaml -r\nba8a24ec9d2d418d400bcf584da5031f20fff453 --patch-mode check --force` reproduces the\ncommitted tree exactly.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318939\n", "files": ["taskcluster/scripts/misc/vendor-verify-expected-fail.yml", "third_party/rlbox/crash-reporting-messages.patch", "third_party/rlbox/moz.yaml", "third_party/rlbox/unaligned-transfer-buffers.patch"], "git_node": "0eeb4e3a1982f06efe9fe3eac8bc75861a3aee23", "git_parents": ["7af3513db13dd2d2d49e15e0090a33f0d9f1fac7"], "node": "f23ac2cf420889d4dbff8f46970c299c26a834d6", "parents": ["6b37b4a0f3a732c592a3cddbb8163e1645b2d29b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2022026 - Add automated test r=smaug\" for causing mochitest failures @test_bug2022026.html.\n\nThis reverts commit a311ac37c550d7ccca4f811e8f392bd52dac3c55.\n", "files": ["layout/generic/test/mochitest.toml", "layout/generic/test/test_bug2022026.html"], "git_node": "cb8e2001b16f1a8d08eb2ce5a3226e0549e2a262", "git_parents": ["0eeb4e3a1982f06efe9fe3eac8bc75861a3aee23"], "node": "c00c3c66f5219bcb6d93ef2ec9a2fea341d0bbbd", "parents": ["f23ac2cf420889d4dbff8f46970c299c26a834d6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2009628 - Enable browser.urlbar.searchModeSwitcher.skipTabStop by default. r=daleharvey\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321934\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js"], "git_node": "b1df5cab96157ed4fe1824041d39fed306aad50f", "git_parents": ["cb8e2001b16f1a8d08eb2ce5a3226e0549e2a262"], "node": "3c8e578f4219a160a5ba1889ea4c735c62f1b193", "parents": ["c00c3c66f5219bcb6d93ef2ec9a2fea341d0bbbd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067305 - Give the newtab search bar the address bar's placeholders. r=daleharvey\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322030\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarNewTabComponentRegistrant.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderHeuristicFallback.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs", "browser/com