84cccce3e978b806518dbbd1", "git_parents": ["e32c4825e5e033da7306d5799d85a1d17cd4cb84"], "node": "ecbd75dec8fa5c8bcf96a3898a8972414d05cfde", "parents": ["faecf03ea19462d00fbdb0c0ed853017b2a78f0a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1899692 - Propagate a root-snapping surface's scale to its child surfaces r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nworld_scale_factors is a surface's space to device scale, which a child surface\nmultiplies its own child-to-parent scale by to obtain child-to-device. A\nroot-snapping surface reported (1, 1), correct only while root raster space is\ndevice space. APZ breaks that when it writes a pinch-zoom scale into a bound\nspatial node transform, so a child establishing its own raster root lost the\nzoom and rasterized its targets that many times too small, stretching the\ncorners of a rounded clip applied over one.\n\nThat field was also standing in for the scale blur radii are clamped against,\nwhich held only because exactly one of it and local_scale was ever non-unit.\nSplit that out into blur_scale_factors, keeping its old per-axis value in every\nbranch, so blur clamping is unchanged.\n\nThe test uses a static scale in place of the zoom, since APZ only writes scale\nfactors into a bound spatial node transform, so it needs no APZ.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321750\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/frame_builder.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/picture.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/space.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/surface.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/transforms/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/transforms/zoomed-rounded-clip-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/transforms/zoomed-rounded-clip.yaml"], "git_node": "83c592ca0845730ca0c90f2782a92c7fce834ca2", "git_parents": ["63759b7b23782df284cccce3e978b806518dbbd1"], "node": "cf04064d1478732906a1fd6446a40fbae5f13b96", "parents": ["ecbd75dec8fa5c8bcf96a3898a8972414d05cfde"], "tags": []}, {"author": 