a3a5ecadf4c2f231a\nms -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\nmy -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\nnb-NO -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\nne-NP -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\nnl -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\nnn-NO -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\noc -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\npa-IN -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\npl -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\npt-BR -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\npt-PT -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\nrm -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\nro -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\nru -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\nsk -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\nsl -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\nson -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\nsq -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\nsr -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\nsv-SE -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\nta -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\nte -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\nth -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\ntl -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\ntr -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\ntrs -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\nuk -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\nur -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\nuz -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\nvi -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\nwo -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\nxh -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\nzam -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\nzh-CN -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\nzh-TW -\u003e 870a61b6c20495e51e1cf0fa3a5ecadf4c2f231a\n", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": "7ffb380260ea66fcdf105c642de00ca80d6f0e7f", "git_parents": ["6b4de0eadb20e6b72c960e8236ba8d2ddfd84018"], "node": "20be66a0724b52f92ae6d560815a3888be4637b1", "parents": ["3d696fe3465c4f28769026153c083532f446b2b1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Denis Palmeiro \u003cdpalmeiro@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066276 - Snapshot monomorphic inline hints once per WarpScriptOracle. r=iain\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321088\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/JitHints.cpp", "js/src/jit/JitHints.h", "js/src/jit/WarpOracle.cpp"], "git_node": "39cd6b355081a2a46dac7292ee32b26d507729a0", "git_parents": ["7ffb380260ea66fcdf105c642de00ca80d6f0e7f"], "node": "954841bfe882e6b5a957550ab25e29e7ef8d6ab1", "parents": ["20be66a0724b52f92ae6d560815a3888be4637b1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnical@fastmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066837 - Carry a device-space coverage rect on every primitive command. r=gw,gfx-reviewers\n\nThe only footprint batching can reach today is\n`ClipChainInstance::pic_coverage_rect`, in the local space of the picture\nbeing rendered into, and it is per *primitive*. Prepare already knows\nbetter than that: the quad paths compute device-space rects, and where a\nprimitive is split into several quads - a repeated pattern's tiles, a\nborder's nine-patch segments - each quad has its own much tighter rect than\nthe primitive it came from.\n\nAdd a device rect to every `PrimitiveCommand` and encode it in the command\nbuffer, so each command can carry the tightest footprint its producer knows\nrather than sharing one per primitive. The quad path supplies its own\nper-quad rect; text runs and split composites have nothing tighter on hand\nthan the primitive's coverage rect, and map that through the surface.\n\nNothing reads the new field yet; subsequent patches convert the consumers.\n\nThe four `f32` words per draw command are paid unconditionally. If that\nshows up in profiles, the alternative is to store the rects in a side\nvector and encode a single index word.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321850\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/batch.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/command_buffer.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/picture.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs"], "git_node": "0dd5c88579e2fed2b6732eb823d363ce7153b0f1", "git_parents": ["39cd6b355081a2a46dac7292ee32b26d507729a0"], "node": "84af8b113ec2df6dcf5524f0d8a1cca98315d2fb", "parents": ["954841bfe882e6b5a957550ab25e29e7ef8d6ab1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnical@fastmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066837 - Batch primitives against their device-space footprint. r=gw,gfx-reviewers\n\nThe batcher's only use for a primitive's rect is overlap testing (to decide\nwhether an instance can join an earlier compatible batch) and a \"large\noccluder\" area heuristic. Both were done in picture space.\n\nTwo things fall out of that. The area heuristic compares against\n`screen_width * screen_height / 4`, in device pixels squared, so on any\nsurface whose device pixel scale is not 1.0 it fires at the wrong size. And\nthe text run path derives a tight per-sub-run bounding rect in device space\nand then builds a `SpaceMapper` purely to unmap it back into picture space\nfor the batcher's benefit.\n\nSwitch `BatchRects` and the `set_params_and_get_batch` family to\n`DeviceRect` and read the rect each command now carries. The text run path\nstill derives its tight rect in picture space; it maps that result forward\ninto device space, which drops one of the two space mappers it needed.\n\nBatching runs per render task, and a task has a single surface, so all the\nrects a given batcher sees share one device space. They are deliberately\nnot task-relative: the content origin is not subtracted, so one command\nstays comparable across every tile of a tile cache. Batches from different\ntasks are only ever merged by key, never overlap-tested against each other,\nwhich is what keeps per-task device spaces from being compared.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321851\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/batch.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/frame_builder.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_target.rs"], "git_node": "c702968694a81be2c330d100403ac25540426502", "git_parents": ["0dd5c88579e2fed2b6732eb823d363ce7153b0f1"], "node": "b855308cdf43e9689845b180ee2339461a1f5f01", "parents": ["84af8b113ec2df6dcf5524f0d8a1cca98315d2fb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnical@fastmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066837 - Derive the text run's tight bounding rect directly in device space. r=gw,gfx-reviewers\n\nBoth branches of the per-sub-run tight bounding rect existed to hand the\nbatcher a picture-space rect, and each built a `SpaceMapper` to get there.\nThe transformed-glyph branch was the perverse one: it accumulated glyph\nrects in device space and then unmapped them back into picture space, which\nthe previous patch had to map forward again.\n\nHave both branches produce a device rect. The transformed-glyph branch just\nreturns what it accumulated, and folds the raster -\u003e device scale into the\nglyph transform so that the sub-pixel snapping floors against the device\npixel grid rather than the raster one - which is what the removed TODO on\nthat transform was asking for. The local-raster branch maps its layout-space\nrect straight to device instead of by way of the surface's picture space.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321852\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/batch.rs"], "git_node": "fd6dcfc9303e23b0fc6692a1274f34ad0ce15c88", "git_parents": ["c702968694a81be2c330d100403ac25540426502"], "node": "2f92108cd3959ececcd9e8098f7a56ba194a7fa1", "parents": ["b855308cdf43e9689845b180ee2339461a1f5f01"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnical@fastmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066837 - Batch quad segments against their own device rect. r=gw,gfx-reviewers\n\nA tiled or nine-patch quad emits one instance per segment, and each of\nthose covers a small, disjoint part of the quad - but they were all batched\nagainst the quad's overall rect, so a primitive drawn between the tiles of\nanother still reported an overlap and broke the batch.\n\nThe segment rects are already in device space by the time prepare hands\nthem to `set_segments`, so carry them through the command buffer alongside\nthe task ids and give each instance its own rect. Quads with no segments\nare unaffected and keep using the rect on their command.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321853\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/batch.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/command_buffer.rs"], "git_node": "4b55fa23f6ee3808ddb7f4d257fa96fb9dadb8cb", "git_parents": ["fd6dcfc9303e23b0fc6692a1274f34ad0ce15c88"], "node": "6929996c8af9663b90e4868cbe6f2cb04b9aa570", "parents": ["2f92108cd3959ececcd9e8098f7a56ba194a7fa1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066837 - Remove the quad command's draw index. r=gw,gfx-reviewers\n\nIt is now unused.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321854\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/batch.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/border_image.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/box_shadow.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/command_buffer.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/picture.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/borders.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/image.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs"], "git_node": "5555bbede0b9562295c4cbf5f764c82b67d7fcaf", "git_parents": ["4b55fa23f6ee3808ddb7f4d257fa96fb9dadb8cb"], "node": "8fac41b17e6d712925f52a4e572b1c8563850747", "parents": ["6929996c8af9663b90e4868cbe6f2cb04b9aa570"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Aaron Train \u003caaron.train@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066799 - Add emulator coverage for 16KB page size in ARM64v8a android-startup task r=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322347\n", "files": ["mobile/android/test_infra/flank-configs/fenix/arm-start-test.yml"], "git_node": "aec3fa62ddf44349854def9023d9fad771fd353a", "git_parents": ["5555bbede0b9562295c4cbf5f764c82b67d7fcaf"], "node": "a1d41ebc5158e2d31d9490d412fa1948b128b9a9", "parents": ["8fac41b17e6d712925f52a4e572b1c8563850747"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Taimur Hasan \u003cthasan@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065689 - Skip the redundant page-ready wait across headless and foreground extraction r=nordzilla,ai-platform-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320622\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/pageextractor/PageExtractorChild.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "0fb77cb8c340fd55cfabfbe2ebc83af3634e0455", "git_parents": ["aec3fa62ddf44349854def9023d9fad771fd353a"], "node": "4fdb6717f1eb61aad22c5464c49c98779cf9d0e9", "parents": ["a1d41ebc5158e2d31d9490d412fa1948b128b9a9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Luca Greco \u003clgreco@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059864 - [a11y] Tweak about:addons page and card layout to be responsive and stay usable on high zoom levels. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,sfoster\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321363\n", "files": ["toolkit/mozapps/extensions/content/aboutaddons.css", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/content/components/aboutaddons-themes-mode.css", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/content/components/aboutaddons-themes-picker.css", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/browser/browser_html_a11y_no_horizontal_overflow.js", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/browser/browser_html_detail_view.js"], "git_node": "4945dc8f17677c1d0fe8ef55c5d8f479934f5d25", "git_parents": ["0fb77cb8c340fd55cfabfbe2ebc83af3634e0455"], "node": "c3cae651cc949f3db251c4a35d803014513b4096", "parents": ["4fdb6717f1eb61aad22c5464c49c98779cf9d0e9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "SaaSha Pina \u003csaasha@heysparkbox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061289 - Match moz-input-search clear button radius to the search field. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,mstriemer\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319227\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/widgets/moz-input-text/moz-input-text.css"], "git_node": "7005a76a9ceba51c1544cec1ad396b12d4821102", "git_parents": ["4945dc8f17677c1d0fe8ef55c5d8f479934f5d25"], "node": "39894678b61c28a620a99f034b9de02555e7aecc", "parents": ["c3cae651cc949f3db251c4a35d803014513b4096"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067604 - Assert non-null in TextInputDelegateTest's getExtractedText() callers. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall\n\nAndroid SDK 37.2 annotates InputConnection.getExtractedText() as @Nullable, so Kotlin rejects the\nunchecked dereferences in these test helpers. GeckoInputConnection genuinely returns null when there\nis no Editable, which is a test failure here, so assert rather than propagate the nullability.\n\nThe assertions are no-ops against SDK 37.1, where the unannotated return is a platform type.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322220\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/TextInputDelegateTest.kt"], "git_node": "b8f7416997b48dc2b7319d06d3a4a9eab4a87cb2", "git_parents": ["7005a76a9ceba51c1544cec1ad396b12d4821102"], "node": "66c3ac6d703c9e6e5161f2b2bd12649b4ec5bd8b", "parents": ["39894678b61c28a620a99f034b9de02555e7aecc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062521 - Don't apply a test's @TimeoutMillis to the rule's pref plumbing. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall\n\nEvery test in a class whose @Before calls setPrefsUntilTestEnd does a SetPrefs and a RestorePrefs round\ntrip through the test support extension, and both waits used the test's mTimeoutMillis, so a short\n@TimeoutMillis caps them at a value the round trip cannot reliably meet on a loaded emulator. The\nrestore runs after the test body, so its timeout comes from the rule and fails the test rather than\nbeing swallowed by @Test(expected). Pass the harness default for both, as cleanupExtensions() does.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322221\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/rule/GeckoSessionTestRule.java"], "git_node": "c65ec07897a802d1784502c8a3af155b0688bf02", "git_parents": ["b8f7416997b48dc2b7319d06d3a4a9eab4a87cb2"], "node": "f45f355ade20d7c8eb247d6705b55b3faf58a5f0", "parents": ["66c3ac6d703c9e6e5161f2b2bd12649b4ec5bd8b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062521 - Clear view focus before the blur in noDismissKeyboardAfterlostFocus. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall\n\nGeckoEditable schedules the dismissal DISMISS_VKB_DELAY_MS after content loses focus, and\nHideSoftInputTask suppresses it by checking View.hasFocus() when it runs. The test blurred first and\ncleared the view's focus afterwards, so on debug, where the blur round trip takes about that long, the\ntask could run just before clearFocus() landed, see a focused view and dismiss. Clear the view's focus\nfirst: hasFocus() is synchronous, so the precondition holds before the dismissal is ever scheduled.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322222\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/TextInputDelegateTest.kt"], "git_node": "905ef9fa61c2333af11650b70fff3e26eca4058d", "git_parents": ["c65ec07897a802d1784502c8a3af155b0688bf02"], "node": "60f3590159052a04117b939ca4b7662a28e6d246", "parents": ["f45f355ade20d7c8eb247d6705b55b3faf58a5f0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062521 - Don't expect a timeout in noDismissKeyboardAfterlostFocus. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall\n\nThe test expected UiThreadUtils.TimeoutException, but @Test(expected) accepts a timeout from any wait\nin the body and @TimeoutMillis(2000) capped all of them, so a slow page load or showSoftInput wait\ncould pass the test without reaching its assertion. When a dismissal did arrive the assertion was\ncollected by ErrorCollector and then discarded, because the expected-exception check fails the method\nbefore the collector's verify() runs, leaving only \"Expected exception: TimeoutException\" in the log.\n\nBound just the negative wait and assert directly. Dropping @TimeoutMillis also stops the test\nshortening the rule's timeout for its own setup and teardown.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322223\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/TextInputDelegateTest.kt"], "git_node": "0f732e2267d449bff15c78f407895474c7e5d954", "git_parents": ["905ef9fa61c2333af11650b70fff3e26eca4058d"], "node": "7b69d8b36f27e9e47f8a3618835c0a9d82edcd37", "parents": ["60f3590159052a04117b939ca4b7662a28e6d246"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Elissa Cha \u003cecha@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065311 - Make the starter prompts row scrollable r=pdahiya,fluent-reviewers,bolsson\n\n- Makes the fullpage starter row horizontally scrollable with edge fades, hover-reveal scroll buttons\n- Caps the fullpage starter row to the same width as the smartbar/header for consistent alignmen\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321060\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-window/ai-window.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-prompts/smartwindow-prompts.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-prompts/smartwindow-prompts.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-prompts/smartwindow-prompts.stories.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_prompts.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/test_smartwindow_prompts_page.html", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/aiWindow.ftl"], "git_node": "497bb28cb850f52e82805d628dd5715b8c5813dd", "git_parents": ["0f732e2267d449bff15c78f407895474c7e5d954"], "node": "69fbe58708d98867d523b1dad3571ff5de2505ca", "parents": ["7b69d8b36f27e9e47f8a3618835c0a9d82edcd37"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067314 - Stop applying the gradle-python-envs plugin in mobile/android. r=ahochheiden\n\nThe Glean Gradle plugin only needs it to bootstrap a Miniconda for glean_parser, which it skips entirely\nwhen `gleanPythonEnvDir` is set - and every consumer here points that at the mach virtualenv, where\nglean_parser is already vendored.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322009\n", "files": ["gradle/libs.versions.toml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/engine-gecko/build.gradle", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/fxsuggest/build.gradle", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/media/build.gradle", "mobile/android/android-components/components/lib/crash/build.gradle", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/nimbus/build.gradle", "mobile/android/android-components/samples/glean/build.gradle", "mobile/android/android-components/samples/glean/samples-glean-library/build.gradle", "mobile/android/fenix/app/build.gradle", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/build.gradle"], "git_node": "e54de45341c7010a10c6e1904cd0d0ddc96e8d02", "git_parents": ["497bb28cb850f52e82805d628dd5715b8c5813dd"], "node": "d7507ebbfb45dd9f74ca2cf7e9b747956273b573", "parents": ["69fbe58708d98867d523b1dad3571ff5de2505ca"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067314 - Stop fetching the gradle-python-envs plugin in CI. r=ahochheiden,geckoview-reviewers,ohall\n\nNothing applies the plugin any more, so the Gradle Plugin Portal fetch it needed, and the extra Maven\nrepository that served it, can go. The packaging directory that fetch also happened to create moves to the\nscript that copies into it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322010\n", "files": ["mobile/android/config/mozconfigs/android-arm-gradle-dependencies/base", "mobile/android/config/mozconfigs/common", "taskcluster/scripts/builder/build-android.sh", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/android-gradle-dependencies/after.sh", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/android-gradle-dependencies/before.sh"], "git_node": "33bfd81f506c1ef22dc5103293522bfd4039e286", "git_parents": ["e54de45341c7010a10c6e1904cd0d0ddc96e8d02"], "node": "f0062f61f1fa17a30af5f2e675e48e92fb969d4f", "parents": ["d7507ebbfb45dd9f74ca2cf7e9b747956273b573"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nika Layzell \u003cnika@thelayzells.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050774 - Part 1: Consider precursor origin in ValidatePrincipal, r=asuth\n\nAn extra tier is added to LoadedOriginSet to track site-origins which\nare only loaded as a null principal precursor. This is then used by\nValidatePrincipal to allow these loaded origins only during precursor\nprincipal validation.\n\nIn order to add this extra level, there are a few simplifications made\nto the LoadedOriginSet type as well, changing the signature of a few\ntypes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319631\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/ContentParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/LoadedOriginSet.cpp", "dom/ipc/LoadedOriginSet.h", "dom/ipc/ProcessIsolation.cpp", "dom/ipc/ProcessIsolation.h"], "git_node": "20828199269d4c55d2bbab1a9e2bb57fda8d9ed7", "git_parents": ["33bfd81f506c1ef22dc5103293522bfd4039e286"], "node": "b87864bd8c9c54bea9f3dff6dd19bdd56d2a2355", "parents": ["f0062f61f1fa17a30af5f2e675e48e92fb969d4f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nika Layzell \u003cnika@thelayzells.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050774 - Part 2: Trust PrincipalToInherit from HTTP(s) redirects, r=vhilla,necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321321\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/ContentChild.cpp", "dom/security/nsContentSecurityManager.cpp", "netwerk/base/LoadInfo.cpp", "netwerk/base/LoadInfo.h", "netwerk/base/TRRLoadInfo.cpp", "netwerk/base/nsILoadInfo.idl", "netwerk/ipc/DocumentChannelChild.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpBaseChannel.cpp"], "git_node": "317f6f2c67839c45d6acf5df5c14758bab9158fb", "git_parents": ["20828199269d4c55d2bbab1a9e2bb57fda8d9ed7"], "node": "839675e9e66f8597f198aaf7635570e9f457767d", "parents": ["b87864bd8c9c54bea9f3dff6dd19bdd56d2a2355"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alastor Wu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065393 - Part 1: Drop queued pre-seek audio when stopping a reused stream. r=padenot,media-playback-reviewers\n\nAn audio stream reused across a seek is never stopped, so its callback keeps\nconsuming the sink's ring buffer while the sink is stopped. That audio belongs to\nthe position being left behind, and it played until the resume dropped the\nremainder, leaking a fragment of the old position on every seek.\n\nSet the discard boundary when the seek begins instead, so the callback skips that\naudio. Emptying the buffer early also has to be told apart from the source\nending, so mark the sink as deliberately starved for that window; otherwise a\nseek issued once the audio queue had finished would drain the stream and lose the\nreuse.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321760\n", "files": ["dom/media/mediasink/AudioSink.cpp", "dom/media/mediasink/AudioSink.h"], "git_node": "ae76e6debc5dc20c6ea7f053acc86155bebae8ae", "git_parents": ["317f6f2c67839c45d6acf5df5c14758bab9158fb"], "node": "2fc792bbb92588ada19f51388bf4d4365afe23d0", "parents": ["839675e9e66f8597f198aaf7635570e9f457767d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alastor Wu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065393 - Part 2: Test that a sink stopped for a seek outputs silence. r=padenot,media-playback-reviewers\n\nThe existing stream-reuse tests only assert on what plays after the resume, so\nnothing covered the window in which the sink is stopped and its stashed stream is\nstill running. Drive the callbacks in that window and require every sample to be\nsilence, then resume and require the stream to be reused and the whole post-seek\nbuffer to play, so the invariant cannot be satisfied by tearing the stream down\ninstead.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321761\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestAudioSinkWrapper.cpp"], "git_node": "0e08974561e5c1269cb735aa0218495ac117d71b", "git_parents": ["ae76e6debc5dc20c6ea7f053acc86155bebae8ae"], "node": "3ffa6b42e38b190882ae771b63ac76ff150c7f5d", "parents": ["2fc792bbb92588ada19f51388bf4d4365afe23d0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alastor Wu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065393 - Part 3: Stop reporting the silence a seek asks for as an underrun. r=padenot,media-playback-reviewers\n\nEmptying the sink's ring buffer for a seek leaves nothing to hand back, so the\nshortfall was reported as a glitch on every callback of the seek. Let the source\nsay when a shortfall is deliberate and skip the reporting then. The zero fill and\nthe frame accounting are unchanged, so the position still holds at the target.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321762\n", "files": ["dom/media/AudioStream.cpp", "dom/media/AudioStream.h", "dom/media/mediasink/AudioSink.cpp", "dom/media/mediasink/AudioSink.h"], "git_node": "573605acaa04b6eab8c2dafed95b27ad842d62c4", "git_parents": ["0e08974561e5c1269cb735aa0218495ac117d71b"], "node": "3a54c41ff980d6b4a8877e4d6932e960304f8513", "parents": ["3ffa6b42e38b190882ae771b63ac76ff150c7f5d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alastor Wu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065393 - Part 4: Document how a reused audio stream behaves across a seek. r=padenot,media-playback-reviewers\n\nThe page covers the seek-resume clock but not what the stream does while the sink\nis stopped, which is now the surprising half: the callback runs against a buffer\nemptied on purpose. Record the resulting silence and the properties that depend\non it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321763\n", "files": ["dom/media/docs/AudioSinkWrapper.md"], "git_node": "e7347c761c30d5f1a696956c631d606eed9fe306", "git_parents": ["573605acaa04b6eab8c2dafed95b27ad842d62c4"], "node": "dbdc3fa64995cf6fe47cd77329b06a4a6db4f20d", "parents": ["3a54c41ff980d6b4a8877e4d6932e960304f8513"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067265 - Update libvpx to 5c880e08d21386049adec8e5537c4e726458b563 r=chunmin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321967\n", "files": ["media/libvpx/config/vpx_version.h", "media/libvpx/libvpx/AUTHORS", "media/libvpx/libvpx/CHANGELOG", "media/libvpx/libvpx/libs.mk", "media/libvpx/libvpx/test/decode_api_test.cc", "media/libvpx/libvpx/test/encode_api_test.cc", "media/libvpx/libvpx/test/pp_filter_test.cc", "media/libvpx/libvpx/test/vpx_image_test.cc", "media/libvpx/libvpx/vp8/encoder/encodeframe.c", "media/libvpx/libvpx/vp8/encoder/onyx_if.c", "media/libvpx/libvpx/vp8/vp8_cx_iface.c", "media/libvpx/libvpx/vp8/vp8_dx_iface.c", "media/libvpx/libvpx/vp9/vp9_cx_iface.c", "media/libvpx/libvpx/vpx/src/vpx_image.c", "media/libvpx/libvpx/vpx/vp8cx.h", "media/libvpx/libvpx/vpx_dsp/mips/deblock_msa.c", "media/libvpx/libvpx/vpx_dsp/x86/deblock_sse2.c", "media/libvpx/libvpx/vpx_ports/aarch64_cpudetect.c", "media/libvpx/libvpx/vpx_util/vpx_pthread.h", "media/libvpx/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "31198a65a18ed325976b46cdebb2775d17e87020", "git_parents": ["e7347c761c30d5f1a696956c631d606eed9fe306"], "node": "7a84f89b54e9ff7f95ff89e295789d644ef3164f", "parents": ["dbdc3fa64995cf6fe47cd77329b06a4a6db4f20d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067265 - Apply mozilla patches for libvpx r=chunmin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321968\n", "files": ["media/libvpx/libvpx/vp8/vp8_cx_iface.c", "media/libvpx/libvpx/vp9/vp9_cx_iface.c", "media/libvpx/libvpx/vpx_ports/aarch64_cpudetect.c", "media/libvpx/libvpx/vpx_util/vpx_pthread.h"], "git_node": "8ad9c96197c7708e17b8582b318c1373bd4de65b", "git_parents": ["31198a65a18ed325976b46cdebb2775d17e87020"], "node": "a1fae6f7f9841bc9cde25f4509826c158c4c6094", "parents": ["7a84f89b54e9ff7f95ff89e295789d644ef3164f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Parks \u003cdaparks@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061235: Clean up some uses of STGMEDIUM r=win-reviewers,gstoll\n\nThis patch includes a bunch of tiny code improvements:\n\n1. The main part of this patch is in nsDataObj::GetText, where it sizes the buffer that we add to the STGMEDIUM by the max char size for the code page, specifically for folks who have configured Windows with the experimental UTF-8 code page, where characters can be 3 bytes.  (NB: An AI checked on stateful code pages.  With state, the max character size can be exceeded.  However, the AI reports that Windows does not allow those pages as CP_ACP.  It says: \"CP_ACP can only resolve to a single-byte code page, a DBCS code page, or 65001. ISO-2022-* and UTF-7 are usable as explicit code-page arguments but Windows won't install them as the system ANSI code page. Every ACP-eligible family is stateless, and all of them held the bound in the measurements above.\".)\n\n2. ScopedOLEMemory checks that the size_t allocation is within bounds.\n\n3. Initializes STGMEDIUM (to TYMED_NULL) in places where it wasn't before.\n\n4. Releases allocated STGMEDIUMs on error (and return an error code when appropriate).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321723\n", "files": ["widget/windows/WinOLELock.h", "widget/windows/nsClipboard.cpp", "widget/windows/nsDataObj.cpp", "widget/windows/nsDataObjCollection.cpp", "widget/windows/nsDragService.cpp"], "git_node": "4a60e484f6ecf6561eb47fdf99beef2ca14848ac", "git_parents": ["8ad9c96197c7708e17b8582b318c1373bd4de65b"], "node": "cc1755db944f6f54fbd7b65d215afb2376a15520", "parents": ["a1fae6f7f9841bc9cde25f4509826c158c4c6094"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2050774 - Part 2: Trust PrincipalToInherit from HTTP(s) redirects, r=vhilla,necko-reviewers,valentin\" for causing reftests failures in ContentParent.cpp.\n\nThis reverts commit 317f6f2c67839c45d6acf5df5c14758bab9158fb.\n\nThis reverts commit 20828199269d4c55d2bbab1a9e2bb57fda8d9ed7.\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/ContentChild.cpp", "dom/ipc/ContentParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/LoadedOriginSet.cpp", "dom/ipc/LoadedOriginSet.h", "dom/ipc/ProcessIsolation.cpp", "dom/ipc/ProcessIsolation.h", "dom/security/nsContentSecurityManager.cpp", "netwerk/base/LoadInfo.cpp", "netwerk/base/LoadInfo.h", "netwerk/base/TRRLoadInfo.cpp", "netwerk/base/nsILoadInfo.idl", "netwerk/ipc/DocumentChannelChild.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpBaseChannel.cpp"], "git_node": "ddf348b43cd0e3fd4a2f0cd3929ad6b3deb70c98", "git_parents": ["4a60e484f6ecf6561eb47fdf99beef2ca14848ac"], "node": "5e50eebfa39a53f99d19abe1f6aa3a696c1c6fc3", "parents": ["cc1755db944f6f54fbd7b65d215afb2376a15520"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gopar \u003cgopardaniel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1981626 - Add ordered field to performance artifact schema r=sparky\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321576\n", "files": ["testing/mozharness/external_tools/performance-artifact-schema.json"], "git_node": "78f55b7830a94b3b534258a379286a446ae37b20", "git_parents": ["ddf348b43cd0e3fd4a2f0cd3929ad6b3deb70c98"], "node": "cf0ad7eb26169a8b6ddc654b9a949611ead1b277", "parents": ["5e50eebfa39a53f99d19abe1f6aa3a696c1c6fc3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058181 - More carefully clamp grid tracks. r=dshin\n\nPull request: https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/pull/352\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsGridContainerFrame.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/firefox-bug-2058181-crash.html"], "git_node": "a7bca7e4b37e40531231d502d13d1b913906e6a9", "git_parents": ["78f55b7830a94b3b534258a379286a446ae37b20"], "node": "e1119d47647851440df46b08e59b7e3fbda6dd6c", "parents": ["cf0ad7eb26169a8b6ddc654b9a949611ead1b277"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emily McDonough \u003cemcdonough@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064453 - Consider collapsing margin when computing the resulting size when clamping for line-clamp r=layout-reviewers,jfkthame,dshin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321432\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsBlockFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsBlockFrame.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-022.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "ec543095aef8fdf5f74883a81f1f6a173e08614f", "git_parents": ["a7bca7e4b37e40531231d502d13d1b913906e6a9"], "node": "5aada86191911c010292a7ca6208c579dc77a150", "parents": ["e1119d47647851440df46b08e59b7e3fbda6dd6c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Exploding-Joysticks \u003cExplodingJoysticks@proton.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1891250 - Remove the network.http.origin.redirectTainted pref r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322378\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpChannel.cpp"], "git_node": "38cabc00d69da70f579ad03d2f1aa9b54b4d1905",