d52dcd595ac65639bfde6446cfcf578ba197", "parents": ["db2c474aa819ceec9236ea54fe7b9011a61739fd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Hynson \u003cmhynson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056749 - Add -moz-scrollbar-inset-{block, inline} for improved scrollbar boundaries for rounded chrome corners. r=emilio,tabbrowser-reviewers,firefox-style-system-reviewers,layout-reviewers,sthompson\n\n- Adds `-moz-scrollbar-inset-block` and `-moz-scrollbar-inset-inline`, chrome-only\n  `\u003cnon-negative-length\u003e{1,2}` longhands. Each names the scrollbar's axis it\n  applies to. The two values are the axis' logical start and end\n  and flip with the writing mode.\n- ScrollContainerFrame::ScrollbarInsets() serves as the one place to extract the inset from for\n    both nsScrollbarFrame and GetBorderRadii\n- Applies inset to nsScrollbarFrame::Reflow similar to stepper buttons\n- ScrollContainerFrame::GetBorderRadii no longer squares a corner off when the\n  inset already holds the scrollbar clear of the curve.\n- Forward the \u003cbrowser\u003e embedder's inset to a root scrollbar for the content viewport\n- Add reftests for css-scrollbars\n- This commit does NOT implement the css property anywhere\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313900\n", "files": ["devtools/server/actors/animation-type-longhand.js", "docshell/base/BrowsingContext.cpp", "docshell/base/BrowsingContext.h", "dom/base/use_counter_metrics.yaml", "layout/base/nsPresContext.cpp", "layout/base/nsPresContext.h", "layout/generic/ScrollContainerFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/ScrollContainerFrame.h", "layout/generic/WritingModes.h", "layout/generic/nsSubDocumentFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsSubDocumentFrame.h", "layout/reftests/css-scrollbars/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/css-scrollbars/scrollbar-inset-change-ref.html", "layout/reftests/css-scrollbars/scrollbar-inset-change.html", "layout/reftests/css-scrollbars/scrollbar-inset-forward-change.html", "layout/reftests/css-scrollbars/scrollbar-inset-forward-inner.html", "layout/reftests/css-scrollbars/scrollbar-inset-forward-notref.html", "layout/reftests/css-scrollbars/scrollbar-inset-forward.html", "layout/reftests/css-scrollbars/scrollbar-inset-inline-notref.html", "layout/reftests/css-scrollbars/scrollbar-inset-inline.html", "layout/reftests/css-scrollbars/scrollbar-inset-radii-change.html", "layout/reftests/css-scrollbars/scrollbar-inset-radii-inline-notref.html", "layout/reftests/css-scrollbars/scrollbar-inset-radii-inline.html", "layout/reftests/css-scrollbars/scrollbar-inset-radii-notref.html", "layout/reftests/css-scrollbars/scrollbar-inset-radii-ref.html", "layout/reftests/css-scrollbars/scrollbar-inset-radii-rtl.html", "layout/reftests/css-scrollbars/scrollbar-inset-radii.html", "layout/reftests/css-scrollbars/scrollbar-inset-rtl.html", "layout/reftests/css-scrollbars/scrollbar-inset-zoom.html", "layout/style/GenerateCSSProperties.py", "layout/style/ServoBindings.toml", "layout/style/nsStyleStruct.cpp", "layout/style/nsStyleStruct.h", "layout/style/test/property_database.js", "layout/tools/reftest/jar.mn", "layout/xul/nsScrollbarFrame.cpp", "layout/xul/nsScrollbarFrame.h", "servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/values/computed/box.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/generics/box.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/box.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/mod.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/cbindgen.toml"], "git_node": "5e4975452794abcda7f5730c646a538163ffda86", "git_parents": ["715cafa4f8527f7d692375d266895c3699141ed1"], "node": "664447017bf518ff7fb58deb4efa8ce5a0b97daa", "parents": ["7c1ad52dcd595ac65639bfde6446cfcf578ba197"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hiroyuki Ikezoe \u003chikezoe.birchill@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059195 - Track each pipeline's embedder LayersId in CompositorBridgeParent::LayerTreeState. r=gfx-reviewers,aosmond\n\nExtend NotifyChildCreated, MapAndNotifyChildCreated, and NotifyChildRecreated\nto carry the LayersId of the pipeline that embeds the newly (re)created one,\nand record it on LayerTreeState as mEmbedderLayersId. It is derived in\nRemoteLayerTreeOwner::Initialize(), once the embedding widget's WindowRenderer\nexists: from the embedding document's BrowserParent for a nested remote frame,\nand from the hosting chrome window's widget otherwise.\n\nAlso extend AdoptChild to carry a freshly-recomputed embedder id, rather than\npreserving whatever was previously recorded: adopting a child under a new\nCompositorBridgeParent can mean a tab was moved to a different top-level\nwindow, which does change who embeds it, so the old value would otherwise go\nstale.\n\nThis establishes a parent-process-trusted ground truth for which LayersId\nembeds which, to be used by a follow-up change to validate scroll-data\nreferent claims from content.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316408\n", "files": ["gfx/ipc/GPUProcessManager.cpp", "gfx/ipc/GPUProcessManager.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/CompositorBridgeChild.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/CompositorBridgeChild.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/CompositorBridgeParent.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/CompositorBridgeParent.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/ContentCompositorBridgeParent.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/ContentCompositorBridgeParent.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/PCompositorBridge.ipdl", "layout/ipc/RemoteLayerTreeOwner.cpp"], "git_node": "016dbe1ee1477bf06968f4c30cec58c800be78d2", "git_parents": ["5e4975452794abcda7f5730c646a538163ffda86"], "node": "7d1ba51d9f9fe2a223f1b48960a06d932a23cb17", "parents": ["664447017bf518ff7fb58deb4efa8ce5a0b97daa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hiroyuki Ikezoe \u003chikezoe.birchill@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059195 - Reject WebRenderScrollData whose referent isn't actually embedded by the sender. r=botond\n\nValidate every referent claim in WebRenderBridgeParent::ProcessDisplayListData\nagainst the parent process's own record of the frame tree (LayerTreeState's\nnew mEmbedderLayersId), and reject the transaction if the referent isn't\nactually embedded by the sender.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316409\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderBridgeParent.cpp", "gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderScrollData.cpp", "gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderScrollData.h"], "git_node": "440bc0a800c2b9fef5a1931f3562572950ba1a4f", "git_parents": ["016dbe1ee1477bf06968f4c30cec58c800be78d2"], "node": "8d85a208a1674e11f33f31ca1a68a28c16686b59", "parents": ["7d1ba51d9f9fe2a223f1b48960a06d932a23cb17"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Bone \u003cpbone@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055507 - pt 1. Purging the spare chunk clears mSpare r=glandium\n\nThis change means that:\n * a purging chunk is never the spare chunk,\n * a spare chunk is never purging.\n * a spare chunk is never in mChunksDirty.\n * RemoveChunk is never called on a spare chunk or a chunk in the\n   mDirtyChunks list.\n * RemoveChunk is never called on a purging chunk and therefore can\n   never fail.\n * Because RemoveChunk cannot fail the mDying flag and hand-off between\n   purging and removing chunks can be removed.\n * After purging an empty chunk should always be demoted to spare\n   (either because it became empty or it was empty and spare earlier).\n * Detection of empty chunks after purging has moved to\n   FinishPurgingInChunk().\n\nThis patch deletes more lines than it inserts, and many of them are\ncomments or assertions. it makes other patches in this stack simpler\ntoo!\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321745\n", "files": ["memory/build/Arena.h", "memory/build/Chunk.h", "memory/build/mozjemalloc.cpp"], "git_node": "21da2c4e53706831b9404f05ed88ca2d499ae8b3", "git_parents": ["440bc0a800c2b9fef5a1931f3562572950ba1a4f"], "node": "fa23a5a6b467b2ec4af631a3c2baa2a306c4e618", "parents": ["8d85a208a1674e11f33f31ca1a68a28c16686b59"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Bone \u003cpbone@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055507 - pt 2. Make arena_t::mSpare a list r=glandium\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312576\n", "files": ["memory/build/Arena.h", "memory/build/mozjemalloc.cpp"], "git_node": "711de31427c70f05cb7435bc92977074daadb735", "git_parents": ["21da2c4e53706831b9404f05ed88ca2d499ae8b3"], "node": "ececbb3bdaebe2a8d2adc28a154766337a317b00", "parents": ["fa23a5a6b467b2ec4af631a3c2baa2a306c4e618"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Bone \u003cpbone@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055507 - pt 3. Add DoublyLinkedList::isSingle() r=sergesanspaille\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312577\n", "files": ["mfbt/DoublyLinkedList.h", "mfbt/tests/TestDoublyLinkedList.cpp"], "git_node": "c66b0bdd380ce398907ce7672a0fca1c66bf3686", "git_parents": ["711de31427c70f05cb7435bc92977074daadb735"], "node": "d3af02b65de86da7fd749ac2f035f2d5b0cb907b", "parents": ["ececbb3bdaebe2a8d2adc28a154766337a317b00"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Bone \u003cpbone@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055507 - pt 4. Making a chunk the spare no longer bumps the old spare r=glandium\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312578\n", "files": ["memory/build/Arena.h", "memory/build/mozjemalloc.cpp"], "git_node": "1183982a83572378982748239cd7bddd5f243b2d", "git_parents": ["c66b0bdd380ce398907ce7672a0fca1c66bf3686"], "node": "e65c06ceb614e9b7dc5ffe05a0a63e14f5a44994", "parents": ["d3af02b65de86da7fd749ac2f035f2d5b0cb907b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Bone \u003cpbone@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055507 - pt 5. Release spare chunks during purging r=glandium\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312579\n", "files": ["memory/build/Arena.h", "memory/build/mozjemalloc.cpp"], "git_node": "2f337b40191a98bee5ae3b63835dfea517296893", "git_parents": ["1183982a83572378982748239cd7bddd5f243b2d"], "node": "7f4554a1f2ef60a828e9de52056585dc80b6394c", "parents": ["e65c06ceb614e9b7dc5ffe05a0a63e14f5a44994"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Bone \u003cpbone@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055507 - pt 6. Don't release chunks during dealloc r=glandium\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312580\n", "files": ["memory/build/Arena.h", "memory/build/mozjemalloc.cpp"], "git_node": "79d627b753dbe850823c423339a01739eb42d959", "git_parents": ["2f337b40191a98bee5ae3b63835dfea517296893"], "node": "4cf78e67f9d9909c9c3c3b040831381012959d39", "parents": ["7f4554a1f2ef60a828e9de52056585dc80b6394c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Bone \u003cpbone@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055507 - pt 7. Make the chunk cache a C++ class r=glandium\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313992\n", "files": ["memory/build/Chunk.cpp", "memory/build/Chunk.h", "memory/build/Extent.h", "memory/build/mozjemalloc.cpp"], "git_node": "90f5d2071062a1133860977e0456fc90a78dbefa", "git_parents": ["79d627b753dbe850823c423339a01739eb42d959"], "node": "8f391f452d75a5bc9a3f9996787be275e39f5b9f", "parents": ["4cf78e67f9d9909c9c3c3b040831381012959d39"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Bone \u003cpbone@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055507 - pt 8. Disable the chunk cache on Windows r=glandium\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313993\n", "files": ["memory/build/Chunk.cpp", "memory/build/Chunk.h", "memory/build/mozjemalloc.cpp"], "git_node": "dbf748e3f44e17227cd1cc52a7ed87e6bc4b62b5", "git_parents": ["90f5d2071062a1133860977e0456fc90a78dbefa"], "node": "d04c97347dcc984bc6a4d49fa0933411f715727b", "parents": ["8f391f452d75a5bc9a3f9996787be275e39f5b9f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mayankleoboy1 \u003cmayankleoboy1@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067346 - Build the introduced filename without snprintf. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nFormatIntroducedFilename concatenates three strings whose length it has\nalready computed, but it does so with two ucrtbase printf calls. In a\nprofile of the bug 1127095 testcase (100k `new Function` calls) those two\ncalls are 32 of the 522 samples under CreateDynamicFunction, and the whole\nfunction is 32 - the memcpys and the malloc do not register.\n\nThis runs for every eval and every Function constructor call that has a\nscripted caller, not just for this testcase.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322038\n", "files": ["js/src/vm/JSScript.cpp"], "git_node": "21e0c8ad665370848e7a53de9d7da3a2b1b6f2b2", "git_parents": ["dbf748e3f44e17227cd1cc52a7ed87e6bc4b62b5"], "node": "6f5f211a1db890473580a0f3e9987b75e89b40ba", "parents": ["d04c97347dcc984bc6a4d49fa0933411f715727b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2056749 - Add -moz-scrollbar-inset-{block, inline} for improved scrollbar boundaries for rounded chrome corners. r=emilio,tabbrowser-reviewers,firefox-style-system-reviewers,layout-reviewers,sthompson\" for causing build bustages.\n\nThis reverts commit 5e4975452794abcda7f5730c646a538163ffda86.\n", "files": ["devtools/server/actors/animation-type-longhand.js", "docshell/base/BrowsingContext.cpp", "docshell/base/BrowsingContext.h", "dom/base/use_counter_metrics.yaml", "layout/base/nsPresContext.cpp", "layout/base/nsPresContext.h", "layout/generic/ScrollContainerFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/ScrollContainerFrame.h", "layout/generic/WritingModes.h", "layout/generic/nsSubDocumentFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsSubDocumentFrame.h", "layout/reftests/css-scrollbars/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/css-scrollbars/scrollbar-inset-change-ref.html", "layout/reftests/css-scrollbars/scrollbar-inset-change.html", "layout/reftests/css-scrollbars/scrollbar-inset-forward-change.html", "layout/reftests/css-scrollbars/scrollbar-inset-forward-inner.h