e/languagePackUpdates.js | Test timed out. r=application-update-reviewers,cdupuis\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322295\n", "files": ["toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_aus_update/languagePackUpdates.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_aus_update/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "fed8faae11e4896c7ce36122a732843f8a89bb6c", "git_parents": ["9f80657039507f244ebab7723ac6a72bea0bceb9"], "node": "f54396fe974b2fa115fbfb2bb91310e52a0a170b", "parents": ["a2181117070b3ab3a52529a2d1e31d9c02e3a68b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067632 - Run the urlbar-ipc test variant on macOS on autoland. r=taskgraph-reviewers,ahal\n\nBug 2062465 added mochitest-browser-chrome to the macosx1500-aarch64-tests set, so macosx1500-aarch64/opt \u2014 the macOS platform autoland builds \u2014 now runs M(bc). Bug 2051959 dropped this autoland entry back when it scheduled nothing.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322237\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/mochitest/kind.yml"], "git_node": "20ba4ab1b73ba296479eb57ccc6095e4b054b85a", "git_parents": ["fed8faae11e4896c7ce36122a732843f8a89bb6c"], "node": "cd59d776d60be65ca057960b2ab33c01e622b49c", "parents": ["f54396fe974b2fa115fbfb2bb91310e52a0a170b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067632 - Run the urlbar-ipc test variant at tier 1. r=taskgraph-reviewers,ahal\n\nTaking the platform default rather than setting tier 1 outright: the variant also composes with the ccov and asan platforms, and a tier-1 task cannot depend on their tier-2 builds.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322238\n", "files": ["taskcluster/test_configs/variants.yml"], "git_node": "f8de20bce29c92f684d2631fb4b65a9eee7e3074", "git_parents": ["20ba4ab1b73ba296479eb57ccc6095e4b054b85a"], "node": "62d1cc27d033955e4686e1b28f63b86e0a848e67", "parents": ["cd59d776d60be65ca057960b2ab33c01e622b49c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067296: Use a fuse in NotV r=mgaudet\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322035\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp"], "git_node": "bfa28acdb0cfa4fc2b87bfc034bf3d65e92ab494", "git_parents": ["f8de20bce29c92f684d2631fb4b65a9eee7e3074"], "node": "0fb9bbe015e6ca90efb029a596795024461fdc79", "parents": ["62d1cc27d033955e4686e1b28f63b86e0a848e67"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054248 part 1 - Use ClassCanHaveExtraEnumeratedProperties in CopyDataPropertiesNative and Object.assign code. r=iain\n\nAlso adds `#ifdef DEBUG` for a `Rooted` in `ClassCanHaveExtraEnumeratedProperties`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322300\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/Object.cpp", "js/src/vm/NativeObject.cpp"], "git_node": "f133c388a1c7bc7481acab24539aabd88593fa1d", "git_parents": ["bfa28acdb0cfa4fc2b87bfc034bf3d65e92ab494"], "node": "6f962207655e9e8353242749d9775c4c5be9d5ba", "parents": ["0fb9bbe015e6ca90efb029a596795024461fdc79"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054248 part 2 - Factor out Object.assign's shape-reuse mechanism. r=iain\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322301\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/Object.cpp", "js/src/vm/NativeObject-inl.h"], "git_node": "e2bdefeee23547b078d61fc0ca82121dac27fe2f", "git_parents": ["f133c388a1c7bc7481acab24539aabd88593fa1d"], "node": "58a7f486df4d334e37b13589a2a9008837d2b4b6", "parents": ["6f962207655e9e8353242749d9775c4c5be9d5ba"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054248 part 3 - Use TryCopyPropertiesReusingShapeOrPropMap in CopyDataPropertiesNative. r=iain\n\nThis lets object spread operations reuse `from`'s Shape or PropMap when the target\nis empty and every property of `from` is a plain enumerable data property.\n\nBased on a patch from Mayank Bansal.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322303\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/basic/object-spread-shape-reuse.js", "js/src/vm/NativeObject.cpp"], "git_node": "183bc67a6d41ab0b72d9fcfb822d0ca67e33a9d4", "git_parents": ["e2bdefeee23547b078d61fc0ca82121dac27fe2f"], "node": "9d12d127f21002e935e0e601d24c7a5f592e8e65", "parents": ["58a7f486df4d334e37b13589a2a9008837d2b4b6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054248 part 4 - Use a cache for the target shape in CopyDataPropertiesNative. r=iain\n\nSimilar to the `Object.assign` fast path, we can add a small cache that maps\nthe input shapes to the new target shape.\n\nThese changes make the object-spread micro-benchmark in the bug \u003e 2x faster.\n\nBased on a patch from Mayank Bansal.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322304\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/Object.cpp", "js/src/jit-test/tests/basic/object-spread-shape-reuse.js", "js/src/vm/NativeObject.cpp", "js/src/vm/Realm.cpp", "js/src/vm/Realm.h"], "git_node": "9030b0d88a1c4e7ca36f49619a128b56ebf19e17", "git_parents": ["183bc67a6d41ab0b72d9fcfb822d0ca67e33a9d4"], "node": "b611a75b5291a8812899845b1708ff09150d0f09", "parents": ["9d12d127f21002e935e0e601d24c7a5f592e8e65"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Calixte Denizet \u003ccalixte.denizet@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066198 - Skip module CORS for trusted loads from resource: principals. r=dveditz\n\nCORS checks on module loads block resource: documents from loading\ncross-origin resource: modules or content-accessible chrome: modules.\n\nSkip CORS when the triggering content principal uses resource: and\nnsContentSecurityUtils::IsTrustedScheme accepts the target. Other URI checks\nstill apply, so moz-src: remains blocked.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322394\n", "files": ["dom/script/ModuleLoader.cpp", "dom/security/test/general/browser.toml", "dom/security/test/general/browser_resource_module_cors.js", "dom/security/test/general/file_resource_module_cors.html", "dom/security/test/general/file_resource_module_cors_dep.mjs", "dom/security/test/general/file_resource_module_cors_server.sjs"], "git_node": "3518dd604c00197939b47dffc88479f01d348c46", "git_parents": ["9030b0d88a1c4e7ca36f49619a128b56ebf19e17"], "node": "2e4807210b5a629dbf2a895ff3124ce3c49af887", "parents": ["b611a75b5291a8812899845b1708ff09150d0f09"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057436 - Deal with transparency not being available in nsMenuPopupFrame's sizing code. r=layout-reviewers,tnikkel\n\nThis is a regression from bug 1933181. Before that patch,\nCalcWidgetBounds would look at mWidget-\u003eGetTransparencyMode(), which GTK\noverrides to \"opaque\" on a non-composited screen:\n\nWe could look at nsMenuPopupFrame's widget instead, but that is finicky\nbecause it means the bounds that we pass to the widget creation code\nwould be wrong. I think it's better to compute the right bounds, and we\nalready expose the right bit via LookAndFeel, so use that.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322435\n", "files": ["layout/xul/nsMenuPopupFrame.cpp", "layout/xul/nsMenuPopupFrame.h"], "git_node": "a70514209e8505921123d9bd20e4de8367e34999", "git_parents": ["3518dd604c00197939b47dffc88479f01d348c46"], "node": "d2553574295573f5eba37aee0121973501b2717c", "parents": ["2e4807210b5a629dbf2a895ff3124ce3c49af887"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Delan Azabani \u003cdazabani@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067979 - Fix error-prone switch case for distro bootstrap r=ahochheiden\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322545\n", "files": ["python/mozboot/mozboot/bootstrap.py"], "git_node": "4ee45d6ceb60d647bf912525a91d944345f8368e", "git_parents": ["a70514209e8505921123d9bd20e4de8367e34999"], "node": "c77cdd62d7403647c99698bbd91ca4c747321639", "parents": ["d2553574295573f5eba37aee0121973501b2717c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Abel Kalu \u003c59095867+BlessedOneKobo@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053553 Remove unused WebRender debug preferences. r=emilio,layout-reviewers\n\nThe following WebRender debug preferences are no longer in use. They are no longer in the GFX_WEBRENDER_DEBUG\nflag table in gfx/thebes/gfxPlatform.cpp.\n\nmodules/libpref/init/all.js:\n\t- gfx.webrender.debug.alpha-primitives\n\t- gfx.webrender.debug.slow-frame-indicator\n\nmodules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml:\n\t- gfx.webrender.debug.slow-cpu-frame-threshold\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322553\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "modules/libpref/init/all.js"], "git_node": "bb40ca97f3aa67723f77b93e34dde3d22c85bd54", "git_parents": ["4ee45d6ceb60d647bf912525a91d944345f8368e"], "node": "a75ea975605fe6661e5d052ccc060f1c1b512fc2", "parents": ["c77cdd62d7403647c99698bbd91ca4c747321639"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067677 - Move instead of copy the memory reporter path in UrlClassifierPrefixSetReporter::Register r=dimi\n\nCoverity CID 1700565.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322268\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/url-classifier/VariableLengthPrefixSet.cpp"], "git_node": "90b2f325f4008b858603bff7ec9c5f70f0fdc14d", "git_parents": ["bb40ca97f3aa67723f77b93e34dde3d22c85bd54"], "node": "3bf21c631fc343e372ff85f715f78ccfc0357000", "parents": ["a75ea975605fe6661e5d052ccc060f1c1b512fc2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Farre \u003cfarre@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default