ulien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055837 - use taskcluster-built python for web-platform-tests tasks. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312749\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/web-platform-tests/kind.yml"], "git_node": "240c342dfb2d1e4a509c6ab14e324f89fd4c7523", "git_parents": ["36adabdc689ce77f1b1865ae8991a405f515a6d8"], "node": "d1fe263a6daed398a6c189ba86232e6fe551f85e", "parents": ["9c1b4ebf52fb5feed02569199223f078d3b803b2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2056841 - Add GTest to reproduce DirtyTrackingAutoLock race conditions. r=dom-storage-reviewers,hsingh\" for causing gtest failures at TestDirtyTrackingRace\n\nThis reverts commit d2179ae04bee2f60d36d513bb256dc5319463f4e.\n", "files": ["dom/quota/DirtyTrackingAutoLock.cpp", "dom/quota/test/gtest/TestDirtyTrackingRace.cpp", "dom/quota/test/gtest/moz.build", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "365dd54e56207156b64613643e0a989e1d61335d", "git_parents": ["240c342dfb2d1e4a509c6ab14e324f89fd4c7523"], "node": "48070b698f77bdfd940fe055d81d77bfbb9a4582", "parents": ["d1fe263a6daed398a6c189ba86232e6fe551f85e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2056841: Eliminate race on OriginInfo changes by holding mutex continuously. r=dom-storage-reviewers,hsingh\" for causing shutdown crashes.\n\nThis reverts commit 24efc699dee41ffd6bb0326016fec8ee594a5b79.\n", "files": ["dom/quota/ActorsParent.cpp", "dom/quota/CanonicalQuotaObject.cpp", "dom/quota/DirtyTrackingAutoLock.cpp", "dom/quota/DirtyTrackingAutoLock.h"], "git_node": "c2b3d69bdfcf0dff2f4d256c3e161e3967a42eb2", "git_parents": ["365dd54e56207156b64613643e0a989e1d61335d"], "node": "1fa5f18dcc9926486ae2e8d63c9c796ca6a4fbe0", "parents": ["48070b698f77bdfd940fe055d81d77bfbb9a4582"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Norisz Fay \u003cnfay@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2057759: apply code formatting via Lando\" for causing reftest failure 720p.png.bt709.bt709.pc.yuv420p.av1.webm / 720p.png\n\nThis reverts commit 3090db88d357c0a1274c5f467f2711aea072a8e0.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2057759 - Preserve FFmpeg decoded frame color metadata r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\"\n\nThis reverts commit 8898eed6d09b1babe13d9c7c9d18d1e9fb56a294.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2057759 - Test FFmpeg decoded frame color metadata r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\"\n\nThis reverts commit c33eae190673e4f23e204c801d1aafc22fc53ac6.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2057759 - Preserve decoded color metadata across remote image transport r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\"\n\nThis reverts commit d421c372bc19e077c26731be35f1e701a3c3d7e2.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2057759 - Test remote decoded color metadata transport r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\"\n\nThis reverts commit ff0070161e7d2939d73fde476677c1c858296f41.\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestMediaDataDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/TestRemoteImageHolder.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/av1-color-metadata.mp4", "dom/media/gtest/generate_color_metadata_video.py", "dom/media/gtest/moz.build", "dom/media/ipc/RemoteImageHolder.cpp", "dom/media/ipc/RemoteVideoDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/SharedPlanarYCbCrImage.cpp"], "git_node": "c9a0c82e582e02fbbfdda068204931209f33a640", "git_parents": ["c2b3d69bdfcf0dff2f4d256c3e161e3967a42eb2"], "node": "2d9eabacbd542c3a8ec8e7f51ab7f9b04bbbb3cd", "parents": ["1fa5f18dcc9926486ae2e8d63c9c796ca6a4fbe0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Merge mozilla-central to autoland\n", "files": ["dom/quota/DirtyTrackingAutoLock.cpp"], "git_node": "fab80ccb7e1a6d449aef47998b2509c52d8c3f63", "git_parents": ["c9a0c82e582e02fbbfdda068204931209f33a640", "c6e08963c19ca94be777dd97bd61ad9d96d4c2f2"], "node": "18dd848f6d790445907b33a0ac474f503a730a7b", "parents": ["2d9eabacbd542c3a8ec8e7f51ab7f9b04bbbb3cd", "8a5eb3c1adf61a5e14b2efe588046827e89350bf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjcoppeard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2029295 - Add testcase r=sfink\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D292495\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/gc/bug-2029295.js"], "git_node": "8741e7f6bc29da1eaf92b75b0f4d161f7fa51f8f", "git_parents": ["fab80ccb7e1a6d449aef47998b2509c52d8c3f63"], "node": "f7ab2a50ca950b681350a6ec8babb94b100fd453", "parents": ["18dd848f6d790445907b33a0ac474f503a730a7b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066662 - Fix test_cache2-35-encryption.js raciness r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nOPEN_TRUNCATE entries are handed to the consumer before their file is opened\n(CacheFile::Init() with aCreateNew builds the metadata up front and passes no listener).\nSo the test writes metadata + data into memory chunks while CacheFileIOManager::OpenFile()\nis still queued.\n\nThe change now dooms the entry instead of preserving it in plaintext.\nThe test also suspends the cache in order to wait for the encryption key to load.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321794\n", "files": ["netwerk/cache2/CacheFile.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_cache2-35-encryption.js"], "git_node": "ad24293ab14dc283285c59ea5f0ee1d1ef5dcde1", "git_parents": ["8741e7f6bc29da1eaf92b75b0f4d161f7fa51f8f"], "node": "ac0148017cac2f1bd302264e52359b3dc8d3e2df", "parents": ["f7ab2a50ca950b681350a6ec8babb94b100fd453"], "tags": []}, {"author": "theidkamp \u003ctheidkamp@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1775757 - Wait for the added login to be selected before entering edit mode in browser_removeAllDialog.js. r=joschmidt,credential-management-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322391\n", "files": ["browser/components/aboutlogins/tests/browser/browser_removeAllDialog.js"], "git_node": "c12147ec1968792c5cdec15b194ef85b20246d38", "git_parents": ["ad24293ab14dc283285c59ea5f0ee1d1ef5dcde1"], "node": "e581476b4b2a17c6ef62caad28a4b4ffe8b43039", "parents": ["ac0148017cac2f1bd302264e52359b3dc8d3e2df"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Titouan Thibaud \u003ctthibaud@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063390 - Create a new job to generate Nightly build without Baseline Profile nor PGO and add it to an android-fenix-prototype preset. r=releng-reviewers,ahal\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318534\n", "files": ["taskcluster/android_taskgraph/transforms/signing_android_app.py", "taskcluster/config.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/build-apk/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/signing-apk/kind.yml", "tools/tryselect/try_presets.yml"], "git_node": "402058c491308bfaa7831a6ffeda3dd079da3436", "git_parents": ["c12147ec1968792c5cdec15b194ef85b20246d38"], "node": "b51b353c502196ceb170f32e77e8cd6dbf37e8f3", "parents": ["e581476b4b2a17c6ef62caad28a4b4ffe8b43039"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maurice Dauer \u003cmdauer@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051013 - Test for inner URI validation when deserializing, r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314669\n", "files": ["netwerk/test/gtest/TestURIMutator.cpp"], "git_node": "ff0a689e8d860d75a4bed6ffff22593c7258abe3", "git_parents": ["402058c491308bfaa7831a6ffeda3dd079da3436"], "node": "bfee7b9817768c098c249cade7bbdd61e99f346b", "parents": ["b51b353c502196ceb170f32e77e8cd6dbf37e8f3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dimi \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062540 - Add the Rust address storage adapter r=joschmidt,credential-management-reviewers\n\nPresent the AutofillRecords address interface over the Application Services\nautofill Store, so it can later back FormAutofillStorage.getAddresses().\nNothing constructs it yet.\n\nReads rebuild the computed fields and drop empty and hidden keys, so a record\nread from Rust matches the same record read from JSON: consumers compare stored\nrecords against freshly normalised input, and a divergence would break\ndeduping. _normalizeRecord, computeFields and a synchronous isEmpty() are part\nof that interface for the same reason -- FormAutofillParent calls them on\nwhichever store is active when it decides whether to offer a doorhanger.\n\nAn edit leaves the metadata to the store: update() writes the content columns\nthrough updateAddress, which increments the sync change counter, where the\nwith-meta call would replace it -- and always with 1, since nothing exposes the\nstored value. That leaves #updatableFieldsWithMeta to the migration, which\ncarries a record's metadata across rather than advancing it.\n\nadd() strips the computed fields now. It ran computeFields on whatever the\ncaller passed, and computeFields only fills in what is missing, so a caller\nhanding back a record it had read stored the derived values it came with.\n\nMegalist read its strip lists off the collection, which this adapter does not\ncarry. Its address and bank card editors are stubbed out rather than ported:\nneither data source is packaged, and what a writer should send is the UI's\ndecision.\n\ntest_rust_autofill_address_adapter.js covers the round trip with computed\nfields, a bulk import that isolates a per-record failure, and get() telling a\nmissing record from an unreadable one.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315621\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/formautofill/test/unit/test_rust_autofill_address_adapter.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/unit/xpcshell.toml", "toolkit/components/formautofill/FormAutofillStorageBase.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/RustAutofillAddressStorage.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/shared/AddressRecord.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/satchel/megalist/aggregator/datasources/AddressesDataSource.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/satchel/megalist/aggregator/datasources/BankCardDataSource.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "e1f06c4e49127d965913fbf89f714ba55fd62db2", "git_parents": ["ff0a689e8d860d75a4bed6ffff22593c7258abe3"], "node": "3b884c1020254d41420de95f0b9b7188f55a6cd2", "parents": ["bfee7b9817768c098c249cade7bbdd61e99f346b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brian Smith \u003cbrian@smith.berlin\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060812 - More details for kiosk mode docs r=mkaply\n\n__Additions__\n\n* More details for the Kiosk Mode section, link to relevant policies\n\n__Changes:__\n* Link out to admin docs site instead of templates.\n\n__Other:__\n* Incidental typo fixes, coming from `cspell` sweep over the docs directory.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320430\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/docs/index.md", "docs/code-quality/coding-style/css_guidelines.md", "docs/code-quality/lint/linters/condprof-addons.md", "docs/code-quality/lint/linters/license.md", "docs/code-quality/static-analysis/writing-new/clang-query.md", "docs/code-quality/static-analysis/writing-new/writing-matchers.md", "docs/contributing/debugging/debugging_firefox_with_pernosco.md", "docs/contributing/debugging/stacktrace_windbg.md", "docs/contributing/jujutsu.md", "docs/contributing/searchfox/blame.md", "docs/contributing/searchfox/class_field_layout.md", "docs/contributing/searchfox/navigation_panel.md", "docs/nspr/nspr_s_position_on_abrupt_thread_termination.md", "docs/nspr/reference/pr_getconnectstatus.md", "docs/performance/bestpractices.md"], "git_node": "3ac7876fe54fb6845d86d7a919e3ccfc9af276e0", "git_parents": ["e1f06c4e49127d965913fbf89f714ba55fd62db2"], "node": "946a428931a587e5abeae6ed737b9d376fd94a25", "parents": ["3b884c1020254d41420de95f0b9b7188f55a6cd2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lars Eggert \u003clars@eggert.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2034287 - Bail out of worker XHR abort() if the proxy went away. r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nAbort() dispatches AbortRunnable synchronously, which spins the worker event\nloop. A cancellation delivered there releases the proxy, so re-check it before\nrunning the request error steps.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322574\n", "files": ["dom/xhr/XMLHttpRequestWorker.cpp", "dom/xhr/tests/mochitest.toml", "dom/xhr/tests/test_worker_xhrAbortDuringTerminate.html", "dom/xhr/tests/xhrAbortDuringTerminate_worker.js"], "git_node": "3259c235420ca907381a9eb6f652c103380bac3c", "git_parents": ["3ac7876fe54fb6845d86d7a919e3ccfc9af276e0"], "node": "e8497eb2cb728f441492fecc265da1d9a3282b4e", "parents": ["946a428931a587e5abeae6ed737b9d376fd94a25"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dimi \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067226 - Make the form autofill migration test tolerate the channel-dependent addresses.supported default. r=joschmidt\n\ntest_check_form_autofill_module_detect hardcoded \"on\" as the expected value of\nextensions.formautofill.addresses.supported. Migration 124 never writes that\npref for the legacy \"detect\" value, so the assertion reads the default from\nall.js, which bug 2065145 made \"detect\" on release and ESR. The test therefore\npermafails on the beta-as-release simulation.\n\nRestore the channel-conditional expected value that bug 2052652 removed, using\nthe same channel check as the pref default rather than NIGHTLY_BUILD, since the\npref is also \"on\" on beta and devedition.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322577\n", "files": ["browser/components/tests/unit/test_browserGlue_migration_formautofill.js"], "git_node": "7acfe26256d99b0cf749e338ab0affc8872155a7", "git_parents": ["3259c235420ca907381a9eb6f652c103380bac3c"], "node": "38eec90addf0b8746667a4734b5423bc819cae51", "parents": ["e8497eb2cb728f441492fecc265da1d9a3282b4e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mayankleoboy1 \u003cmayankleoboy1@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067346 - Build the dynamic function source as two-byte from the start. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nCreateDynamicFunction appends the whole source into a Latin1 StringBuilder\nand then calls ensureTwoByteChars() unconditionally right before\nfinishString(), so the buffer is always inflated. Inflating it while it is\nstill empty costs nothing and avoids allocating the Latin1 buffer at all.\n\nIn a profile of the bug 1127095 testcase, inflateChars is 23 of the 522\nsamples under CreateDynamicFunction, 15 of them in the allocation. With the\nprevious patch the appends inflate with the same converter inflateChars\nused, so the conversion work is unchanged and only the second allocation\nand the Latin1 copy go away.\n\nFunctionCompiler::init in vm/CompilationAndEvaluation.cpp already builds its\nfunction source this way.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322040\n", "files": ["js/src/vm/JSFunction.cpp"], "git_node": "112f6ae363211704ede1a43c0dd7bc327ca84f38", "git_parents": ["7acfe26256d99b0cf749e338ab0affc8872155a7"], "node": "5848119d95e2ad031f5982be15a2ab369fd9db66", "parents": ["38eec90addf0b8746667a4734b5423bc819cae51"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058181 - Fix repeat auto edge case handling.\n\nBefore my change, the repeat(auto) expansion was guaranteed to happen,\nnow we may bail out before.\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsGridContainerFrame.cpp"], "git_node": "09e5fdd55c6d74ba2e47d349db8ecc5c7bda0dce", "git_parents": ["112f6ae363211704ede1a43c0dd7bc327ca84f38"], "node": "d7dd07ee2ce23b79c6320efbea1fb87a046154f2", "parents": ["5848119d95e2ad031f5982be15a2ab369fd9db66"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067570 - gfxPlatform::InitPlatformHardwareDRMConfig must trigger on pref changes. r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nmedia.wmf.media-engine.enabled is used in the config computation.\nNormally this doesn't change much, but in the gfx sanity test, it\ndoes turn it off temporarily during its compositor test. We should\nmonitor pref changes in gfxPlatform so that we are always accurate.\nOtherwise we run the risk of a race when the GPU process launches\nand now contains an unexpected value for gfxVars::UseWMFHWDRM.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322160\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxPlatform.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxPlatform.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxWindowsPlatform.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxWindowsPlatform.h"], "git_node": "632865799a51760f148fd0621b713adcd6e7a579", "git_parents": ["09e5fdd55c6d74ba2e47d349db8ecc5c7bda0dce"], "node": "23242a2fe2e85d1b3588b0c87ccfbe5c5b029cf5", "parents": ["d7dd07ee2ce23b79c6320efbea1fb87a046154f2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067454 - Part 1. Refactor the gfx sanity test to be verifiable in CI. r=gfx-reviewers,media-playback-reviewers,nical,padenot\n\nWe disable the actual sanity test in CI so that we don't\naccidentally disable hardware compositing and/or hardware video\ndecoding. Hence the only way it is tested is in local or release\nbuilds.\n\nThis patch refactors the gfx sanity test into a new module,\nSanityTestChecks.sys.mjs, leaving the original SanityTest.sys.mjs\nto be a wrapper around it to determine when to run and what to do\nwith the results. This will allow a mochitest to be written in a\nlater part in this series.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322112\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/gfx/SanityTest.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/gfx/SanityTestChecks.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/gfx/moz.build"], "git_node": "f78b980a1029858257e0f69ce81adeafa02e091d", "git_parents": ["632865799a51760f148fd0621b713adcd6e7a579"], "node": "8d1b265e137cc3fe1744c71d585a880f45ab4757", "parents": ["23242a2fe2e85d1b3588b0c87ccfbe5c5b029cf5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067454 - Part 2. Add hardware video encoding checks to the gfx sanity test. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nIt uses WebCodecs and H264 to do this, since H264 is almost always\navailable on modern hardware. If there is no hardware encoding, it\naccepts the result as passing.\n\nWe also add checking the secondary gfx adapter for changes here,\njust like the primary, so that device/driver updates will cause us\nto retest. Secondary devices can be used alongside the primary for\nhardware encoding.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322113\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxPlatform.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxPlatform.h", "toolkit/components/gfx/SanityTest.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/gfx/SanityTestChecks.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/gfx/content/gfxFrameScript.js"], "git_node": "15f65f2633b708148296e5b093c007654c66319a", "git_parents": ["f78b980a1029858257e0f69ce81adeafa02e091d"], "node": "ad3428590e2d96c7b4bf1b29f91022e54f5949b1", "parents": ["8d1b265e137cc3fe1744c71d585a880f45ab4757"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067454 - Part 3. Add a media-gpu mochitest for the gfx sanity test. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nRunning on a real host means we get at least H264 hardware\nencoding, and so we can verify that the test passes as expected.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322114\n", "files": ["dom/media/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/media/test/test_gfx_sanity_gpu.html"], "git_node": "967422c3783477876888366fe46952846e0a3ae3", "git_parents": ["15f65f2633b708148296e5b093c007654c66319a"], "node": "e64997438d5d2cec02f4e527598ada71c3db54f1", "parents": ["ad3428590e2d96c7b4bf1b29f91022e54f5949b1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067454 - Part 4. Update Glean/telemetry documentation for new gfx sanity test values. r=chutten\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322161\n", "files": ["gfx/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/telemetry/Histograms.json"], "git_node": "1dfd7ee250576b60aa0240a75c0f58c708de2888", "git_parents": ["967422c3783477876888366fe46952846e0a3ae3"], "node": "5b6c1d7fa1392a7ae7309e94c2fbc1760c699f52", "parents": ["e64997438d5d2cec02f4e527598ada71c3db54f1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067206 - Test that a graph message tail dispatched from a microtask during shutdown is not stranded. r=karlt\n\nA microtask runs after XPCOMThreadWrapper::AfterProcessNextEvent has fired the\ntail dispatcher, so a message queued from one lands in a fresh tail dispatcher\nthat the graph's shutdown handover does not drain. It is then never run and\nnever discarded.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322499\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestAudioTrackGraph.cpp"], "git_node": "e9a6b81695534751d7a31ee3bb9e53887e729646", "git_parents": ["1dfd7ee250576b60aa0240a75c0f58c708de2888"], "node": "20e083668d35dd223a3654dec9d4eb89d9ff934c", "parents": ["5b6c1d7fa1392a7ae7309e94c2fbc1760c699f52"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067206 - Hand tail dispatched messages to the main thread at graph shutdown. r=karlt\n\nWhen the main thread takes over the graph's messages at forced shutdown it\ndrained only mBackMessageQueue. Messages queued after the tail dispatcher last\nfired, e.g. from a microtask, were left in it and, with the graph never running\nagain, were neither run nor discarded -- leaving whatever they were to set up\nhalf built.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322500\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp"], "git_node": "272e2cb1a291481b9fd8d0c0883f017090ad893b", "git_parents": ["e9a6b81695534751d7a31ee3bb9e53887e729646"], "node": "a32239a27959c7f12baa7872eb6054bc20df147f", "parents": ["20e083668d35dd223a3654dec9d4eb89d9ff934c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maryam \u003cmomar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067997 - Fix Allow X content toggle not showing up. r=manuel\n\nThe trust panel now also matches the x.com domain.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322568\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-siteProtections.js", "browser/base/content/browser-trustPanel.js"], "git_node": "7b561db81af8524492b726152cedb610bfdf01d0", "git_parents": ["272e2cb1a291481b9fd8d0c0883f017090ad893b"], "node": "5b223f46713411ce6f24dbd46e8b8591f221c337", "parents": ["a32239a27959c7f12baa7872eb6054bc20df147f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Mehic \u003cdmehic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062060 - Correct the Reset Private Browsing descriptions in the ETP capability matrix r=manuel\n\nBoth rows described the feature as clearing private browsing data when the\nlast private window is closed. ResetPBMPanel is a user-initiated toolbar\nbutton shown in private windows that restarts the private session: it clears\nsite data and closes the private tabs and windows itself rather than reacting\nto them being closed. browser.privatebrowsing.resetPBM.enabled gates whether\nthat button exists.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317336\n", "files": ["docs/_addons/etp_matrix.py"], "git_node": "e99ad6934217da6f99cbd76c1430accffede59c7", "git_parents": ["7b561db81af8524492b726152cedb610bfdf01d0"], "node": "35b552384be69ebdfaafa434fc4fad3f30fe98b1", "parents": ["5b223f46713411ce6f24dbd46e8b8591f221c337"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Striemer \u003cmstriemer@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064736 - Expose --font-size-small to chrome documents r=dao,morgan,desktop-theme-reviewers\n\nProvide `--font-size-small` in chrome documents and target its relative\nfont size to be \u003e= 11px. On macOS this means using 1rem, on Windows it's\n(11 / 12)rem and Linux is left unchanged at expected 12.72px (14.6719 * 0.867)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319833\n", "files": ["toolkit/themes/linux/global/global.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/semantic-categories.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-platform.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-table.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/base/font.tokens.json"], "git_node": "f6a1cf4564e977b0b258fd8de9a652f0ab636bef", "git_parents": ["e99ad6934217da6f99cbd76c1430accffede59c7"], "node": "c856d53207d7457135ea3acb722c8b9a534edd67", "parents": ["35b552384be69ebdfaafa434fc4fad3f30fe98b1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Striemer \u003cmstriemer@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062774 - Use design tokens for Account menu small fonts r=nsharpley,desktop-theme-reviewers,dao\n\nUse --font-size-small and .text-deemphasized rather than rolling the\ncustom 0.9em font size and helper styles.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321738\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/appmenu-viewcache.inc.xhtml", "browser/themes/shared/customizableui/panelUI-shared.css"], "git_node": "0916222bc3a70e60f2e2a644b9209ee0e01f61fb", "git_parents": ["f6a1cf4564e977b0b258fd8de9a652f0ab636bef"], "node": "0cd3b94412933eafe4725f9d723bc55fde7fe168", "parents": ["c856d53207d7457135ea3acb722c8b9a534edd67"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067058 - add a macosx64-aarch64-xz toolchain r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nNative arm64 macOS build of the xz/liblzma development library, needed by\nthe arm64 macOS python toolchain (the arm64 build workers don't ship it).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321864\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/toolchain/misc.yml"], "git_node": "da1242eae7237c7f3500f5d5b9fa6cb11ebe46a2", "git_parents": ["0916222bc3a70e60f2e2a644b9209ee0e01f61fb"], "node": "2ae240eb361bf41ce103802a99e1d8a2ff11025c", "parents": ["0cd3b94412933eafe4725f9d723bc55fde7fe168"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067058 - add a macosx64-aarch64-openssl toolchain r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nNative arm64 macOS build of openssl 1.1.1w, needed as a private dependency\nof the arm64 macOS python toolchain: the arm64 build workers don't ship a\nlibssl, so cpython's _ssl/_hashlib have nothing to link against.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321865\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/fetch/toolchains.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/toolchain/misc.yml", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-openssl.sh"], "git_node": "d2aa1dd552129a42fed2837c6a539bb4f61687b9", "git_parents": ["da1242eae7237c7f3500f5d5b9fa6cb11ebe46a2"], "node": "0cd2fd5b65a9f16c06531bc1819033975a0473ea", "parents": ["2ae240eb361bf41ce103802a99e1d8a2ff11025c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067058 - add macosx64-aarch64-python toolchains r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nAdd native arm64 macOS cpython 3.9/3.11 toolchains (worker b-osx-arm64).\n\nThe build is self-contained: it fetches the macosx64-aarch64-openssl and\nmacosx64-aarch64-xz toolchains rather than relying on libraries the arm64\nworkers do not ship. build-cpython.sh points --with-openssl at the fetched\nopenssl and, since the fetched libssl/liblzma bake absolute install names\nthat do not exist at build time, sets DYLD_FALLBACK_LIBRARY_PATH so the\nbuild-time module import checks (and the pip bootstrap) resolve them; the\npost-build fixup rewrites the references to @rpath so the shipped python\nstays relocatable. Also fix the Darwin arch check (macOS uname -m is\narm64, not aarch64) so the deployment target is set correctly.\n\nThis is needed to switch macOS test tasks away from system python\nwithout relying on Rosetta for translation.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321866\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/toolchain/python.yml", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-cpython.sh"], "git_node": "83849711e40ad2525f9690fa7a78cf1e70afc746", "git_parents": ["d2aa1dd552129a42fed2837c6a539bb4f61687b9"], "node": "8947fc83f416e9844f57e55f05091f1d6e872a2c", "parents": ["0cd2fd5b65a9f16c06531bc1819033975a0473ea"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vincent Hilla \u003cvhilla@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2021375 - Skip initial about:blank for session history. r=smaug,asuth,dom-core-reviewers,dom-worker-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320395\n", "files": ["docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp", "dom/serviceworkers/test/browser-common.toml", "dom/serviceworkers/test/browser_initial_about_blank_subframe_history.js", "dom/serviceworkers/test/subframe_container.html", "dom/serviceworkers/test/subframe_message_navigate.html"], "git_node": "fad7c139f14eb01487f53169557dbee2fb57ed95", "git_parents": ["83849711e40ad2525f9690fa7a78cf1e70afc746"], "node": "60f0aa5efade436142e433b10d75b776e586b26c", "parents": ["8947fc83f416e9844f57e55f05091f1d6e872a2c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vincent Hilla \u003cvhilla@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2021375 - Add WPTs for iframe history restore on container navigation. r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321701\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/history-traversal/iframe-history-restore-about-blank.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/history-traversal/iframe-history-restore-on-container-traversal.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/history-traversal/iframe-history-restore-about-blank.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/history-traversal/iframe-history-restore-on-container-traversal.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/resources/has-initial-about-blank-iframe.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/resources/navigates-to-blank.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/lint.ignore"], "git_node": "166c15341bec5c3680b67d2cc5740cb9e64f1131", "git_parents": ["fad7c139f14eb01487f53169557dbee2fb57ed95"], "node": "6c9f7b10cd28c96158a3494437299848bddb5ef1", "parents": ["60f0aa5efade436142e433b10d75b776e586b26c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067319 - Only create/enumerate hardware WMF encoders in the GPU process. r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322118\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/wmf/MFTEncoder.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/wmf/MFTEncoder.h", "dom/media/platforms/wmf/WMFDataEncoderUtils.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/wmf/WMFDataEncoderUtils.h", "dom/media/platforms/wmf/WMFEncoderModule.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/wmf/WMFEncoderModule.h", "dom/media/platforms/wmf/WMFMediaDataEncoder.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/wmf/WMFMediaDataEncoder.h", "gfx/ipc/GPUParent.cpp"], "git_node": "03967bf3476d65c273d3459b1634acbac77af7af", "git_parents": ["166c15341bec5c3680b67d2cc5740cb9e64f1131"], "node": "0de3ed5f15d085f249ce59fbe263652b1a29be3f", "parents": ["6c9f7b10cd28c96158a3494437299848bddb5ef1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "noahvarghese \u003cvarghese.noah@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1625924 - Convert browser/components/syncedtabs/sidebar from xhtml to html. r=firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,desktop-theme-reviewers,mossop,dao\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322498\n", "files": ["browser/components/DesktopActorRegistry.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sidebar/browser-sidebar.js", "browser/components/syncedtabs/jar.mn", "browser/components/syncedtabs/sidebar.html", "browser/components/syncedtabs/sidebar.xhtml", "dom/security/nsContentSecurityUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "548abb538fe85fe312a49cc9826fcd7bcc67e2a1", "git_parents": ["03967bf3476d65c273d3459b1634acbac77af7af"], "node": "c10df8abd258d5df54867c46ab577eba07261535", "parents": ["0de3ed5f15d085f249ce59fbe263652b1a29be3f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065137 - Let promiseSuggestionsPresent find suggestions in a content-process urlbar. r=mbeier\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322269\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/tests/NewtabSearchbarContentTestUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/UrlbarTestUtils.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "79f2d86eb21f2a91269800a9ed79d51424ebe9f9", "git_parents": ["548abb538fe85fe312a49cc9826fcd7bcc67e2a1"], "node": "0ac4bd2b0f43cac14e5384c158653c97a16ebb3a", "parents": ["c10df8abd258d5df54867c46ab577eba07261535"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065137 - Test the newtab searchbar SAP by driving a real search. r=mbeier\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322270\n", "files": ["browser/components/search/test/browser/telemetry/browser.toml", "browser/components/search/test/browser/telemetry/browser_search_telemetry_sap_newtab_searchbar.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-newtab/browser.toml", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-newtab/browser_searchTelemetry.js"], "git_node": "7716114a7dd39b6d08b4c030e3f45bcdaac3d3aa", "git_parents": ["79f2d86eb21f2a91269800a9ed79d51424ebe9f9"], "node": "f615ff33f4889fd0907a57d67e9c28cfd57e6d9e", "parents": ["0ac4bd2b0f43cac14e5384c158653c97a16ebb3a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063327 - Test picking a search suggestion from an engine that submits by POST. r=mbeier\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322255\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-search/browser.toml", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-search/browser_searchSuggestions_postData.js"], "git_node": "7201eb4ef5a3ab8768d5e6600e294af76bb0bc77", "git_parents": ["7716114a7dd39b6d08b4c030e3f45bcdaac3d3aa"], "node": "4d5137d4f275487d4cf5e6c792384e5e796c737e", "parents": ["f615ff33f4889fd0907a57d67e9c28cfd57e6d9e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055935 - Resolve a result reconstructed from the wire to the parent's own result. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers\n\nThe engagement payload's visible results now resolve too, where the recorder passed them through as reconstructions, so providers' impression hooks get the parent's own objects and read the ping position from the merged rowIndex.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322299\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarParentController.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/actors/UrlbarParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarQueryContext.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarResult.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarTelemetryUtils.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/private/AmpSuggestions.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/test_UrlbarResult_wireSerialization.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/test_UrlbarTelemetryUtils_wireSerialization.js"], "git_node": "9c7803d7a4d53db0f70d8e0288486df833b2e27b", "git_parents": ["7201eb4ef5a3ab8768d5e6600e294af76bb0bc77"], "node": "ebe7594f5d51a5824cbd26d6d2b3552d7be39e29", "parents": ["4d5137d4f275487d4cf5e6c792384e5e796c737e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "giorga \u003cgiorga@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064877 - Wire the store into Fenix as a long-lived singleton r=android-reviewers,moyin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322293\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/.buildconfig.yml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/build.gradle", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/Components.kt"], "git_node": "be16d9ca2ceec98ad2e497b32d52fb90022d331c", "git_parents": ["9c7803d7a4d53db0f70d8e0288486df833b2e27b"], "node": "3224a8658ab7dd9b5b7c93ee3c1ed6789d73683f", "parents": ["ebe7594f5d51a5824cbd26d6d2b3552d7be39e29"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maurice Dauer \u003cmdauer@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066770 - Keep the window name as UTF-16, r=geckoview-reviewers,win-reviewers,layout-reviewers,dshin,emilio,gstoll,m_kato\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322278\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsGlobalWindowOuter.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientOpenWindowUtils.cpp", "dom/documentpip/DocumentPictureInPicture.cpp", "gfx/vr/nsFxrCommandLineHandler.cpp", "layout/tools/layout-debug/src/nsLayoutDebugCLH.cpp", "security/manager/pki/nsNSSDialogHelper.cpp", "security/manager/ssl/PKCS11ModuleDB.cpp", "toolkit/components/alerts/nsXULAlerts.cpp", "toolkit/components/windowwatcher/nsIWindowWatcher.idl", "toolkit/components/windowwatcher/nsPIWindowWatcher.idl", "toolkit/components/windowwatcher/nsWindowWatcher.cpp", "toolkit/components/windowwatcher/nsWindowWatcher.h", "toolkit/xre/ProfileReset.cpp", "toolkit/xre/nsAppRunner.cpp", "widget/android/nsWindow.cpp", "widget/uikit/nsWindow.mm", "widget/windows/nsPrintDialogWin.cpp"], "git_node": "b038e2a05e4452859c9b1bd6ba05aa839c6bf263", "git_parents": ["be16d9ca2ceec98ad2e497b32d52fb90022d331c"], "node": "b6d48482af45b7dd57c56a4f236708c47c76cc03", "parents": ["3224a8658ab7dd9b5b7c93ee3c1ed6789d73683f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Gaul \u003candrew@gaul.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067982 - jit: compute wasm derived pointers with one effective-address op. r=bvisness\n\nvisitWasmDerivedPointer spelled base + offset as a register copy\nfollowed by an in-place add, matching neither its sibling\nvisitWasmDerivedIndexPointer nor the single lea (x86) or add (arm64)\nthe operation needs. When the register allocator reused the base\nregister for the output, the copy was a no-op self-move.\n\nMeasured on JetStream 3 with --wasm-compiler=optimizing, which\nIon-compiles the whole wasm corpus and makes the counts deterministic\nand identical on both architectures: 23,456 emission sites, all in\nwasm function bodies.\n\nx86-64: 221,270 -\u003e 157,149 bytes, 63 KB of JIT code saved, mostly the\n3-byte mov (less where the old add could use rax's short immediate\nform); 7,141 of the removed movs were self-moves.\n\narm64: 252,376 -\u003e 173,088 bytes, 77 KB saved: one 4-byte mov per\nsite, except the 3,753 self-moves, which vixl already elided.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322549\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp"], "git_node": "e4d8e6130f2f6d5413075389fa830b798cee8947", "git_parents": ["b038e2a05e4452859c9b1bd6ba05aa839c6bf263"], "node": "1240a6fbb6195b49d23ee3caba2885135b182214", "parents": ["b6d48482af45b7dd57c56a4f236708c47c76cc03"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dale Harvey \u003cdale@arandomurl.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038596 - Avoid flicker when opening trustpanel. r=urlbar-reviewers,daisuke\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319646\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-trustPanel.js"], "git_node": "435eb8b616f60df292b05dfef375409b3b2180d6", "git_parents": ["e4d8e6130f2f6d5413075389fa830b798cee8947"], "node": "3e6469ec93d99ffde44668dd2fb24eba9fcfe0c0", "parents": ["1240a6fbb6195b49d23ee3caba2885135b182214"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067989 - Send engine icons to a content-process view as data URLs. r=daleharvey\n\nThe engine store's icons are no longer converted on the chrome message path, where the child global is in this process and a blob URL resolves as it does on the direct path.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322572\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarParentController.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderAiChat.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderAliasEngines.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderPrivateSearch.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderSearchSuggestions.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderSearchTips.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderTokenAliasEngines.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/actors/UrlbarParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/NewtabSearchbarContentTestUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/NewtabSearchbarTestUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-newtab/browser.toml", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-newtab/browser_engineIcon.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-newtab/browser_resultIcon.js"], "git_node": "5721e298585357d2d180a0bb5742edec5252a036", "git_parents": ["435eb8b616f60df292b05dfef375409b3b2180d6"], "node": "fd1a97661a4582355c237d60cf80f93c08775e0c", "parents": ["3e6469ec93d99ffde44668dd2fb24eba9fcfe0c0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067248 - Accept several pipe-separated homepages in the Homepage policy. r=bsmth\n\nbrowser.startup.homepage holds one URL or several separated by \"|\", and\nadministrators have long set the whole list as Homepage.URL rather than using\nAdditional. No JSON Schema format describes that value, and \"uri\" rejects \"|\"\noutright, so the list no longer validates.\n\nGive Homepage.URL a \"moz-homepage-url-list\" format: split on \"|\" the way\nHomePage.sys.mjs splits the pref, and require every entry to parse as a URL.\nThe field hydrates to a normalized string instead of a URL object, since no\nsingle URL object can hold a list.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321965\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.sys.mjs", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/browser/browser_policy_set_homepage.js", "toolkit/components/enterprisepolicies/EnterprisePoliciesParent.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "b924677bda6ba7a0d4a553ce328b778be89deacf", "git_parents": ["5721e298585357d2d180a0bb5742edec5252a036"], "node": "b1027db11326a324476e568872ac6867bb178ad5", "parents": ["fd1a97661a4582355c237d60cf80f93c08775e0c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ayoub hedri \u003cahedri@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066074 - Removed telemetry probes for mixed_content_page_load r=freddyb,chutten\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320880\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.cpp", "dom/security/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/telemetry/Histograms.json", "toolkit/components/telemetry/histogram-allowlists.json"], "git_node": "b4a236a8943b5895badb9bd9a8c3a9cf285678d2", "git_parents": ["b924677bda6ba7a0d4a553ce328b778be89deacf"], "node": "c014916c0172f503a7f61e6612030a2a689a2a8f", "parents": ["b1027db11326a324476e568872ac6867bb178ad5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067801 - Remove the write-only clip fast-path flag. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nClipNodeFlags::USE_FAST_PATH was set in ClipNodeInfo::create_instance and never\nread anywhere. The quad clip path derives the rounded-rect fast path\nindependently from the radius and clip rect (quad::write_rounded_rect_clip_blocks\nvia ClipItemKind::can_use_fast_path_in), so this flag has no consumer.\n\nComputing it was the only reason create_instance - and, transitively,\nClipStore::build_clip_chain_instance - needed the spatial tree, and the transform\nit queried was the primitive's root-relative one. Whether a clip mask can take an\naxis-aligned fast path depends on the clip's orientation in the space the mask is\nrasterized in, not in the root's, so this was also asking the wrong question.\n\nClipNodeInstance is per-frame scratch rather than a cache or invalidation key, so\ndropping the bit has no observable effect.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322342\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/clip.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/tile_cache/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/visibility.rs"], "git_node": "69386f218ea3e34453f09eb4f96ef8c6d4aa0c07", "git_parents": ["b4a236a8943b5895badb9bd9a8c3a9cf285678d2"], "node": "fe3990ed2604138446b19c64220bb7172290b2ec", "parents": ["c014916c0172f503a7f61e6612030a2a689a2a8f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067801 - Remove the unused hit-test viewport transform. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nHitTestSpatialNode::world_viewport_transform was populated for every spatial node\neach time the hit tester read the spatial tree, and never read: hit testing only\never uses world_content_transform.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322343\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/hit_test.rs"], "git_node": "8d0527fb57ff3d30c64497c8db01928c13b7ba22", "git_parents": ["69386f218ea3e34453f09eb4f96ef8c6d4aa0c07"], "node": "1e4134c873a111cce68630c6033763bc1fe8f8e1", "parents": ["fe3990ed2604138446b19c64220bb7172290b2ec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067801 - Rasterize line decorations at the target surface's scale. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nThe cached line decoration mask was sized from the primitive's root-relative\ntransform, then used directly as a layout-to-device scale. Those are the same\nthing only when the surface rasterizes in root space at a device pixel scale of\none, or - approximately - for a tile cache, whose device pixel scale tracks the\nworld scale of its own raster node. They diverge for a surface that establishes a\nnon-snapping raster root (preserve-3d, perspective, RasterSpace::Local, huge\nscale): there the surface deliberately rasterizes at a clamped or\nclient-supplied scale, so the mask was sized for a resolution the surface never\nuses, and MAX_LINE_DECORATION_RESOLUTION could cap it based on that unused scale.\n\nTake the scale from the QuadTransformState the caller already holds, which is the\nprimitive-to-raster-node transform times the surface's device pixel scale, i.e.\nthe resolution the mask is actually composited at. This also removes the need for\nthe spatial tree here, and with it the caveat about perspective in the world\ntransform: a perspective raster root is inside the perspective, so the\nprimitive-to-raster transform doesn't carry it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322344\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/line_dec.rs"], "git_node": "cc409b9790fe3e53fb6e07eadf30d5029b8d3994", "git_parents": ["8d0527fb57ff3d30c64497c8db01928c13b7ba22"], "node": "1fda30432d7c1e5102ec77224a83934893ff9919", "parents": ["1e4134c873a111cce68630c6033763bc1fe8f8e1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067801 - Rasterize borders at the target surface's scale. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nThe border rasterization scale and the device grid the edge widths and radii are\nsnapped to were both derived from the primitive's root-relative transform\nmultiplied by the surface's device pixel scale. Those two factors overlap: a\nsurface's device pixel scale already accounts for the world scale of its raster\nnode, so for any surface whose device pixel scale is not one - every tile cache\nwhose node has a non-unit world scale, i.e. a hidpi display, or page or pinch zoom\nabove the cache - that node's scale was applied twice.\n\nThe consequences were an over-resolved cached texture for every rounded, dashed or\ndotted corner (quadratically so, and hitting MAX_BORDER_RESOLUTION at a smaller\ncorner size than intended), and a snapping grid finer than the real device grid,\nwhich defeats the whole-device-pixel guarantee the snapping in bugs 1258112,\n1950029 and 2062877 relies on.\n\nTake both from the QuadTransformState the caller already holds. Its raster scale\nis quantized to a power of two for the rasterization scale, as before, while the\nsnapping uses the unquantized local-to-device scale.\n\nA surface that establishes a non-snapping raster root (preserve-3d, perspective,\nRasterSpace::Local, huge scale) was wrong in the other direction: its device pixel\nscale is deliberately a clamped or client-supplied scale rather than the live world\nscale. Going through the raster node also avoids taking scale factors from a\nperspective matrix, since such a raster root sits inside the perspective.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322345\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/borders.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs"], "git_node": "80e4a9ed550751821e53b3d3819eb7493a83fd20", "git_parents": ["cc409b9790fe3e53fb6e07eadf30d5029b8d3994"], "node": "c6f4877193b588c076674ebd58c9f9099a71c3f8", "parents": ["1fda30432d7c1e5102ec77224a83934893ff9919"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067801 - Pick the glyph raster scale from the target surface's scale. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nWhen a text run's spatial node is zooming or animating, the glyphs are rasterized\nin local space at a power-of-two quantization of the scale they will be composited\nat. That scale was taken from the primitive's root-relative transform, which\nmatches the composited scale only for a surface that rasterizes in root space at a\ndevice pixel scale of one, or - approximately - for a tile cache, whose device\npixel scale tracks the world scale of its own raster node.\n\nA surface that establishes a non-snapping raster root rasterizes at a clamped or\nclient-supplied scale instead, which is by design not the live world scale. Text\ninside a picture that requested RasterSpace::Local(1.0) while being scaled 8x on\nscreen would rasterize its glyphs 8x too large - 64x the glyph cache footprint -\nand have them minified back down on composite.\n\nQuantize the prim to raster scale times the surface's device pixel scale instead,\nwhich is the scale the glyphs are actually composited at. This is unchanged for\nthe two common surface configurations.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322346\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/text_run.rs"], "git_node": "cf30d44fd4098a8f083d06a9482a5dc8a20ea59c", "git_parents": ["80e4a9ed550751821e53b3d3819eb7493a83fd20"], "node": "294009d059caa1b9c0473e55d874bcdf3fc6a60e", "parents": ["c6f4877193b588c076674ebd58c9f9099a71c3f8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2003767 - Wrap the TSan and LSan interface headers as system headers. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322120\n", "files": ["config/system-headers.mozbuild"], "git_node": "c22f6a0b02202e53f28b7897f4b59f91759b3511", "git_parents": ["cf30d44fd4098a8f083d06a9482a5dc8a20ea59c"], "node": "e5d1a39343c35b8b9c87861951f93a998d6324a4", "parents": ["294009d059caa1b9c0473e55d874bcdf3fc6a60e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067508 - updated abseil-cpp patch stack. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nRebased onto chromium third_party cd3dd0a61f8. Drops the ABSL_HAVE_THREAD_SANITIZER\nand ABSL_HAVE_LEAK_SANITIZER disables, which the preceding system-header change makes\nunnecessary; the -Wsign-compare suppression, which protobuf v36 no longer needs; and\nthe android api \u003c 17 SYS_mmap2 patch, replaced by the next commit. Consolidates the\nremaining eleven local patches into six.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322121\n", "files": ["third_party/abseil-cpp/moz-patch-stack/0001.patch", "third_party/abseil-cpp/moz-patch-stack/0002.patch", "third_party/abseil-cpp/moz-patch-stack/0003.patch", "third_party/abseil-cpp/moz-patch-stack/0004.patch", "third_party/abseil-cpp/moz-patch-stack/0005.patch", "third_party/abseil-cpp/moz-patch-stack/0006.patch", "third_party/abseil-cpp/moz-patch-stack/0007.patch", "third_party/abseil-cpp/moz-patch-stack/0008.patch", "third_party/abseil-cpp/moz-patch-stack/0009.patch", "third_party/abseil-cpp/moz-patch-stack/0010.patch", "third_party/abseil-cpp/moz-patch-stack/0011.patch", "third_party/abseil-cpp/moz-patch-stack/0012.patch", "third_party/abseil-cpp/moz-patch-stack/0013.patch", "third_party/abseil-cpp/moz-patch-stack/0014.patch", "third_party/abseil-cpp/moz-patch-stack/0015.patch"], "git_node": "2ef77c8c6d3a1c33b8cdd3f9041621d45f2fa314", "git_parents": ["c22f6a0b02202e53f28b7897f4b59f91759b3511"], "node": "b83479b0e748936bbf8139bd1677dd4865c011de", "parents": ["e5d1a39343c35b8b9c87861951f93a998d6324a4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067508 - give abseil's externally-provided symbol declarations default visibility. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nThe Annotate* race annotations and __tsan_read1 come from the sanitizer runtime,\n__mmap2 from Bionic. Under the tree-wide -fvisibility=hidden they become hidden\nundefined symbols, failing the libxul link on TSan and on 32-bit Android.\n\nProposed upstream as https://github.com/abseil/abseil-cpp/pull/2136.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322122\n", "files": ["third_party/abseil-cpp/moz-patch-stack/0007.patch"], "git_node": "61040359a808ca1bb1b58bfc673fdc38025950c0", "git_parents": ["2ef77c8c6d3a1c33b8cdd3f9041621d45f2fa314"], "node": "27e8d8029f3b46d87ce48cc5bbd645b6aef72c12", "parents": ["b83479b0e748936bbf8139bd1677dd4865c011de"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067508 - define O_NONBLOCK to 0 on platforms lacking it. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\ncctz opens zoneinfo files with O_NONBLOCK, which mingw does not define, breaking all\nfour mingwclang builds. Mirrors the O_CLOEXEC fallback two lines above.\n\nMerged upstream as https://github.com/google/cctz/pull/372, but abseil has not\nimported it yet.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322123\n", "files": ["third_party/abseil-cpp/moz-patch-stack/0008.patch"], "git_node": "ec1c42439575b256aa6db5b1b64c4525891df631", "git_parents": ["61040359a808ca1bb1b58bfc673fdc38025950c0"], "node": "97942d713968bcb4c10e9dca5201937df5220286", "parents": ["27e8d8029f3b46d87ce48cc5bbd645b6aef72c12"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067508 - vendor abseil-cpp from libwebrtc/third_party cd3dd0a61f8. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nAlso adds absl/base/throw_delegate.cc to the hand-maintained sandbox source lists;\nstr_format/bind.cc now calls absl::ThrowStdLengthError, breaking the standalone\nWindows link in noopt/debug builds.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322124\n", "files": ["security/sandbox/linux/moz.build", "security/sandbox/moz.build", "third_party/abseil-cpp/.style.yapf", "third_party/abseil-cpp/BUILD.gn", "third_party/abseil-cpp/CMake/AbseilDll.cmake", "third_party/abseil-cpp/MODULE.bazel", "third_party/abseil-cpp/README.chromium", "third_party/abseil-cpp/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/abseil-cpp/absl.gni", "third_party