d110f75cbf3a6cb40", "parents": ["8ad71a18389483618b2e31422a0d40b22bdc84a0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068042 - Fix :host matching regression. r=dshin\n\nIf `:host` is in the document we currently don't bucket them.\n\nPull request: https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/pull/354\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/selector_map.rs", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-shadow/host-in-document-descendant.html"], "git_node": "7f3bc24872c69b2c39c3a8824df525ae90a52133", "git_parents": ["7704558f70d275d7d97a7b6e42d35f19deb2cfc0"], "node": "eeb045b3a49673a688a0aa223614aea90634273e", "parents": ["b7d785de380faa515b81d9ed110f75cbf3a6cb40"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067844 - Remove Rust color -\u003e nscolor conversion. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,layout-reviewers,dshin\n\nWe want to have just one of those. This doesn't change behavior right\nnow but would when we enable gamut mapping in e.g. canvas.\n\nHowever it seems to me like we need deeper changes there, because\nprobably we shouldn't turn those into srgb upfront...\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322384\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsAttrValue.cpp", "dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.cpp", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditUtils.cpp", "gfx/layers/AnimationInfo.cpp", "gfx/layers/CompositorAnimationStorage.cpp", "layout/inspector/InspectorUtils.cpp", "layout/style/PreferenceSheet.cpp", "layout/style/ServoCSSParser.cpp", "layout/style/ServoCSSParser.h", "layout/style/StyleAnimationValue.cpp", "layout/style/StyleAnimationValue.h", "layout/svg/SVGImageContext.cpp", "servo/components/style/color/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/device/gecko.rs", "servo/components/style/device/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/device/servo.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/glue.rs", "widget/nsXPLookAndFeel.cpp"], "git_node": "029a20c844ce3baef9bbfb3491d69c447543faca", "git_parents": ["7f3bc24872c69b2c39c3a8824df525ae90a52133"], "node": "f507dae59a7913fd12bbcef54e19fe633aabc037", "parents": ["eeb045b3a49673a688a0aa223614aea90634273e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068184 - Check for visibility CSS property in PopupNotifications. r=robwu,jsudiaman\n\nBefore bug 2064683, the tab bar was hidden via display: none, and now it\nonly has collapsed attribute which uses visibility: collapse.\n\nPopupNotifications should account for visibility: collapse / hidden,\njust like checkForAnchorChange does.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322746\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-trustPanel.js", "browser/base/content/browser.js", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_request_permissions.js", "browser/components/sidebar/sidebar-permissions.mjs", "toolkit/modules/PopupNotifications.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "db246620fb987a788758388dd10044596e44ec97", "git_parents": ["029a20c844ce3baef9bbfb3491d69c447543faca"], "node": "265dd25cd7700a8a91d9b705c1a30efe05a581b6", "parents": ["f507dae59a7913fd12bbcef54e19fe633aabc037"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068138 - Don't parse for/form in non-null namespaces as an atom. r=dom-core-reviewers,jjaschke\n\nOnly lang needs this special-case (because of xml:lang). Noticed while\nI was trying to make xml:lang less weird.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322647\n", "files": ["dom/base/Element.cpp"], "git_node": "ed47cc6488223a921b75ea8ddb3897581edf7f02", "git_parents": ["db246620fb987a788758388dd10044596e44ec97"], "node": "8a88d102ddf87e513a78cdb3b50cbb8af0b0e1c1", "parents": ["265dd25cd7700a8a91d9b705c1a30efe05a581b6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "hanna.alemu \u003chalemu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2041980 - Drive the DoH opt-out decision directly in tests instead of through the CFR doorhanger. r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nThe DoH rollout prompt was a cfr_doorhanger, so head.js wired ASRouter to\nlocalProvider: \"CFRMessageProvider\" and asserted on the\ncontextual-feature-recommendation popupnotification, which bug 2041980 removes.\nIt is replaced by simulateUserDecision(), writing exactly what the ACCEPT_DOH and\nDISABLE_DOH actions write so the assertions on TRR mode, breadcrumbs and\nheuristics telemetry all still hold; browser_doorhangerUserReject.js is renamed\nto browser_userOptOut.js.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318364\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/doh/test/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/doh/test/browser/browser_cleanFlow.js", "toolkit/components/doh/test/browser/browser_doorhangerUserReject.js", "toolkit/components/doh/test/browser/browser_policyOverride.js", "toolkit/components/doh/test/browser/browser_rollback.js", "toolkit/components/doh/test/browser/browser_trrSelection_disable.js", "toolkit/components/doh/test/browser/browser_userInterference.js", "toolkit/components/doh/test/browser/browser_userOptOut.js", "toolkit/components/doh/test/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "335105f4c576abb823024d61b57712dca03e8549", "git_parents": ["ed47cc6488223a921b75ea8ddb3897581edf7f02"], "node": "d16bde74e27f64937c619af62d5b338a5f9291e4", "parents": ["8a88d102ddf87e513a78cdb3b50cbb8af0b0e1c1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kelly Cochrane \u003ckcochrane@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050444 - Change sidebar width to 50x wide when vertical tabs are enabled in compact and standard UI densities to make room for scrollbar r=desktop-theme-reviewers,tabbrowser-reviewers,jsudiaman,dao\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321983\n", "files": ["browser/components/customizableui/test/browser_uidensity_auto_compact.js", "browser/themes/shared/sidebar.css", "browser/themes/shared/tabbrowser/tabs.css"], "git_node": "a20b76cf3b9dd945bb08805e481295315428c2fe", "git_parents": ["335105f4c576abb823024d61b57712dca03e8549"], "node": "c71ff9806eea369c3f408399a54a172b5fa392b4", "parents": ["d16bde74e27f64937c619af62d5b338a5f9291e4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065813 - Fix the tabbrowser's JSDoc types that name the wrong shape. r=kcochrane,tabbrowser-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320691\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "35c9992d39526995f47692c8dd805b4b83966958", "git_parents": ["a20b76cf3b9dd945bb08805e481295315428c2fe"], "node": "cf7c2613d5f752463d21b0c376d7475032a3f396", "parents": ["c71ff9806eea369c3f408399a54a172b5fa392b4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065813 - Give the split view's session state shape a name. r=kcochrane,tabbrowser-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320692\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/types/elements.ts", "browser/components/tabbrowser/types/globals.ts"], "git_node": "cf008a66422f9cde177ea42f3e713c546a578c8a", "git_parents": ["35c9992d39526995f47692c8dd805b4b83966958"], "node": "cb21b987bea9214cdb3aaef5b0ae20be0d1f47bb", "parents": ["cf7c2613d5f752463d21b0c376d7475032a3f396"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065813 - Type the tabbrowser's per-tab maps. r=jsudiaman,tabbrowser-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322865\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/types/globals.ts"], "git_node": "487fab039cfef333033f2fa545ef78f76f0eddb7", "git_parents": ["cf008a66422f9cde177ea42f3e713c546a578c8a"], "node": "4acd7ca5b1996fb08b84f6f8fb77bd6f848fb5ad", "parents": ["cb21b987bea9214cdb3aaef5b0ae20be0d1f47bb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Magnus Melin \u003cmkmelin+mozilla@iki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068614 - Set mSourceNode after hiding the previous tooltip in MouseMove. r=emilio,layout-reviewers\n\nFollow-up to https://hg.mozilla.org/mozilla-central/rev/3bfa78cb60f7\n\ncomm/mail/components/im/test/browser/browser_tooltips.js regressed on\nbug 2001695 and passes again with this: its second task moves the mouse into a\nfresh conversation browser while a node from the first task is still tracked.\n\nnsXULTooltipListener::MouseMove() recorded mSourceNode and ran\nCheckTreeBodyMove() before hiding the tooltip of the node the mouse just left.\nBoth of those HideTooltip() paths end in DestroyTooltip(), which clears\nmSourceNode, so the timer armed a few lines later fired into a ShowTooltip()\nwith no source node: GetTooltipFor(nullptr) fails and no tooltip is shown for\nthe new node, ever.\n\nMove the mSourceNode assignment and CheckTreeBodyMove() call to after the teardown,\nso the source survives for the timer callback.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322942\n", "files": ["layout/xul/nsXULTooltipListener.cpp"], "git_node": "1a10fc73a8c5079c7fff0095df1332f6cbf79a44", "git_parents": ["487fab039cfef333033f2fa545ef78f76f0eddb7"], "node": "5f8d0c62aadad4188b6adcdd35e3768490905352", "parents": ["4acd7ca5b1996fb08b84f6f8fb77bd6f848fb5ad"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068565 - Update PDF.js to 74515c623c1a0a555e6ca684c435202bf3a91752 r=pdfjs-reviewers,calixte\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322893\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.scripting.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.worker.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/viewer-gec