=mxinden,necko-reviewers,leggert,valentin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322680\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "netwerk/socket/neqo_glue/src/lib.rs"], "git_node": "745ffd25670a4c0a39335a2b5d9f3dad3fd8c2f2", "git_parents": ["f6d0eefca99d4afd9d39e91ef81de4e8ba726b62"], "node": "f7983b15082674d80ff056451a3ec7966f4b6bd2", "parents": ["e22d897cefadfe6deea3d666c795e87ce421eec9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068240 - Make mForm a RefPtr. r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322736\n", "files": ["dom/html/HTMLFormElement.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLImageElement.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLImageElement.h", "dom/html/nsGenericHTMLElement.cpp", "dom/html/nsGenericHTMLElement.h"], "git_node": "f4b841d6d3e969a4f9e91ab647bdb2063a19122c", "git_parents": ["745ffd25670a4c0a39335a2b5d9f3dad3fd8c2f2"], "node": "21c82f196613fd457f68ae0a5bc27a0b828a9bce", "parents": ["f7983b15082674d80ff056451a3ec7966f4b6bd2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Giulia Cardieri \u003cgcardieri@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2048916: Fix ai-action-result header text on hover in HCM mode r=ngrato\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323030\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-action-result/ai-action-result.css"], "git_node": "ed349265a5144e3cd612c4eabe41a7d833deb7fb", "git_parents": ["f4b841d6d3e969a4f9e91ab647bdb2063a19122c"], "node": "b63e3effd9425f4b8c16c60e1b35b796f348f847", "parents": ["21c82f196613fd457f68ae0a5bc27a0b828a9bce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Mehic \u003cdmehic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 830718 - Reenable the private browsing notification xpcshell tests r=timhuang\n\nBoth tests had been disabled since 2012. They could not simply be\nreenabled: \"last-pb-context-exited\" is now fired from a private context\nrefcount kept on CanonicalBrowsingContext, which only counts content\nbrowsing contexts, so the chrome windowless browser the tests used never\nmoved the count and the notification never fired. An attached content\ncontext cannot have its origin attributes changed either, so the context\nhas to be created private.\n\ntest_pb_notification.js now uses XPCShellContentUtils to load a private\ncontent page and closes it.\n\ntest_pb_notification_ipc.js is inverted. The private context can only be\ncreated in the parent process, so the parent drives it and the child only\nobserves, which covers the ContentParent -\u003e ContentChild relay of the\ntopic that the content process consumers depend on.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322105\n", "files": ["docshell/test/unit/test_pb_notification.js", "docshell/test/unit/xpcshell.toml", "docshell/test/unit_ipc/child_pb_notification.js", "docshell/test/unit_ipc/test_pb_notification_ipc.js", "docshell/test/unit_ipc/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "0cb8ececeff037ec9c66235293b2f4bd492c42ae", "git_parents": ["ed349265a5144e3cd612c4eabe41a7d833deb7fb"], "node": "84ffc08267a2f50a4901f0343d0aaf1ed498c357", "parents": ["b63e3effd9425f4b8c16c60e1b35b796f348f847"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Mehic \u003cdmehic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1597849 - Dehardcode browser_privatebrowsing_windowtitle.js r=manuel\n\nThe test hardcoded the en-US \"Private Browsing\" suffix, so a wording change\nin browser.ftl had to be mirrored here (see bug 1758961). Fetch the three\nstrings that getWindowTitleForBrowser() composes from Fluent instead, and keep\nonly the platform-specific composition rules the test is actually asserting.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322127\n", "files": ["browser/components/privatebrowsing/test/browser/browser_privatebrowsing_windowtitle.js"], "git_node": "71203a67756a7869654f14026d27bc8aab529371", "git_parents": ["0cb8ececeff037ec9c66235293b2f4bd492c42ae"], "node": "8525fb98492bf2d6e8048a446bd80fd17bd121b2", "parents": ["84ffc08267a2f50a4901f0343d0aaf1ed498c357"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Mehic \u003cdmehic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067524 - Remove unused NS_ERROR_PLUGIN_BLOCKLISTED error code r=manuel\n\nLast producer of the error was removed in bug 1682030.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322132\n", "files": ["tools/ts/config/error_list.json", "xpcom/base/ErrorList.py"], "git_node": "42edb8ce319606130ea3038c00d12e028524fd52", "git_parents": ["71203a67756a7869654f14026d27bc8aab529371"], "node": "e517bc8ea5d6df63f7d6494b979fe4a826f4be15", "parents": ["8525fb98492bf2d6e8048a446bd80fd17bd121b2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "any1here \u003cany1here@duck.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057730 - Fix Picture-in-Picture auto-toggle loop on deliberate close r=kpatenio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321446\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/pictureinpicture/PictureInPicture.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/pictureinpicture/tests/browser_autotoggle.js"], "git_node": "3a1385e1aca3ec5cb1346c07c50e69803c7b2132", "git_parents": ["42edb8ce319606130ea3038c00d12e028524fd52"], "node": "5c797c474904fe26e9f28634555f79cad76c2088", "parents": ["e517bc8ea5d6df63f7d6494b979fe4a826f4be15"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068437. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322843\n", "files": ["gfx/2d/DrawTargetCairo.cpp", "gfx/2d/DrawTargetCairo.h"], "git_node": "6a8b28132e122dc673aae452e7c03cd071f9c133", "git_parents": ["3a1385e1aca3ec5cb1346c07c50e69803c7b2132"], "node": "1ea765ebc7aa6657c57c636a8d23c1444d5eeb78", "parents": ["5c797c474904fe26e9f28634555f79cad76c2088"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Marc Leclair \u003cmleclair@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068675 - Use lld-link's call-graph profile sort instead of the PGO orderfile on Windows r=sergesanspaille\n\nselect_linker is not evaluated for Windows targets, so pgo_cg_sort was\nfalse there and configure passed -ORDER:@ to lld-link, which disables its\ndefault /call-graph-profile-sort.\n\nSpeedometer 3 on windows11-64-24h2-shippable improves by 0.3%: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/attachment.cgi?id=9635493\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322990\n", "files": ["build/moz.configure/lto-pgo.configure"], "git_node": "aa1cf5d66ed4704f3a0bc9bec20036788feda949", "git_parents": ["6a8b28132e122dc673aae452e7c03cd071f9c133"], "node": "5fdba034a40063d8f10190ece966674019615bc3", "parents": ["1ea765ebc7aa6657c57c636a8d23c1444d5eeb78"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rolf Rando \u003crrando@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066218 - Update autofill models, introduce smoke tests to check for regressions r=perftest-reviewers,credential-management-reviewers,ai-platform-reviewers,dimi,aglavic,valentinp\n\nonnx-native was exhibiting a regression on certain chipsets on FormAutfill in fx154\n\nThis patch adds smoke testing in form autofill on model quality based on 100 entries, and uses the newer models that were re-quantized to not have the chipset dependent issues.\n\ntry run (linux only): https://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&revision=8d8401957957423fe58e72fb42b18c19c4445dd7&selectedTaskRun=DqKsVwfUTQmwsw_MCN-gZA.0\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321037\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/fetch/onnxruntime-web-fetch.yml", "toolkit/components/formautofill/shared/FormAutofillML.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/browser_ml_autofill_perf.js", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/data/autofill/testing-supported.txt", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "a4ae60a8bf54c2318081d88a5e6045dbe27ab603", "git_parents": ["aa1cf5d66ed4704f3a0bc9bec20036788feda949"], "node": "736b965f3c9134615227c1b2a9136fe88ae8df44", "parents": ["5fdba034a40063d8f10190ece966674019615bc3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Mehic \u003cdmehic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2006309 - Remove privacy.clearSiteDataHeader.cache.bfcache.enabled r=manuel\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317367\n", "files": ["docshell/base/CanonicalBrowsingContext.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/meta/clear-site-data/clear-cache-bfcache-partitioning.tentative.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/clear-site-data/clear-cache-bfcache.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "453945f2a523a22e485a356700fbb0804cd86b66", "git_parents": ["a4ae60a8bf54c2318081d88a5e6045dbe27ab603"], "node": "36c466f029e9446df7f5324bcf77f909e65141f9", "parents": ["736b965f3c9134615227c1b2a9136fe88ae8df44"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068718 - Update opus to 8f39f9725c9546d64c6eb8fff4d8c1b19abba1e6 r=kinetik\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323026\n", "files": ["media/libopus/moz.build", "media/libopus/moz.yaml", "media/libopus/src/opus_decoder.c"], "git_node": "eb05a3551d5425bff664be01e42b274d11370b9f", "git_parents": ["453945f2a523a22e485a356700fbb0804cd86b66"], "node": "0cf79d16b3799f89ac30f443c2994cdf42750aae", "parents": ["36c466f029e9446df7f5324bcf77f909e65141f9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065813 - Add the casts the tabbrowser's element and XPCOM values need. r=jsudiaman,tabbrowser-reviewers\n\nThe `tagName` comparison becomes the class's own `isSplitViewWrapper`, which tests exactly that and narrows, and `triggeringEvent.target` loses an optional chain the preceding clause already guarantees. The rest is casts.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320693\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/types/elements.ts"], "git_node": "4ec91a40ff360e66c65903d12f57e1c938d8a36f", "git_parents": ["eb05a3551d5425bff664be01e42b274d11370b9f"], "node": "8bb06eb8bd7ca50ec110b8bd5b6535c719f9d5ae", "parents": ["0cf79d16b3799f89ac30f443c2994cdf42750aae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Irene Ni \u003cini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058284 - Add Section Layout Name telemetry to newtab content impression & click events. r=thecount,mlplyler\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314478\n", "files": ["browser/components/newtab/metrics.yaml", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/NewTabContentPing.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/TelemetryFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_NewTabContentPing.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_TelemetryFeed.js"], "git_node": "bf4d162eb10a3d054d82ed76ec02ee2b1c127ee5", "git_parents": ["4ec91a40ff360e66c65903d12f57e1c938d8a36f"], "node": "770c3652d7bdf996c8e6804e37965b793f48eb9c", "parents": ["8bb06eb8bd7ca50ec110b8bd5b6535c719f9d5ae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Irene Ni \u003cini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067937 - Remove section_position telemetry from newtab_content impression and click events. r=thecount\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322481\n", "files": ["browser/components/newtab/metrics.yaml", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/NewTabContentPing.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_NewTabContentPing.js"], "git_node": "bfda84aefc183c14bee767998a30ec9767e283b3", "git_parents": ["bf4d162eb10a3d054d82ed76ec02ee2b1c127ee5"], "node": "bcad397c3a7a9ca9d5a640741c32fde30512552e", "parents": ["770c3652d7bdf996c8e6804e37965b793f48eb9c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Mehic \u003cdmehic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061979 - Add descriptive header comments to the ETP shims that lack them r=webcompat-reviewers,twisniewski\n\nMost shims open with a block comment naming the bug and explaining what breaks\nwithout them. Twelve did not. Each now has a header in that style, describing\nwhat the shim stubs out or works around and why a site would break otherwise.\n\nThe bug numbers, names and match patterns come from data/shims.js; the\ndescriptions come from reading each shim.\n\nComments only, so there is no behaviour change: the diff is 112 added lines and\nno removed ones.\n\nA note on the file list, which differs from the one in the bug. That list was\nbuilt by looking for a leading /** block and turned out to over-count. Four\nshims use /* rather than /** for their header (crave-ca.js, history.js,\ninstagram.js, tsn-ca.js), aliexpress-language.js writes \"Bug 1912228  -\" with\ntwo spaces, and jira-zendesk-support.js puts its header after a console.warn\nrather than before it. All six already document themselves and are left alone.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317289\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/webcompat/shims/artstationLogin.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/shims/bmauth.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/shims/cambridgeDictionaryLogin.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/shims/disqus-embed.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/shims/google-analytics-legacy.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/shims/instagram-embed.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/shims/microsoftAccountIcon.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/shims/microsoftLogin.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/shims/rambler-authenticator.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/shims/stackoverflow-login.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/shims/tiktok-embed.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/shims/twitter-embed.js"], "git_node": "ebf366412f2bd043316f1cf70d0af1f279584ced", "git_parents": ["bfda84aefc183c14bee767998a30ec9767e283b3"], "node": "aa24a1a46c7132e0a4a48fb048c7c049348b21db", "parents": ["bcad397c3a7a9ca9d5a640741c32fde30512552e"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788409269, "git_changesets": ["1a35a380384089ebc17478177466182c5788f00f", "837c31e8c4464a23f7541f51a2728033e9eb9da5", "245c3144ed16e6c1be43ea7c1739b352ab9865e0", "557b7744427f961aec5fca79ca4c5f2f5b091839", "7704558f70d275d7d97a7b6e42d35f19deb2cfc0", "7f3bc24872c69b2c39c3a8824df525ae90a52133", "029a20c844ce3baef9bbfb3491d69c447543faca", "db246620fb987a788758388dd10044596e44ec97", "ed47cc6488223a921b75ea8ddb3897581edf7f02", "335105f4c576abb823024d61b57712dca03e8549", "a20b76cf3b9dd945bb08805e481295315428c2fe", "35c9992d39526995f47692c8dd805b4b83966958", "cf008a66422f9cde177ea42f3e713c546a578c8a", "487fab039cfef333033f2fa545ef78f76f0eddb7", "1a10fc73a8c5079c7fff0095df1332f6cbf79a44", "89824195e5fbc49553846c2ebb6bf7924884a09b", "f256bb4d76e357c3256e4fd265eea2a6a8b3b046", "f6d0eefca99d4afd9d39e91ef81de4e8ba726b62", "745ffd25670a4c0a39335a2b5d9f3dad3fd8c2f2", "f4b841d6d3e969a4f9e91ab647bdb2063a19122c", "ed349265a5144e3cd612c4eabe41a7d833deb7fb", "0cb8ececeff037ec9c66235293b2f4bd492c42ae", "71203a67756a7869654f14026d27bc8aab529371", "42edb8ce319606130ea3038c00d12e028524fd52", "3a1385e1aca3ec5cb1346c07c50e69803c7b2132", "6a8b28132e122dc673aae452e7c03cd071f9c133", "aa1cf5d66ed4704f3a0bc9bec20036788feda949", "a4ae60a8bf54c2318081d88a5e6045dbe27ab603", "453945f2a523a22e485a356700fbb0804cd86b66", "eb05a3551d5425bff664be01e42b274d11370b9f", "4ec91a40ff360e66c65903d12f57e1c938d8a36f", "bf4d162eb10a3d054d82ed76ec02ee2b1c127ee5", "bfda84aefc183c14bee767998a30ec9767e283b3", "ebf366412f2bd043316f1cf70d0af1f279584ced"], "user": "agoloman@mozilla.com"}, "45239": {"changesets": [{"author": "@Giulia Cardieri \u003cgcardieri@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061059: Style SFF autocomplete row item r=omarg,fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,credential-management-reviewers,mkennedy,hjones,bolsson,mtigley\n\n- Update the SFF autocomplete with its Figma style\n- Make the summary pills (when we have more than 2 sources) and the edit button clickable and focusable via keyboard\n- Add a aria-label that changes depending on the status of the SFF trigger status (loading/fill/not able to find sources) - this is needed because the content from the richlistitem is not visible to screen readers (per my understanding)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318806\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/assets/sff-autofill-icon.svg", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/jar.mn", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/SmartFormFillAutocomplete.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_smartformfill_autocomplete.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/browser_autocomplete_footer.js", "browser/locales-preview/aiWindow.ftl", "browser/themes/shared/autocomplete.css", "toolkit/components/satchel/autocomplete-row-item/autocomplete-row-item.css", "toolkit/components/satchel/autocomplete-row-item/autocomplete-row-item.mjs", "toolkit/components/satchel/test/browser/browser_autocomplete.js", "toolkit/content/widgets/autocomplete-popup.js"], "git_node": "57066504cb5a1f50c71993d7173e956541b89ad1", "git_parents": ["ebf366412f2bd043316f1cf70d0af1f279584ced"], "node": "9711a41c236d7c31ca7e79003941eb8dfdc197b7", "parents": ["aa24a1a46c7132e0a4a48fb048c7c049348b21db"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Mehic \u003cdmehic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1713712 - Quality-of-life cleanups for the Eluminate and Google Analytics e-commerce shims r=webcompat-reviewers,twisniewski\n\nTwo of the small improvements asked for in comment 0, limited to changes that\ncannot alter what the shims do.\n\neluminate.js assigns nine properties to noopfn twice each:\ncmCreateManualImpressionTag, cmCreateManualLinkClickTag,\ncmCreateManualPageviewTag, cmCreatePageviewTag, cmSetClientID,\ncmSetCurrencyCode, cmSetFirstPartyIDs, cmSetupCookieMigration and\ncmSetupNormalization. It also assigns cmSetupOther to noopfn and then\noverwrites it a few lines later with a real implementation, so that first\nassignment never takes effect. Drop the redundant lines. The set of properties\nthe shim defines is unchanged; only the number of times each is assigned is.\n\ngoogle-analytics-ecommerce-plugin.js had no descriptive header. Add one in the\nsame style as the other shims, describing what the script is and why it is\nshimmed, with the bug number from shims.js.\n\nDeliberately not included:\n\n- The try/catch suggestion from comment 0. Shims run against arbitrary pages,\n  so changing which exceptions escape them is an observable behaviour change and\n  wants per-shim judgement rather than a sweep.\n- Wider modernisation of these files. Both already use const and arrow\n  functions, and rewriting further would add review surface without changing\n  behaviour.\n- Headers for the other shims that lack one. There are 18 of those, excluding\n  test fixtures, and each needs a description that says something useful rather\n  than restating the filename. That is worth its own bug, and would suit a new\n  contributor.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317288\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/webcompat/shims/eluminate.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/shims/google-analytics-ecommerce-plugin.js"], "git_node": "a36a55f99588e40b9a83e128d3392b622f3c4cf1", "git_parents": ["57066504cb5a1f50c71993d7173e956541b89ad1"], "node": "c5c416646cb494f1b1cb2169d03a43ce212335c4", "parents": ["9711a41c236d7c31ca7e79003941eb8dfdc197b7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Ritter \u003ctom@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054072 - Persist ETP Strict/Custom fingerprinting protection on Fenix r=timhuang,android-reviewers,gmalekpour\n\nFingerprinting protection is applied to the engine's default pref branch,\nwhich is not serialized to prefs.js. Unlike the tracking protection\npolicy - which is re-derived from the persisted ETP mode and re-applied\nthrough a single engine setter on both startup and runtime changes -\nfingerprinting protection would be set when the user edited their Settings\nbut never on startup (unless the Nimbus Feature was set.)\n\nCarry the fingerprinting-protection state on TrackingProtectionPolicy\n(strict = on/on, recommended = off/on, custom = the user's selection) and\napply it inside the GeckoEngine trackingProtectionPolicy setter, so it\nrides the same single application path as the rest of the policy for both\nengine creation and runtime policy updates. Remove the now-redundant\nruntime writer in TrackingProtectionFragment. The Nimbus rollout keeps\nowning the Standard default and the overrides at engine creation\nhowever this seems like it will still have a bug tracked in 2054143\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311582\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/engine-gecko/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/engine/gecko/GeckoEngine.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/concept/engine/src/main/java/mozilla/components/concept/engine/EngineSession.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/TrackingProtectionPolicyFactory.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/TrackingProtectionFragment.kt"], "git_node": "2b8f1313764053ef01030f0d0bbdd3abf9b24bbb", "git_parents": ["a36a55f99588e40b9a83e128d3392b622f3c4cf1"], "node": "80358e1ddba0aefaea91b54b4627ed44722d63a9", "parents": ["c5c416646cb494f1b1cb2169d03a43ce212335c4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Ritter \u003ctom@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054072 - Test fingerprinting protection carried by the tracking protection policy r=timhuang,android-reviewers,gmalekpour\n\nCover the policy carrying the expected fingerprinting protection\n(EngineSessionTest), the GeckoEngine trackingProtectionPolicy setter\napplying it to the runtime and leaving the pref untouched when it is\nunspecified (GeckoEngineTest), and the Fenix factory propagating it for\nstrict/standard/custom (TrackingProtectionPolicyFactoryTest).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311633\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/engine-gecko/src/test/java/mozilla/components/browser/engine/gecko/GeckoEngineTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/concept/engine/src/test/java/mozilla/components/concept/engine/EngineSessionTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/TrackingProtectionPolicyFactoryTest.kt"], "git_node": "e5f9c613f5009c62ac173165a32940d265584bf4", "git_parents": ["2b8f1313764053ef01030f0d0bbdd3abf9b24bbb"], "node": "202ec665f28a0681064c00ae9767d264a6802f7c", "parents": ["80358e1ddba0aefaea91b54b4627ed44722d63a9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nico Burns \u003cnico@nicoburns.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068247 - Enable `scroll-behavior` and `overscroll-behavior` properties on Servo. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis imports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/420\n\n\u003e A couple more keyword/bitflag properties that I'm implementing in Blitz,\n\u003e and would like to enable behind the `layout.unimplemented` pref.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322769\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/properties/shorthands.toml"], "git_node": "d4629cc172f27ac47d2b944074afe07e9c799057", "git_parents": ["e5f9c613f5009c62ac173165a32940d265584bf4"], "node": "624f8c476e373ca4b53543a22886dad42fb9a91e", "parents": ["202ec665f28a0681064c00ae9767d264a6802f7c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon W\u00fclker \u003csimon.wuelker@arcor.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068247 - Implement iterator over all known non-custom properties. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis imports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/406\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322770\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/properties/mod.rs"], "git_node": "588b6800d53e42046c0bd9df5e5d9da223bd835d", "git_parents": ["d4629cc172f27ac47d2b944074afe07e9c799057"], "node": "ad493e0a6e4430ee3c868c86e6964b4fc4cbbe03", "parents": ["624f8c476e373ca4b53543a22886dad42fb9a91e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Psychpsyo (Cameron) \u003c60073468+Psychpsyo@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068247 - Enable box-decoration-break for Servo. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis imports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/386\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322771\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml"], "git_node": "1c098b7a7aff1c166c536306d350221ea360c751", "git_parents": ["588b6800d53e42046c0bd9df5e5d9da223bd835d"], "node": "1bf82a761b2db08cfdbd47ac3fd0011dcd9d99d5", "parents": ["ad493e0a6e4430ee3c868c86e6964b4fc4cbbe03"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mohamed Mostafa \u003cmu.mostafa98@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068247 - Enable basic SVG-related CSS properties for Servo. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis imports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/383\n\nRemoves `engine = \"gecko\"` from 11 SVG-specific CSS properties to be\nenabled for servo:\n\n- **Fill (3):** `fill`, `fill-opacity`, `fill-rule`\n- **Stroke (8):** `stroke`, `stroke-width`, `stroke-linecap`,\n`stroke-linejoin`, `stroke-dasharray`, `stroke-dashoffset`,\n`stroke-miterlimit`, `stroke-opacity`\n\nAlso updates the `ComputedValues` size test (224 \u2192 232) for the new\nfields.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322772\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/properties/properties.mako.rs"], "git_node": "5182e0bfd80e41762db2cc06055b6bba5c5bb0c9", "git_parents": ["1c098b7a7aff1c166c536306d350221ea360c751"], "node": "0d1bb8bd67449a4b013fe332aad8900fd0ebf153", "parents": ["1bf82a761b2db08cfdbd47ac3fd0011dcd9d99d5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mohamed Mostafa \u003cmu.mostafa98@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068247 - Enable SVG geometric properties for Servo. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis imports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/427\n\nRemoves `engine = \"gecko\"` from 8 SVG-geometric properties to be enabled\nfor servo:\n\n- `x`\n- `y`\n- `cx`\n- `cy`\n- `rx`\n- `ry`\n- `r`\n- `d`\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322773\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml"], "git_node": "f59d5f0cf15b09f3554122ecea8ebadd7fb8c5bf", "git_parents": ["5182e0bfd80e41762db2cc06055b6bba5c5bb0c9"], "node": "5b83c23a6ad8617d8486b7c49739387e4b7d7efe", "parents": ["0d1bb8bd67449a4b013fe332aad8900fd0ebf153"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon W\u00fclker \u003csimon.wuelker@arcor.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068247 - Support `font-variant-alternates` and `@font-feature-values` for servo. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis imports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/377, with some tweak\ndue to changes from https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315884\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322774\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/properties/shorthands.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/shorthands.toml", "servo/components/style/stylesheets/font_feature_values_rule.rs", "servo/components/style/stylesheets/rule_parser.rs", "servo/components/style/values/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/font.rs"], "git_node": "3115c57b1f416102225e0ae9588c1d30b4c5d570", "git_parents": ["f59d5f0cf15b09f3554122ecea8ebadd7fb8c5bf"], "node": "fa3bea60387f40026227f3e0c8c30a6e443f02ac", "parents": ["5b83c23a6ad8617d8486b7c49739387e4b7d7efe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon W\u00fclker \u003csimon.wuelker@arcor.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068247 - Enable font-language-override for servo. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis imports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/429\n\nOddly enough the longhand itself was already enabled, so just taking\ncare of it in the `font` shorthand.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322775\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/properties/shorthands.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/shorthands.toml"], "git_node": "cc1ccfde3c02638752d45b5392b9559fcf3b3f11", "git_parents": ["3115c57b1f416102225e0ae9588c1d30b4c5d570"], "node": "5865e4fb4cbf277df034dc5716bd92225a9b9ea5", "parents": ["fa3bea60387f40026227f3e0c8c30a6e443f02ac"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Robinson \u003cmrobinson@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068247 - Also update `AnimationState::Paused` in `Animation::update_from_other` if delay changes. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis imports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/422\n\nIf the delay in an animation changes, we still might need to update the\n`Paused` state if the animation is moving from `Playing` to `Paused`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322776\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/servo/animation.rs"], "git_node": "b037b8d6446fbcf3dea4ad1b6052dda1e8054d6d", "git_parents": ["cc1ccfde3c02638752d45b5392b9559fcf3b3f11"], "node": "8b5c6dc5f5bcc8402e4e05f273a00705d9bc6ac2", "parents": ["5865e4fb4cbf277df034dc5716bd92225a9b9ea5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nico Burns \u003cnico@nicoburns.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068247 - Enable text-decoration-thickness; more text decoration properties for Blitz. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis imports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/426\n\nEnables `text-decoration-thickness`, `text-decoration-inset`,\n`text-underline-offset`, and `text-underline-position` for Servo builds\nof Stylo, behind the `layout.unimplemented` feature flag.\n\nThe shorthand `text-decoration` is updated to account for\n`text-decoration-thickness` being enabled (this aligns Servo's\nimplementation with Gecko's for this property).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322777\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/properties/shorthands.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/shorthands.toml"], "git_node": "a1d36e82f9eefc2092dcf8f3ea663490cc2959de", "git_parents": ["b037b8d6446fbcf3dea4ad1b6052dda1e8054d6d"], "node": "c635d63d294adaac1fe7a530d3f4214f9d066a65", "parents": ["8b5c6dc5f5bcc8402e4e05f273a00705d9bc6ac2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Sapin \u003csimon@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068247 - Change repr of Servo enum PseudoElement from usize to u8. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis imports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/437\n\nEvery fragment in the fragment tree stores:\n\n```rust\npub struct PseudoElementChain {\n    pub primary: Option\u003cPseudoElement\u003e,\n    pub secondary: Option\u003cPseudoElement\u003e,\n}\n```\n\n\u2026 so this change reduces memory use slightly\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322778\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/servo/selector_parser.rs"], "git_node": "4f6f8984f80bb1856443954670d8ab62349d4b2f", "git_parents": ["a1d36e82f9eefc2092dcf8f3ea663490cc2959de"], "node": "31074eb309c3ba7b77afd155bbb953f5d0fe82a3", "parents": ["c635d63d294adaac1fe7a530d3f4214f9d066a65"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Sapin \u003csimon@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068247 - Fix Stylo's unit tests for Servo. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis imports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/436\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322779\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/selector_parser.rs", "servo/components/style/servo/shadow_parts.rs"], "git_node": "967618ef4326880112f1f2fc6911617bdb12ddd5", "git_parents": ["4f6f8984f80bb1856443954670d8ab62349d4b2f"], "node": "11be714e57fa6075900939381c5d65204913ad9e", "parents": ["31074eb309c3ba7b77afd155bbb953f5d0fe82a3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tim van der Lippe \u003cTimvdLippe@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068247 - Support color-scheme in Servo. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis imports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/438\n\nWith these changes, both the `color-scheme` CSS property is supported,\nas well as the required logic to act upon it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322780\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/device/servo.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml"], "git_node": "b0fd255195354d9ec49c523ee5b581d8a69a9b15", "git_parents": ["967618ef4326880112f1f2fc6911617bdb12ddd5"], "node": "773abf7bea8fa3f5abeffdc62a66623e9e3dff36", "parents": ["11be714e57fa6075900939381c5d65204913ad9e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Sapin \u003csimon@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068247 - Enable `text-transform: math-auto` for Servo. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis imports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/442\n\nHowever, it has been modified to keep `math-auto` as a case transform.\nThat's because Gecko expects to get it when doing a bitwise AND with\nStyleTextTransform::CASE_TRANSFORMS.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322781\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/values/specified/text.rs"], "git_node": "dd1823bc9cce91c20ccb693ac216b6d349947828", "git_parents": ["b0fd255195354d9ec49c523ee5b581d8a69a9b15"], "node": "75e1b6381f52ef2d29c4b47f7d876832ba0ebdca", "parents": ["773abf7bea8fa3f5abeffdc62a66623e9e3dff36"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Josh Matthews \u003cjosh@joshmatthews.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068247 - Adjust Servo's restyle damage for clip-path. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nImports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/444\n\nclip-path's calculations in servo occur while building the stacking\ncontext. If the value changes, we need to rebuild the stacking context.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322782\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml"], "git_node": "abca82b793a784475a150f8f433f572094b895cc", "git_parents": ["dd1823bc9cce91c20ccb693ac216b6d349947828"], "node": "4605d82b7fa596169fd1bca1b9170afac0acb6df", "parents": ["75e1b6381f52ef2d29c4b47f7d876832ba0ebdca"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nico Burns \u003cnico@nicoburns.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068247 - Implement `animation-composition` for Servo. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis imports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/445\n\nChanges made:\n- Implement the `animation-composition` CSS property.\n- Shares animation matrix decomposition logic with Gecko (fixes a couple\nof regressions due to the Servo version of the code not rejecting\nmatrices with a zero determinant)\n\nImplementation is entirely in Stylo.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322783\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/properties/properties.mako.rs", "servo/components/style/servo/animation.rs", "servo/components/style/values/animated/transform.rs"], "git_node": "f984fb69a0fbe10c1b84b00e18266229c3ca7d29", "git_parents": ["abca82b793a784475a150f8f433f572094b895cc"], "node": "5e8f37ac84670be78dc56302d169d0060190816a", "parents": ["4605d82b7fa596169fd1bca1b9170afac0acb6df"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nico Burns \u003cnico@nicoburns.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068247 - Add prefs for `:has()` and `:nth-child(An+B of S)` selector parsing in Servo. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis imports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/447\n\nServo-only change. Gecko already unconditionally parses these selectors.\n\nThis allows support for these features to be implemented in a pref-gated\nway in Servo and Blitz\n(and for those engines to differ as to which they have enabled).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322784\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/servo/selector_parser.rs"], "git_node": "c072c9cef99b9b31e165286406b8d7dfa7fa15eb", "git_parents": ["f984fb69a0fbe10c1b84b00e18266229c3ca7d29"], "node": "f6426a83674f3cbcd2fdd0c7a9674bb624ef8fea", "parents": ["5e8f37ac84670be78dc56302d169d0060190816a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Euclid Ye \u003ceuclid.ye@huawei.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068247 - Enable `touch-action` on Servo. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis imports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/439\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322785\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml"], "git_node": "a9a7d1bceb331fd7aa0503fa78392d125a20cef0", "git_parents": ["c072c9cef99b9b31e165286406b8d7dfa7fa15eb"], "node": "9ffe49939c2a859a65f2f263d11333f05c70fd89", "parents": ["f6426a83674f3cbcd2fdd0c7a9674bb624ef8fea"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068247 - Some tweaks so that Servo compiles. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nSince https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313759, `font-optical-sizing`\nand `font-variation-settings` are no longer gated by a pref in Gecko.\n\nHowever, they are still behind a pref in Servo. So the logic needs to handle\nan Option for Servo.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322786\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/properties/shorthands.rs"], "git_node": "cfd5bb202bcaec6750bf3083c0619d05c005404f", "git_parents": ["a9a7d1bceb331fd7aa0503fa78392d125a20cef0"], "node": "c879704855f467f076878f3aec1cfafe690d1f23", "parents": ["9ffe49939c2a859a65f2f263d11333f05c70fd89"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068247 - Introduce a way to check prefs that only exist in Gecko or Servo. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nD313757 and D313761 removed some preferences in Gecko, thus enabling\nsome features unconditionally. The problem is that Servo had these prefs\ndisabled, so we should continue to check the prefs for Servo.\n\nTo make it easier, this introduces a macro for prefs that only exist in\none engine. For example,\n\n    crate::pref!(\"layout.css.font-tech.enabled\", gecko = true)\n\nresolves to true in Gecko, but in Servo it checks the pref.\n\nIt can also be used with a single argument, e.g. these are the same:\n\n    crate::pref!(\"layout.css.font-tech.enabled\")\n    static_prefs::pref!(\"layout.css.font-tech.enabled\")\n\nFor consistency, I have replaced static_prefs::pref with crate::pref.\n\nI'm also removing some conditional compilation that would only check\n`static_prefs::pref!()` on Gecko, since it's fine to just introduce the\npref to Servo.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322787\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/color/parsing.rs", "servo/components/style/driver.rs", "servo/components/style/font_face.rs", "servo/components/style/gecko/media_features.rs", "servo/components/style/gecko/pseudo_element.rs", "servo/components/style/gecko/selector_parser.rs", "servo/components/style/gecko/wrapper.rs", "servo/components/style/global_style_data.rs", "servo/components/style/lib.rs", "servo/components/style/parallel.rs", "servo/components/style/prefs.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/cascade.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/helpers/animated_properties.mako.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/properties.mako.rs", "servo/components/style/queries/condition.rs", "servo/components/style/queries/feature_expression.rs", "servo/components/style/servo/selector_parser.rs", "servo/components/style/stylesheets/keyframes_rule.rs", "servo/components/style/stylesheets/rule_parser.rs", "servo/components/style/stylesheets/supports_rule.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/font.rs", "servo/components/style/values/generics/animation.rs", "servo/components/style/values/generics/box.rs", "servo/components/style/values/generics/calc.rs", "servo/components/style/values/generics/length.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/animation.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/background.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/basic_shape.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/border.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/box.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/calc.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/color.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/grid.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/image.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/length.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/motion.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/position.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/svg.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/text.rs"], "git_node": "0ae05a079e69cad519d514f8727e11070d11bfbb", "git_parents": ["cfd5bb202bcaec6750bf3083c0619d05c005404f"], "node": "cfd59ad878ebe056f39e4cf40b132ca769d40271", "parents": ["c879704855f467f076878f3aec1cfafe690d1f23"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris Martin \u003cmarti4d@live.ca\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068333 - Restore minidump-writer behavior of ignoring fpregs errors r=supply-chain-reviewers,afranchuk,tcampbell\n\nIn Isolated Processes #2, I accidentally changed the behavior of floating-\npoint register reading to return a hard error on failure instead of ignoring\nthe error and simply returning the default value.\n\nThis has blocked all minidump generation on ARM on older Linux Kernels that\ndon't support the new PTRACE_GETREGSET APIs.\n\nThis hotfix simply restores the previous behavior.\n\nLink to bug-introducing diff: https://github.com/rust-minidump/minidump-writer/pull/175/changes#diff-a3ec3f7ac451b5fb1ad7c5f5f28898d16b06d36c94936bcbf5257180edb3b37cL60\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323003\n", "files": [".cargo/config.toml.in", "Cargo.lock", "supply-chain/audits.toml", "supply-chain/config.toml", "third_party/rust/minidump-writer/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/minidump-writer/src/linux/thread_info/arm.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_client/Cargo.toml", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/Cargo.toml", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_server/Cargo.toml", "toolkit/crashreporter/rust_minidump_writer_linux/Cargo.toml"], "git_node": "f44de7009a49c262aaa7e955d13e37b205ad8ac5", "git_parents": ["0ae05a079e69cad519d514f8727e11070d11bfbb"], "node": "429338b23d648b205ab181651d690c73adfa914e", "parents": ["cfd59ad878ebe056f39e4cf40b132ca769d40271"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067079 - Don't throw from takeMeasurements() when there is no default backup directory, r=sthompson.\n\nDEFAULT_PARENT_DIR_PATH returns \"\" when neither a OneDrive nor a Documents\nfolder resolves. takeMeasurements() passed that to PathUtils.join, which throws,\nso nothing after location_on_device was measured on such a machine. Every other\nconsumer of DEFAULT_PARENT_DIR_PATH already guards the empty value; this was the\nlast one that did not.\n\nThe call is fire-and-forget from onIdle(), so the throw surfaced as an uncaught\nrejection charged to whatever code was running when the idle callback fired,\nwhich made `mach mochitest --verify` fail tree-wide.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321926\n", "files": ["browser/components/backup/BackupService.sys.mjs", "browser/components/backup/metrics.yaml", "browser/components/backup/tests/xpcshell/test_BackupService_takeMeasurements.js"], "git_node": "ea2a4ec3d1021d0d12f519d62f667c5b271b535c", "git_parents": ["f44de7009a49c262aaa7e955d13e37b205ad8ac5"], "node": "0bd927c925bed5f79e1edeac0cdb068ceeac450e", "parents": ["429338b23d648b205ab181651d690c73adfa914e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2002602 - Don't depend on the machine's Documents folder in browser_settings_turn_on_scheduled_backups.js, r=sthompson.\n\nSince c89eda214d99, confirming the dialog only dispatches\nBackupUI:EnableScheduledBackups if a real IOUtils.getChildren() on the default\nbackup directory succeeds, and that directory is the machine's Documents\nfolder. On the macOS workers that cannot list it,\ntest_enable_fails_without_backup_dir - the one task here that does not stub\nprobeDefaultDirAccess - never sees the event and times out.\n\nPoint the default backup location at a directory the test creates, so that no\ntask depends on what the machine happens to have.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321927\n", "files": ["browser/components/backup/tests/browser/browser_settings_turn_on_scheduled_backups.js"], "git_node": "56f3be03a8201e3e784e40deeac0b096d1767273", "git_parents": ["ea2a4ec3d1021d0d12f519d62f667c5b271b535c"], "node": "8db9fd2bbf3bee35b87c13611202fd7fddf76c67", "parents": ["0bd927c925bed5f79e1edeac0cdb068ceeac450e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067137 - Don't depend on the machine's Documents folder in browser_settings_create_backup.js, r=sthompson.\n\nDEFAULT_PARENT_DIR_PATH is \"\" when neither a OneDrive nor a Documents folder\nresolves, which on Linux is the case whenever XDG user directories are\nunconfigured, and the second half of test_no_default_folder then calls\nPathUtils.filename(\"\") and throws.\n\nPoint the default backup location at a directory the test creates, the same way\nbug 2002602 does for browser_settings_turn_on_scheduled_backups.js.\ndocsDirFolderPath is stubbed where the task restores its own stub rather than in\nadd_setup, because stubbing it twice on the same object throws.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321928\n", "files": ["browser/components/backup/tests/browser/browser_settings_create_backup.js"], "git_node": "c16b93e2bbec2cedc2533ea6b9fa09a7432c06a3", "git_parents": ["56f3be03a8201e3e784e40deeac0b096d1767273"], "node": "62066e48b4b2da2b21f520664ed2e3aebd4ec2b6", "parents": ["8db9fd2bbf3bee35b87c13611202fd7fddf76c67"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067120 - Handle null operands in Assert's numeric comparisons, r=Standard8.\n\ncompareNumbers() dereferenced its operands to test for a Date, so Assert.greater(null, 0)\nthrew a TypeError out of the assertion helper instead of failing with a message naming the\nvalue. Operands created with Object.create(null) threw the same way.\n\nAssert is used by essentially every test in the tree, so this changes the shape of any\nexisting failure with a null operand. Under browser-chrome, where the reporter is\noverridden and report() records rather than throws, such a test now gets one clean\nassertion failure and still runs its cleanup, instead of an aborted task.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321929\n", "files": ["testing/modules/Assert.sys.mjs", "testing/modules/tests/xpcshell/test_assert.js"], "git_node": "6cc460abc05f76dde3987c083df5cdb0aae9afa3", "git_parents": ["c16b93e2bbec2cedc2533ea6b9fa09a7432c06a3"], "node": "2f90a9e6449f24c56b313aca7e209cac1d9d3f2f", "parents": ["62066e48b4b2da2b21f520664ed2e3aebd4ec2b6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067119 - Give the startup timeline test its own manifest, r=sthompson,chutten.\n\nsession_restore.startup_timeline is recorded once while the browser starts and cannot be\nrecorded again, so a test reading it depends on no other test in its manifest having called\nServices.fog.testResetFOG(): browser-chrome gives one browser to a whole manifest.\nbrowser_bfcache_telemetry.js legitimately resets, which is why this assertion, parked in\nbrowser_reopen_all_windows.js by bug 1972836, read null and left that test permanently\nintermittent. Asking the neighbours not to reset would keep the dependency working but leave\nit invisible from the tests that have to respect it.\n\nThe FOG testing docs recommend testResetFOG without mentioning any of this, so they now say\nthat a test reading a startup metric needs a manifest of its own, and point at this one.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321930\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/moz.build", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_reopen_all_windows.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_startup_telemetry.toml", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_startup_timeline_telemetry.js", "toolkit/components/glean/docs/user/instrumentation_tests.md"], "git_node": "c40ba6af478d855316545e856928530d10f905a1", "git_parents": ["6cc460abc05f76dde3987c083df5cdb0aae9afa3"], "node": "6ec15847f7dfefa35556014509f0527635849e9a", "parents": ["2f90a9e6449f24c56b313aca7e209cac1d9d3f2f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067553 - Re-anchor downgrade-mangling-error_clang_23.patch on stable context. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nUpstream keeps appending to the err_unsupported_itanium_mangling %enum_select list the hunk was anchored\non; anchor it on the one-off definitions after it instead. The applied result is unchanged.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323045\n", "files": ["build/build-clang/downgrade-mangling-error_clang_23.patch"], "git_node": "d61a0a52e945057dbf6b48d28814baea231da4b6", "git_parents": ["c40ba6af478d855316545e856928530d10f905a1"], "node": "5152a3ad99626159f2b2ed1a138dccca00fa69eb", "parents": ["6ec15847f7dfefa35556014509f0527635849e9a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Reem H \u003c42309026+reemhamz@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068409 - Remove dead CSS from weather widget. r=nina-py\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322823\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Weather/_Weather.scss"], "git_node": "dcb4ae31b0bd95dc6549ef99a0c75f033873d6e2", "git_parents": ["d61a0a52e945057dbf6b48d28814baea231da4b6"], "node": "133b9afdde01763a34678a0a291ebf6a231b5354", "parents": ["5152a3ad99626159f2b2ed1a138dccca00fa69eb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Zoya \u003czfatima@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066542 - Extract article text & language in feature module r=android-reviewers,matt-tighe\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322447\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ListenAction.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ListenMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ListenReducer.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/content/ContentProvider.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/content/PageContentExtractor.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/content/PageMetadataExtractor.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ListenMiddlewareTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/content/ContentProviderTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/readerview/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/readerview/ReaderViewFeature.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/readerview/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/readerview/ReaderViewFeatureTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/BrowserFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/Components.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/FenixListenPageExtractor.kt"], "git_node": "3ff08531a37f63585b4c1ce889bb667268fbe865", "git_parents": ["dcb4ae31b0bd95dc6549ef99a0c75f033873d6e2"], "node": "50b30b28eee5679e0742f897d1ebf6e9ea0384f9", "parents": ["133b9afdde01763a34678a0a291ebf6a231b5354"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Raul Salvat \u003crootzero.brain@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066877 - Report and ignore null messages in L10nCache. r=adw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323019\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/L10nCache.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/test_l10nCache.js"], "git_node": "ea0563a508aed4715f913012b3acc6c5e2560f7f", "git_parents": ["3ff08531a37f63585b4c1ce889bb667268fbe865"], "node": "c57e8a70d96bbb6f9333949cc68cb935e449e4e6", "parents": ["50b30b28eee5679e0742f897d1ebf6e9ea0384f9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Erik Nordin \u003cenordin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063863 - Improve TranslationsEngine port lifetime management r=translations-reviewers,gregtatum\n\nThis commit fixes TranslationsEngine port lifetime management by\ntracking each port independently and notifying its client when the\nassociated language-pair engine is destroyed.\n\nIt also adds test-only control over the engine timeout and regression\ncoverage for multiple clients and independently cached engines.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317556\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/translations/actors/TranslationsEngineChild.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/translations/actors/TranslationsEngineParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/translations/content/Translator.mjs", "toolkit/components/translations/content/translations-engine.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/translations/tests/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_engine_lifetime.js", "toolkit/components/translations/tests/browser/shared-head.js", "toolkit/components/translations/translations.d.ts"], "git_node": "7fb58365a54be84c90b83e7252818329b0636b8b", "git_parents": ["ea0563a508aed4715f913012b3acc6c5e2560f7f"], "node": "3c4c0a51728b7dd110dd337ea4a8f48b054d8d61", "parents": ["c57e8a70d96bbb6f9333949cc68cb935e449e4e6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Erik Nordin \u003cenordin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067578 - Add Full-Page TranslationsEngine lifetime regression coverage r=translations-reviewers,gregtatum\n\nThis commit adds Full-Page Translations regression coverage to ensure\nthat newly intersecting and modified content continues to translate\nafter an engine timeouts.\n\nThe tests cover recreating the inference process as well as recreating\nonly the engine while the process is kept alive by another actor.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322759\n", "files": ["browser/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_full.toml", "browser/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_full_page_intersection_engine_timeout.js", "browser/components/translations/tests/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "6e46a88dbd66f8f0d912d44bbffb622659a82d6f", "git_parents": ["7fb58365a54be84c90b83e7252818329b0636b8b"], "node": "e09a9b02c7edf5632fee89c52b2b2f3f2009fde6", "parents": ["3c4c0a51728b7dd110dd337ea4a8f48b054d8d61"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Erik Nordin \u003cenordin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063863 - Add about:translations engine lifetime regression coverage r=translations-reviewers,gregtatum\n\nThis commit expands the about:translations engine-destruction test to\ncover idle timeouts. It ensures that about:translations can acquire a\nnew port and continue translating after its engine is destroyed.\n\nThe tests cover recreating the inference process as well as recreating\nonly the engine while the process is kept alive by another actor.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322760\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_about_translations_engine_destroy.js", "toolkit/components/translations/tests/browser/shared-head.js"], "git_node": "497fd87ccebc833be91675504864af92b69deb40", "git_parents": ["6e46a88dbd66f8f0d912d44bbffb622659a82d6f"], "node": "27393752d9fac7965c1bf1b870eeb9f68915235c", "parents": ["e09a9b02c7edf5632fee89c52b2b2f3f2009fde6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Erik Nordin \u003cenordin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063863 - Release SelectTranslations ports after each request r=translations-reviewers,gregtatum\n\nThis commit ensures that Select Translations releases each short-lived\nTranslator and its port after a translation request completes.\n\nThe tests cover recreating the inference process as well as recreating\nonly the engine while the process is kept alive by another actor.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322761\n", "files": ["browser/components/translations/content/selectTranslationsPanel.js", "browser/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_select_panel_engine_cache.js", "browser/components/translations/tests/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "819276e09143cb228686ea27b8d37df470c5948d", "git_parents": ["497fd87ccebc833be91675504864af92b69deb40"], "node": "40c9dc37e0b0598760d4ed14c34475c995e7a96f", "parents": ["27393752d9fac7965c1bf1b870eeb9f68915235c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Omar Gonzalez \u003cs9tpepper@apache.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059870 - add batch concurrency limit for generate values requests r=mshillabeer\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322821\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/SmartFormFillModel.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_smart_form_fill_model.js"], "git_node": "51f84738b8bcfe4e7e349887855b16ab309dbe8b", "git_parents": ["819276e09143cb228686ea27b8d37df470c5948d"], "node": "5ce48e243e3ef7a9f1dcf4d15a33513e117546f2", "parents": ["40c9dc37e0b0598760d4ed14c34475c995e7a96f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Roger Yang \u003croyang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068155 - Remove redundant VPN location switch requested on every country list update. r=android-reviewers,mavduevskiy\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322791\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/ipprotection/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/ipprotection/store/IPProtectionLocationMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/ipprotection/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/ipprotection/store/IPProtectionLocationMiddlewareTest.kt"], "git_node": "87f8297247621d7ea51de4e3637c9008c7ad5b67", "git_parents": ["51f84738b8bcfe4e7e349887855b16ab309dbe8b"], "node": "b0ee611081f0a0ea9b3fb72685c71c996540fdda", "parents": ["5ce48e243e3ef7a9f1dcf4d15a33513e117546f2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065120 - [efficiency] Harden efficiency test lifecycle and state isolation. r=aaronmt\n\nDirect-fleet execution cannot rely on Android Test Orchestrator to clear\nstate, and the inherited rule ordering previously hid what arrived dirty.\n\nCapture arrival before legacy setup, enforce named cleanup boundaries for\napp, activity, input, and runtime state, and retain lifecycle evidence when\nthe body or cleanup fails. Add contracts for per-test page and registry\nlifecycle so shared-process execution cannot silently reuse stale context.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321635\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/devtools/PageContextLifecycleTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/ActivityLifecycleTrace.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/ActivityStateCleaner.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/AppDataCleaner.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/BaseTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/InputStateCleaner.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/RuntimeStateCleaner.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/StateProbe.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/logging/log-format.json", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/NavigationRegistry.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tools/StateLeakDemoTest.kt"], "git_node": "3a74cc6be39af3a3a3f940d617eb32b0146ba82b", "git_parents": ["87f8297247621d7ea51de4e3637c9008c7ad5b67"], "node": "d2806e9e8706b075cf24731e70083e4ab25b9ab5", "parents": ["b0ee611081f0a0ea9b3fb72685c71c996540fdda"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065120 - [efficiency] Harden efficiency navigation graph registration. r=aaronmt\n\nPage construction registered duplicate and misplaced navigation edges,\nmaking graph shape depend on construction order and hiding invalid routes.\n\nMove transitions to their source owners, remove duplicate registrations,\nand make registry reset part of the test lifecycle. Characterize the graph\nwith a contract test that rejects dangling, duplicated, and unstable edges.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321636\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/devtools/NavigationGraphContractTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/NavigationRegistry.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/BrowserPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/HomePage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/MainMenuPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsAddonsManagerPage.kt"], "git_node": "67f46e65941027a67bed696e8f0b4bda04f5c3fb", "git_parents": ["3a74cc6be39af3a3a3f940d617eb32b0146ba82b"], "node": "0eaf942239cd164602e294f8784710c5a17bf6a2", "parents": ["d2806e9e8706b075cf24731e70083e4ab25b9ab5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065120 - [efficiency] Introduce versioned state capture contributors. r=aaronmt\n\nThe state probe exposed one unversioned map, so consumers could not identify\nfield ownership, capture cost, sensitivity, or compatible schema changes.\n\nSplit state capture into named, versioned contributors with deterministic\nmetadata while preserving the compatibility projection. Add contract\ncoverage for contributor identity, fields, and schema stability.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321637\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/devtools/StateContributorContractTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/StateContributor.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/StateProbe.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/logging/log-format.json"], "git_node": "d5e12368c31c658f713c1dad3bcc8987806dc7b7", "git_parents": ["67f46e65941027a67bed696e8f0b4bda04f5c3fb"], "node": "95bc56d7829f48f5b9b21517ba1f5a71cf8d58af", "parents": ["0eaf942239cd164602e294f8784710c5a17bf6a2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065120 - [efficiency] Enforce permission and session state isolation. r=aaronmt\n\nSite-permission and saved-session data could survive a test boundary without\nbeing represented in the isolation verdict.\n\nAdd both resources to state observation and cleanup enforcement so inherited\nor leaked values fail the boundary explicitly instead of contaminating the\nnext test.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321638\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/AppDataCleaner.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/StateProbe.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/logging/log-format.json"], "git_node": "b74498ca3b70e5b3273dcad8f334f55c9c5d0318", "git_parents": ["d5e12368c31c658f713c1dad3bcc8987806dc7b7"], "node": "3137a3b376162d2f0c622fb40aac349d5264d5dc", "parents": ["95bc56d7829f48f5b9b21517ba1f5a71cf8d58af"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065120 - [efficiency] Add typed search state observations. r=aaronmt\n\nSearch-engine configuration spans the browser store and the app-level\ntemporary selection, but neither was represented by a typed contributor.\n\nPublish typed observations for default, private, custom, hidden, disabled,\nadditional, and temporary engine state. Keep these diagnostic identities out\nof the legacy flat compatibility projection while exposing their completeness\nand contributor metadata to structured consumers.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321639\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/devtools/StateContributorContractTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/StateContributor.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/StateProbe.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/logging/log-format.json"], "git_node": "69128abab8ae1d996a4da4cba35db4f32e08e250", "git_parents": ["b74498ca3b70e5b3273dcad8f334f55c9c5d0318"], "node": "6a6680b27b784681bff8a2cdfe69c47a10400790", "parents": ["3137a3b376162d2f0c622fb40aac349d5264d5dc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065120 - [efficiency] Enforce tab organization state isolation. r=aaronmt\n\nTab groups, assignments, recently closed tabs, and recoverable-tab state can\noutlive visible tabs and influence later homepage and navigation behavior.\n\nObserve these stores, clear them through their owning APIs, and require the\ndeclared empty baseline after cleanup. This makes hidden tab organization\nstate part of the same boundary verdict as ordinary tabs.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321640\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/AppDataCleaner.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/StateProbe.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/logging/log-format.json"], "git_node": "b4af395fbedbc382ec4e312209518f9adc831cd2", "git_parents": ["69128abab8ae1d996a4da4cba35db4f32e08e250"], "node": "200266c133aef79b438048d7181fe9799fdeeafe", "parents": ["6a6680b27b784681bff8a2cdfe69c47a10400790"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065120 - [efficiency] Enforce test preference state isolation. r=aaronmt\n\nEfficiency tests can override launch and feature preferences that remain in\nshared storage after the test body finishes.\n\nIntroduce a catalog of harness-owned preference overrides, report their\nstable identities, and clear them at test boundaries. Keep launch defaults\nseparate from test-authored overrides so cleanup does not erase product\nconfiguration indiscriminately.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321641\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/devtools/StateContributorContractTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/AppDataCleaner.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/BaseTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/HarnessPreferenceState.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/StateProbe.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/logging/log-format.json"], "git_node": "b674fa2efdf486b4cbae50694c72003d8594e23d", "git_parents": ["b4af395fbedbc382ec4e312209518f9adc831cd2"], "node": "969987128d123bcf99a2cbfbeed0b72152ad2cd5", "parents": ["200266c133aef79b438048d7181fe9799fdeeafe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065120 - [efficiency] Publish state boundary control contracts. r=aaronmt\n\nA captured field did not state whether the harness merely observed it or was\nresponsible for restoring and enforcing a baseline.\n\nPublish boundary policy, baseline, and control-driver metadata with each\ncontributor. Use those declarations to build isolation verdicts and give\nconsumers one machine-readable explanation of controlled and residual state.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321642\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/devtools/StateContributorContractTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/StateContributor.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/StateProbe.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/logging/log-format.json"], "git_node": "eadf00a1de3e3860350e866d1636b532507c7f25", "git_parents": ["b674fa2efdf486b4cbae50694c72003d8594e23d"], "node": "7c643fffa6c7feb6023712a9a09537ca38acc200", "parents": ["969987128d123bcf99a2cbfbeed0b72152ad2cd5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065120 - [efficiency] Enforce persistent search state isolation. r=aaronmt\n\nResetting transient search state alone leaves selected engines, custom\nengines, shortcut changes, and metadata overrides in durable storage.\n\nAdd a search-state owner that observes both runtime and persisted layers,\nrestores the regional/default relationships, and verifies the resulting\nbaseline. Expose the minimal production seam needed to perform that reset.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321643\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/devtools/StateContributorContractTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/AppDataCleaner.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/HarnessSearchState.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/StateProbe.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/Core.kt"], "git_node": "f1ae0e3951892c513414e41fb0bb9802baad0461", "git_parents": ["eadf00a1de3e3860350e866d1636b532507c7f25"], "node": "fcb6b8ade2641160c79474dbd75de6140555c89c", "parents": ["7c643fffa6c7feb6023712a9a09537ca38acc200"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065120 - [efficiency] Add typed efficiency event envelopes. r=aaronmt\n\nExisting structured records lacked stable run, shard, test, and attempt\nidentity, which made retries and distributed execution difficult to separate.\n\nAdd a versioned event envelope with dispatcher-provided identity, per-attempt\nidentity, ordered sequence numbers, and wall and monotonic timestamps. Retain\nlegacy fields while consumers migrate, and cover the schema with contracts.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321644\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/logging/EventEnvelope.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/logging/EventEnvelopeContractTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/logging/JsonSink.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/logging/LoggingBridge.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/logging/log-format.json"], "git_node": "875c905272ab4ba3e68394d6e2b11428ad1f1250", "git_parents": ["f1ae0e3951892c513414e41fb0bb9802baad0461"], "node": "8fc7ffb11d71500f5a4ec2724bda9b86f6c5d0e0", "parents": ["fcb6b8ade2641160c79474dbd75de6140555c89c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065120 - [efficiency] Finalize attempts after cleanup. r=aaronmt\n\nA passing test body could be reported before cleanup and legacy teardown\ncompleted, allowing a failed or interrupted boundary to look successful.\n\nFinalize the attempt in the outer lifecycle rule after body, cleanup,\nisolation verification, tracing, and teardown. Report body and cleanup\noutcomes independently and mark missing or incomplete terminal work clearly.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321645\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/BaseTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/logging/AttemptFinalization.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/logging/AttemptFinalizationContractTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/logging/log-format.json"], "git_node": "cf3eea77abc600d4d0744bb44ee4b66aa1a0e517", "git_parents": ["875c905272ab4ba3e68394d6e2b11428ad1f1250"], "node": "909fcfa70a6946f4c81681ea837daa5ce704e3b1", "parents": ["8fc7ffb11d71500f5a4ec2724bda9b86f6c5d0e0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065120 - [efficiency] Add opt-in attempt process-death fault injection. r=aaronmt\n\nThe collector needs a deterministic way to prove that a body PASS without a\nterminal event is incomplete rather than a successful attempt.\n\nAdd an opt-in, exact-method allowlisted fault that terminates instrumentation\nafter the body result and before cleanup finalization. Reject broad or unknown\nrequests and cover the activation contract without affecting normal runs.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321646\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/BaseTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/logging/DiagnosticFaultInjection.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/logging/DiagnosticFaultInjectionContractTest.kt"], "git_node": "e447257b677eb8ad3b02896f187a2159d2ee722d", "git_parents": ["cf3eea77abc600d4d0744bb44ee4b66aa1a0e517"], "node": "e91a2c3f3e799777575eca4afa45734e285b59f7", "parents": ["909fcfa70a6946f4c81681ea837daa5ce704e3b1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065120 - [efficiency] Preserve typed step event identity. r=aaronmt\n\nStep completion records reused the event type field for scope classification,\nso downstream readers could lose the declared event identity.\n\nKeep the event type as stepEnd and publish command, step, and locator scope in\na separate scopeType field. Add a contract that protects the producer schema\nand its compatibility representation.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321647\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/logging/StructuredStepContractTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/logging/TimedReporter.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/logging/log-format.json"], "git_node": "bf5e0809fb61c609590cabddd36fdcdb731c477e", "git_parents": ["e447257b677eb8ad3b02896f187a2159d2ee722d"], "node": "8cee3f52212f4cd4a61a34becb7871a58d9f98f3", "parents": ["e91a2c3f3e799777575eca4afa45734e285b59f7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065120 - [efficiency] Persist provider-collectable attempt evidence. r=aaronmt\n\nApp-private JSONL does not survive every provider cleanup or process-death\npath, and logcat alone cannot prove completeness or ordering.\n\nSpool allowlist-redacted attempt events to provider-collectable storage and\natomically publish a terminal manifest with sequence checks and a SHA-256\ninventory. Keep incomplete streams distinguishable from finalized bundles\nand cover retention, redaction, and integrity contracts.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321648\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/ActivityLifecycleTrace.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/logging/JsonSink.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/logging/ProviderAttemptSpool.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/logging/ProviderAttemptSpoolContractTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/logging/ProviderEvidencePolicy.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/logging/StructuredStepContractTest.kt"], "git_node": "d6544363dd95d17feef6f54cb4e3d514abd65732", "git_parents": ["bf5e0809fb61c609590cabddd36fdcdb731c477e"], "node": "ce6fa1aab1bfb2dfee036c5afa9981559cba82a8", "parents": ["8cee3f52212f4cd4a61a34becb7871a58d9f98f3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065120 - [efficiency] Poll grouped UI verification until settled. r=aaronmt\n\nPage identity groups were evaluated immediately even when their Compose or\nview elements were still converging after navigation.\n\nUse the shared polling policy for grouped page verification so arrival waits\nfor a stable observable identity instead of producing a timing-only failure.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321649\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/BasePage.kt"], "git_node": "c932ee84a229a411cdb5fb89d2cca57412102fc9", "git_parents": ["d6544363dd95d17feef6f54cb4e3d514abd65732"], "node": "daaae994e37e8a7846b6989887fd7cf23775a954", "parents": ["ce6fa1aab1bfb2dfee036c5afa9981559cba82a8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065120 - [efficiency] Distinguish persisted toolbar defaults from overrides. r=aaronmt\n\nToolbar preferences may be persisted with the same value supplied by Nimbus,\nwhich is not evidence that a test changed the effective configuration.\n\nCompare persisted toolbar values with their current Nimbus defaults and\nreport only meaningful differences as overrides. This avoids false state-leak\nverdicts while preserving detection of real test-authored changes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321650\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/HarnessPreferenceState.kt"], "git_node": "b0c41e0bef0f6df68591ffd009f90201fbc8c16b", "git_parents": ["c932ee84a229a411cdb5fb89d2cca57412102fc9"], "node": "751148583704dbcce0c0c0f3fd1bdf61018834ce", "parents": ["daaae994e37e8a7846b6989887fd7cf23775a954"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065120 - [efficiency] Keep permission reset outside instrumentation. r=aaronmt\n\nMutating package permission flags from inside instrumentation can disrupt the\nrunning package and behaves differently across local and provider runners.\n\nRemove the in-test shell reset and make the QR flow assert its required denied\ncamera baseline. Permission preparation remains a runner-owned operation\nperformed before instrumentation starts.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321651\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/SearchTest.kt"], "git_node": "2a3e320308a6470718d82c983042e1304d70ec7f", "git_parents": ["b0c41e0bef0f6df68591ffd009f90201fbc8c16b"], "node": "a4c26af523f725146f9cbd38860ee144f0fb24a8", "parents": ["751148583704dbcce0c0c0f3fd1bdf61018834ce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065120 - [efficiency] Declare denied runtime permission requirements. r=aaronmt\n\nPermission-sensitive tests need a machine-readable precondition rather than\nan ad hoc assertion embedded in one test body.\n\nAdd a method annotation for denied runtime permissions, validate it during\nsetup before Activity launch, and emit the resolved requirement as evidence.\nDeclare the camera requirement on the QR scanning test.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321652\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/BaseTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/RequiresDeniedRuntimePermission.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/SearchTest.kt"], "git_node": "d8bdfc7babb3e1732b3f4c97aa8b9205b58537a1", "git_parents": ["2a3e320308a6470718d82c983042e1304d70ec7f"], "node": "f544fcc675c5c4ecabb89d3caad362589dbfdb55", "parents": ["a4c26af523f725146f9cbd38860ee144f0fb24a8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065120 - [efficiency] Scroll system permission rows into view. r=aaronmt\n\nAndroid system settings can place a requested permission below the visible\nviewport, causing a direct verification and click to fail by device layout.\n\nResolve the permission row through the shared swipe-to contract before\nclicking it, then continue to verify and select the system allow option.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321653\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SystemSettingsPage.kt"], "git_node": "1aee3f5829ead24979b4b5d010254531783f314c", "git_parents": ["d8bdfc7babb3e1732b3f4c97aa8b9205b58537a1"], "node": "c3e7531978e697ddb24f0d26381acd5c8dedbab7", "parents": ["f544fcc675c5c4ecabb89d3caad362589dbfdb55"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065120 - [efficiency] Clear tab undo state without restoration. r=aaronmt\n\nRestoring recoverable tabs as an intermediate cleanup step recreates domain\nstate and can trigger product behavior that cleanup is supposed to remove.\n\nClear pending undo state directly, remove tabs as non-recoverable, clear any\nnew undo state, and wait for both stores to become empty. Remove the duplicate\nteardown path so one owner defines the tab boundary.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321654\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/AppDataCleaner.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/BaseTest.kt"], "git_node": "89334794aeb531f7c67915ed8d816d5a3d1605d1", "git_parents": ["1aee3f5829ead24979b4b5d010254531783f314c"], "node": "1aaf80b87296cd8fb2e2fb759dbab40638569b62", "parents": ["c3e7531978e697ddb24f0d26381acd5c8dedbab7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065120 - [efficiency] Preserve deterministic navigation route identity. r=aaronmt\n\nMultiple legitimate routes can share endpoints, while endpoint-only deduping\nand path flattening discard which transition was actually selected.\n\nGive routes stable identities and purposes, reject only byte-identical\nduplicates, and select variants deterministically. Preserve route identity in\nnavigation reporting and move remaining transitions to their source owners.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321655\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/devtools/NavigationGraphContractTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/BasePage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/NavigationEdge.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/NavigationRegistry.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/HomePage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/MainMenuPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsSavedPasswordsPage.kt"], "git_node": "e29c8d967bd39afc6bc7cc00825dcf8173852897", "git_parents": ["89334794aeb531f7c67915ed8d816d5a3d1605d1"], "node": "5bfa76089b39303d76beb48e66c04af3a61dac37", "parents": ["1aaf80b87296cd8fb2e2fb759dbab40638569b62"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065120 - [efficiency] Preserve structured evidence sequence order. r=aaronmt\n\nConcurrent sink work could write structured records in a different order from\ntheir assigned envelope sequence, making a complete stream appear corrupted.\n\nSerialize JSONL publication in sequence order and make boundary writes\nsynchronous where durability is required. Add contract coverage for ordered\nrecords and monotonic sequence preservation.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321656\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/logging/EventEnvelope.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/logging/EventEnvelopeContractTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/logging/JsonSink.kt"], "git_node": "6ec81dc940c538402de4e869aa9b41db6baf9eea", "git_parents": ["e29c8d967bd39afc6bc7cc00825dcf8173852897"], "node": "ae8dd78169bc34937fb351275c067e1d7d5c61d8", "parents": ["5bfa76089b39303d76beb48e66c04af3a61dac37"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065120 - [efficiency] Unify Compose selector resolution across verbs. r=aaronmt\n\nCompose selectors were resolved through separate branches for ordinary,\ncollection, and child-text operations, allowing tree and pick semantics to\ndrift between verbs.\n\nCentralize Compose matcher and candidate selection in the resolver layer and\nreuse it from BasePage. Preserve unmerged-tree, first-match, displayed-node,\nand child-text behavior through one implementation.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321657\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/core/Resolvers.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/BasePage.kt"], "git_node": "4471365f93f4c586d4586afd3f163403deca4a4b", "git_parents": ["6ec81dc940c538402de4e869aa9b41db6baf9eea"], "node": "b731e4d9ff7739a1596dc2466236d8d0ee39f596", "parents": ["ae8dd78169bc34937fb351275c067e1d7d5c61d8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065120 - [efficiency] Reject vacuous page identity groups. r=aaronmt\n\nAn empty selector group satisfies an all-elements predicate vacuously, so an\nunfinished page oracle could be treated as a successful navigation arrival.\n\nFail empty groups explicitly, add a page-object identity contract, and mark\nintentional unfinished pages as unsupported instead of successful. Extend the\ngraph contract and planner to respect that distinction.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321658\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/core/VerbContractTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/core/VerbHost.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/core/Verbs.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/devtools/NavigationGraphContractTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/NavigationTestPlanner.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/PageCatalog.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/PageObjectContract.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/CollectionsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/MicrosurveysPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/ShortcutsPage.kt"], "git_node": "96a85289782715bb626d178a40bb77236eb2f5b6", "git_parents": ["4471365f93f4c586d4586afd3f163403deca4a4b"], "node": "952155e027b30c48e471b7610fbbdeb478d3d477", "parents": ["b731e4d9ff7739a1596dc2466236d8d0ee39f596"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065120 - [efficiency] Resolve single-element verbs through UiElement. r=aaronmt\n\nSingle-element verbs leaked Compose, Espresso, and UiAutomator handles into\ncallers, duplicating backend branching across actions and state probes.\n\nMake VerbHost return the backend-neutral UiElement facade and keep unwrapping\ninside core utilities. Route actions, gestures, relations, and state checks\nthrough the same typed boundary without changing the fluent test interface.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321659\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/core/ElementState.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/core/Gestures.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/core/Relations.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/core/Resolvers.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/core/UiActions.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/core/UiElement.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/core/VerbContractTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/core/VerbHost.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/core/Verbs.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/BasePage.kt"], "git_node": "a420bee42e8a75db79c483f75cc30f84b643a878", "git_parents": ["96a85289782715bb626d178a40bb77236eb2f5b6"], "node": "72a10e6e62c2103c35f85aa4cb2df816ecc471c9", "parents": ["952155e027b30c48e471b7610fbbdeb478d3d477"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065120 - [efficiency] Classify element resolution failures. r=aaronmt\n\nNullable lookup results collapsed true absence, unsupported selectors, and\nresolver failures, while optional actions could swallow unrelated errors.\n\nIntroduce exhaustive found, absent, unsupported, and error outcomes and carry\nthem through polling and failure evidence. Optional actions now skip only\nconfirmed absence or disappearance, and secure password-dialog lookup uses a\nbackend that can resolve the system-visible secure window.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321660\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/core/ElementResolution.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/core/Resolvers.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/core/VerbContractTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/core/VerbHost.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/core/Verbs.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/BasePage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/SettingsSavedPasswordsSelectors.kt"], "git_node": "20b99c819d5b0900a8d1f3d4dee502712c2dcffb", "git_parents": ["a420bee42e8a75db79c483f75cc30f84b643a878"], "node": "e5990f1641dca25eda5f070babfb7feccac4c6b5", "parents": ["72a10e6e62c2103c35f85aa4cb2df816ecc471c9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065120 - [efficiency] Repair full-sweep harness regressions. r=aaronmt\n\nPrefer browser-free navigation paths while choosing the shortest suitable route, and keep Android system pages outside the Fenix navigation graph.\n\nRecover known system overlays across transient Compose lifecycle gaps and use stable UiAutomator2 clicks for toolbar transitions.\n\nSerialize recoverable-tab persistence before recently-closed cleanup and correct stale selector-group assertions exposed by strict page identity checks.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323008\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/core/ElementResolution.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/core/VerbContractTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/core/Verbs.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/devtools/NavigationGraphContractTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/AppDataCleaner.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/NavigationRegistry.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/BrowserPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SearchBarComponent.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SystemSettingsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/TabHistoryPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/ToolbarSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/MainMenuTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/SearchTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/TabbedBrowsingTest.kt"], "git_node": "04a2a4077e21238a2006dbc34335968b7a115b4c", "git_parents": ["20b99c819d5b0900a8d1f3d4dee502712c2dcffb"], "node": "c2ec94c0bfa8dff6eeecb9b808e5c05f411a310a", "parents": ["e5990f1641dca25eda5f070babfb7feccac4c6b5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065120 - [efficiency] Add state-aware navigation path constraints. r=aaronmt\n\nModel navigation as page-and-fact states so routes can declare preconditions and effects. Let callers require ordered waypoints, routes, and final facts; exclude pages or routes; and express soft avoidance preferences. Verify explicit waypoints before continuing and include current facts in failure diagnostics.\n\nTrack whether Settings was opened from Home or Browser and choose the matching return route instead of relying on history-dependent shortcuts. Add contract coverage for constrained paths, state transitions, guards, and same-page navigation, and make the affected prompt and checkbox interactions resilient.\n\nWait for the Sync Debug preference before selecting Autofill so the Settings relayout cannot retarget the click. Give Android task removal additional bounded settling time to avoid false cleanup failures on slower devices.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323009\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/devtools/NavigationGraphContractTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/ActivityStateCleaner.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/BasePage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/PageContext.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/PageStateTracker.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/ScreenDump.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/NavigationEdge.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/NavigationRegistry.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/NavigationState.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/AddToHomeScreenComponent.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/BookmarkSearchPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/BookmarksPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/BrowserPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/DownloadsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/FindInPagePage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/MainMenuPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/NotificationPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SearchBarComponent.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsAccessibilityPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsAddonsManagerPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsAppIconPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsAutofillPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsCustomizePage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsDeleteBrowsingDataPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsHTTPSOnlyModePage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsPrivateBrowsingPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsSearchAddSearchEnginePage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsSearchManageShortcutsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsSiteSettingsPermissionsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsTurnOnSyncPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/ShareOverlayPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/TabDrawerPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/TabHistoryPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/UnifiedTrustPanelPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/WebCompatReporterPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/SettingsSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/CreditCardAutofillTest.kt"], "git_node": "542a2946786db195065a1c03df28021bcc491068", "git_parents": ["04a2a4077e21238a2006dbc34335968b7a115b4c"], "node": "c2ce8d7f90e377ea8f341ebf489d7015a96d4c3f", "parents": ["c2ec94c0bfa8dff6eeecb9b808e5c05f411a310a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2061059: Style SFF autocomplete row item r=omarg,fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,credential-management-reviewers,mkennedy,hjones,bolsson,mtigley\" for causing bc failures @browser_smartwindow_smartformfill_autocomplete.js.\n\nThis reverts commit 57066504cb5a1f50c71993d7173e956541b89ad1.\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/assets/sff-autofill-icon.svg", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/jar.mn", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/SmartFormFillAutocomplete.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_smartformfill_autocomplete.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/browser_autocomplete_footer.js", "browser/locales-preview/aiWindow.ftl", "browser/themes/shared/autocomplete.css", "toolkit/components/satchel/autocomplete-row-item/autocomplete-row-item.css", "toolkit/components/satchel/autocomplete-row-item/autocomplete-row-item.mjs", "toolkit/components/satchel/test/browser/browser_autocomplete.js", "toolkit/content/widgets/autocomplete-popup.js"], "git_node": "8473c10e29201515ded0382ee7a9e3f0c7bc2380", "git_parents": ["542a2946786db195065a1c03df28021bcc491068"], "node": "7c6fb87236b38482d9d6de0990519d84ee76b3dc", "parents": ["c2ce8d7f90e377ea8f341ebf489d7015a96d4c3f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2043477 - Update wasi-sdk toolchain to v34. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nwasi-sdk builds its sysroot with cmake now, rather than the Makefile we drove with stub files.\nThe sysroot build produces compiler-rt itself, so those tasks lose their dependency on the\ncompiler-rt artifact, and they need cmake 3.26, hence the deb13 image. LTO, shared libraries and\nexceptions are pinned off; the wasm sandbox uses none of them, and upstream defaults the first two on\nand exceptions on from clang 23.\n\nv34 drops the wasm32-wasi target, so the sysroot is built for wasm32-wasip1.\n\nwasi-libc now defines pthread_create for the non-threaded target, so the pthread_create probe has to\nskip wasi to keep -pthread off the wasm build.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D303335\n", "files": ["build/moz.configure/libraries.configure", "taskcluster/kinds/fetch/toolchains.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/toolchain/compiler-rt.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/toolchain/sysroot.yml", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-compiler-rt-wasi.sh", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-sysroot-wasi.sh", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-wasi-sdk.sh", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/wasi-sdk-compat.patch", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/wasi-sdk-no-llvm-patches.patch", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/wasi-sdk.patch"], "git_node": "0b38800ba7621ce8f8f388efbdfd6f42914d12a6", "git_parents": ["8473c10e29201515ded0382ee7a9e3f0c7bc2380"], "node": "c8990b7f4a2c4439ec18b4604da18e04b3e0a645", "parents": ["7c6fb87236b38482d9d6de0990519d84ee76b3dc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Boris Chiou \u003cboris.chiou@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2046973 - Update SetPlaybackRate() to match the spec. r=layout-scroll-driven-animation-reviewers,dshin\n\nWe missed the implementation for finite timelines. The spec udpate was added\ninto web-animations-1 [1] directly, instead of web-animations-2.\n\n[1] https://drafts.csswg.org/web-animations-1/#set-the-playback-rate\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322841\n", "files": ["dom/animation/Animation.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/scroll-timelines/setting-playback-rate.html.ini"], "git_node": "bad01910529d5b62b04f4abde93241f8fb5188a7", "git_parents": ["0b38800ba7621ce8f8f388efbdfd6f42914d12a6"], "node": "04b05b83e804f0e1850ceab3445445df059ed664", "parents": ["c8990b7f4a2c4439ec18b4604da18e04b3e0a645"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Boris Chiou \u003cboris.chiou@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2046973 - Fix Reverse() to make sure we call Play() to update the animation for zero playback rate. r=layout-scroll-driven-animation-reviewers,dshin\n\nOtherwise, calling reverse() is no-op and our behavior may mismatch\nother browers because the start time and current time is not correct\nafter calling reverse() with zero playback rate. This also matches the spec.\n\nAlso, we intentionally preserve zero playback rate (instead of setting to\n`-0`); otherwise, we may get new failures in\nweb-animations/timing-model/animations/reversing-an-animation.html and\nscroll-animations/scroll-timelines/reverse-animation.html.\n\nIn addition, need to update the test of animation mutation observers\nbecause we update the animation after we call reverse() for zero\nplayback rate.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322842\n", "files": ["dom/animation/Animation.cpp", "dom/animation/test/chrome/test_animation_observers_sync.html", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/scroll-timelines/reverse-animation.html.ini"], "git_node": "6ba4be10618f03f894a5d68b1f8b2b889ff7be2b", "git_parents": ["bad01910529d5b62b04f4abde93241f8fb5188a7"], "node": "4fbf969ba677e87035d7e7defa7821ec99496fbd", "parents": ["04b05b83e804f0e1850ceab3445445df059ed664"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rolf Rando \u003crrando@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068278 - Allow AutoFill model version to be set in Nimbus. Custom configs for form tokenization for select and text input fields. r=dimi\n\nAdd ability to set model version via nimbus\n\nEnable new featurizations of autofill data controlled by a flag. The max field count and select form popup fields weren't being sent to the ML model, which made it blind to data to do a better job on some fields.\n\nOn validation data the accuracy for cc-exp-year is improved 10.9%  (0.826 to 0.935) and for tel-country-code it's improved 7.7% (0.929 to 0.984). Telephone is improved a small amount\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322762\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/browser_ml_mldata_features.js", "modules/libpref/init/all.js", "toolkit/components/formautofill/shared/FormAutofillHeuristics.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/shared/FormAutofillML.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/shared/FormAutofillUtils.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/nimbus/FeatureManifest.yaml"], "git_node": "5801c833848c0e07147911e3817140ef9eab47f3", "git_parents": ["6ba4be10618f03f894a5d68b1f8b2b889ff7be2b"], "node": "77ac55bb02108a3c4ad300d5922f30782c48618e", "parents": ["4fbf969ba677e87035d7e7defa7821ec99496fbd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Juliana Gaibler \u003cgit@juliana.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062751 - Polished the Nova app menu update banner and fixed spacing issues. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,mstriemer\n\n- Top-card spacing: the cards at the top of the app menu (update banner,\n  menu-message, sign-in promo, addon banners) each hand-rolled their own\n  margins, so the insets were inconsistent.\n- Private tabs aren't restored on restart, so the new update banner's \"Your\n  tabs will reopen\" description was misleading there.\n- The update-restart pulse animation was too subtle.\n- The update icon did not have enough contrast in dark themes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317939\n", "files": ["browser/components/customizableui/content/panelUI.js", "browser/themes/shared/customizableui/panelUI-shared.css"], "git_node": "b2bbba90a14130e40527b012dedd19cbd2f73481", "git_parents": ["5801c833848c0e07147911e3817140ef9eab47f3"], "node": "bd6570ec75f6ea2b8da1301da3c0a54ea0df162a", "parents": ["77ac55bb02108a3c4ad300d5922f30782c48618e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Import translations from https://github.com/mozilla-l10n/android-l10n CLOSED TREE\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-lv/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/res/values-bg/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/res/values-bqi/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/res/values-cs/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/res/values-cy/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/res/values-de/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/res/values-dsb/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/res/values-el/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/res/values-en-rGB/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/res/values-es-rAR/string