ferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322822\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Lists/Lists.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Lists/_Lists.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/unit/content-src/components/Widgets/Lists.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_ListsFeed.js"], "git_node": "386012d50b4cac1db59133e2fcefa23bfd1c2766", "git_parents": ["298cf786229591e2159a3933605df11e07709d6f"], "node": "5c744bd6adb2007c212c0d85d11819bb4effc33d", "parents": ["3dc0b00c483ccb5bf8372c567eec313a6e67bf28"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068199 - Generate FillCircle events for circles with valid, positive radii. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322695\n", "files": ["gfx/2d/DrawTargetRecording.cpp", "gfx/2d/DrawTargetRecording.h"], "git_node": "e8d96f1472da9b7b16083a51ba73bf61429ed1c7", "git_parents": ["386012d50b4cac1db59133e2fcefa23bfd1c2766"], "node": "a1d7e386f54d3d5a09415e57ea0559aecd4e7b06", "parents": ["5c744bd6adb2007c212c0d85d11819bb4effc33d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058744 - Make `AbstractRange::UpdateDescendantsInFlattenedTree` use `TreeIterator\u003cFlattenedChildIteratorForSelection\u003e` r=emilio\n\nCurrently, we treat selection across shadow DOM ignore UA widgets.\nTherefore, the method should use `FlattenedChildIteratorForSelection`\ninstead of `FlattenedChildIterator` to set the selected flag of the\nnodes in the range.\n\nWith this change, the default summary of `\u003cdetails\u003e` won't be rendered\nas selected when the default `\u003csummary\u003e` is completely in a selection\nrange. This is different from Chrome, but we don't copy the default\nsummary to clipboard. Therefore, until we support to copy the default\nsummary, the new behavior matches with the result.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322801\n", "files": ["dom/base/AbstractRange.cpp", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/selection/default-summary-selection-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/selection/default-summary-selection.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/editing/crashtests/selectall-containing-textarea-and-subscript.html"], "git_node": "33599940e3f810bf5da7c669d0d41e3eb2ed7fc4", "git_parents": ["e8d96f1472da9b7b16083a51ba73bf61429ed1c7"], "node": "5b63c579d0b8cd42072bdf4cbdfb5a7986d2516f", "parents": ["a1d7e386f54d3d5a09415e57ea0559aecd4e7b06"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2068199 - Generate FillCircle events for circles with valid, positive radii. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\" for causibg build bustages @DrawTargetRecording.cpp.\n\nThis reverts commit e8d96f1472da9b7b16083a51ba73bf61429ed1c7.\n", "files": ["gfx/2d/DrawTargetRecording.cpp", "gfx/2d/DrawTargetRecording.h"], "git_node": "40e92c7949df9f8d6de0bb3be0344cc55668f293", "git_parents": ["33599940e3f810bf5da7c669d0d41e3eb2ed7fc4"], "node": "9e419e71655f21b6ecba362dcdb61ce56573109b", "parents": ["5b63c579d0b8cd42072bdf4cbdfb5a7986d2516f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Farrell \u003cmicolous+git@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1958000 - Resolve and stage rusttest deps r=ahochheiden\n\nTo be able to have a regular Rust test that depends on an in-tree non-Rust\nlibrary:\n\n* `rusttests` to be built with recursive library dependency resolution, so\n  that all libraries are available before building and running the tests.\n\n* On non-Darwin systems, dynamic libraries need to be staged somewhere the\n  test binary can find them, as its `DT_RUNPATH` (on non-Windows systems)\n  only applies to direct dependencies.\n\n  `cargo run` and `cargo test` both set `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` (or platform\n  equivalents) to the base output directory and the `deps` directory, so we\n  can copy them from `dist/bin` to `deps` (on all non-Darwin systems, not\n  just Windows).\n\nThis also removes `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` from the `rusttests` environment on\nLinux CI runners, because this change renders it unnecessary, it's different\nto how `rusttests` runs locally, and it wasn't set for `x86_64` release\nbuilds.\n\nThis is tested by adding `lockstore_rs`' existing tests to the build system.\nI've disabled these tests on Windows or when running with code coverage, as\nthe tests have dead references to `libxul` via `kvstore` and cause linker\nfailures.\n\n`noise` Rust tests in D316170 won't need these workarounds.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318374\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "config/makefiles/rust.mk", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/recursivemake.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/rust-library-archive-dep/middle/middle.c", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/rust-library-archive-dep/middle/moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/rust-library-archive-dep/moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/rust-library-archive-dep/rust/moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/test_recursivemake.py", "security/lockstore/lockstore_rs/Cargo.toml", "security/lockstore/lockstore_rs/build.rs", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_linux_configs/32_rusttests.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_linux_configs/32_rusttests_debug.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_linux_configs/64_rusttests.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_linux_configs/64_rusttests_debug.py", "toolkit/library/rust/moz.build"], "git_node": "f2fdb4f8d94d57271cc85b207f14ea3f2e4f54f1", "git_parents": ["40e92c7949df9f8d6de0bb3be0344cc55668f293"], "node": "4b24885656dc4699b53ae932fa2937ecb6c2fe84", "parents": ["9e419e71655f21b6ecba362dcdb61ce56573109b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068199 - Generate FillCircle events for circles with valid, positive radii. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322695\n", "files": ["gfx/2d/DrawTargetRecording.cpp", "gfx/2d/DrawTargetRecording.h"], "git_node": "66721cbbc9aba84b35998cae3898094dc4c43a10", "git_parents": ["f2fdb4f8d94d57271cc85b207f14ea3f2e4f54f1"], "node": "35ddc7df589830a5801707c701e1a033cc0539e1", "parents": ["4b24885656dc4699b53ae932fa2937ecb6c2fe84"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068185 - Add a --bundle option to robustcheckout r=releng-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nrobustcheckout gains a --bundle option that applies a local Mercurial bundle\nbefore resolving the requested revision. When the bundle contains the wanted\nrevision, the subsequent pull from the remote is skipped entirely.\n\nApplying the bundle is best-effort: if it can't be applied (missing base\nchangesets, corrupt or absent file), robustcheckout logs a warning and falls\nback to pulling from the remote, so the option is a pure optimization.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322863\n", "files": ["testing/mozharness/external_tools/robustcheckout.py"], "git_node": "c4a02d1d9ba5a22fef850e33893f38ebaf3f1007", "git_parents": ["66721cbbc9aba84b35998cae3898094dc4c43a10"], "node": "91bccc7f81c3ca91dcc8b321a01032f2de31e210", "parents": ["35ddc7df589830a5801707c701e1a033cc0539e1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068185 - Serve a source bundle from the decision task for downstream hg checkouts r=releng-reviewers,taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nThe decision task already performs one checkout per push, pulling the\ndelta between the CDN clone bundle and the head revision from\nhg.mozilla.org via a expensive (particularly on try) getbundle. Every\ndownstream hg-cloning task then repeats that same getbundle, multiplying\nthe load on the hg app servers.\n\nHave the decision task bundle the changesets newer than 48h (public\nonly, so try drafts are always carried) and publish it as\npublic/checkout.bundle.  run-task downloads it and hands it to\nrobustcheckout's --bundle option, which applies it before the\nlocal-revision check so the remote pull is skipped entirely. Any failure\nfalls back to the normal pull, so the feature is a pure optimization.\n\nWired for Mercurial-resolved checkouts (clone_type() == \"hg\") via an\nartifact-reference to the decision task.\n\nThe flip side is this adds a bit of latency to the critical path (on a\nsample of 1 try push I saw the bundle creation taking ~2.4s).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322864\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/decision.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/job/run_task.py", "taskcluster/scripts/run-task"], "git_node": "ebf0d35d326d46f0e06e3ebf786703212e0f5c50", "git_parents": ["c4a02d1d9ba5a22fef850e33893f38ebaf3f1007"], "node": "9bf8a20a3cedcf293f43d468b612e2cd8cf1076d", "parents": ["91bccc7f81c3ca91dcc8b321a01032f2de31e210"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Bumping Firefox l10n changesets r=release a=l10n-bump DONTBUILD CLOSED TREE\n\nach -\u003e e8b8ec92f1c53f3d028818e6157220ba4b234c80\naf -\u003e e8b8ec92f1c53f3d028818e6157220ba4b234c80\nan -\u003e e8b8ec92f1c53f3d028818e6157220ba4b234c80\nar -\u003e e8b8ec92f1c53f3d028818e6157220ba4b234c80\nast -\u003e e8b8ec92f1c53f3d028818e6157220ba4b234c80\naz -\u003e e8b8ec92f1c53f3d028818e6157220ba4b234c80\nbe -\u003e e8b8ec92f1c53f3d028818e6157220ba4b234c80\nbg -\u003e e8b8ec92f1c53f3d028818e6157220ba4b234c80\nbn -\u003e e8b8ec92f1c53f3d028818e6157220ba4b234c80\nbo -\u003e e8b8ec92f1c53f3d028818e6157220ba4b234c80\nbqi -\u003e e8b8ec92f1c53f3d028818e6157220ba4b234c80\nbr -\u003e e8b8ec