ion, and makes the getter more consistent with the setter.\n\nthis is covered by updates to [html#10995], and fixes 270 of the subtest regressions in [wpt#60283].\n\n[webcomponents#1114]: \u003chttps://github.com/WICG/webcomponents/issues/1114\u003e\n[html#10995]: \u003chttps://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/10995\u003e\n[wpt#60283]: \u003chttps://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/60283\u003e\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322834\n", "files": ["dom/base/Element.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/shadow-dom/reference-target/tentative/property-reflection-idl-setters.html.ini"], "git_node": "e301b58c4e4f4d8a8c9e39d5f3dfbb9933d29c1c", "git_parents": ["de5597d7d28b20eece6ecb76df90c52422776d5b"], "node": "2e1c0a0c83848a3444b60eb8834ffd63c99b9638", "parents": ["dbf487945e8ae5e6718a621ef8eb727890ced667"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068854 - switch back from ftpmirror to ftp.gnu.org for toolchain fetches.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323163\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/fetch/toolchains.yml"], "git_node": "b5aac0d214e1c25c6c40faa45f45d74cd1455dd0", "git_parents": ["e301b58c4e4f4d8a8c9e39d5f3dfbb9933d29c1c"], "node": "51aab5319b65aa8734cc9a8ec86f1e606e49099e", "parents": ["2e1c0a0c83848a3444b60eb8834ffd63c99b9638"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sotaro Ikeda \u003csotaro.ikeda.g@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068438 r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323156\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/ImageContainer.cpp", "gfx/layers/client/TextureClient.cpp", "gfx/layers/client/TextureClient.h"], "git_node": "eb05f7288c75dd338c62604a7849195932b9748b", "git_parents": ["b5aac0d214e1c25c6c40faa45f45d74cd1455dd0"], "node": "60e515b4e168ed21c6acbbd8923031090ae2599b", "parents": ["51aab5319b65aa8734cc9a8ec86f1e606e49099e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriel Luong \u003cgabriel.luong@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067029 - Wire up the Darkest theme option to the app night mode r=android-reviewers,007\n\n- Selecting \"Darkest\" and `shouldUseOledTheme` applies `MODE_NIGHT_YES` and recreates the activity.\n- Return `PreferredColorScheme.Dark` for the OLED theme in `getPreferredColorScheme()` so Gecko content matches the chrome.\n- \"Darkest\" is still visually identical to \"Dark\". The OLED colors will be applied in later work.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321932\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/FenixApplication.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/Core.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/CustomizationFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/utils/SettingsTest.kt"], "git_node": "a9f23af655a3002d6f7e2793a92a61a10f3bf0c5", "git_parents": ["eb05f7288c75dd338c62604a7849195932b9748b"], "node": "64867c293b87c0b8626ce13f3901c78e7f765180", "parents": ["60e515b4e168ed21c6acbbd8923031090ae2599b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriel Luong \u003cgabriel.luong@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067019 - Add telemetry for the OLED theme usage r=android-reviewers,007\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321942\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/metrics.yaml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/FenixApplication.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/CustomizationFragment.kt"], "git_node": "e078901738131c184f92ee63e05eeb75b9379ea5", "git_parents": ["a9f23af655a3002d6f7e2793a92a61a10f3bf0c5"], "node": "164236044bacaaf37d80c3de9534ee8e19ce4cf1", "parents": ["64867c293b87c0b8626ce13f3901c78e7f765180"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061548 - [devtools] Remove skip-if nova for webconsole chrome mochitests r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320009\n", "files": ["devtools/shared/webconsole/test/chrome/chrome.toml"], "git_node": "a6aece6b92cb44d5efa6030d6e6b5ab7a17eeb9e", "git_parents": ["e078901738131c184f92ee63e05eeb75b9379ea5"], "node": "b0ace564d2f38d2272ea0867b667d215c4e16925", "parents": ["164236044bacaaf37d80c3de9534ee8e19ce4cf1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061548 - Remove nova from skip if annotation for backup/tests/browser/browser_settings.js r=hsohaney\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320010\n", "files": ["browser/components/backup/tests/browser/browser.toml"], "git_node": "84694e3f9e0655591356feafe47d4232e74f54e6", "git_parents": ["a6aece6b92cb44d5efa6030d6e6b5ab7a17eeb9e"], "node": "78c43b5fc743dd30982a928432627d2cf5a1189c", "parents": ["b0ace564d2f38d2272ea0867b667d215c4e16925"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Makoto Kato \u003cm_kato@ga2.so-net.ne.jp\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067339 - Call DateFormat.is24HourFormat on non-UI/non-Gecko thread. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall\n\nWe gets current time format setting by `DateFormat.is24HourFormat`. But\naccording to profiler data, it is slow. This profile data is a first\ncall that ICU is used. But even if next, it it still 3ms on Pixel 6a.\n\nThis call is on UI thread, so I would like to move it to background\nthread since `getIs24HourFormat` isn't called immediately.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322032\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/GeckoRuntime.java"], "git_node": "9872595699ab09267f3f0e2f066aa70e8ace29e2", "git_parents": ["84694e3f9e0655591356feafe47d4232e74f54e6"], "node": "e3cdbb6f3450219b62474ef5abcf8b5feda8ef29", "parents": ["78c43b5fc743dd30982a928432627d2cf5a1189c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Schuster \u003ctschuster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068510 - Remove nsContentSecurityUtils exemptions for about:sync-log. r=tjr\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322911\n", "files": ["dom/security/nsContentSecurityUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "02accc93a3e51008936536e1b5363236f00420f4", "git_parents": ["9872595699ab09267f3f0e2f066aa70e8ace29e2"], "node": "a64b0c08bd839f68e60d7c586a13226a2bed10eb", "parents": ["e3cdbb6f3450219b62474ef5abcf8b5feda8ef29"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Schuster \u003ctschuster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068510 - Remove more about: page exemptions from nsContentSecurityUtils::ValidateScriptFilename. r=tjr\n\nConsidering that these pages are shipping with a strict CSP these should\nbe unnecessary.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322912\n", "files": ["dom/security/nsContentSecurityUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "0c969d9a4d4ea190c3a2169e0404044450b92875", "git_parents": ["02accc93a3e51008936536e1b5363236f00420f4"], "node": "1a5745733bbff4a02f199c233ef31f11a4250567", "parents": ["a64b0c08bd839f68e60d7c586a13226a2bed10eb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandre Poirot \u003cpoirot.alex@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058286 - [devtools] Avoid fetching breakable position from all original source's matching actors. r=devtools-reviewers,bomsy\n\nOnly some edgecase of original sources will have more than one range,\nbut we can keep the same logic.\nThis help also reuse the same logic regarding retrieving the relevant source actors.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321592\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/src/actions/breakpoints/breakpointPositions.js"], "git_node": "c26f3040af776af5b296d8e8426687d16228827c", "git_parents": ["0c969d9a4d4ea190c3a2169e0404044450b92875"], "node": "165a26d1e1221b19b562ff8caa5d00b1369e0cbf", "parents": ["1a5745733bbff4a02f199c233ef31f11a4250567"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoshi Cheng-Hao Huang \u003callstars.chh@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061080 - Part 1: Creating a JavaScript module script should return an empty script when the script is disabled. r=jonco\n\nCurrently when compiling a Javascript module, it returns an error when\nthe script is disabled. But according to the spec, it should succeed\nwith an empty module script.\n\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/#creating-a-javascript-module-script\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320508\n", "files": ["dom/script/ModuleLoader.cpp", "dom/script/ModuleLoader.h", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/scripting/the-script-element/module-script-disabled-scripting.html"], "git_node": "8e4e2492d76fecd950bc5edcdf9d86174d7e65ac", "git_parents": ["c26f3040af776af5b296d8e8426687d16228827c"], "node": "d8ad19c87af6df3a9aca657c453db07eeea267bd", "parents": ["165a26d1e1221b19b562ff8caa5d00b1369e0cbf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoshi Cheng-Hao Huang \u003callstars.chh@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061080 - Part 2: Prevent onFetchComplete from being called twice on failure. r=jonco\n\nIf CreateModuleScript fails in OnFetchComplete, LoadFailed() is called\nto clear the import data, and then goes back to the ScriptLoader. Later\nScriptLoader calls OnFetchComplete again with the error. This triggers\nthe assertion of the mPayload is not empty.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320510\n", "files": ["dom/script/ModuleLoader.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.cpp", "js/loader/ModuleLoadRequest.cpp", "js/loader/ModuleLoadRequest.h", "js/loader/ModuleLoaderBase.cpp", "js/loader/ModuleLoaderBase.h", "js/xpconnect/loader/SyncModuleLoader.cpp"], "git_node": "f8b961dfa38f514c6d4bbf1d18506cc014318d04", "git_parents": ["8e4e2492d76fecd950bc5edcdf9d86174d7e65ac"], "node": "164b1b09c71d3d6714ccb92207066499f6ab8951", "parents": ["d8ad19c87af6df3a9aca657c453db07eeea267bd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoshi Cheng-Hao Huang \u003callstars.chh@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061080 - Part 3: Don't run promise version of LoadRequestedModules if script is disabled. r=jonco\n\nIf calling the promise version of the LoadRequestedModules after the\nscript is disabled, the promise can't be settled and the reference of\nModuleLoadRequest can't be released, which causes memory leak. This\nfixes the leak by calling the sync version instead.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320511\n", "files": ["dom/base/test/jsmodules/mochitest.toml", "dom/base/test/jsmodules/scriptDisabled_frame.html", "dom/base/test/jsmodules/scriptDisabled_module.mjs", "dom/base/test/jsmodules/test_scriptDisabled_modules.html", "js/loader/ModuleLoaderBase.cpp"], "git_node": "812a72803f1a2ba12ba996ba9fd34e02a52330f1", "git_parents": ["f8b961dfa38f514c6d4bbf1d18506cc014318d04"], "node": "ac37386637584801c0b5e1bf1df5905c16de3fc8", "parents": ["164b1b09c71d3d6714ccb92207066499f6ab8951"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoshi Cheng-Hao Huang \u003callstars.chh@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061080 - Part 4: Cancel dynamic imports after canceling fetching requests. r=jonco\n\nA dynamic import may be added to the mWaiting requests if the URI is also fetching.\nDuring a worker shutdown, if we canceled dynamic imports first, later the canceled\ndynamic import is canceled again during canceling fetching requests. The fix is\nto reorder the canceling sequence to align the canceling order in\nScriptLoader::Destroy.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320512\n", "files": ["js/loader/ModuleLoaderBase.cpp"], "git_node": "ee267c39b065041121317b72055a696f85b68b50", "git_parents": ["812a72803f1a2ba12ba996ba9fd34e02a52330f1"], "node": "1e32ee9553ee8cf5f2587c1a2763e3c5b9825bd8", "parents": ["ac37386637584801c0b5e1bf1df5905c16de3fc8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoshi Cheng-Hao Huang \u003callstars.chh@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061080 - Part 5: A Web-Ext test to reproduce the crashes. r=jonco,extension-reviewers,robwu\n\nFor the crash caused by the web-ext case, an import is still pending while the\ndocument is destroyed: that nukes the add-on realm's wrappers and blocks script\non it.\n\nThis test uses the web-ext way to reproduce the crash stack.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320513\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_ext_module_import_while_scripting_disabled.js", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/xpcshell-common.toml"], "git_node": "e284cc94fbb5720abddf93e37d06ef99c1baa9d7", "git_parents": ["ee267c39b065041121317b72055a696f85b68b50"], "node": "f48f1f97df316f814217f357cc3608ecce29d20e", "parents": ["1e32ee9553ee8cf5f2587c1a2763e3c5b9825bd8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoshi Cheng-Hao Huang \u003callstars.chh@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061080 - Part 6: Don't cache the empty module, and discard any pending off-thread compilation. r=arai\n\nDrop the disk cache reference and the SRI for the empty module script created\nduring scripting is disabled.\n\nAlso the result of an off-thread compilation is never consumed here either,\ncancel it as well.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322567\n", "files": ["dom/base/test/jsmodules/mochitest.toml", "dom/base/test/jsmodules/scriptDisabledDiskCache_module.sjs", "dom/base/test/jsmodules/test_scriptDisabled_modules.html", "dom/script/ModuleLoader.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.cpp"], "git_node": "e3c5c2dbeca9202196b33559e9f1fcdee01f3691", "git_parents": ["e284cc94fbb5720abddf93e37d06ef99c1baa9d7"], "node": "f464a4c8ac528e019663398f794f87831afa86b4", "parents": ["f48f1f97df316f814217f357cc3608ecce29d20e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051973 - Vendor the Metal backend at the pinned llama.cpp revision. r=ai-platform-reviewers,valentinp\n\nThe Metal files were taken from an older llama.cpp than the revision moz.yaml\npins, which is why they had to be in \"keep\" rather than revendored.\n\nThis vendors the backend at 74ade527 instead, matching llama.cpp. At that rev,\nit is split into a few files. The embedding of the shader source is unchanged: the\n.metal file still has the __embed_ggml-common.h__ and ggml-metal-impl.h\nplaceholders generate_metal_embed.py substitutes. etc.\n\nggml-metal-device.m and ggml-metal-device.cpp would compile to the same object\nname, so run_parser.py renames the former to ggml-metal-device-m.m, like it\nalready does for ggml.c and ggml-cpu.c.\n\nTwo patches are needed on top: \u003cmemory\u003e for std::unique_ptr in ggml-metal.cpp,\nand a guard around -[MTLSharedEvent waitUntilSignaledValue:timeoutMS:], which\nis macOS 12 while we deploy to 10.15 (11.0 on aarch64).\n\n`mach vendor --patch-mode check` now reproduces the tree.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322929\n", "files": ["third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-common.cpp", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-common.h", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-context.h", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-context.m", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device-m.m", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device.cpp", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device.h", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-impl.h", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-ops.cpp", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-ops.h", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal.cpp", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal.m", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal.metal", "third_party/llama.cpp/metal-event-availability.patch", "third_party/llama.cpp/missing-includes.patch", "third_party/llama.cpp/moz.build", "third_party/llama.cpp/moz.yaml", "third_party/llama.cpp/run_parser.py"], "git_node": "1e6254cb9780625db2213495c565341406af8ee2", "git_parents": ["e3c5c2dbeca9202196b33559e9f1fcdee01f3691"], "node": "257df0560db00cb109e5f806b91e11699a8f0e81", "parents": ["f464a4c8ac528e019663398f794f87831afa86b4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandra Borovova \u003caborovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068871 - Update metadata for html/semantics/interactive-elements/the-summary-element/interactive-content.html.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323193\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/interactive-elements/the-summary-element/interactive-content.html.ini"], "git_node": "c610e7b246e4f6643b6d9b084e11db57ee2499d3", "git_parents": ["1e6254cb9780625db2213495c565341406af8ee2"], "node": "953c9726ad57850599875ffe49836a27bfeecd84", "parents": ["257df0560db00cb109e5f806b91e11699a8f0e81"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Arnaud Bienner \u003cabienner@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066923 - Quota manager: use signed integers for usage values which we know can underflow. r=dom-storage-reviewers,jari\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322186\n", "files": ["dom/quota/ActorsParent.cpp", "dom/quota/Assertions.cpp", "dom/quota/Assertions.h", "dom/quota/AssertionsImpl.h", "dom/quota/CanonicalQuotaObject.cpp", "dom/quota/ClientUsageArray.cpp", "dom/quota/ClientUsageArray.h", "dom/quota/CommonMetadata.cpp", "dom/quota/CommonMetadata.h", "dom/quota/GroupInfo.cpp", "dom/quota/GroupInfo.h", "dom/quota/OriginInfo.cpp", "dom/quota/OriginInfo.h", "dom/quota/OriginOperations.cpp", "dom/quota/QuotaManager.h", "dom/quota/QuotaResults.cpp"], "git_node": "fa9a83b65bd9849e92a6293bdca583a811f0955c", "git_parents": ["c610e7b246e4f6643b6d9b084e11db57ee2499d3"], "node": "26dfca9c0180abf68e21a3c37e2439e7d5eacac0", "parents": ["953c9726ad57850599875ffe49836a27bfeecd84"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067971. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322591\n", "files": ["image/decoders/nsJPEGDecoder.cpp"], "git_node": "e310acdf34b11303e088741e3570584eccea0a54", "git_parents": ["fa9a83b65bd9849e92a6293bdca583a811f0955c"], "node": "045bf969c45ca9c0131fc8a73776099d2104f5c7", "parents": ["26dfca9c0180abf68e21a3c37e2439e7d5eacac0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dave Townsend \u003cdtownsend@oxymoronical.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068619: Don't allow external callers to set the isInitial parameter to init. r=niklas\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322933\n", "files": ["browser/components/profiles/SelectableProfileService.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "f022e98032cebe2dcf05e56fe06384c620afc778", "git_parents": ["e310acdf34b11303e088741e3570584eccea0a54"], "node": "28eeb0f4994cd94b0b379f387660b58fa8698393", "parents": ["045bf969c45ca9c0131fc8a73776099d2104f5c7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Eden Chuang \u003cechuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2001265 - Enforce Local Network Access checks on notification icon loads r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nNotification icon loads have no requesting node, so their LoadInfo has no\nbrowsing context and the parent IP address space resolved to Unknown, which\nmakes IsLocalOrPrivateNetworkAccess() false for any target. Read the address\nspace from the policy container instead, which Document::InitPolicyContainer\nalready propagates for exactly this reason, and share that resolution with\nthe two copies of it in nsHttpChannel.\n\nThese loads have no tab to anchor a permission prompt on, and can outlive the\npage that created the notification, so treat them like shared and service\nworker requests: never prompt, and only allow when the origin already has a\npersistent LNA permission.\n\nAlso add a regression test for the document CSP being applied to these loads.\nThat already works, since bug 1997282 moved icon decoding into the content\nprocess and the load carries the creating global's ClientInfo, but it is the\nother half of this bug and was untested.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319466\n", "files": ["dom/notification/test/mochitest/file_notification_icon_csp.html", "dom/notification/test/mochitest/file_notification_icon_csp_self.html", "dom/notification/test/mochitest/mochitest.toml", "dom/notification/test/mochitest/test_notification_icon_csp.html", "netwerk/base/LNAPermissionRequest.cpp", "netwerk/base/nsNetUtil.cpp", "netwerk/base/nsNetUtil.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpChannel.cpp", "netwerk/test/browser/browser.toml", "netwerk/test/browser/browser_test_local_network_access_notification.js", "netwerk/test/browser/page_notification_icon.html"], "git_node": "de4391eeaa52a35ba7a188105c5ab629f6f6c4b7", "git_parents": ["f022e98032cebe2dcf05e56fe06384c620afc778"], "node": "0e553e6c8de9c652d2989229aa3303aad7778bcc", "parents": ["28eeb0f4994cd94b0b379f387660b58fa8698393"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Eden Chuang \u003cechuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053725 - Enable Async Clipboard custom format support in nightly. r=edgar\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322579\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "a37a5ac4acfefab57cbdea6aca111f32ca5c8318", "git_parents": ["de4391eeaa52a35ba7a188105c5ab629f6f6c4b7"], "node": "5f85543ca897ac68906baa90d3c976a0cb61b346", "parents": ["0e553e6c8de9c652d2989229aa3303aad7778bcc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "giorga \u003cgiorga@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054384 - Download notifications should truncate long filenames in the middle. r=android-reviewers,tthibaud\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321546\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/downloads/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/downloads/DownloadNotification.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/downloads/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/downloads/DownloadNotificationTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/support/ktx/src/main/java/mozilla/components/support/ktx/kotlin/String.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/support/ktx/src/test/java/mozilla/components/support/ktx/kotlin/StringTest.kt"], "git_node": "37969182a870be7a98f336c2eaf8d4eb22769f76", "git_parents": ["a37a5ac4acfefab57cbdea6aca111f32ca5c8318"], "node": "d8de459a2e39249ea48ddd51c1b3cdb64ce69961", "parents": ["5f85543ca897ac68906baa90d3c976a0cb61b346"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@proton.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065919 - Check shutdown again before async write on read fulfill r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322987\n", "files": ["dom/streams/ReadableStreamPipeTo.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/streams/piping/crashtests/shutdown.html"], "git_node": "8f580a73d6b904bfcf94fbd7e087595d3bd2db27", "git_parents": ["37969182a870be7a98f336c2eaf8d4eb22769f76"], "node": "01a2a5bb2e637d83b4682ac4df8a3c37ec9ff1dd", "parents": ["d8de459a2e39249ea48ddd51c1b3cdb64ce69961"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sotaro Ikeda \u003csotaro.ikeda.g@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067381 - Remove RemoteDecoderVideoSubDescriptor r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nBy Bug 2066982 fix, RemoteDecoderVideoSubDescriptor could be removed.\nThe content process does not need full RemoteDecoderVideoSubDescriptor.\nIn compositing process, necessary SurfaceDescriptor could be got from TextureHost of VideoBridgeParent.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322054\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.cpp", "dom/canvas/ClientWebGLContext.cpp", "dom/canvas/TexUnpackBlob.cpp", "dom/canvas/WebGLTextureUpload.cpp", "dom/webgpu/ExternalTexture.cpp", "gfx/layers/BufferTexture.h", "gfx/layers/DcompSurfaceImage.cpp", "gfx/layers/DcompSurfaceImage.h", "gfx/layers/LayersTypes.h", "gfx/layers/client/TextureClient.cpp", "gfx/layers/client/TextureClient.h", "gfx/layers/composite/TextureHost.h", "gfx/layers/d3d11/TextureD3D11.cpp", "gfx/layers/d3d11/TextureD3D11.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/CanvasTranslator.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/LayersMessageUtils.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/LayersSurfaces.ipdlh", "gfx/layers/opengl/DMABUFTextureClientOGL.cpp", "gfx/layers/opengl/DMABUFTextureClientOGL.h", "gfx/layers/opengl/DMABUFTextureHostOGL.cpp", "gfx/layers/opengl/DMABUFTextureHostOGL.h", "gfx/layers/opengl/MacIOSurfaceTextureClientOGL.cpp", "gfx/layers/opengl/MacIOSurfaceTextureClientOGL.h", "gfx/layers/opengl/MacIOSurfaceTextureHostOGL.cpp", "gfx/layers/opengl/MacIOSurfaceTextureHostOGL.h", "gfx/layers/opengl/TextureClientOGL.cpp", "gfx/layers/opengl/TextureClientOGL.h", "gfx/layers/opengl/TextureHostOGL.cpp", "gfx/layers/opengl/TextureHostOGL.h"], "git_node": "38e471d38fba9277ec978868eadefb75de06abf0", "git_parents": ["8f580a73d6b904bfcf94fbd7e087595d3bd2db27"], "node": "6529e985896f507ec0a42105996f518c24660100", "parents": ["01a2a5bb2e637d83b4682ac4df8a3c37ec9ff1dd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandru Marc \u003camarc@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2065919 - Check shutdown again before async write on read fulfill r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\" for causing lint failure @ shutdown.html\n\nThis reverts commit 8f580a73d6b904bfcf94fbd7e087595d3bd2db27.\n", "files": ["dom/streams/ReadableStreamPipeTo.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/streams/piping/crashtests/shutdown.html"], "git_node": "73db385bb2d47d005dc340c54da0a5517bea8cf4", "git_parents": ["38e471d38fba9277ec978868eadefb75de06abf0"], "node": "d61cc4782572c690a06ecbc739b209442a475a83", "parents": ["6529e985896f507ec0a42105996f518c24660100"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Mehic \u003cdmehic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061367 - Remove the Legacy Telemetry mirrors of the strip_on_share probes r=timhuang,urlbar-reviewers,chumphreys,Standard8\n\nOnly the Legacy Telemetry mirrors are removed. The Glean metrics\ncontentblocking.strip_on_share_params_removed and\ncontentblocking.strip_on_share_length_decrease are left in place, so what\nFirefox collects is unchanged. StripForCopyOrShare in URLQueryStringStripper.cpp\nalready records exclusively through Glean, so no instrumentation changes are\nneeded.\n\nbrowser_strip_on_share_telemetry.js asserted on the legacy histograms only, with\nno Glean equivalent to fall back on, so those assertions are converted to Glean\nrather than dropped. The legacy assertions checked that a single sample landed\nin the bucket for the expected value; the Glean equivalents check the\ndistribution sum and count, which pins the recorded values exactly rather than\nto a bucket. TelemetryTestUtils is no longer used and its import is removed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317373\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser_strip_on_share_telemetry.js", "toolkit/components/antitracking/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/telemetry/Histograms.json"], "git_node": "3b2333671ed43a9b6f2c888acf50e62edf6c4283", "git_parents": ["73db385bb2d47d005dc340c54da0a5517bea8cf4"], "node": "e4913fabc916a256730f81da33ea40c6a4547c1e", "parents": ["d61cc4782572c690a06ecbc739b209442a475a83"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jieke Jiang \u003cjieke@live.cn\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067179 - Remove unused AboutReaderParent._getArticle. r=firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,dao\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323185\n", "files": ["browser/actors/AboutReaderParent.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "c1549b739a729bf4f2b67454f25d3123e80c8784", "git_parents": ["3b2333671ed43a9b6f2c888acf50e62edf6c4283"], "node": "dccd5616f27edec466823f53de46bb29857583aa", "parents": ["e4913fabc916a256730f81da33ea40c6a4547c1e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068615 - Give the open bar's top corners the input's radius plus the background's overhang. r=daisuke,daleharvey\n\nThe address bar's radii come out unchanged: it derived the overhang from the radius, and this derives the radius from the overhang. Touch density is the exception, gaining a pixel of each. The New Tab bar takes the shared overhang, which it can now that it only runs with Nova enabled.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322925\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/urlbar.css"], "git_node": "f68397b608876f4ab5063883be483cb737a07083", "git_parents": ["c1549b739a729bf4f2b67454f25d3123e80c8784"], "node": "487ea5c179ccac02352d1fcfc5a9b72ae0788ae0", "parents": ["dccd5616f27edec466823f53de46bb29857583aa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Antonio Borondo \u003caborondo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066065 - Add a new command-line argument to receive push messages r=hsohaney,firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,mossop,saschanaz\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320937\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/moz.build", "toolkit/components/push/PushCommandLineHandler.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/push/components.conf", "toolkit/components/push/moz.build", "toolkit/components/push/test/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/push/test/browser/browser_receive_push_messages.js"], "git_node": "0e01e9de979884d19ac9f6d203a9d913b1504fac", "git_parents": ["f68397b608876f4ab5063883be483cb737a07083"], "node": "1a33de43db56c08bf9444524743288954ff3e018", "parents": ["487ea5c179ccac02352d1fcfc5a9b72ae0788ae0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Antonio Borondo \u003caborondo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066065 - Don't receive push messages if Firefox is already running r=firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,mossop,saschanaz\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320938\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/push/PushCommandLineHandler.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/push/test/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/push/test/browser/browser_receive_push_messages.js", "toolkit/components/push/test/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "ecde6b6dd8b2c6a45e861a4a6e30dac11a0d63d7", "git_parents": ["0e01e9de979884d19ac9f6d203a9d913b1504fac"], "node": "6876c8febddc5e16206805de703d7329cb7d78db", "parents": ["1a33de43db56c08bf9444524743288954ff3e018"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Antonio Borondo \u003caborondo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066065 - Don't display a window with the --receive-push-messages argument r=hsohaney,firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,mossop,saschanaz\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321181\n", "files": ["browser/components/BrowserGlue.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/push/PushCommandLineHandler.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/push/test/browser/browser_receive_push_messages.js"], "git_node": "5c793c0c99ffd8f7042d99671277c9b3f8f77605", "git_parents": ["ecde6b6dd8b2c6a45e861a4a6e30dac11a0d63d7"], "node": "0e36171bded3c0562ef38e08d9f739be7edbb2b1", "parents": ["6876c8febddc5e16206805de703d7329cb7d78db"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Antonio Borondo \u003caborondo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066065 - Keep Firefox alive while receiving push messages r=firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,mossop,saschanaz\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321208\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/push/PushCommandLineHandler.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/push/test/browser/browser_receive_push_messages.js"], "git_node": "147ae0b6ae7f4f999237684f12f2e5839276e3df", "git_parents": ["5c793c0c99ffd8f7042d99671277c9b3f8f77605"], "node": "14f2fc6c7b19f100155f48f79e53f529f4d9774f", "parents": ["0e36171bded3c0562ef38e08d9f739be7edbb2b1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Antonio Borondo \u003caborondo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066065 - Ensure the Push Service is ready r=hsohaney,firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,mossop\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321498\n", "files": ["dom/push/PushComponents.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/push/PushCommandLineHandler.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/push/test/browser/browser_receive_push_messages.js"], "git_node": "ee523aa3867eafc4ed0b1be51659abe4a348affd", "git_parents": ["147ae0b6ae7f4f999237684f12f2e5839276e3df"], "node": "b67b81f614212de739422ecd115339fe9f0f7827", "parents": ["14f2fc6c7b19f100155f48f79e53f529f4d9774f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Antonio Borondo \u003caborondo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066065 - Receive push messages r=firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,mossop,saschanaz\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321567\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "toolkit/components/push/PushCommandLineHandler.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/push/test/browser/browser_receive_push_messages.js"], "git_node": "22202314d0db367d032399412736f579bf5eafc1", "git_parents": ["ee523aa3867eafc4ed0b1be51659abe4a348affd"], "node": "ddbbc4f9d6667f0a857a66c167355b85dca24aab", "parents": ["b67b81f614212de739422ecd115339fe9f0f7827"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dave Townsend \u003cdtownsend@oxymoronical.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063316: Remove data relating to background tasks from the downgrade ping as it is never sent from background tasks. r=nika\n\nHandleDetectedDowngrade bails out when run headlessly which is the case for background tasks, so we\ncurrently never submit a downgrade ping from a background task so none of the fields added to track\nthe background task state are ever set.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320427\n", "files": ["toolkit/xre/nsAppRunner.cpp"], "git_node": "d303bd05637383dec423dbb1087867cffdccbe2b", "git_parents": ["22202314d0db367d032399412736f579bf5eafc1"], "node": "927331e571ec4740c07c3ae86b86fa888650be18", "parents": ["ddbbc4f9d6667f0a857a66c167355b85dca24aab"], "tags": []}, {"author": "delan azabani \u003cdazabani@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067041 - Editor support for Sublime Text. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,emilio,sergesanspaille,ahochheiden\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321804\n", "files": [".gitignore", ".hgignore", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/mach_commands.py"], "git_node": "30e331dd82c63d0251f571a2b5c388adbaf3ee61", "git_parents": ["d303bd05637383dec423dbb1087867cffdccbe2b"], "node": "ca8c07599c051c08d814c9d5b262263f9ff5bbdd", "parents": ["927331e571ec4740c07c3ae86b86fa888650be18"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063947. Reapply libFuzzer's local patches to the vendored sources. r=truber\n\nThe five patches listed in moz.yaml are not applied to the vendored sources. FuzzerIO.cpp\nin the tree is byte for byte identical to compiler-rt/lib/fuzzer/FuzzerIO.cpp at the\nrevision moz.yaml records, and the same holds for the other fourteen files this touches, so\nthe sources went in without the patch step when libFuzzer was upgraded in bug 1996685.\n\nIt does not seem like it was an intentional decision to drop them. The same change rebased\nall five patch files against the new upstream and deleted a sixth,\n14-explicit-allocator.patch, which is the opposite of what retiring the rest would look\nlike. They were added deliberately too: bug 1635762 added four of them along with vendoring\nlibFuzzer from git, and bug 1695761 added 15-return-to-exit so that libFuzzer returns\ninstead of calling exit(), as its title says.\n\nPatches are applied by a separate `mach vendor --patch-mode only` step, so it is easy for\nthe sources to go in without them, and until now nothing checked that vendoring reproduced\nwhat is committed.\n\nAlso point the moz.yaml at Core :: Fuzzing rather than Core :: General, which is where\nlibFuzzer bugs are filed anyway, including the upgrade in bug 1996685. Updatebot files from\nthat block, so its update bugs were going to the wrong place.\n\nThis is what `./mach vendor tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/moz.yaml -r\n5b7a5f7c5f3c1dcd8ea9debf56983b85e393bc86 --patch-mode check --force` produces, so the\npatches still apply cleanly and no rebasing was needed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318987\n", "files": ["taskcluster/scripts/misc/vendor-verify-expected-fail.yml", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerDataFlowTrace.cpp", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerDataFlowTrace.h", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerDriver.cpp", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerFork.cpp", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerFork.h", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerIO.cpp", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerIO.h", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerIOPosix.cpp", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerIOWindows.cpp", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerInternal.h", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerLoop.cpp", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerMerge.cpp", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerMerge.h", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerTracePC.cpp", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerTracePC.h", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "588c704a86c005116227f43b260da8870e781a60", "git_parents": ["30e331dd82c63d0251f571a2b5c388adbaf3ee61"], "node": "8a5cef2ca45c8f8f95405fc1ac0d596d4bf50eba", "parents": ["ca8c07599c051c08d814c9d5b262263f9ff5bbdd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063947. Fix a corrupted hunk in libFuzzer's 15-return-to-exit.patch. r=truber\n\nThe previous patch busted the build because one hunk in 15-return-to-exit.patch is\nmalformed. It changes WriteNewControlFile to take a size_t &NumFiles out-param, but the\nline removing the old end of the parameter list is missing, so the generated\nFuzzerMerge.cpp closes the parameter list twice:\n\n                    const std::vector\u003cMergeFileInfo\u003e &KnownFiles) {\n                    size_t &NumFiles) {\n\nThe hunk was correct before bug 1996685 rebased it against the new upstream, where the\n\"-\" line was dropped along with the patches themselves. Restoring it is the whole fix;\nthe hunk's line counts were already right for the corrected form.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320103\n", "files": ["tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerMerge.cpp", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/patches/15-return-to-exit.patch"], "git_node": "e1671e244b977ad1b24824b49acb80e9c437d89d", "git_parents": ["588c704a86c005116227f43b260da8870e781a60"], "node": "af84a2d5e492f38599ee59606566a875dbbf11bb", "parents": ["8a5cef2ca45c8f8f95405fc1ac0d596d4bf50eba"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2066923 - Quota manager: use signed integers for usage values which we know can underflow. r=dom-storage-reviewers,jari\" for causing build bustages in nsRFPService.cpp.\n\nThis reverts commit fa9a83b65bd9849e92a6293bdca583a811f0955c.\n", "files": ["dom/quota/ActorsParent.cpp", "dom/quota/Assertions.cpp", "dom/quota/Assertions.h", "dom/quota/AssertionsImpl.h", "dom/quota/CanonicalQuotaObject.cpp", "dom/quota/ClientUsageArray.cpp", "dom/quota/ClientUsageArray.h", "dom/quota/CommonMetadata.cpp", "dom/quota/CommonMetadata.h", "dom/quota/GroupInfo.cpp", "dom/quota/GroupInfo.h", "dom/quota/OriginInfo.cpp", "dom/quota/OriginInfo.h", "dom/quota/OriginOperations.cpp", "dom/quota/QuotaManager.h", "dom/quota/QuotaResults.cpp"], "git_node": "b46a320e038177a9573d9e4203529a22062e7d6d", "git_parents": ["e1671e244b977ad1b24824b49acb80e9c437d89d"], "node": "9a4a36bd4a0272d284b53a189d7b42b0f202a95d", "parents": ["af84a2d5e492f38599ee59606566a875dbbf11bb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2051973 - Vendor the Metal backend at the pinned llama.cpp revision. r=ai-platform-reviewers,valentinp\" for causing @ ggml_metal_encoder_set_pipeline related mochitests failures.\n\nThis reverts commit 1e6254cb9780625db2213495c565341406af8ee2.\n", "files": ["third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-common.cpp", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-common.h", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-context.h", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-context.m", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device-m.m", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device.cpp", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device.h", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-impl.h", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-ops.cpp", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-ops.h", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal.cpp", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal.m", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal.metal", "third_party/llama.cpp/metal-event-availability.patch", "third_party/llama.cpp/missing-includes.patch", "third_party/llama.cpp/moz.build", "third_party/llama.cpp/moz.yaml", "third_party/llama.cpp/run_parser.py"], "git_node": "e632432a41206c04c00ac25588ebaef5987bd07b", "git_parents": ["b46a320e038177a9573d9e4203529a22062e7d6d"], "node": "d6eeba45df1919e40156ddaa1345b0bee8602abb", "parents": ["9a4a36bd4a0272d284b53a189d7b42b0f202a95d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2067041 - Editor support for Sublime Text. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,emilio,sergesanspaille,ahochheiden\" for causing vendor failures.\n\nThis reverts commit 30e331dd82c63d0251f571a2b5c388adbaf3ee61.\n", "files": [".gitignore", ".hgignore", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/mach_commands.py"], "git_node": "80c11dc756df2ecbe7c3f59640d2590c33e3f40d", "git_parents": ["e632432a41206c04c00ac25588ebaef5987bd07b"], "node": "1c8fe246f6ff62657942a8a52201ee4b011b3602", "parents": ["d6eeba45df1919e40156ddaa1345b0bee8602abb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068440 - Validate fieldset listed elements. r=smaug,dom-core-reviewers\n\nMake sure we have a fieldset. We can't check _which_ fieldset because\nfieldset.elements work across multiple fieldsets.\n\nTrack elements inside legends and check the disabled-ness more\nexplicitly instead.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322883\n", "files": ["dom/html/HTMLElement.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLFieldSetElement.cpp", "dom/html/nsGenericHTMLElement.cpp", "dom/html/nsGenericHTMLElement.h", "testing/web-platform/tests/custom-elements/form-associated/fieldset-elements-after-upgrade.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/custom-elements/form-associated/fieldset-elements-during-construction.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/custom-elements/form-associated/form-disabled-legend.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-fieldset-element/disabled-nested-legend.html"], "git_node": "c77e3d9e37632230256c8d678a0fae4fabbd03a5", "git_parents": ["80c11dc756df2ecbe7c3f59640d2590c33e3f40d"], "node": "d838c072cbf148fe3855e0908d69fcb571d5387e", "parents": ["1c8fe246f6ff62657942a8a52201ee4b011b3602"], "tags": []}, {"author": "@Giulia Cardieri \u003cgcardieri@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066894: fix smart window switcher on vertical tabs and browser update r=sfoster,Mardak\n\nalso fix organize tabs for initial vertical tabs\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322003\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AIWindow.sys.mjs", "browser/components/customizableui/CustomizableUI.sys.mjs", "browser/components/customizableui/test/browser.toml", "browser/components/customizableui/test/browser_vertical_tabs_default_area.js"], "git_node": "bbc3f31a2a1ecc744866a9def919bb78fbaac225", "git_parents": ["c77e3d9e37632230256c8d678a0fae4fabbd03a5"], "node": "e3b125ef4440ae80386f3133ec53ad61476f53af", "parents": ["d838c072cbf148fe3855e0908d69fcb571d5387e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kershaw Chang \u003ckershaw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063452 - Give h3-only connection infos their own connection entry, r=mxinden,necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nEager Alt-Svc H3 validation marks its connection info as `Http3Only`, so Happy Eyeballs races H3 without a TCP fallback. Previously, this attempt shared the origin's `ConnectionEntry`, allowing a normal transaction to claim a race that could never fall back to TCP. At the same time, the unconnected UDP attempt kept `HasActiveH3Connection()` true, causing `AtActiveConnectionLimit()` to reject any new connections to the origin. When UDP was blocked, the origin was effectively pinned to this single connection attempt until it was reaped.\n\nThis patch combines `Http3Disabled` and `Http3Only` into a single `Http3Policy` field and gives H3-only connection info a separate hash key (`[h3only]`, alongside the existing `[!h3]`). This isolates H3-only attempts in their own connection entry. Once an H3 connection is successfully established, it is handed over to the origin's regular connection entry.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322675\n", "files": ["netwerk/ipc/NeckoChannelParams.ipdlh", "netwerk/protocol/http/AlternateServices.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/ConnectionEntry.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/ConnectionEntry.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/HappyEyeballsConnMgrDelegate.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/HappyEyeballsConnectionAttempt.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http3Session.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http3Session.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpConnectionUDP.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpConnectionUDP.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpChannel.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpConnectionInfo.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpConnectionInfo.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpConnectionMgr.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpConnectionMgr.h", "netwerk/test/gtest/TestHappyEyeballsConnectionAttempt.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_happy_eyeballs_altsvc_h3_only_claim.js", "netwerk/test/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "e72064d9c929b8b6c663a982300b1dbccecb078d", "git_parents": ["bbc3f31a2a1ecc744866a9def919bb78fbaac225"], "node": "45e24e6abbfcb336e2f19a466b7cab67aeb0927a", "parents": ["e3b125ef4440ae80386f3133ec53ad61476f53af"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@proton.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065919 - Check shutdown again before async write on read fulfill r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322987\n", "files": ["dom/streams/ReadableStreamPipeTo.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/streams/piping/crashtests/shutdown.html"], "git_node": "d4bea9f805fc73867ff7ee7a344e86308569dc46", "git_parents": ["e72064d9c929b8b6c663a982300b1dbccecb078d"], "node": "d1eb98680c78518236c3a84df132498eb6e7fdf9", "parents": ["45e24e6abbfcb336e2f19a466b7cab67aeb0927a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harshit \u003chsohaney@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067218 - Setup the push notification helper for windows. r=aborondo\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322008\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "Cargo.toml", "build/workspace-hack/Cargo.toml", "toolkit/moz.build", "toolkit/mozapps/pushnotificationhelper/Cargo.toml", "toolkit/mozapps/pushnotificationhelper/moz.build", "toolkit/mozapps/pushnotificationhelper/src/main.rs"], "git_node": "409169d0ff14d79a929b43dff1299e2d6665a961", "git_parents": ["d4bea9f805fc73867ff7ee7a344e86308569dc46"], "node": "304b4ae0a3afeae0eb031b3e76ae5826bc67488f", "parents": ["d1eb98680c78518236c3a84df132498eb6e7fdf9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emma Zuehlcke \u003cemz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2019300 - Expose BTP purge history with bounce chain context in webcompat reporter. r=twisniewski,android-reviewers,webcompat-reviewers,timhuang,007,data-stewards\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D285069\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/metrics.yaml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/webcompat/middleware/WebCompatReporterSubmissionMiddleware.kt", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/BounceTrackingMapEntry.h", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/BounceTrackingProtection.cpp", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/nsIBounceTrackingProtection.idl", "toolkit/components/reportbrokensite/ReportBrokenSiteChild.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/reportbrokensite/ReportBrokenSiteHelpers.mjs", "toolkit/components/reportbrokensite/ReportBrokenSiteParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/reportbrokensite/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "1067ca5d893b313e6ec364d8054c83962ea59b07", "git_parents": ["409169d0ff14d79a929b43dff1299e2d6665a961"], "node": "23fcfdfa204c282e60280790fcd038351f91bc6e", "parents": ["304b4ae0a3afeae0eb031b3e76ae5826bc67488f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emma Zuehlcke \u003cemz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2019300 - Add tests for BTP purge history in webcompat reporter. r=twisniewski,android-reviewers,webcompat-reviewers,timhuang,007\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D285070\n", "files": ["browser/components/reportbrokensite/test/browser/browser_antitracking_data_sent.js", "browser/components/reportbrokensite/test/browser/send.js", "browser/components/reportbrokensite/test/browser/send_more_info.js", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/webcompat/middleware/WebCompatReporterSubmissionMiddlewareTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/webcompat/testdata/WebCompatTestData.kt", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/test/browser/browser_bouncetracking_simple.js"], "git_node": "521ed3f7207fb4c6a6d6afe8024798f354641626", "git_parents": ["1067ca5d893b313e6ec364d8054c83962ea59b07"], "node": "30aa6ea47cea1927c809a9f5516fa871e0a548dd", "parents": ["23fcfdfa204c282e60280790fcd038351f91bc6e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Moritz Beier \u003cmbeier@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068072 - New Tab search bar searches that open in a new tab are recorded on the results page with an unknown source and no New Tab visit. r=urlbar-reviewers,search-reviewers,dao,scunnane\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322656\n", "files": ["browser/components/search/BrowserSearchTelemetry.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarParentController.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarParentControllerProxy.mjs"], "git_node": "b47d3ef01ab15d2ea976a4793b0812362a8a21a0", "git_parents": ["521ed3f7207fb4c6a6d6afe8024798f354641626"], "node": "0f8ec2a2ccce7a965340d8370a8bfe3e75b57cd9", "parents": ["30aa6ea47cea1927c809a9f5516fa871e0a548dd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "longsonr \u003clongsonr@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068354 - Check whether we're reflowing when observing changes r=emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323194\n", "files": ["layout/svg/SVGObserverUtils.cpp", "layout/svg/SVGTextFrame.cpp"], "git_node": "d9d16f10961bd15b96165f368f1cf4551d837e3c", "git_parents": ["b47d3ef01ab15d2ea976a4793b0812362a8a21a0"], "node": "587f5b19d2749ddf53d38f0631bcbe33b516467b", "parents": ["0f8ec2a2ccce7a965340d8370a8bfe3e75b57cd9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@proton.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068945 - Remove legacy histogram fallback for api_notify r=janerik\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323220\n", "files": ["dom/push/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/telemetry/Histograms.json", "toolkit/components/telemetry/histogram-allowlists.json"], "git_node": "1fb17c