 "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068549 - Use a more reasonable default size for remote browsers. r=layout-reviewers,dshin\n\nThe fallback intrinsic size seems way better than 0, and reasonable\nenough.\n\nThis should fix the various intermittent failures linked from comment 0.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323106\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsFrameLoader.cpp", "layout/generic/nsSubDocumentFrame.cpp"], "git_node": "d2f7c679438a461242399d46d59b6bf9ce046b6a", "git_parents": ["1fb17c60033c0e67f16b038f11ef45594d4daf90"], "node": "140fb57c0552601bbd0f6cd31bfc16e473d5092a", "parents": ["80c3d9ccdbe702460993cdb38b0fb97777335740"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Moritz Beier \u003cmbeier@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068529 - Remove parent controller forwarders in UrlbarChildController. r=dao,urlbar-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322875\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_smartbar_context_paste.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_smartbar_suggestions.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/head.js", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SearchEngineStore.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SearchModeSwitcher.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarChildController.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarChildTelemetry.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarView.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-quickactions/browser_general.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-search/browser_engineStoreQueryGate.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser_dns_first_for_single_words.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser_edit_invalid_url.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser_handleCommand_fallback.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/test_UrlbarProviderSemanticHistorySearch.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/test_UrlbarTelemetryUtils_wireSerialization.js"], "git_node": "40598deabf58b864a55a5068497866712f986928", "git_parents": ["d2f7c679438a461242399d46d59b6bf9ce046b6a"], "node": "7787166afae12a9a6c89d4c9c65a53ed47600e91", "parents": ["140fb57c0552601bbd0f6cd31bfc16e473d5092a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Moritz Beier \u003cmbeier@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068529 - Improve formatting of UrlbarChildController. r=urlbar-reviewers,Standard8\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322876\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarChildController.mjs"], "git_node": "a78d91745d8847f7eb3a0492fe1157f09e70ca71", "git_parents": ["40598deabf58b864a55a5068497866712f986928"], "node": "471fa17a5f7b68fec57b1e494fea009672fb8e4a", "parents": ["7787166afae12a9a6c89d4c9c65a53ed47600e91"], "tags": []}, {"author": "elkal98 \u003ckhalid.alhaddad98@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2046450 - [wdspec] \"browsing_context.locate_nodes\" should return \"nodes\" and not the \"result\". r=whimboo\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322592\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/browser/close/pending_download.py", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/browser/set_download_behavior/download_behavior_allowed.py", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/browsing_context/navigate/error.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/webdriver/webdriver/bidi/modules/browsing_context.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/browsing_context/locate_nodes/context.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/browsing_context/locate_nodes/locator.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/browsing_context/locate_nodes/max_node_count.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/browsing_context/locate_nodes/serialization_options.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/browsing_context/locate_nodes/start_nodes.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/input/perform_actions/wheel.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/network/continue_request/url.py"], "git_node": "08e198f596cc69565af62027953dec10011fa658", "git_parents": ["a78d91745d8847f7eb3a0492fe1157f09e70ca71"], "node": "1c1f844f287f32f939d71bf0421c962b27d7d458", "parents": ["471fa17a5f7b68fec57b1e494fea009672fb8e4a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lars Eggert \u003clars@eggert.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068481 - Don't block the main thread when cancelling off-thread script compilation. r=arai,smaug,dom-core-reviewers\n\nCancelling marks the task and returns: one that has already started runs to\ncompletion off-thread and discards its result, so the HTML parser no longer\nstalls for the remainder of a compile when LookupPreloadRequest drops a\nmismatched speculative preload. The same stall reached this path from module\npreload invalidation, cycle collection and document teardown.\n\nCancelled tasks are waited for at XPCOMShutdownThreads so that one which is\nstill running does not outlive the process-wide frontend state that JS_ShutDown\nfrees. A decode task owns the serialized stencil bytes it reads and returns them\nwhen its result is taken, so that a cancelled decode keeps its input alive.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322872\n", "files": ["dom/script/ScriptLoadContext.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoadContext.h", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.cpp", "js/loader/LoadedScript.h"], "git_node": "71feb2e5c718fb9f8f8157a010c9606a78d61eec", "git_parents": ["08e198f596cc69565af62027953dec10011fa658"], "node": "9114798fde65ed2a4841cfe90e5c0ffe0c5f9292", "parents": ["1c1f844f287f32f939d71bf0421c962b27d7d458"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068601 - Keep rule matching loop tight. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nThe issue seems to be that since we're passing `element` by value, and\nmutating, but then passing it by reference around to selectors llvm adds\na stack-to-stack copy of the element per iteration, which grows this\nsuper-hot loop enough.\n\nMeasured locally, but try push imminent.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323065\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/selector_map.rs", "servo/components/style/stylist.rs"], "git_node": "0a9f66d2ab2f21a22d540027435ec7c7bf48f1d9", "git_parents": ["71feb2e5c718fb9f8f8157a010c9606a78d61eec"], "node": "aeb5b9469c52f226708d853614c5f0d52e9aa41b", "parents": ["9114798fde65ed2a4841cfe90e5c0ffe0c5f9292"], "tags": []}, {"author": "ISHIKAWA, Chiaki \u003cishikawa@yk.rim.or.jp\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2031796 - TSAN_OPTIONS set by user is overwritten by mochitestharness., r=mozbase-reviewers,ahal\n\nTSAN_OPTIONS set in environment is overwritten by mochitest harness, preventing user-set options from reaching the browser process\n\nIn testing/mozbase/mozrunner/mozrunner/utils.py, test_environment() sets TSAN_OPTIONS for the browser process with a blind assignment:\npython\n\ntsan = bool(mozinfo.info.get(\"tsan\"))\nif tsan and mozinfo.isLinux:\n    if os.path.isfile(llvmsym):\n        env[\"TSAN_OPTIONS\"] = \"external_symbolizer_path=%s\" % llvmsym\n\nAlthough env is initialized from os.environ.copy(), this line silently discards any TSAN_OPTIONS the user had set in their shell \u2014 for example, suppressions for local system libraries not covered by __tsan_default_suppressions() in build/sanitizers/TsanOptions.cpp.\n\nWithout being able to pass TSAN_OPTIONS, some browser mochitest tests hang on TSAN builds because unsuppressed races in system libraries (e.g. libglycin) slow GTK window operations beyond the test timeout.\n\nNote that runxpcshelltests.py already handles this correctly by reading and appending to the existing value. This fix brings mozrunner/utils.py in line with that approach.\n\nVerified: After this fix, browser mochitest tests that were previously hanging on a local TSAN build now run successfully when TSAN_OPTIONS is set appropriately in the shell.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D294265\n", "files": ["testing/mozbase/mozrunner/mozrunner/utils.py"], "git_node": "235b7ac8c2e9ad7d53c6b0ed612724e9496e7cae", "git_parents": ["0a9f66d2ab2f21a22d540027435ec7c7bf48f1d9"], "node": "593c085f82494c752929c3364c30941e7f198bd6", "parents": ["aeb5b9469c52f226708d853614c5f0d52e9aa41b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandru Marc \u003camarc@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2065919 - Check shutdown again before async write on read fulfill r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\" for causing multiple failures\n\nThis reverts commit d4bea9f805fc73867ff7ee7a344e86308569dc46.\n", "files": ["dom/streams/ReadableStreamPipeTo.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/streams/piping/crashtests/shutdown.html"], "git_node": "f88dc2eee3af6587d116aa5af8d5c5c095d144ab", "git_parents": ["235b7ac8c2e9ad7d53c6b0ed612724e9496e7cae"], "node": "f7c617595dfad5ea4516dcc26549accaf748adaf", "parents": ["593c085f82494c752929c3364c30941e7f198bd6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068673 - Remove legacy telemetry mirrors for dom.contentprocess.os_priority_*. r=mconley,TravisLong\n\nAs of bug 1923028, these are now recorded directly with Glean,\nso the legacy telemetry mirrors are no longer needed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323016\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/ProcessPriorityManager.cpp", "dom/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/telemetry/Scalars.yaml"], "git_node": "4e730eb91b7ea13b4edc9e90b22d8996c583ab2c", "git_parents": ["f88dc2eee3af6587d116aa5af8d5c5c095d144ab"], "node": "6f3b511e31500e83bfd3d98e4b0d90563cc48d50", "parents": ["f7c617595dfad5ea4516dcc26549accaf748adaf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068956 - Update android nightly application-services version bump to a0dafe8407bda1e01477a319adc66ee3036def9a r=release-managers,pascalc\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323232\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/plugins/dependencies/src/main/java/ApplicationServices.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/plugins/dependencies/src/main/java/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "ab6b374b43739155e02982244a71133ef94b5724", "git_parents": ["4e730eb91b7ea13b4edc9e90b22d8996c583ab2c"], "node": "167981bfa246c3212311c4e7d74dec5bd81db79b", "parents": ["6f3b511e31500e83bfd3d98e4b0d90563cc48d50"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Schuster \u003ctschuster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066321 - Update nonceable attribute checks for link elements. r=freddyb\n\nPending PR: https://github.com/w3c/webappsec-csp/pull/810\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322966\n", "files": ["dom/security/nsContentSecurityUtils.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/content-security-policy/script-src/non-nonceable-elements.html.ini"], "git_node": "14faf842ea3b514671b36a2d30e221525e976454", "git_parents": ["ab6b374b43739155e02982244a71133ef94b5724"], "node": "2a5d4037875690fc82bbd47ef047e07e9cee4808", "parents": ["167981bfa246c3212311c4e7d74dec5bd81db79b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Marco Bonardo \u003cmbonardo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066019. r=Standard8,places-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321246\n", "files": ["browser/components/places/content/controller.js", "browser/components/places/tests/browser/browser_toolbar_drop_bookmarklet.js", "browser/components/places/tests/browser/browser_toolbar_drop_multiple_with_bookmarklet.js"], "git_node": "5bef4181fda733de08a1f349406897679db53dda", "git_parents": ["14faf842ea3b514671b36a2d30e221525e976454"], "node": "868296537d2b9e4959a4f3ff934767f8a21c27e8", "parents": ["2a5d4037875690fc82bbd47ef047e07e9cee4808"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064785 - Clear both whitespace flags in nsTextFrame::Init. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323217\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsTextFrame.cpp"], "git_node": "530d1b729c49b5e072a81d205cd3a741c20e6ad0", "git_parents": ["5bef4181fda733de08a1f349406897679db53dda"], "node": "be055b2e34b74c4c3f1ae77c8a35bbee3ad12eb0", "parents": ["868296537d2b9e4959a4f3ff934767f8a21c27e8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064785 - Add testcase as a crashtest. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323218\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ruby/crashtests/whitespace-reframe.html"], "git_node": "725832dc97491ce1bf95f62b00f266f4c6cf7d0c", "git_parents": ["530d1b729c49b5e072a81d205cd3a741c20e6ad0"], "node": "6d9e7247ee6947d3d6c0ccc5064076a243c36431", "parents": ["be055b2e34b74c4c3f1ae77c8a35bbee3ad12eb0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068684 - Coalesce the select option list ancestor walks r=emilio\n\nFour places walked an option's ancestors to work out which select or optgroup\nit belongs to, each with its own copy of the boundary and nested-optgroup\nrules: HTMLOptionsCollection::IsValidOption, HTMLOptionElement's disabled state\nand cached nearest ancestor select, and HTMLSelectElement::IsOptionDisabled.\n\nThis change generalises HTMLOptionElement::ComputeNearestAncestorSelect into a\nsingle HTMLSelectElement::ComputeNearestAncestors, which takes any node and\nreturns both the nearest ancestor select and the optgroup that groups it, and\nrefactors all four callers to use it. IsOptionListBoundary moves alongside it,\nso that the whole option list concept lives in HTMLSelectElement.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322996\n", "files": ["dom/html/HTMLOptGroupElement.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLOptionElement.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLOptionElement.h", "dom/html/HTMLOptionsCollection.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLSelectElement.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLSelectElement.h"], "git_node": "da3254486e4adca3391f740158adafc82f0e3078", "git_parents": ["725832dc97491ce1bf95f62b00f266f4c6cf7d0c"], "node": "48e50fda4cf46fd8d8fd911133f5b0672e52b31a", "parents": ["6d9e7247ee6947d3d6c0ccc5064076a243c36431"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068707 - Recognise a placeholder label option inside a wrapper element r=emilio\n\n`\u003cselect required\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003coption value=\"\" selected\u003e\u003c/option\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/select\u003e` does\nnot match :invalid, but it should. The option is in the select's list of\noptions, so it is selected and counts as a value, but IsValueMissing doesn't\ntreat it as the placeholder label option because its parent node is a `\u003cdiv\u003e`\nrather than the select.\n\nThis is also a spec bug, as the spec mentions the parent element should be a\n`\u003cselect\u003e`. https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/12892 has been filed to\naddress this in spec.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323011\n", "files": ["dom/html/HTMLSelectElement.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/placeholder-label-option-wrapper.html"], "git_node": "3e5fa42a8ebbbbe467e36b871f22c1696a7f2741", "git_parents": ["da3254486e4adca3391f740158adafc82f0e3078"], "node": "c33dbc0b9e2e643fb80a40260232db64834ae798", "parents": ["48e50fda4cf46fd8d8fd911133f5b0672e52b31a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068709 - Count listbox rows from the DOM's option list r=emilio,layout-reviewers\n\nnsListControlFrame::CountOptionsAndOptgroups walked the frame tree to count\nrows, checking each content to determine if it was an option element. It can\ninstead walk the DOM to get the same info. By counting frames it became\nyet-another copy of the option list traversal, and had the same issue around\ndeeply traversing option lists due to parser relaxation.\n\nThis change moves more of the option list traversal code into HTMLSelectElement,\nand calls out to it in nsListControlFrame.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323013\n", "files": ["dom/html/HTMLSelectElement.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLSelectElement.h", "layout/forms/nsListControlFrame.cpp"], "git_node": "3b182041b584f40f531e10e835cb72ca9b51273f", "git_parents": ["3e5fa42a8ebbbbe467e36b871f22c1696a7f2741"], "node": "6079b49cfe704601d1710a34332f5f6e1f757b3f", "parents": ["c33dbc0b9e2e643fb80a40260232db64834ae798"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068633 - Fall back to the handoff search bar on New Tab when Nova is disabled. r=mbeier,mconley\n\nThe bar is only themed for Nova, so this stands until Proton is removed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322943\n", "files": ["browser/components/search/SearchUIUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarNewTabComponentRegistrant.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarPrefs.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-newtab/browser.toml", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/test_UrlbarNewTabComponentRegistrant.js"], "git_node": "4804f518f1bd382d8cb2e2fb7d701f61874add6c", "git_parents": ["3b182041b584f40f531e10e835cb72ca9b51273f"], "node": "039c1aeb9626de4e629bf1493f56570f3bc474b4", "parents": ["6079b49cfe704601d1710a34332f5f6e1f757b3f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "kycn \u003c35106533+kycn@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067066 - Add browser_thumbnails.capture_attempted labeled counter. r=android-reviewers,pollymce\n\nIntroduces BrowserThumbnailsFacts and wires the capture_attempted metric\nend-to-end: labeled by the trigger that fired the capture (load_completed,\ntab_counter_click, external_request). Routed from AC via the Fact\nframework and recorded to Glean from Fenix's MetricController.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321871\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/thumbnails/build.gradle", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/thumbnails/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/thumbnails/BrowserThumbnails.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/thumbnails/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/thumbnails/facts/BrowserThumbnailsFacts.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/thumbnails/src/test/java/mozilla/components/browser/thumbnails/BrowserThumbnailsTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/thumbnails/src/test/java/mozilla/components/browser/thumbnails/facts/BrowserThumbnailsFactsTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/metrics.yaml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/BaseBrowserFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/BrowserFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/metrics/MetricController.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/toolbar/BrowserToolbarMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/metrics/MetricControllerTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/toolbar/BrowserToolbarMiddlewareTest.kt"], "git_node": "df7ff08258fc964189342420bcd87eacb4246f2b", "git_parents": ["4804f518f1bd382d8cb2e2fb7d701f61874add6c"], "node": "77b76b1db87defe4214aa7c2d0a7d382ddda60a5", "parents": ["039c1aeb9626de4e629bf1493f56570f3bc474b4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "kycn \u003c35106533+kycn@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067066 - Add browser_thumbnails.capture_result labeled counter. r=android-reviewers,pollymce\n\nRecords the outcome of each capture attempt (succeeded, null_bitmap,\nlow_memory) via Fact emission from BrowserThumbnails and routing to\nGlean in Fenix's MetricController. Ratio of succeeded / total quantifies\nthe compositor-detach race and low-memory gate rate.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322676\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/thumbnails/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/thumbnails/BrowserThumbnails.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/thumbnails/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/thumbnails/facts/BrowserThumbnailsFacts.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/thumbnails/src/test/java/mozilla/components/browser/thumbnails/BrowserThumbnailsTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/metrics.yaml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/metrics/MetricController.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/metrics/MetricControllerTest.kt"], "git_node": "0563b41653b220d067f4c39957b5dc1f9106c82c", "git_parents": ["df7ff08258fc964189342420bcd87eacb4246f2b"], "node": "c78875da55c8cf2f6f0ff5584efd1b868dfe72cf", "parents": ["77b76b1db87defe4214aa7c2d0a7d382ddda60a5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "kycn \u003c35106533+kycn@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067066 - Add browser_thumbnails.capture_duration timing distribution. r=android-reviewers,pollymce\n\nRecords wall-clock time from EngineView.captureThumbnail() to its\nonFinish callback. Emits a Fact with the duration in metadata on every\ncallback (regardless of outcome), routed to Glean in Fenix's\nMetricController via accumulateSamples. Long tails indicate compositor\npressure or surface-teardown races.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322677\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/thumbnails/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/thumbnails/BrowserThumbnails.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/thumbnails/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/thumbnails/facts/BrowserThumbnailsFacts.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/thumbnails/src/test/java/mozilla/components/browser/thumbnails/BrowserThumbnailsTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/metrics.yaml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/metrics/MetricController.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/metrics/MetricControllerTest.kt"], "git_node": "de317d9434025aab819a2bb87e21e140fd2c7b47", "git_parents": ["0563b41653b220d067f4c39957b5dc1f9106c82c"], "node": "3ca65623fb95089509fd0d26a73499d0d133b26d", "parents": ["c78875da55c8cf2f6f0ff5584efd1b868dfe72cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "kycn \u003c35106533+kycn@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067066 - Add browser_thumbnails.disk_write_duration timing distribution. r=android-reviewers,pollymce\n\nMeasures wall-clock time from ThumbnailsMiddleware dispatching a\nThumbnailStorage.saveThumbnail(...) job to that job's completion via\ninvokeOnCompletion. Emits a Fact with the duration in metadata,\nrouted to Glean in Fenix's MetricController via accumulateSamples.\nReveals disk pressure and I/O queue length under real load.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322678\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/thumbnails/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/thumbnails/ThumbnailsMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/thumbnails/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/thumbnails/facts/BrowserThumbnailsFacts.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/thumbnails/src/test/java/mozilla/components/browser/thumbnails/BrowserThumbnailsTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/thumbnails/src/test/java/mozilla/components/browser/thumbnails/HomepageThumbnailsTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/thumbnails/src/test/java/mozilla/components/browser/thumbnails/ThumbnailsMiddlewareTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/metrics.yaml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/metrics/MetricController.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/metrics/MetricControllerTest.kt"], "git_node": "0a9a43f7dbf44411ce60797707d725897ae93d1d", "git_parents": ["de317d9434025aab819a2bb87e21e140fd2c7b47"], "node": "6767094798c2719a9b7273b2d1b3d9ac069e446e", "parents": ["3ca65623fb95089509fd0d26a73499d0d133b26d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065637 - Enable TypeScript for the sessionstore modules that already pass. r=Standard8,jswinarton\n\nFifteen of the directory's twenty modules type-check as-is. The other five are listed in `exclude` and come off the list as they are fixed, so the gate is meaningful from the start.\n\n`SessionStore.sys.mjs` stays excluded and accounts for 216 of the directory's 250 errors, so the `{integer}` to `{number}` changes in it have no effect yet. TypeScript is the only consumer of these comments that rejects `integer`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320586\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/SessionFile.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/SessionWriter.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/tsconfig.json", "browser/components/sessionstore/types/sessionstore.ts", "taskcluster/kinds/source-test/mozlint.yml", "tools/@types/lib.gecko.tweaks.d.ts", "tools/lint/typescript.yml"], "git_node": "def2efe32fc21181fffd992a83368343ad7899b1", "git_parents": ["0a9a43f7dbf44411ce60797707d725897ae93d1d"], "node": "e2eafdebc0ccffef6d7905d709127f39d82127a1", "parents": ["6767094798c2719a9b7273b2d1b3d9ac069e446e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "delan azabani \u003cdazabani@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067041 - Editor support for Sublime Text. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,emilio,sergesanspaille,ahochheiden\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321804\n", "files": [".gitignore", ".hgignore", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/mach_commands.py"], "git_node": "ef8b6aa8de19e8a1c4d485e9c012fc22acd4c383", "git_parents": ["def2efe32fc21181fffd992a83368343ad7899b1"], "node": "4b5b5494c68aec45f38cc98713003b0efd845e2f", "parents": ["e2eafdebc0ccffef6d7905d709127f39d82127a1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Raiber \u003cmraiber@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1969804 - Fix shim for store.steampowered.com/steamcommunity.com asking for permissions it already has r=timhuang,webcompat-reviewers,twisniewski\n\nFix the shim asking for permssions for the current site by checking\nif the tab is already showing the destination site and not asking\nfor permission in this case.\nThis can happen when a site is refreshed by the user.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316764\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/webcompat/lib/shims.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/manifest.json"], "git_node": "7844e7f4ea12a360e72a236545ecbb0f2ce63edb", "git_parents": ["ef8b6aa8de19e8a1c4d485e9c012fc22acd4c383"], "node": "3e1b63c6ddc07338614566222642771728765778", "parents": ["4b5b5494c68aec45f38cc98713003b0efd845e2f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrea Marchesini \u003camarchesini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068898 - Remove toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/test_basic.html r=timhuang\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323197\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/test_basic.html"], "git_node": "d6ef6bef1036605fe54fe1e2e936c0ff6581fb95", "git_parents": ["7844e7f4ea12a360e72a236545ecbb0f2ce63edb"], "node": "ae7cbc4d86dac71f915f9cc99bd23a31ba24c6e3", "parents": ["3e1b63c6ddc07338614566222642771728765778"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2064785 - Add testcase as a crashtest. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\" for causing wpt failures in whitespace-reattach.html.\n\nThis reverts commit 725832dc97491ce1bf95f62b00f266f4c6cf7d0c.\n\nThis reverts commit 530d1b729c49b5e072a81d205cd3a741c20e6ad0.\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsTextFrame.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ruby/crashtests/whitespace-reframe.html"], "git_node": "90d63030bb5c66ddaa73d8f68bbb4b1cc2df0492", "git_parents": ["d6ef6bef1036605fe54fe1e2e936c0ff6581fb95"], "node": "21d43ef1fcf2a4f314a2cd34c1e52a18dc3daa9f", "parents": ["ae7cbc4d86dac71f915f9cc99bd23a31ba24c6e3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Merge mozilla-central to autoland\n", "files": [], "git_node": "53b7c2bcaa3d063dcbfd07c27de0545b3f412f3c", "git_parents": ["90d63030bb5c66ddaa73d8f68bbb4b1cc2df0492", "edfb027f321fd2584c8fd2df528e665b7f5b8dac"], "node": "61aa47ffab432788575918e8c8496148c743ac20", "parents": ["21d43ef1fcf2a4f314a2cd34c1e52a18dc3daa9f", "9b69ffb62ec6dc0a6f579f8e1c7d9b65b2189673"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2068956 - Update android nightly application-services version bump to a0dafe8407bda1e01477a319adc66ee3036def9a r=release-managers,pascalc\" for causing fenix-debug failures in FxSuggestSuggestionProviderTest.kt.\n\nThis reverts commit ab6b374b43739155e02982244a71133ef94b5724.\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/plugins/dependencies/src/main/java/ApplicationServices.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/plugins/dependencies/src/main/java/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "c841c51c3464fa19b3e91e756de10b84c0c2f535", "git_parents": ["53b7c2bcaa3d063dcbfd07c27de0545b3f412f3c"], "node": "be8058e750dcc282cc069d6d8fb922008525a9a6", "parents": ["61aa47ffab432788575918e8c8496148c743ac20"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Henrik Skupin \u003cmail@hskupin.info\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068874 - [marionette] Detect XPCOM exceptions when event dispatching fails. r=Sasha\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323177\n", "files": ["remote/marionette/actors/MarionetteCommandsChild.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "c9ccc78915ec72dffcec5d950aae2bfd1858b31d", "git_parents": ["c841c51c3464fa19b3e91e756de10b84c0c2f535"], "node": "6b49efb9717734303fc47e71a506d29f005ba4ae", "parents": ["be8058e750dcc282cc069d6d8fb922008525a9a6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057292 - Improve detection of refcounted types in CanRunScriptChecker. r=sergesanspaille\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317608\n", "files": ["build/clang-plugin/CanRunScriptChecker.cpp", "build/clang-plugin/CustomMatchers.h", "build/clang-plugin/tests/TestCanRunScript.cpp"], "git_node": "407c8081a31aa79568767d9f2e6ac40d386a0447", "git_parents": ["c9ccc78915ec72dffcec5d950aae2bfd1858b31d"], "node": "89df74bcac247f487403ce68eaa524af9900dd65", "parents": ["6b49efb9717734303fc47e71a506d29f005ba4ae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoshi Cheng-Hao Huang \u003callstars.chh@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058630 - Report OOM if appending an empty wasm module failed. r=dminor\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323216\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/modules/bug-2058630.js", "js/src/shell/ModuleLoader.cpp"], "git_node": "07987f4c23cf3020a1ff8e50f659b74b8310de8a", "git_parents": ["407c8081a31aa79568767d9f2e6ac40d386a0447"], "node": "f2f2127e40e6e621f440b4775192d8103a919770", "parents": ["89df74bcac247f487403ce68eaa524af9900dd65"], "tags": []}, {"author": "acreskeyMoz \u003cacreskey@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2043896 - Add google, facebook, yahoo and google-docs to the nav-bench benchmark. r=kshampur,perftest-reviewers\n\nCovers the top desktop sites by pageload volume not already measured, plus the\ntp6 google-docs document, measured cold and then warm.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318199\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/browsertime/desktop.yml", "testing/perfdocs/generated/raptor.md", "testing/performance/nav_sites.json", "testing/raptor/browsertime/support-scripts/nav_bench.py", "testing/raptor/raptor/perfdocs/config.yml", "testing/raptor/raptor/tests/nav-bench/browsertime-nav-bench.toml", "testing/raptor/raptor/tooltool-manifests/nav-bench/mitm12-darwin-firefox-facebook-nav.manifest", "testing/raptor/raptor/tooltool-manifests/nav-bench/mitm12-darwin-firefox-google-docs-nav.manifest", "testing/raptor/raptor/tooltool-manifests/nav-bench/mitm12-darwin-firefox-google-nav.manifest", "testing/raptor/raptor/tooltool-manifests/nav-bench/mitm12-darwin-firefox-yahoo-nav.manifest"], "git_node": "6f41da4d6612fd98835922c5301a3b84a63ef03c", "git_parents": ["07987f4c23cf3020a1ff8e50f659b74b8310de8a"], "node": "1954ffe7eba38314e7ab3a8bab597df53963269a", "parents": ["f2f2127e40e6e621f440b4775192d8103a919770"], "tags": []}, {"author": "acreskeyMoz \u003cacreskey@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2043896 - Wait for mitmproxy's CA certificate before starting the browser. r=perftest-reviewers,kshampur\n\nmozproxy waits on the listen socket, which accepts long before mitmproxy has\nwritten the certificate, so the browser can start and distrust every connection.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321558\n", "files": ["testing/mozbase/mozproxy/mozproxy/backends/mitm/desktop.py", "testing/mozbase/mozproxy/mozproxy/backends/mitm/mitm.py"], "git_node": "096654d7fd88037d3bdd975171a210f242fd77b5", "git_parents": ["6f41da4d6612fd98835922c5301a3b84a63ef03c"], "node": "b5c2c1a0bfb4c851c57dade0dd60fd6672577f2f", "parents": ["1954ffe7eba38314e7ab3a8bab597df53963269a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065800 - Write the session state shapes as JSDoc typedefs. r=jswinarton\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320678\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/RecentlyClosedTabsAndWindowsMenuUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/TabGroupState.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/TabState.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/tsconfig.json", "browser/components/sessionstore/types/sessionstore.ts"], "git_node": "9ca91198c60b2e8601ffd9f72bb0984d70b1dba3", "git_parents": ["096654d7fd88037d3bdd975171a210f242fd77b5"], "node": "43088649e6cdf0bda609584d18efaad4ebaa2753", "parents": ["b5c2c1a0bfb4c851c57dade0dd60fd6672577f2f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065811 - Type-check RecentlyClosedTabsAndWindowsMenuUtils.sys.mjs. r=sfoster\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320682\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/RecentlyClosedTabsAndWindowsMenuUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/tsconfig.json"], "git_node": "6407dd8b2bf94b68315041dd556e115687b0fb3d", "git_parents": ["9ca91198c60b2e8601ffd9f72bb0984d70b1dba3"], "node": "a50b9e5cb3de71bfbbb427097c7344db6a460870", "parents": ["43088649e6cdf0bda609584d18efaad4ebaa2753"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067068 - Fix Reopen All Tabs for closed tabs from closed windows. r=jswinarton\n\nRegression from bug 1944328, which misspelled undoClosedTabFromClosedWindow while moving the call into the undoAllInTabData helper.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321824\n", "files": ["browser/components/customizableui/test/browser_history_recently_closed.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/RecentlyClosedTabsAndWindowsMenuUtils.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "6f2e8af0771e7af68c072a71273d0d5479b275c7", "git_parents": ["6407dd8b2bf94b68315041dd556e115687b0fb3d"], "node": "1db6a84305dad1ac180449cc7de2cb6946f89b80", "parents": ["a50b9e5cb3de71bfbbb427097c7344db6a460870"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067072 - Use declareLazy in remaining sessionstore modules so their cross-module calls get type-checked. r=jswinarton\n\ndeclareLazy resolves each entry to a real type, so every lazy.* reference in these modules is checked for the first time. The conversion is behavior-neutral; the JSDoc annotations it contradicts are corrected here.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321825\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/PageWireframes.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/RecentlyClosedTabsAndWindowsMenuUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/SessionCookies.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/SessionLogger.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/SessionMigration.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/SessionWindowUI.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/StartupPerformance.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/TabGroupState.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/tsconfig.json"], "git_node": "e1ff17fdf3f0b0c03f82ecb12c479da612df69d5", "git_parents": ["6f2e8af0771e7af68c072a71273d0d5479b275c7"], "node": "6e70162263251f1d3362a65d19707bd566807a9b", "parents": ["1db6a84305dad1ac180449cc7de2cb6946f89b80"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dave Townsend \u003cdtownsend@oxymoronical.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068119: Add a Nimbus feature for controlling Nova. r=beth\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322639\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/nimbus/FeatureManifest.yaml"], "git_node": "e1cbde4bffdbfd773ddc3beb5f6bf95138ab89f3", "git_parents": ["e1ff17fdf3f0b0c03f82ecb12c479da612df69d5"], "node": "561277e2072090876272989d10342d30b79b39be", "parents": ["6e70162263251f1d3362a65d19707bd566807a9b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandre Lissy \u003clissyx@lissyx.dyndns.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068972 - Add 'enterprise' to manifestparser and mozinfo r=jmendez\n\nThunderbird Enterprise changes are landing on comm-central, so being\nable to properly skip/run tests there using \"enterprise\" is important.\nLinters are also unhappy because they do not know about it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323258\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/mozinfo.py", "testing/mozbase/manifestparser/manifestparser/token.py"], "git_node": "d6594e2d2cfa4e14a291153631a3c313a69614d0", "git_parents": ["e1cbde4bffdbfd773ddc3beb5f6bf95138ab89f3"], "node": "34bc468cf16dc433a40a996f4a1c1de87ecd9a3d", "parents": ["561277e2072090876272989d10342d30b79b39be"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2036966 - Support an overscroll-behavior value, \"chain\". r=hiro\n\n\"chain\" is defined in\nhttps://drafts.csswg.org/css-overscroll-behavior/#propdef-overscroll-behavior .\n\nThis patch has three parts.\n\n1. Parsing and plumbing. \"chain\" is added to the specified value in\n   enum in servo and APZ, so that it is preserved through the scroll\n   metadata.\n\n2. APZ behavior. The places that consult overscroll-behavior while scrolling,\n   such as AsyncPanZoomController::CallDispatchScroll() and\n   OverscrollHandoffChain::FindFirstScrollable(), all reach it through\n   Axis::OverscrollBehaviorAllowsHandoff() and\n   Axis::OverscrollBehaviorAllowsOverscrollEffect(). The behavior change is\n   therefore contained in those two methods.\n\n3. Tests. The existing WPTs covering the handoff feature are enabled.\n   Regarding overscroll-effect and swipe-to-nav, they are covered by\n   new APZ mochitests.\n\nIn order to make the WPT work on Android, this patch add a meta tag on the WPT case.\nThe case \"overscroll-behavior-x: none prevents scroll propagation on x axis\" got successful\nby that, thought it has nothing to do with \"chain\" value.\n\nJust in case, manual testing on an android device was done and showed that handoff\nand downward swipe (page refresh) behave as specified there.\nNote that overscroll effect couldn't be checked on Android due to Bug 1809969.\n\nRegarding testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overscroll-behavior/overscroll-behavior.html.ini,\nthere was a test marked as failing on mac. I inspected the reason why mac is marked\nas failed, but didn't find any reason preventing me from removing that. Actually, the\ntest succeeds on try. So I removed this mark.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323146\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/FrameMetrics.cpp", "gfx/layers/FrameMetrics.h", "gfx/layers/apz/src/Axis.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_overscroll_behavior_chain_no_effect.html", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/test_group_overscroll.html", "layout/style/test/property_database.js", "servo/components/style/values/specified/box.rs", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overscroll-behavior/overscroll-behavior-without-overflow.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overscroll-behavior/overscroll-behavior.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overscroll-behavior/parsing/overscroll-behavior-computed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overscroll-behavior/parsing/overscroll-behavior-valid.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overscroll-behavior/overscroll-behavior.html", "widget/tests/browser/browser_test_swipe_gesture.js"], "git_node": "afcdb0d90fc13092e6d4d4b7e036acbc281ade4b", "git_parents": ["d6594e2d2cfa4e14a291153631a3c313a69614d0"], "node": "02b53e1822da21ed62b67dc52f84593907105cd7", "parents": ["34bc468cf16dc433a40a996f4a1c1de87ecd9a3d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masha Lifshin \u003cmlifshin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066944 - Update Android fxsuggest tests for the new required suggestion_id r=android-reviewers,skhan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321422\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/fxsuggest/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/fxsuggest/FxSuggestSuggestionProviderTest.kt"], "git_node": "c3bd3bee5a827f099705e62eb31d11b50efde626", "git_parents": ["afcdb0d90fc13092e6d4d4b7e036acbc281ade4b"], "node": "9dcba11dc6fd392c2cc3cdc6251f031e7794eff8", "parents": ["02b53e1822da21ed62b67dc52f84593907105cd7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2068619: Don't allow external callers to set the isInitial parameter to init. r=niklas\" for causing linux marionette failures in test_backup_selectable_to_selectable.py.\n\nThis reverts commit f022e98032cebe2dcf05e56fe06384c620afc778.\n", "files": ["browser/components/profiles/SelectableProfileService.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "b3bb8982b8dbcf2c1a6f193cb2a92ec7aa620c1e", "git_parents": ["c3bd3bee5a827f099705e62eb31d11b50efde626"], "node": "b36f756cd86e101fc6b040a0d362e9ec38390646", "parents": ["9dcba11dc6fd392c2cc3cdc6251f031e7794eff8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Greg Stoll \u003cgreg@gregstoll.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058647 r=beth\n\nTwo issues here:\n- There was some inconsistency in how we handled domains with multiple dots at the end. Instead of making this consistent, I just did the easier thing and return an error if a domain ends with more than one dot, because I don't think there's a realistic use case for it.\n- Also, places that we called `Preferences::UnregisterCallback()` assumed that it succeeded and would always release the last reference to the `PrefCallback`, so if it didn't succeed a `PrefCallback` would get freed but would still be in `mObservers`. So now we check if `UnregisterCallback()` fails and if so, add the `PrefCallback` back to `mObservers`. (I decided to do it this way since `UnregisterCallback()` failing should be very rare so I didn't want to incur a lookup followed by a remove in the normal case)\n\n(technically we only need to fix one of these to close the hole, but fixing both made sense)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323047\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/Preferences.cpp", "modules/libpref/Preferences.h", "modules/libpref/test/gtest/Basics.cpp"], "git_node": "f35e75640c4794b582872d124cf56bd3fd2dcc50", "git_parents": ["b3bb8982b8dbcf2c1a6f193cb2a92ec7aa620c1e"], "node": "feaef451dd87b7c838bc51e236e30b48e37ab5ff", "parents": ["b36f756cd86e101fc6b040a0d362e9ec38390646"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mathieu Leplatre \u003cmathieu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068952 - Handle verification failures consistently in _importChanges r=Gijs,acottner\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323231\n", "files": ["services/settings/RemoteSettingsClient.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "fa38b789cc56f0086a4618ccd1f350c71857eadc", "git_parents": ["f35e75640c4794b582872d124cf56bd3fd2dcc50"], "node": "1d6751fb84e1f59af4de15ce1a53018c9865c6f7", "parents": ["feaef451dd87b7c838bc51e236e30b48e37ab5ff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Mehic \u003cdmehic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1857519 - Wait for PBM clearing before asserting resetAction in test_panel r=emz\n\nResetPBMPanel.onConfirm records confirmPanel synchronously but only records\nresetAction after awaiting _restartPBM, which awaits\nclearData.clearPrivateBrowsingData. test_panel asserted both as soon as the\npanel's popuphidden fired, so it raced the panel hide animation against PBM\ndata clearing. Clearing usually wins, which is why this failed intermittently\nrather than always; when it ran long the assertion saw an empty resetAction\nlist.\n\nAssert after the completion toast instead, matching what the second\nassertTelemetry call in the same task already does. ConfirmationHint.show() is\nthe last statement of _restartPBM, so resetAction is recorded in the microtask\nchain that resolves _restartPBM, and always precedes the toast's popupshown.\n\nwaitForPBMDataClear() is not a barrier for this. It observes\nlast-pb-context-exited, which ClearDataService fires at the start of clearing\nrather than on completion, as the helper's own docstring notes. The promise it\ncreated in this block never guarded anything, so it is removed. The remaining\nuse later in the task is a progress checkpoint rather than a guard, so it\nstays, but its log lines claimed clearing had finished. Reword them to say\nwhat the notification actually signals.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317325\n", "files": ["browser/components/privatebrowsing/test/browser/browser_privatebrowsing_resetPBM.js"], "git_node": "725645d00d26727c778503b0cf05f5edb8b5db9c", "git_parents": ["fa38b789cc56f0086a4618ccd1f350c71857eadc"], "node": "15167be908af5fad3fa63e574d7ec880661f077a", "parents": ["1d6751fb84e1f59af4de15ce1a53018c9865c6f7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrej Glavic \u003caglavic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1999037 - Run simpleperf versions on applink startup tests regularly. r=perftest-reviewers,taskgraph-reviewers,releng-reviewers,ahal,sparky\n\nThe applink profiling runs only on-demand, but to determine changes better we are going to start running profiling jobs on central regularly\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319613\n", "files": [".cron.yml", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/actions/gecko_profile.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/target_tasks.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/test/python.toml", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/test/test_target_tasks.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/test/test_transforms_perftest.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/perftest.py"], "git_node": "9f6237c82b70b722eaa0fbd5b7c25862b35c2894", "git_parents": ["725645d00d26727c778503b0cf05f5edb8b5db9c"], "node": "ab7e7b413753a0af3be88e020d341d09a87ecb66", "parents": ["15167be908af5fad3fa63e574d7ec880661f077a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Shin \u003cdshin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2047776: Bring AtProgressTimelineBoundary up-to-date with spec. r=layout-scroll-driven-animation-reviewers,boris\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322991\n", "files": ["dom/animation/Animation.cpp", "dom/animation/Animation.h", "dom/animation/AnimationEffect.cpp", "gfx/layers/AnimationHelper.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/view-timelines/contain-alignment.html.ini"], "git_node": "21f7739985da2212c9f84509e409564f38dac901", "git_parents": ["9f6237c82b70b722eaa0fbd5b7c25862b35c2894"], "node": "ffe4c32bad2c06f722840300fb87a6a1ec05d14b", "parents": ["ab7e7b413753a0af3be88e020d341d09a87ecb66"], "tags": []}, {"author": "@Giulia Cardieri \u003cgcardieri@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061361: Apply styling to form fill review flow r=omarg,fluent-reviewers,flod\n\nFigma: https://www.figma.com/design/sIgXsbSFZjKIcfErMoBgLr/Smart-Window-Q3?node-id=12022-11842&p=f&m=dev\n\n- Updated the UI for all the fill/review suggestions flow\n- Added a \"jump to bottom\" button when the review form is too tall\n- Added a \"try again\" button when the suggestion filling fails for the first time\n- Added tests to test the try again button flow\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321947\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/assets/applied-policy.svg", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/assets/warning.svg", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-sff-form-review/ai-sff-form-review.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-sff-form-review/ai-sff-form-review.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-window/ai-window.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-history-menu/smartwindow-history-menu.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/content/ai-window-shared.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/content/smartformfill-form-review-content.html", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/jar.mn", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartformfill_form_review_filling.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/head_smartformfill_form_review.js", "browser/locales-preview/aiWindow.ftl"], "git_node": "f82a86d6fbfe05f527569deaf8ab304949898435", "git_parents": ["21f7739985da2212c9f84509e409564f38dac901"], "node": "6de4b7e6936326a235aada492cc81533c0423a89", "parents": ["ffe4c32bad2c06f722840300fb87a6a1ec05d14b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067058 - use the arm64 macOS python/uv on Apple Silicon workers. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nget_platform() mapped every macOS worker to the x86_64 macosx64-python\ntoolchain, so use-python could never pick up a native arm64 python.\nReturn macosx64-aarch64 for Apple Silicon workers, i.e. the b-osx-arm64\nbuilders and the M-series test pools (t-osx-1500-m4 etc.), so use-python\nand use-uv resolve to the macosx64-aarch64-python and\nmacosx64-aarch64-uv toolchains there.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321867\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/test/test_transforms_job.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/job/__init__.py"], "git_node": "0ca9f8d7c3e98064e055d88de9ced9d79007551a", "git_parents": ["f82a86d6fbfe05f527569deaf8ab304949898435"], "node": "0a4cca94f5e5fc2586e195d090a7ffce59100258", "parents": ["6de4b7e6936326a235aada492cc81533c0423a89"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067058 - Revert \"Bug 2055837 - mozharness: avoid arch mismatch between python and venv on mac.\" r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nThis reverts commit d17a86064272fe44a72b9ee721ff51aa4dcdf1b2.\n\nThat commit worked around Apple Silicon mac tasks fetching an x86_64 uv\nwhile running an arm64 (system) python, by forcing uv --python-platform\nto the interpreter arch. Now that get_platform() gives arm64 mac workers\nthe native macosx64-aarch64-uv (and matching python), uv and the\ninterpreter are always the same arch on mac, so uv resolves the right\nwheels on its own and the override is no longer needed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321868\n", "files": ["testing/mozharness/mozharness/base/python.py"], "git_node": "dcf57df707de8b15b13beee3bb330989fed7f5dd", "git_parents": ["0ca9f8d7c3e98064e055d88de9ced9d79007551a"], "node": "2054125d88e04b7bc716f00a71b1cfea8c77e7a1", "parents": ["0a4cca94f5e5fc2586e195d090a7ffce59100258"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2019381 - Support early media reception for bundled recvonly/sendrecv transceivers. r=webrtc-reviewers,bwc\n\nWhen a transceiver is bundled onto a transport that an earlier m-section\nalready negotiated, that transport is already live, so packets can\narrive before this transceiver's own answer exists. Add\nRTCRtpReceiver::CanTentativelyReceive() to detect that case and\nconfigure the conduit from our offered codecs, so early media isn't\ndropped while we wait for our own answer.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313333\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/PeerConnectionImpl.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/RTCRtpReceiver.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/RTCRtpReceiver.h", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/RTCRtpTransceiver.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/RTCRtpTransceiver.h", "dom/media/webrtc/jsep/JsepTrack.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsep/JsepTrack.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/rtp-stats-lifetime.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "b727d270f576a6090d60f04a1ebd239784989552", "git_parents": ["dcf57df707de8b15b13beee3bb330989fed7f5dd"], "node": "ce0f8ab66b9df26c30243b24ae71aec9839bb186", "parents": ["2054125d88e04b7bc716f00a71b1cfea8c77e7a1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2019381 - Enhance CanTentativelyReceive() to cover reoffers of already-negotiated transceivers. r=webrtc-reviewers,bwc\n\nExtend CanTentativelyReceive() to also apply when a transceiver that\nwas already negotiated is reoffered (e.g. setting the recv bit,\nwidening codecs), not just when it's never been negotiated at all.\nGate on having a pending local offer whose own recv-relevant content\nactually changed (JsepSession::LocalOfferedRecvParamsChanged()), so an\nunrelated, unchanged transceiver elsewhere in the bundle keeps using\nits real negotiated details instead of getting reset on every reoffer.\n\nCache whether a bundle group has a negotiated member directly on\nJsepTransceiver, computed once in SetLocalDescription(), instead of\nrecomputing it on every check by walking the SDP and every transceiver\non demand. Also fix EnsureHasOwnTransport() to reuse an already-live\ntransport when a follower is promoted to bundle tag because its own\nowner just dropped out, instead of discarding it and minting a new one\nthat can't finish ICE/DTLS before the answer arrives.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315142\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/PeerConnectionImpl.h", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/RTCRtpReceiver.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/RTCRtpReceiver.h", "dom/media/webrtc/jsep/JsepSession.h", "dom/media/webrtc/jsep/JsepSessionImpl.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsep/JsepSessionImpl.h", "dom/media/webrtc/jsep/JsepTransceiver.h", "media/webrtc/signaling/gtest/jsep_session_unittest.cpp"], "git_node": "5695e9492be258b35eff92e87154c03804217ca9", "git_parents": ["b727d270f576a6090d60f04a1ebd239784989552"], "node": "42950592289c62be55cbc943f6cf11e8905d6ef2", "parents": ["ce0f8ab66b9df26c30243b24ae71aec9839bb186"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2019381 - Add early media reoffer test coverage. r=webrtc-reviewers,bwc\n\nAdds test_peerConnection_earlyMediaReoffer.html, covering reoffers that\nset the recv bit, add a recv codec, add an RTP extension, add RTX, add\nan rtcp-fb type, or add a new bundled m-section.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315143\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/tests/mochitests/mochitest_peerconnection.toml", "dom/media/webrtc/tests/mochitests/test_peerConnection_earlyMediaReoffer.html"], "git_node": "5f091da12bab3ab2000293c55e66774a53c2b638", "git_parents": ["5695e9492be258b35eff92e87154c03804217ca9"], "node": "73c57cfca8ab5b798791ffb656a278a589657277", "parents": ["42950592289c62be55cbc943f6cf11e8905d6ef2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2019381 - Propagate setCodecPreferences() to the send track. r=webrtc-reviewers,bwc\n\nRTCRtpReceiver::SyncToJsep() already applies the transceiver's\npreferred codecs to the recv track via PopulateCodecs(). Do the same\nfor the send track in RTCRtpSender::SyncToJsep(), so the negotiation\naccounting for what we send matches what setCodecPreferences()\nactually restricted our own offer/answer to, instead of the full,\nunrestricted codec set.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315144\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/RTCRtpSender.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsep/JsepTrack.cpp"], "git_node": "9a3820bb8bdc6e5aa41455972d01ba5b32ac79f0", "git_parents": ["5f091da12bab3ab2000293c55e66774a53c2b638"], "node": "f8f8b651d8209a1d2ee9941599589450d3ec1aac", "parents": ["73c57cfca8ab5b798791ffb656a278a589657277"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2019381 - Use the pending offer's RTP extensions when building the early-media demux filter. r=webrtc-reviewers,bwc\n\nThe demux filter used GetNegotiatedDetails(), which is stale during a\npending offer, so a newly-restored extension (e.g. MID) wasn't\nrecognized until the real answer landed. Read the pending offer's own\nextmap instead in that window.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316105\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/RTCRtpReceiver.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsep/JsepTrack.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsep/JsepTrack.h"], "git_node": "896ddc914b75bc203029c8ec17237a9d99665131", "git_parents": ["9a3820bb8bdc6e5aa41455972d01ba5b32ac79f0"], "node": "950142e0b1b3232146c0ed0ac4ee2355aca71de8", "parents": ["f8f8b651d8209a1d2ee9941599589450d3ec1aac"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2019381 - Add a MID-only demux test for early media reoffers. r=webrtc-reviewers,bwc\n\nreofferAddsRtpExtension only has one transceiver, so it never proves an\nextension is actually used to demux between candidates. Add\nreofferRestoresMidDemuxing: 3 bundled recvonly transceivers, no SSRC\ninformation at all, so receiving early media on the right one depends\nentirely on the restored MID extension.\n\nAlso add reofferReplacesBundleOwner: stops the m-section that owns the\nshared bundle transport and adds a brand new one in the same reoffer,\nso the new m-section ends up owned by the promoted survivor instead.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316106\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/tests/mochitests/test_peerConnection_earlyMediaReoffer.html"], "git_node": "7a2ca5901d206bb0db35d7abdb9fcb54375d30e4", "git_parents": ["896ddc914b75bc203029c8ec17237a9d99665131"], "node": "46c8bcb476925ec3c29634173033b3c96456fa94", "parents": ["950142e0b1b3232146c0ed0ac4ee2355aca71de8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2019381 - Don't let a re-gather discard a pending StartIceChecks. r=webrtc-reviewers,bwc\n\nGatherIfReady() unconditionally cleared the shared ICE-ctx operation\nqueue, which could also be holding an already-queued but not-yet-run\nStartIceChecks. Stop clearing it: a stale queued gather running\nalongside a fresh one is harmless, since EnsureIceGathering() is a\nno-op once gathering for the round is already underway.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316988\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/PeerConnectionImpl.cpp"], "git_node": "5ef9b74bf6fbb95daf746762312dc3a6fc64591b", "git_parents": ["7a2ca5901d206bb0db35d7abdb9fcb54375d30e4"], "node": "5d1169150368288a2a71717dc1f108685c667d46", "parents": ["46c8bcb476925ec3c29634173033b3c96456fa94"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2019381: apply code formatting via Lando\n\n# ignore-this-changeset\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/RTCRtpReceiver.cpp"], "git_node": "29a043c67b9d9a35e16fa1858bd984cdd7cd450e", "git_parents": ["5ef9b74bf6fbb95daf746762312dc3a6fc64591b"], "node": "7bf0964c811933614ce526a99acbf49cbf5ae15d", "parents": ["5d1169150368288a2a71717dc1f108685c667d46"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tiaan Louw \u003ctlouw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1995348 - Implement the \"grid-lanes\" value for the \"display\" property r=layout-reviewers,dholbert\n\nUse the \"display: grid-lanes\" value to conform to current usage in web\nplatform tests.\n\nTwo tests are marked as CRASH, because the masonry code uses a sort\ncomparitor that is not valid strick weak ordering as required, so it\nasserts in debug builds. See bug 2068688.\n\nSee: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-grid-3/#masonry-model\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D273845\n", "f