he Organize Tabs panel down when its window closes r=pdahiya\n\nSee bug for testing issues\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323339\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AutoTabGrouping.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_group_tabs_button.js"], "git_node": "28a9985add5dc52faa580c15f29e3fd33f914af8", "git_parents": ["f8f83b90ee33119c864942e74f36a0f7851ce967"], "node": "c34ce375e4946a0e596791744722bac41eea2371", "parents": ["afb997fed7dd82b944d058094b42e34613373dde"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sotaro Ikeda \u003csotaro.ikeda.g@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069205 - Fix wait sync in SharedSurface_AndroidHardwareBuffer::WaitForBufferOwnership() r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nIn SharedSurface_AndroidHardwareBuffer::WaitForBufferOwnership(), eglClientWaitSync() is called. It is better to call eglWaitSync().\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323471\n", "files": ["gfx/gl/SharedSurfaceAndroidHardwareBuffer.cpp"], "git_node": "d30a7e372c7656013b6725b48da8acee335779b7", "git_parents": ["28a9985add5dc52faa580c15f29e3fd33f914af8"], "node": "e22ac96d275968c6b2b0673b0c3d35c88e8f257e", "parents": ["c34ce375e4946a0e596791744722bac41eea2371"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tymur Boiko \u003ctboiko@nvidia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068764 [Linux][Vulkan Video] Reuse cached selected device name across decoders. r=stransky,media-playback-reviewers\n\nWhen DrmRenderDevice is empty, SelectVulkanDecoderPhysicalDevice caches\nenumeration in sVulkanEnumerated but only wrote the GPU name onto the\nfirst decoder. Later decoders kept \"\" and VulkanDeviceHolder created a\nsecond VkDevice. Cache name/vendor/device IDs process-wide and refuse\nGetOrCreate with an empty name.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323227\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVulkanVideoDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/VulkanDeviceHolder.cpp"], "git_node": "9f4afdaa9fedca1ccd157b7b82d70a6efb5d46a2", "git_parents": ["d30a7e372c7656013b6725b48da8acee335779b7"], "node": "9dcaf4fe0a10473eaf5ed1a798723c9fbd868c0e", "parents": ["e22ac96d275968c6b2b0673b0c3d35c88e8f257e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tymur Boiko \u003ctboiko@nvidia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067923 - Allow RDD to read nvidia_drm modeset. r=jld,sandbox-reviewers\n\nInitVulkanDecoder skips Vulkan when modeset is off; that sysfs file was\ndenied in the RDD broker, so the check never ran.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322728\n", "files": ["security/sandbox/linux/broker/SandboxBrokerPolicyFactory.cpp"], "git_node": "cbd9996e5bd0ad2438856c4c828e679de29371bb", "git_parents": ["9f4afdaa9fedca1ccd157b7b82d70a6efb5d46a2"], "node": "093464c47908a894670acbe1085a1bb6b9de2ec5", "parents": ["9dcaf4fe0a10473eaf5ed1a798723c9fbd868c0e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vincent Hilla \u003cvhilla@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049792 - Sanity-check content-provided result and original URI. r=nika,dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319828\n", "files": ["docshell/base/nsDocShellLoadState.cpp"], "git_node": "9b0a52c776fb98e9c5832156c54c08b6afadbf5d", "git_parents": ["cbd9996e5bd0ad2438856c4c828e679de29371bb"], "node": "5b997dcca4dc0e66f5d8de363267f1d5115bef58", "parents": ["093464c47908a894670acbe1085a1bb6b9de2ec5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vincent Hilla \u003cvhilla@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049792 - Don't allow content to set result or original URI on SH. r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319829\n", "files": ["docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp", "docshell/base/nsDocShell.h", "dom/ipc/ContentParent.cpp"], "git_node": "5510135fdcb38ed8f00180f60d7be5c36c4aca35", "git_parents": ["9b0a52c776fb98e9c5832156c54c08b6afadbf5d"], "node": "40d9189e892a55922ef608edeb185584cf0e6c14", "parents": ["5b997dcca4dc0e66f5d8de363267f1d5115bef58"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049792: apply code formatting via Lando\n\n# ignore-this-changeset\n", "files": ["docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp"], "git_node": "5886d3514b04452a81e4ea4e83ab069118922891", "git_parents": ["5510135fdcb38ed8f00180f60d7be5c36c4aca35"], "node": "723bba28b95358c4fb6cd5c3486a7d403dcdb9eb", "parents": ["40d9189e892a55922ef608edeb185584cf0e6c14"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068114 - Test fast fallback at connection limit r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323189\n", "files": ["netwerk/test/unit/test_http3_fast_fallback.js"], "git_node": "1d24cda9b028d57cea5b21f2cc114bfad2602b3e", "git_parents": ["5886d3514b04452a81e4ea4e83ab069118922891"], "node": "b8b011ca38a44f2bfe0b1252265b53c4ec085ccc", "parents": ["723bba28b95358c4fb6cd5c3486a7d403dcdb9eb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068114 - Don't drop the HTTPS RR fast fallback when the backup connection can't be created r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323190\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpConnectionMgr.cpp"], "git_node": "2997b2c4de23a54655bbade181d927816896e52c", "git_parents": ["1d24cda9b028d57cea5b21f2cc114bfad2602b3e"], "node": "ed190211fb9d49e30b6dd2e38429bba9256b402b", "parents": ["b8b011ca38a44f2bfe0b1252265b53c4ec085ccc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Seward \u003cjseward@acm.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068386 - Try to avoid unnecessary OOMs in the MIR loop unroller.  r=iain.\n\nTry to avoid unnecessary OOMs in the MIR loop unroller by periodically\nrefreshing the allocator's ballast area.  This was not being done, and could\nlead to OOMs whilst processing functions with many unrollable loops.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323284\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/regress/bug2068386.js", "js/src/jit/UnrollLoops.cpp"], "git_node": "f3baee9153cb0e835e49af87c07bc7c6f52afa1a", "git_parents": ["2997b2c4de23a54655bbade181d927816896e52c"], "node": "343f4eec39458ab5fa078cb51938d7639cd4ca90", "parents": ["ed190211fb9d49e30b6dd2e38429bba9256b402b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "iulian moraru \u003cimoraru@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2049792: apply code formatting via Lando\" for causing build bustages on nsDocShellLoadState.cpp.\n\nThis reverts commit 5886d3514b04452a81e4ea4e83ab069118922891.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2049792 - Don't allow content to set result or original URI on SH. r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\"\n\nThis reverts commit 5510135fdcb38ed8f00180f60d7be5c36c4aca35.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2049792 - Sanity-check content-provided result and original URI. r=nika,dom-core-reviewers,smaug\"\n\nThis reverts commit 9b0a52c776fb98e9c5832156c54c08b6afadbf5d.\n", "files": ["docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp", "docshell/base/nsDocShell.h", "docshell/base/nsDocShellLoadState.cpp", "dom/ipc/ContentParent.cpp"], "git_node": "7aae4c3cce206282ad68aab55ef8fc8644c00abe", "git_parents": ["f3baee9153cb0e835e49af87c07bc7c6f52afa1a"], "node": "f171a1cf80eba872572777aeb8c5e9813f281f38", "parents": ["343f4eec39458ab5fa078cb51938d7639cd4ca90"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067674 - Use a signed comparison in the lazyExports binary searches r=jseward\n\nBoth BinarySearchIf comparators over Code::lazyExports returned the difference\nof two uint32_t values. BinarySearchIf stores the comparator result in an\n`auto` variable, so the result was unsigned and its `result \u003c 0` branch was\nnever taken, which Coverity reports as dead code (CID 1700568).\n\nIn lookupLazyFuncExport the search therefore never descends into the lower\nhalf and can miss an entry that is present. In createManyLazyEntryStubs the\nsame defect additionally yields a wrong insertion point on a failed lookup,\nleaving lazyExports unsorted.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322266\n", "files": ["js/src/wasm/WasmCode.cpp"], "git_node": "71cf7f578a7b07aa29ec6690bc34e94ecfa58ebc", "git_parents": ["7aae4c3cce206282ad68aab55ef8fc8644c00abe"], "node": "7407eaf655ea54160b5204cfb0d9c51cd73f5d72", "parents": ["f171a1cf80eba872572777aeb8c5e9813f281f38"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067675 - Hold mMutex while reading mCompileResult in WasmCompileTask::StealResult r=dminor\n\nmCompileResult is written by Run() with mMutex held, and read here without it.\nThe read happens on the main thread once the task has completed, so there is\nno actual race, but taking the lock is uncontended here and silences Coverity\n(CID 1700566).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322267\n", "files": ["dom/script/ScriptLoader.cpp"], "git_node": "655f079fa58b502441c5918e4bc98a96eff7897b", "git_parents": ["71cf7f578a7b07aa29ec6690bc34e94ecfa58ebc"], "node": "904341b854da55eb06c687cdf5e88f068f8a2028", "parents": ["7407eaf655ea54160b5204cfb0d9c51cd73f5d72"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065925 - Don't bind the metric in the codegen'd Lazy unless its size is measured. r=TravisLong\n\nOnly event and object metrics use the binding. Fixes ~2600\nclippy::let_and_return in the generated metrics.rs.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320732\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/glean/build_scripts/glean_parser_ext/templates/rust.jinja2", "toolkit/components/glean/tests/pytest/metrics_test_output"], "git_node": "a53d15dfc0a9d9de3bbb579b44eef3b66fa6d7eb", "git_parents": ["655f079fa58b502441c5918e4bc98a96eff7897b"], "node": "e7c4492df09f2f785a4f5811ca7ef36f57d840bb", "parents": ["904341b854da55eb06c687cdf5e88f068f8a2028"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065925 - Move string event extras into the FFI map instead of cloning them. r=TravisLong\n\ninto_ffi_extra takes self by value, so a string extra can be moved straight\ninto the HashMap\u003cString, String\u003e. Fixes ~2800 clippy::implicit_clone.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320733\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/glean/build_scripts/glean_parser_ext/templates/rust.jinja2", "toolkit/components/glean/tests/pytest/metrics_test_output"], "git_node": "c7000d06782bb31f28038a8a637a528ed55764b9", "git_parents": ["a53d15dfc0a9d9de3bbb579b44eef3b66fa6d7eb"], "node": "8440ea62812dd2cc04bd74db46865f38cab473ef", "parents": ["e7c4492df09f2f785a4f5811ca7ef36f57d840bb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065925 - Implement From rather than Into for codegen'd label enums. r=TravisLong\n\nFrom gives Into for free, so the existing .into() callers are unaffected.\nFixes 434 clippy::from_over_into.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320734\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/glean/build_scripts/glean_parser_ext/templates/rust.jinja2", "toolkit/components/glean/tests/pytest/metrics_test_output"], "git_node": "f7f163579a85da67d51b0554ccb06b9685d2e64c", "git_parents": ["c7000d06782bb31f28038a8a637a528ed55764b9"], "node": "a0c303dd159eeba85e79682099a3a7548683a97b", "parents": ["8440ea62812dd2cc04bd74db46865f38cab473ef"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065925 - Fix assorted small clippy lints across the Rust codegen. r=TravisLong\n\nmap_or over map().unwrap_or(), is_empty() over len() == 0, no tail return,\ninlined format args, a hoisted extern block, a MetricMap\u003cT\u003e alias, plain\ncomments for the factory.rs header, and no .into() on an already-u32 ping id.\nThe two create_and_register_* entry points mirror the metric constructors, so\ntheir long argument lists get a targeted allow instead.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320735\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/glean/build_scripts/glean_parser_ext/templates/jog_factory.jinja2", "toolkit/components/glean/build_scripts/glean_parser_ext/templates/rust.jinja2", "toolkit/components/glean/build_scripts/glean_parser_ext/templates/rust_pings.jinja2", "toolkit/components/glean/tests/pytest/jogfactory_output", "toolkit/components/glean/tests/pytest/metrics_test_output", "toolkit/components/glean/tests/pytest/pings_test_output"], "git_node": "1e2973747b8aa14976e9f5c5cd7e125ce3a69590", "git_parents": ["f7f163579a85da67d51b0554ccb06b9685d2e64c"], "node": "cbc8089e12a1ca6bc3a34c1409e1e7da9603dac8", "parents": ["a0c303dd159eeba85e79682099a3a7548683a97b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065925 - Render codegen'd integer literals with digit separators. r=TravisLong\n\nMetric ids and metrics.yaml range values are up to twelve digits. Fixes\n~19600 clippy::unreadable_literal.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320736\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/glean/build_scripts/glean_parser_ext/jog.py", "toolkit/components/glean/build_scripts/glean_parser_ext/rust.py", "toolkit/components/glean/build_scripts/glean_parser_ext/templates/jog_factory.jinja2", "toolkit/components/glean/tests/pytest/jogfactory_output"], "git_node": "abcab783602b0bdc42509f96f94d8ee3359a7472", "git_parents": ["1e2973747b8aa14976e9f5c5cd7e125ce3a69590"], "node": "d4a30f8df70446069f1ca1f1b97a17b5d0162999", "parents": ["cbc8089e12a1ca6bc3a34c1409e1e7da9603dac8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051115 - Reject unescaped nulls from mimeheader r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321827\n", "files": ["netwerk/mime/nsMIMEHeaderParamImpl.cpp"], "git_node": "d98a7cdf9a2145c823e8553d96bf4b151198b3ec", "git_parents": ["abcab783602b0bdc42509f96f94d8ee3359a7472"], "node": "85b4f62a19f8961903e4a9fdae5a1df3c584aa40", "parents": ["d4a30f8df70446069f1ca1f1b97a17b5d0162999"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067123 - Record and surface policies that only partially applied. r=fluent-reviewers,bolsson,gerard-majax\n\nA policy whose callback failed was indistinguishable from one that applied\ncleanly: getActivePolicies() listed it, and an async callback's rejection was\nnot observable at all, so nothing reached about:policies.\n\nThe policy engine now records a failure against the policy whose callback\nthrew or whose returned promise rejected. Policy implementations that need to\nkeep going after a single failed operation report it the same way, so one bad\npreference, certificate or match pattern no longer looks like a clean\napplication. Preferences also no longer discards the entries after one that\nfails.\n\nreportFailure lives in PoliciesHelpers next to PolicyFailures, the state it\nwrites to, so that both Policies and the helpers themselves report through one\nfunction rather than each keeping a copy.\n\nCleanup callbacks run without a policy name, so their failures are logged but\nnot attributed to a policy that does not exist.\n\nabout:policies flags those policies in the Active list and names the policy\neach message belongs to in a new column of the Errors tab. Failures logged\nfrom PoliciesHelpers were never displayed there at all.\n\ngetActivePolicies() is unchanged: those parameters are what the administrator\nasked for, and callers rely on that.\n\nHandlers still reports through the engine's generic handler; containing its\nmimeTypes loop so it can name the entry that failed is left for a follow-up.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322420\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.sys.mjs", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/content/aboutPolicies.css", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/content/aboutPolicies.html", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/content/aboutPolicies.js", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/helpers/BookmarksPolicies.sys.mjs", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/helpers/ProxyPolicies.sys.mjs", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/helpers/WebsiteFilter.sys.mjs", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/browser/browser_policies_about_policies.js", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/xpcshell/test_policy_failures.js", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/aboutPolicies.ftl", "toolkit/components/enterprisepolicies/EnterprisePoliciesParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/enterprisepolicies/PoliciesHelpers.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "97652a82f9b00fd400a94271fc8f0352585ddd6c", "git_parents": ["d98a7cdf9a2145c823e8553d96bf4b151198b3ec"], "node": "2dfecab43c5eb15fbf0a08080e7dc2ecfb292944", "parents": ["85b4f62a19f8961903e4a9fdae5a1df3c584aa40"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brian Smith \u003cbrian@smith.berlin\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067123 - Name the Handlers entry that failed and say why a preference could not be set. r=gerard-majax\n\nHandlers catches and logs every failure of its own, so nothing reached the\nengine's generic handler and none of it was attributed to the policy. Its\nloops and processMIMEInfo now report through reportFailure, so one bad MIME\ntype, extension or scheme names the entry that failed instead of failing\nsilently. processMIMEInfo takes the policy it is working for, since\nDisableBuiltinPDFViewer calls it too.\n\n\"Probable type mismatch\" was a guess that covered every way setting a\npreference can fail. describePreferenceFailure sits next to setAndLockPref,\nthe call whose failure it explains, and reports the type the preference\ntakes against the type the policy provided, whole numbers, and otherwise the\nunderlying error.\n\nWith PoliciesHelpers failures now attributed to a policy, about:policies no\nlonger needs to list it as a module whose log messages go in the Errors tab.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322672\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.sys.mjs", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/content/aboutPolicies.js", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/xpcshell/test_policy_failures.js", "toolkit/components/enterprisepolicies/PoliciesHelpers.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "c6bac48c25adacb20339375b1666e1af0c4d3d32", "git_parents": ["97652a82f9b00fd400a94271fc8f0352585ddd6c"], "node": "39e5fc8f6fd9743e508b41bcf6fe4c9688f7e038", "parents": ["2dfecab43c5eb15fbf0a08080e7dc2ecfb292944"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1970802 - Wait for the new tab to be reflowed in openNewForegroundTab, r=Gijs.\n\nA remote browser has a 0x0 viewport until we reflow it and send\nUpdateDimensions, so a caller that synthesizes input as soon as\nopenNewForegroundTab resolves can hit test against an empty area, and the event\nresolves to the document rather than to an element.\n\nThe wait runs alongside the load, so it only costs anything when nothing else\nalready waited for a tick.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322870\n", "files": ["testing/mochitest/BrowserTestUtils/BrowserTestUtils.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "17868e9d509245fe803177ceb9bd0c6a85cc7050", "git_parents": ["c6bac48c25adacb20339375b1666e1af0c4d3d32"], "node": "5cbd9394a35f7323f047b0dacaaa5abfff113bc3", "parents": ["39e5fc8f6fd9743e508b41bcf6fe4c9688f7e038"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069062 - Fix position of Speech Recognition entry in about:preferences AI Controls. r=nordzilla,hjones\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323327\n", "files": ["browser/components/preferences/config/aiFeatures.mjs"], "git_node": "efd40ebb904d4f2db452a210d14dd753b95038fd", "git_parents": ["17868e9d509245fe803177ceb9bd0c6a85cc7050"], "node": "5e4419f60a11f370dd0751e9bfac8e39b6a752c1", "parents": ["5cbd9394a35f7323f047b0dacaaa5abfff113bc3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1982990 - Skip GDK frame clock synchronization on X11. r=stransky,gtk-reviewers\n\nSee the comments on the bug. The TLDR is that gtk_window_resize waits\nfor the GTK frame clock via gtk_widget_queue_resize_no_redraw:\n\n * https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gtk/-/blob/b30343717dc9b02cf157d2ea87da585d8d518845/gtk/gtkwindow.c#L5436\n\nOn automation that never advances (that waits for _NET_WM_FRAME_DRAWN,\nand the counter is stuck at 1...). Since GTK has an opt-out for this\nprecise mechanism, and the benefit we get from it seems not-huge, I\nthink this is probably the least risky?\n\nAlternatives would be:\n\n * Try to get an updated mutter on CI or so, in case this is fixed in\n   the ubuntu repos already (hopefully?).\n\n * Go through gdk_window_resize rather than gtk_window_resize on X11,\n   which skips the gtk wait and does a direct X11 request. That is\n   closer to what gtk_window_move does, but I'm a bit worried about some\n   GTK state getting out of sync due to that.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323370\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/nsWindowX11.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsWindowX11.h"], "git_node": "571e8708dd065223071e63564a937b6f23926c9f", "git_parents": ["efd40ebb904d4f2db452a210d14dd753b95038fd"], "node": "51bc57dbb9e4f3d71481572afc3a84b4b979dbf3", "parents": ["5e4419f60a11f370dd0751e9bfac8e39b6a752c1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068160 - Part 1 - Remove the write-only PictureContext visibility spatial node. r=gw\n\nIt was assigned the root reference frame and never read. The TODO on it about\nswitching to raster space described work that doesn't need doing: the prepare\npass has no consumer for a visibility spatial node.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322969\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/frame_builder.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/picture.rs"], "git_node": "dfca3ebdb78e049fcc60d2fef128b88c11c11778", "git_parents": ["571e8708dd065223071e63564a937b6f23926c9f"], "node": "fea17028c05efa67d7406e0428f4ee122018059a", "parents": ["51bc57dbb9e4f3d71481572afc3a84b4b979dbf3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068160 - Part 2 - Remove the tile cache's unused visible-tile culling rect. r=gw\n\nTileCacheInstance::pre_update accumulated the union of visible tiles' device\nrects and returned it; update_prim_visibility took it as root_culling_rect and\nonly ever forwarded it to its own recursive call. Nothing consumed it, so the\noptimization the comment described - skipping primitives outside the visible\ntiles, and shrinking off-screen surfaces allocated for child pictures - did not\nhappen. A tile cache surface's culling rect is the whole screen rect for the\nduration of the frame, set once by SurfaceInfo::new.\n\nRemoving it rather than wiring it up, since wiring it up changes what gets\nculled and belongs in its own patch with its own measurements.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322970\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/frame_builder.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/tile_cache/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/visibility.rs"], "git_node": "39ae5d9140e995c82a75d617550e8d7ab00107db", "git_parents": ["dfca3ebdb78e049fcc60d2fef128b88c11c11778"], "node": "e833522a4223c3d690da7537285fce313daa7830", "parents": ["fea17028c05efa67d7406e0428f4ee122018059a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068160 - Part 3 - Map backdrop-filter debug rects to device space directly. r=gw\n\nPictureState::map_pic_to_vis had one consumer: the HIGHLIGHT_BACKDROP_FILTERS\noverlay, which cast its result to a device rect and pushed it as a debug item.\nDebug items are drawn onto the screen framebuffer, so that mapping wants root\nspace rather than the visibility space its name suggested, and the TODO about\nswitching it to raster space would have broken it.\n\ntake_context already built an identical root-relative mapper for the picture\nbounds, differing only in its projection bounds, so keep that one and drop the\nduplicate.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322971\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/frame_builder.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/picture.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs"], "git_node": "4cf52c66f4cb5f2550a7e73b30dd274e516a9b82", "git_parents": ["39ae5d9140e995c82a75d617550e8d7ab00107db"], "node": "078fa86ac1783c4b38f55342ba7ccf0c8469ba75", "parents": ["e833522a4223c3d690da7537285fce313daa7830"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068160 - Part 4 - Remove the unused vis_rect_as_world shim. r=gw\n\nA cast_unit helper with no callers anywhere in gfx/wr.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322972\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/units.rs"], "git_node": "76cfa5ba07b4b1db48fd390db494e49c5e7f0181", "git_parents": ["4cf52c66f4cb5f2550a7e73b30dd274e516a9b82"], "node": "fdaf65758aca8041c33c6c4dcdba2967579570f1", "parents": ["078fa86ac1783c4b38f55342ba7ccf0c8469ba75"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068160 - Part 5 - Single-source the choice of visibility spatial node. r=gw\n\nIntroduces surface::visibility_node(), which every site that needs the space\nvisibility, clipping, dirty-region and invalidation calculations happen in now\ngoes through. It still returns the root reference frame, so there is no\nbehaviour change; the point is that there is now exactly one place to change.\n\nThe tile cache had a second, divergent source for the same decision: a\nscene-build-time visibility_node_index threaded from the slice builder through\nTileCacheParams into TileCacheInstance, where the field was never read and the\nDirtyRegion built from it was re-targeted every frame by post_update, which\ncomputed the root itself. Resolve the tile cache's visibility node per frame in\npre_update from its surface instead, which makes the field live and removes the\nscene-time plumbing. A scene-time value could not have followed a surface's\nraster space anyway, since that is decided per frame in assign_surface.\n\nDirtyRegion now starts each instance's life pointing at INVALID rather than the\nroot, with a debug assertion in add_dirty_region, so that a region used before\npost_update targets it fails loudly instead of silently mapping to the root.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322973\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/invalidation/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/surface.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/tile_cache/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/tile_cache/slice_builder.rs"], "git_node": "dbe6ac1c58a01b4b2ebb1d3f85e07df4078eb873", "git_parents": ["76cfa5ba07b4b1db48fd390db494e49c5e7f0181"], "node": "4b15349c959d52945123a03fd5fbe04abec528d4", "parents": ["fdaf65758aca8041c33c6c4dcdba2967579570f1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067761 - Disable custom select colors for color: transparent. r=mconley\n\nMuch like for background images, if you're messing with the color\nproperty like that we can't guarantee contrast.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323228\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/forms/browser_selectpopup_colors.js", "toolkit/actors/SelectChild.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "0a47378abe6bc909bff2efd09c785bf535d48c8c", "git_parents": ["dbe6ac1c58a01b4b2ebb1d3f85e07df4078eb873"], "node": "c4cb92802ab163b7c2effda218f0c4fa11865cd7", "parents": ["4b15349c959d52945123a03fd5fbe04abec528d4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Olli Pettay \u003cOlli.Pettay@helsinki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068361 - modernize ChromeTooltipListener a bit, r=dom-core-reviewers,jjaschke\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323365\n", "files": ["docshell/base/nsDocShellTreeOwner.cpp"], "git_node": "defbd6d2a9a199e04936191341d04b3912ff20a4", "git_parents": ["0a47378abe6bc909bff2efd09c785bf535d48c8c"], "node": "3177b7a3c322de86a7c9d6f09a39c0bcd2f2a539", "parents": ["c4cb92802ab163b7c2effda218f0c4fa11865cd7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Frederik Braun \u003cfbraun@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1380146 - Fix assertion failure on malformed integrity attribute r=tschuster\n\nRemove overly restrictive MOZ_ASSERT(question \u003e 0) in SRIMetadata constructor\nthat caused crashes on malformed integrity values like \"?-=\". The subsequent\ncheck for question \u003c= hashStart already handles this case correctly by\nreturning early with an error.\n\nAlso add WPT tests for various malformed integrity edge cases to ensure\ncross-browser interoperability.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D279334\n", "files": ["dom/security/SRIMetadata.cpp", "dom/security/test/sri/mochitest.toml", "dom/security/test/sri/test_bug_1380146_incorrect_integrity.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/subresource-integrity/subresource-integrity.html"], "git_node": "d91ce23e019f9acb5dead435830ebcde1f690773", "git_parents": ["defbd6d2a9a199e04936191341d04b3912ff20a4"], "node": "5b2950ce4c2a0cd30ae85018743410961bc073d3", "parents": ["3177b7a3c322de86a7c9d6f09a39c0bcd2f2a539"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maryam \u003cmomar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1960853 - Copy Clean Link: Adds \u2018=\u2018 after empty parameters when stripping. r=timhuang,urlbar-reviewers,jteow\n\nURLParams's parse/serialize round-trip can't distinguish a valueless\nparam (\u2018x\u2019) from one with an explicit empty value (\u2018x=\u2018), since\nURLParams::Param only stores {key, value} with no record of whether\nthe original segment contained an \u2018=\u2018. This caused \u2018Copy Clean Link\u2019\nand automatic query-string stripping to turn \u2018?fbclid=test&x\u2019 into\n\u2018?x=\u2018 instead of \u2018?x\u2019.\n\nAdds a local QueryParam struct (scoped to this file) that tracks the\npresence of an \u2018=\u2018, plus split/serialize helpers built on\nURLParams::ParseWithEquals() that preserve it through stripping. Both\nStripQueryString and StripForCopyOrShareInternal now use these instead\nof URLParams for parsing/serializing the query string.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317442\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/contextMenu/browser_strip_on_share_link.js", "browser/base/content/test/contextMenu/browser_strip_on_share_nested_link.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser_strip_on_share.js", "toolkit/components/antitracking/URLQueryStringStripper.cpp", "toolkit/components/antitracking/test/browser/browser_urlQueryStringStripping.js"], "git_node": "c928c49b92817c268de246313d369307b8453712", "git_parents": ["d91ce23e019f9acb5dead435830ebcde1f690773"], "node": "9756739978ff4af4cc8c9c28011075dcb8d3edf4", "parents": ["5b2950ce4c2a0cd30ae85018743410961bc073d3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maryam \u003cmomar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1960853 - Add URLParams::ParseWithEquals() helper for parsing parameters with explicit equals signs r=necko-reviewers,timhuang,valentin\n\nURLParams::Parse() and Serialize() cannot distinguish \"x\" from \"x=\":\nboth parse to {name: \"x\", value: \"\"}, which is correct for\nSerialize()'s spec-mandated name=value output (used by\nURLSearchParams), but loses information a caller needs to reproduce\nthe original query string with a minimal edit.\n\nAdds ParseWithEquals(), which additionally passes whether the parsed\nsegment contained an '=' to the handler. Parse() is now implemented in\nterms of ParseWithEquals() to avoid duplicating the parsing loop.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318411\n", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsURLHelper.cpp", "netwerk/base/nsURLHelper.h"], "git_node": "ebfaec8b19e491b07e2eb068962693dce3a3c58a", "git_parents": ["c928c49b92817c268de246313d369307b8453712"], "node": "407ef5228dc8082e32ba0df68a4abcea1cc1fc64", "parents": ["9756739978ff4af4cc8c9c28011075dcb8d3edf4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicol\u00f2 Ribaudo \u003cnribaudo@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051654 - Account for the font scale factor when mapping SVG text rects to user space r=firefox-svg-reviewers,longsonr\n\nRange.getBoundingClientRect() was wrong for a sub-range of an SVG \u003ctext\u003e element that\nis scaled up inside the SVG coordinate system.\n\nAfter converting the rect to user space, it needs to be scaled by the inverse of the\nfont scale factor. Note that the opposite inverse happens in the opposite operation\nTransformFramePointToTextChild, which already scales by the font scale factor.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D309638\n", "files": ["layout/svg/SVGTextFrame.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/cssom-view/getBoundingClientRect-svg.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom-view/getBoundingClientRect-svg.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/text/scripted/range-getboundingclientrect-scaled.html"], "git_node": "9cbf5d852830d817c2a37d94263c5c9fe8d6cef0", "git_parents": ["ebfaec8b19e491b07e2eb068962693dce3a3c58a"], "node": "5d5c08f1219db3371695ac096e4305ec357a522c", "parents": ["407ef5228dc8082e32ba0df68a4abcea1cc1fc64"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kershaw Chang \u003ckershaw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062172 - Propagate TLS errors through TLSTransportLayer, r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323506\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/TLSTransportLayer.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/TLSTransportLayer.h", "netwerk/test/httpserver/NodeServer.sys.mjs", "netwerk/test/unit/test_cert_verification_failure.js", "netwerk/test/unit/test_websocket_fails_2.js"], "git_node": "a326349b65cc56c957b3a08cea72c6b3100c90f0", "git_parents": ["9cbf5d852830d817c2a37d94263c5c9fe8d6cef0"], "node": "21d54e31d9c5685ad230b1d166c6d11432eb8056", "parents": ["5d5c08f1219db3371695ac096e4305ec357a522c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dimi \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068497 - Support per-field-type fallback from the ML model to the regexp heuristic. r=rrando\n\nThe ML model is not equally reliable for every field type. Credit card expiry\nfields are a known case where the regexp heuristics do better, but until now\nthe only way to avoid a bad prediction for one field type was to turn ML off\nfor the whole form.\n\nAdd extensions.formautofill.useml.ignoreFieldTypes, a comma separated list of\nthe field types the model is not trusted with. Those types are left to the\nregexp heuristics, and the model goes on classifying the rest of the form.\n\nThe list gets a Nimbus feature of its own, autofill-ml-ignore-field-types,\nrather than a variable of autofill-ml, so that moving a field type back to the\nregexp heuristics does not have to wait for, or collide with, an autofill-ml\nenrollment.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322894\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/browser_ml_ignore_field_types.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/browser_ml_nimbus.js", "modules/libpref/init/all.js", "toolkit/components/formautofill/shared/FormAutofillHeuristics.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/shared/FormAutofillML.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/shared/FormAutofillUtils.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/nimbus/FeatureManifest.yaml"], "git_node": "463fd894a30e4d1ebf42df477ac99c45de34db33", "git_parents": ["a326349b65cc56c957b3a08cea72c6b3100c90f0"], "node": "c5e274a5307d1ed0c958f3349916d440794ffe5e", "parents": ["21d54e31d9c5685ad230b1d166c6d11432eb8056"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069174 - [remote] Handle killed processes in mach puppeteer-test r=Sasha\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323507\n", "files": ["remote/mach_commands.py"], "git_node": "a499b9d7a379725ae15efa9dab003ba7f6856625", "git_parents": ["463fd894a30e4d1ebf42df477ac99c45de34db33"], "node": "d8f6143ff29d23ea902f64961778ccef64f85db6", "parents": ["c5e274a5307d1ed0c958f3349916d440794ffe5e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069174 - [remote] Disable npm audit and funding checks to avoid npm network requests in CI r=Sasha\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323508\n", "files": ["remote/mach_commands.py"], "git_node": "b5ac97bf54b6f1df66d1dfb0b6a92086ce5206a6", "git_parents": ["a499b9d7a379725ae15efa9dab003ba7f6856625"], "node": "f6d408775e3c1e96e6a9712e862570c51b0b8a38", "parents": ["d8f6143ff29d23ea902f64961778ccef64f85db6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068442 - Make `EditorBase::InsertTextIntoTextNodeWithTransaction` not use `CompositionTransaction` if it's not caused by a composition change r=m_kato\n\n`insertText` command etc may be used during a composition and we need\nto handle them for the backward compatibility and compatibility with\nthe other browsers.\n\nHowever, we should not treat such coming commands as a part of\ncomposition. Therefore, we should make the related methods take\n`InputTextFor` and consider to make an `InsertTextTransaction` for\na text insertion not caused by a composition change.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323152\n", "files": ["editor/libeditor/EditorBase.cpp", "editor/libeditor/EditorBase.h", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditSubActionHandler.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditor.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditor.h", "editor/libeditor/TextEditSubActionHandler.cpp", "editor/libeditor/WhiteSpaceVisibilityKeeper.cpp", "editor/libeditor/WhiteSpaceVisibilityKeeper.h"], "git_node": "68689e51f91ae02dfec26a8b3534c700410f8c9b", "git_parents": ["b5ac97bf54b6f1df66d1dfb0b6a92086ce5206a6"], "node": "1c44f03d654cdb6563bafff7f0b66ffbc281f193", "parents": ["f6d408775e3c1e96e6a9712e862570c51b0b8a38"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062600 - Properly cite llama.cpp in our license file r=sylvestre\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317806\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/license.html"], "git_node": "3d1f858795c9aad0d8a17d0183b276a0756f3177", "git_parents": ["68689e51f91ae02dfec26a8b3534c700410f8c9b"], "node": "63410b81faa291a03c5afd2a1550220e57ec1108", "parents": ["1c44f03d654cdb6563bafff7f0b66ffbc281f193"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068128 - Improve generation of white-listed files for clang-tidy r=sylvestre\n\nCurrent algorithm for third party identification iterates over a list of\ndirectory and checks if any of them contains individual files.\n\nThis list is built from tools/rewriting/ThirdPartyPaths.txt, which also\ncontains many directories or files that do not contains any file that\nmatters for clang-tidy.\n\nRemoving those entries leads to much faster third party identification,\nsaving more than 200ms per file for some C++ sources. It saves 0.3% of\nbuild time on spidermonkey.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322642\n", "files": ["build/clang-plugin/ThirdPartyPaths.py", "tools/rewriting/ThirdPartyPaths.txt"], "git_node": "d63f5809f68189ebad5405836b8bd5e4c2572a7b", "git_parents": ["3d1f858795c9aad0d8a17d0183b276a0756f3177"], "node": "69787c17cd2a675c55f52a8e35a68547153a9b61", "parents": ["63410b81faa291a03c5afd2a1550220e57ec1108"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tiaan Louw \u003ctlouw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1995348 - Implement the \"grid-lanes\" value for the \"display\" property r=layout-reviewers,firefox-style-system-reviewers,dholbert,emilio\n\nUse the \"display: grid-lanes\" value to conform to current usage in web\nplatform tests.\n\nTwo tests are marked as CRASH, because the masonry code uses a sort\ncomparitor that is not valid strick weak ordering as required, so it\nasserts in debug builds. See bug 2068688.\n\nSee: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-grid-3/#masonry-model\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D273845\n", "files": ["layout/base/nsCSSFrameConstructor.cpp", "layout/generic/nsGridContainerFrame.cpp", "layout/inspector/tests/test_bug877690.html", "layout/style/test/property_database.js", "layout/style/test/test_position_float_display.html", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "servo/components/style/values/specified/box.rs", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-anchor-position/__dir__.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-anchor-position/grid-lanes-position-area-basic.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/__dir__.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column