"git_node": "d03571f4f35f7f749d6fdbbb2064f3faafb9fc74", "git_parents": ["7cade52dc7066306a812aa51fb56981906ce6978"], "node": "45cdef60f0069fe6a193897b7c5009ef6d591772", "parents": ["d309506f2f80895cc1b9228851937b9e2dd4163f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Striemer \u003cmstriemer@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069042 - Use currentColor to set toolbarbutton backgrounds in nativeTheme r=dao,desktop-theme-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323345\n", "files": ["toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/semantic-categories.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-platform.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-table.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/components/toolbarbutton.nova.tokens.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/components/toolbarbutton.tokens.json"], "git_node": "c04b2431bf9bdd9598d0deccc352aa2fe0e6d2e9", "git_parents": ["d03571f4f35f7f749d6fdbbb2064f3faafb9fc74"], "node": "0f1f0e4cf0b47383eef6433ddd549902a84e394f", "parents": ["45cdef60f0069fe6a193897b7c5009ef6d591772"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Olivia Hall \u003cohall@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061832 - Turn on pdfjs.annotationEditorMode for Nightly on Android r=calixte\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323596\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/pdfjs/PdfJsOverridePrefs.js"], "git_node": "f1634dc0502a0e4d0081f96adc5ef031ce8bebec", "git_parents": ["c04b2431bf9bdd9598d0deccc352aa2fe0e6d2e9"], "node": "0da206a2dede0e2613d1030d2049b5678d4ddc48", "parents": ["0f1f0e4cf0b47383eef6433ddd549902a84e394f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068385: Don't support sparse arrays in SpreadMathMinMax r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nMarking the testcase --slow because it takes 7+ minutes on my laptop in an opt-debug build.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323120\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/BaselineIC.cpp", "js/src/jit/CacheIR.cpp"], "git_node": "61e706aa7eee837b3a39f3bf69088faa4e3f5584", "git_parents": ["f1634dc0502a0e4d0081f96adc5ef031ce8bebec"], "node": "4b8d85febe3c6b03baa4c48636b240409b206b34", "parents": ["0da206a2dede0e2613d1030d2049b5678d4ddc48"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1378104 - Wait for the page action button to be laid out before triggering _execute_page_action, and destroy the popup when anchoring fails, r=extension-reviewers,robwu.\n\nbrowser_ext_commands_execute_page_action.js presses the _execute_page_action\nshortcut as soon as pageAction.show() has been called, but show() only places\nthe button in the urlbar from a requestAnimationFrame callback, and\npanelAnchorNodeForAction() measures its candidates with\ngetBoundsWithoutFlushing(), so a button that has no frame yet measures 0x0 and\nis skipped. On an ordinary page none of the other candidates is usable either:\n#pageActionButton is also a .urlbar-page-action, and the\nbrowser.urlbar.trustPanel featureGate hides the #identity-icon-box that\ncontains #identity-icon. The lookup therefore throws.\n\nThe throw surfaces as an uncaught rejection, because handleClick()'s callers\ndrop its promise. The popup it was opening is also never shown, and so never\nhidden, which leaves its browser and refresh driver alive for the lifetime of\nthe window; the end-of-test vsync check then fails for every test that follows\nin the manifest.\n\nWait for the button to be laid out before pressing the shortcut. Also destroy\nthe popup when anchoring throws anyway, so that a path that still fails cannot\npin vsync on for the rest of the manifest.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317513\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/parent/ext-pageAction.js", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser-action.toml", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_commands_execute_page_action.js", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_pageAction_popup_anchor.js"], "git_node": "fdf2baf6d9a54932147bda421b4a411dd4a2bb07", "git_parents": ["61e706aa7eee837b3a39f3bf69088faa4e3f5584"], "node": "d60431c361ee0e91fbcf62bf8fc907124738be02", "parents": ["4b8d85febe3c6b03baa4c48636b240409b206b34"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2039637 - Don't open a page action popup for an extension that has already shut down, r=extension-reviewers,robwu.\n\nhandleClick() anchors the popup only after awaiting its content, by which time\nthe extension may have shut down and its button be gone. Today that throws, and\nPanelPopup.closePopup() cannot clean up a popup that never started opening, so\nthe panel keeps its browser and its refresh driver for the lifetime of the\nwindow.\n\nTear the popup down when it has not started opening, resolve contentReady when a\npopup is destroyed so that whoever waits to show it can resume, and give up in\nhandleClick() when its popup has been destroyed. Without this, the panel of a\nfully shut down extension is anchored to the urlbar and shown.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317528\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/ExtensionPopups.sys.mjs", "browser/components/extensions/parent/ext-pageAction.js"], "git_node": "a0b1be3c1555ab181249f1b4b1c4689a6a57a481", "git_parents": ["fdf2baf6d9a54932147bda421b4a411dd4a2bb07"], "node": "1a1ef0cfde76bdaa441715629b73fbdc16869e4d", "parents": ["d60431c361ee0e91fbcf62bf8fc907124738be02"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1307759 - Wait for the window to have actually been resized before resolving windows.update(), and re-enable browser_ext_windows_update.js on linux 24.04 x11, r=extension-reviewers,emilio,robwu.\n\nWidgets report the sizemode change before resizing the window to the size of its\nnew state, so windows.update() resolved with the geometry of the previous state\nstill in place. The resize wait that exiting fullscreen already used now covers\nevery transition between the normal, maximized and fullscreen states. Minimized\ntransitions are excluded: they leave the size unchanged, so waiting for a resize\nthat never comes would cost the whole no-window-manager timeout.\n\nThe headless widget shows this without a window manager: it reports the size mode\nchange first and resizes on the next tick, so windows.update({state:\n\"fullscreen\"}) resolved with the pre-fullscreen size. It is also the shape of the\nfailure this test still hits where it runs, \"Got expected value for window.width\".\n\nWindow managers apply the geometry of a restored size mode in several steps, so\non Linux the test waits for the size the window is restoring to rather than\nasserting on the first value windows.update() reports.\n\nMoves are left unwaited for, in the API and in the widget: no wait would be\nreliable, since a good number of window managers report nothing once a move is\ndone. testPositionBoundaryCheck instead polls for the position rather than\nreading it as soon as windows.update() resolves, and each of its steps asks for\na position no earlier step used, in place of resetting to 50,50 in between, so\nthat a move still in flight cannot satisfy the wait. The poll is bounded and a\nwindow manager that never gets there fails the test rather than passing it.\n\nThe skip for linux 24.04 x11 was carried over from the 18.04 one during the 24.04\ngreenup (bug 1969523) rather than diagnosed, and it is the whole of the Linux\ncoverage of this test.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318269\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/parent/ext-browser.js", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser-windows.toml", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_windows_update.js"], "git_node": "aba1daa7fc9bab11fd6395964ac8b2b26e057a57", "git_parents": ["a0b1be3c1555ab181249f1b4b1c4689a6a57a481"], "node": "71b297a100beb378f681864c4d4870b789acc1fa", "parents": ["1a1ef0cfde76bdaa441715629b73fbdc16869e4d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062229 - Ignore tab hover previews when checking whether a panel blocks extension openPopup(), r=extension-reviewers,tabbrowser-reviewers,robwu,sclements.\n\nisGloballyBlockingOpenPopup() counts every open panel in the window, tab hover\npreviews included, so an extension openPopup() triggered from a keyboard\nshortcut fails whenever the pointer happens to rest on a tab.\n\nThe check exists to keep an extension popup from covering menus and panels the\nuser is interacting with. Tab hover previews are tooltip-like panels tied to the\npointer being over the tab strip, so exclude them from the check instead of\nrejecting openPopup() because of them.\n\nTabHoverPanelSet exposes isHoverPanel() so that the preview panels are\nrecognized from the panel set that owns them rather than from a list of ids.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317521\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/ExtensionPopups.sys.mjs", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser-action.toml", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_action_openPopup_tabPreview.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tab-hover-preview.mjs"], "git_node": "05eab40ec13d12d71ae03a7ff38133eb681a6954", "git_parents": ["aba1daa7fc9bab11fd6395964ac8b2b26e057a57"], "node": "552e35ee283c07de4a09518171f3a21ee82fdde0", "parents": ["71b297a100beb378f681864c4d4870b789acc1fa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lars Eggert \u003clars@eggert.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067308 - Take network timings from the channel's own per-attempt record. r=devtools-reviewers,necko-reviewers,jdescottes,kershaw\n\nThe activity statuses do not distinguish connection attempts, so a restarted\ntransaction inflates dns, connect, ssl and send. Take the phases from\nnsITimedChannel, which keeps them per attempt, clamp the once-per-transaction\nstatuses to the serving attempt, and credit the failed attempt's time to\nblocked. Throttling, simulated by delaying the response activities, still\nmeasures the response from them.\n\nRestart drops the failed attempt's timings and accepted-0-RTT state. Report\nRESPONSE_COMPLETE when Http2Session marks a response complete from the stream\nend.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322859\n", "files": ["devtools/shared/network-observer/NetworkTimings.sys.mjs", "devtools/shared/network-observer/test/xpcshell/test_network_timings_restart.js", "devtools/shared/network-observer/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpTransaction.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpTransaction.h", "netwerk/test/unit/test_transaction_restart_activity.js", "netwerk/test/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "fc19d74aa06860241044a83e9a66afe53acc9a8f", "git_parents": ["05eab40ec13d12d71ae03a7ff38133eb681a6954"], "node": "6c1f724f9f72cced58dc060e24e711d81260e00f", "parents": ["552e35ee283c07de4a09518171f3a21ee82fdde0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan Horak \u003cjhorak@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1955255 Allow passing returned GUnixFDList to the DBusCallFDListPromise; r=emilio\n\nWe want to use the returned fds when g_dbus_proxy_call_with_unix_fd_list_finish is called.\nThis change passes the argument as a std::pair to the fulfillment handler.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D242322\n", "files": ["toolkit/system/gnome/nsGIOService.cpp", "widget/gtk/AsyncDBus.cpp", "widget/gtk/AsyncDBus.h", "widget/gtk/FileTransferPortal.cpp"], "git_node": "c1474be383fe9a0270d9f35d9e7ff653e3441923", "git_parents": ["fc19d74aa06860241044a83e9a66afe53acc9a8f"], "node": "0e910e69da9f09466781c590fb232012050d681a", "parents": ["6c1f724f9f72cced58dc060e24e711d81260e00f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan Horak \u003cjhorak@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1955255 Implement native messaging using xdg-native-messaging-proxy; r=robwu,extension-reviewers,ahal\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D242328\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/mozbase/manifestparser/manifestparser/token.py", "toolkit/components/extensions/NativeMessaging.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/extensions/NativeMessagingProxy.cpp", "toolkit/components/extensions/NativeMessagingProxy.h", "toolkit/components/extensions/components.conf", "toolkit/components/extensions/docs/native-messaging-portal-design.md", "toolkit/components/extensions/moz.build", "toolkit/components/extensions/nsINativeMessagingProxy.idl", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/native_messaging.toml", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_ext_native_messaging_proxy_real.js", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.xpcom.d.ts", "widget/gtk/WidgetUtilsGtk.cpp", "widget/gtk/WidgetUtilsGtk.h"], "git_node": "8a999da4940ce33fcdeb0bec7667ea9a9bcd991e", "git_parents": ["c1474be383fe9a0270d9f35d9e7ff653e3441923"], "node": "57d257f105089b4f9a5b4ce6ae0614cd8dee823d", "parents": ["0e910e69da9f09466781c590fb232012050d681a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1955255: apply code formatting via Lando\n\n# ignore-this-changeset\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/AsyncDBus.h", "widget/gtk/FileTransferPortal.cpp"], "git_node": "31c816e13d51ececb15651e7ae35356908ad47cb", "git_parents": ["8a999da4940ce33fcdeb0bec7667ea9a9bcd991e"], "node": "04fe5436a91bfcd92841b4ad0e45403c26991ccb", "parents": ["57d257f105089b4f9a5b4ce6ae0614cd8dee823d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Minor \u003cdminor@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068418 - Use pref to control regexp buffer boundaries; r=iain\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323313\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/JitContext.cpp", "js/src/jit/JitOptions.cpp", "js/src/jsapi.cpp", "js/src/jsapi.h", "js/src/shell/js.cpp", "js/xpconnect/src/XPCJSContext.cpp"], "git_node": "773860548ecad0f18d9569be65b043cf929460c8", "git_parents": ["31c816e13d51ececb15651e7ae35356908ad47cb"], "node": "efd6ebd2fa35e6122c458dc5992ed7de3722d475", "parents": ["04fe5436a91bfcd92841b4ad0e45403c26991ccb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Minor \u003cdminor@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067391 - Only run test_wasm_offthread_compile on Nightly; r=arai\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323002\n", "files": ["dom/base/test/mochitest.toml"], "git_node": "3373604e7d4622d24fd6f50f5da3bbf9a77757a1", "git_parents": ["773860548ecad0f18d9569be65b043cf929460c8"], "node": "3a3bc359665eb5a25c5c9d65945efc4590ec6a49", "parents": ["efd6ebd2fa35e6122c458dc5992ed7de3722d475"], "tags": []}, {"author": "sarah541 \u003csarahkhan1107@hotmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2023540 - Make the homepage expanded toolbar transparent over the edge-to-edge wallpaper r=android-reviewers,devota\n\nHomeNavigationBar re-wraps its content in FirefoxTheme, which resets the color\nscheme applied by HomeToolbarComposable, and it only re-applied a transparent\nsurface when the universal edge-to-edge wallpapers flag was set. With the\ndedicated edge-to-edge wallpaper the navigation bar still  kept an opaque\nbackground while the address bar next to it was transparent.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322353\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/HomeFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/toolbar/HomeNavigationBar.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/toolbar/HomeToolbarComposable.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/toolbar/HomepageToolbarColors.kt"], "git_node": "0f281e244b3263d41e6d1186aef549cf3a9b6a5d", "git_parents": ["3373604e7d4622d24fd6f50f5da3bbf9a77757a1"], "node": "7324866b4d7d221dcf9fc0bc73540c859207a3f2", "parents": ["3a3bc359665eb5a25c5c9d65945efc4590ec6a49"], "tags": []}, {"author": "lilly \u003c173393835+cupidsity@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065723 [wpt PR 62123] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322215, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export: corner-shape: square and notch corners are built as round and scoop on outlines and box-shadow spread (#62123)\n\nhttps://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322215\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a2dc05da185270baf676cfbd1c440949d270f9ac\nwpt-pr: 62123\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-bevel-round-scoop-square-outset-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-bevel-round-scoop-square-outset.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-notch-squircle-outset-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-notch-squircle-outset.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-superellipse-concave-outset-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-superellipse-concave-outset.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-superellipse-convex-outset-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-superellipse-convex-outset.html"], "git_node": "43a552d7802e3a5649b0d4520aaf8fd566ad8cae", "git_parents": ["0f281e244b3263d41e6d1186aef549cf3a9b6a5d"], "node": "ff4502c6e6d20d7b1b5f071f3ef5b24abbd975d9", "parents": ["7324866b4d7d221dcf9fc0bc73540c859207a3f2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brandon Walderman \u003cbrwalder@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065717 [wpt PR 62119] - [css-mixins] Give each effective MixinMap a unique identity, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-mixins] Give each effective MixinMap a unique identity\n\n@apply is flattened into the RuleSet built for a stylesheet, so a\nRuleSet is only valid for the exact set of mixins it was flattened\nagainst. That set is per tree scope, but StyleSheetContents caches a\nsingle RuleSet and is shared between tree scopes (inline \u003cstyle\u003e text\ncache, adopted stylesheets) and between Documents (the parsed stylesheet\ncache on CSSStyleSheetResource). A RuleSet therefore records the\nidentity of the mixin map it was built against; see\nRuleSet::DependingOnOutdatedMixins().\n\nThat identity used to be a counter owned by StyleSheetCollection, so two\nscopes could hand out the same value for different sets of mixins and\nreuse each other's flattened RuleSet, leaving the winning mixin\ndependent on which scope built its RuleSet first. It is now allocated by\nMixinMap::AllocateMapIdentifier(), unique across every scope and\nDocument on the renderer main thread, and renamed from \"generation\" to\n\"map_identifier\" to reflect that it is an opaque identity.\n\nThis also fixes a second bug: RuleSet recorded a dependency on the mixin\nmap only when an @apply resolved to a mixin, so a RuleSet flattened\nwhere the mixin is undefined looked mixin-independent and leaked into\nscopes that do define it. The identity is now recorded for every @apply,\nand AddRulesFromSheet() no longer clears it, as it recurses for @import.\n\nBug: 496807669\nTest: external/wpt/css/css-mixins/mixins/mixin-shadow-dom.html\nTest: external/wpt/css/css-mixins/mixins/mixin-shared-across-documents.html\nChange-Id: Id4ad99b6bbd717a82a86ba3b98cdb27b6b2be4c3\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8252237\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Brandon Walderman \u003cbrwalder@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1684976}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: bc957dbac9045c22fdd0fa61d0608a55f63f6c3c\nwpt-pr: 62119\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-mixins/mixins/mixin-shadow-dom.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-mixins/mixins/mixin-shared-across-documents.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-mixins/mixins/mixin-shared-sheet-no-mixins-in-scope.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-mixins/mixins/support/mixin-shared-across-documents-frame.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-mixins/mixins/support/mixin-shared-across-documents.css", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-mixins/mixins/support/mixin-shared-across-documents.css.headers"], "git_node": "ff527849384b146cc492d13184bce10507561cc1", "git_parents": ["43a552d7802e3a5649b0d4520aaf8fd566ad8cae"], "node": "cd192c498e13a80dce0efe6eff34b7ce1624884a", "parents": ["ff4502c6e6d20d7b1b5f071f3ef5b24abbd975d9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065717 [wpt PR 62119] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62119\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-mixins/mixins/mixin-shadow-dom.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-mixins/mixins/mixin-shared-across-documents.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-mixins/mixins/mixin-shared-sheet-no-mixins-in-scope.html.ini"], "git_node": "0753119a0eb05055bd3ed4847bd4fd2cdabc235c", "git_parents": ["ff527849384b146cc492d13184bce10507561cc1"], "node": "a392c7315ff0b861d40eb7ed6d02a63f66c051d2", "parents": ["cd192c498e13a80dce0efe6eff34b7ce1624884a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067911 [wpt PR 62264] - Fix \u003clink\u003e stylesheet cascade and refetch with moveBefore, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix \u003clink\u003e stylesheet cascade and refetch with moveBefore\n\nThis fixes two bugs during state-preserving atomic moves on \u003clink\u003e\nelements, one where we weren't invaliding the stylesheet properly and\nanother where we were incorrectly re-fetching the resource.\n\nThe first bug is during RemovedFrom - we need to update the cascade\norder via RemoveStyleSheetCandidateNode.\n\nThe refetch bug initiates in InsertedInto, where we need to early-exit\nin LinkStyle::Process to avoid re-fetching.\n\nThis adds two WPT's that both pass in Gecko and fail in Blink without\nthis change.\n\nstylesheet-cascade-order.html fails with:\n\nThis is a testharness.js-based test. [FAIL] Moving loaded link\nstylesheets updates their cascade order\n  assert_equals: removing the purple stylesheet makes blue win again expected \"rgb(0, 0, 255)\" but got \"rgb(0, 0, 0)\"\n\nstylesheet-no-refetch.html fails with: [FAIL] Moving a loaded link\nstylesheet preserves its resource\n  assert_equals: moving the stylesheet does not fetch it again expected 1 but got 2\n\nHarness: the test ran to completion.\nChange-Id: Ie94630259a09fd6d4ae84e4b3b1be152c8158222\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8236492\nReviewed-by: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688119}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4bb4984b67940cde4c18bbeb9d2b2cd54eb6b3df\nwpt-pr: 62264\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/moveBefore/resources/stylesheet-cascade-blue.css", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/moveBefore/resources/stylesheet-cascade-blue.css.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/moveBefore/resources/stylesheet-cascade-purple.css", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/moveBefore/resources/stylesheet-cascade-purple.css.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/moveBefore/stylesheet-cascade-order.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/moveBefore/stylesheet-no-refetch.html"], "git_node": "222a9e9b209b1452a5a5e7ba15cb03be054a5fe8", "git_parents": ["0753119a0eb05055bd3ed4847bd4fd2cdabc235c"], "node": "6a6fe587809bbb4ef1345143e66e35cef5c1aa35", "parents": ["a392c7315ff0b861d40eb7ed6d02a63f66c051d2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Joanne Pan \u003c71951015+J0pan@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067917 [wpt PR 62288] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319919, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319919 (#62288)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: fb24b8bbf32ce4dffb00bc79e4a5e1f386b2d373\nwpt-pr: 62288\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-values/random-item-computed.html"], "git_node": "f1c90ce825a22c5366ae00c2eeff2c5a7845cb34", "git_parents": ["222a9e9b209b1452a5a5e7ba15cb03be054a5fe8"], "node": "ec0319029baadef2afb3dd6b9762fe6c5d2d7a00", "parents": ["6a6fe587809bbb4ef1345143e66e35cef5c1aa35"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067917 [wpt PR 62288] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62288\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-values/animations/scale-interpolation-crash.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-values/random-item-computed.html.ini"], "git_node": "5f1632cac47d4f1ef17bc7438f209f6a13c2aa46", "git_parents": ["f1c90ce825a22c5366ae00c2eeff2c5a7845cb34"], "node": "196e315defa1944de7bbd827b4ffc0aed9fc50d0", "parents": ["ec0319029baadef2afb3dd6b9762fe6c5d2d7a00"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066904 [wpt PR 62222] - Avoid cyclic insertion in adoption agency, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAvoid cyclic insertion in adoption agency\n\nCyclic insertion can happen due to iframe pagehide, when the iframe\nis removed during the adoption agency algorithm.\n\nSeparate the removal from the insertion, and check for cyclic\nreferences *after* the removal.\n\nSee https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10194\nand https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12708\n\nBug: 547963403\nChange-Id: Ib37ca63359ecfc9f8bce86a69be6eada62d8abb7\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8261279\nCommit-Queue: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688198}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e07b5f3859bc4deca3a23f249cb86d8d346187b6\nwpt-pr: 62222\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/syntax/parsing/crashtests/adoption-agency-cycle-mutation.html"], "git_node": "2f37fd309b18bf4dc78dd07d79a30ec3aff7c179", "git_parents": ["5f1632cac47d4f1ef17bc7438f209f6a13c2aa46"], "node": "dcd99d69bcf775fa28dc5d5d0e7da63ca8450779", "parents": ["196e315defa1944de7bbd827b4ffc0aed9fc50d0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sammy Gill \u003csammy.gill@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067926 [wpt PR 62274] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=312152, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=312152 (#62274)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 77b39c35b360813f9ef2e0828aba32692971984e\nwpt-pr: 62274\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/abspos-relayout-with-scrollable-descendant-vertical-lr.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/abspos-relayout-with-scrollable-descendant.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/flex-column-container-with-scrollable-descendant-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/flex-column-container-with-scrollable-descendant.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/flex-container-multiple-items-with-scrollable-descendant-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/flex-container-multiple-items-with-scrollable-descendant.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/flex-container-with-scrollable-descendant-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/flex-container-with-scrollable-descendant.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/flex-nested-container-with-scrollable-descendant-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/flex-nested-container-with-scrollable-descendant.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/grid-container-with-scrollable-descendant-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/grid-container-with-scrollable-descendant.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/grid-nested-container-with-scrollable-descendant-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/grid-nested-container-with-scrollable-descendant.html"], "git_node": "6ffd9760b68d24564306a0c234fb7a87b1a352f1", "git_parents": ["2f37fd309b18bf4dc78dd07d79a30ec3aff7c179"], "node": "d37b6a1590d8c27b3fa25115b05e2df87c905b24", "parents": ["dcd99d69bcf775fa28dc5d5d0e7da63ca8450779"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067926 [wpt PR 62274] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62274\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/abspos-relayout-with-scrollable-descendant-vertical-lr.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/abspos-relayout-with-scrollable-descendant.html.ini"], "git_node": "cef6e2bc2043b0839acdd419bee2954b86864e32", "git_parents": ["6ffd9760b68d24564306a0c234fb7a87b1a352f1"], "node": "13accb3a5b9df49776581fe3044fdb5df634a85e", "parents": ["d37b6a1590d8c27b3fa25115b05e2df87c905b24"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sammy Gill \u003csammy.gill@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067929 [wpt PR 62279] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322620, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322620 (#62279)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c6246b74d4c085f6804f15ece40711f289e194ec\nwpt-pr: 62279\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scrollable-overflow-from-grid-container-contents.html"], "git_node": "bc7115e2b8c025348ff11921855ef8f602c65310", "git_parents": ["cef6e2bc2043b0839acdd419bee2954b86864e32"], "node": "f5df33f6b1e2d6baf9300202ae0e5f30260f63d8", "parents": ["13accb3a5b9df49776581fe3044fdb5df634a85e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tim Nguyen \u003cnt1m@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067931 [wpt PR 62277] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322843, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export: [css-overflow-4] `text-overflow: \u003cstring\u003e` should work on `\u003cinput\u003e` (#62277)\n\nhttps://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322843\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f01d70241ee0aebcdd2fd68ea4e9e2ff309d78ce\nwpt-pr: 62277\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/text-overflow-string-in-input-notref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/text-overflow-string-in-input.html"], "git_node": "675adee1a1210ed176f3a86dad25527d0f20167b", "git_parents": ["bc7115e2b8c025348ff11921855ef8f602c65310"], "node": "7d457583997d166479762f8a3ea18dcd41ab4c97", "parents": ["f5df33f6b1e2d6baf9300202ae0e5f30260f63d8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mattias Buelens \u003c649348+MattiasBuelens@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049111 [wpt PR 60771] - Streams: fix `ReadableStream.from` tests returning non-objects from `return()`, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nStreams: fix `ReadableStream.from` tests returning non-objects from `return()` (#60771)\n\n* Return objects from `return()` in `ReadableStream.from` tests\n\n* Move assertion out of `next()`\n\n* Test whether `cancel()` fulfills inside `next()`\n\n* Use `unreached_func` instead\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 54078e9ec9d5c73f8815ff38b42b8fcbf1f3200b\nwpt-pr: 60771\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/streams/readable-streams/from.any.js"], "git_node": "1ae1efbbb4f940d01491eb74eda6a750698f782d", "git_parents": ["675adee1a1210ed176f3a86dad25527d0f20167b"], "node": "186f03abcf705123370c082c2d896b27894dbace", "parents": ["7d457583997d166479762f8a3ea18dcd41ab4c97"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mattias Buelens \u003c649348+MattiasBuelens@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067934 [wpt PR 62297] - [css-borders] Fix duplicate fuzzy metadata breaking the manifest build, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-borders] Fix duplicate fuzzy metadata breaking the manifest build (#62297)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5af6acac29b1e384a3fa6aeec15b9fc81875a5c9\nwpt-pr: 62297\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-superellipse-concave-outset.html"], "git_node": "fa26107d9afb46c19f444d268f38d691fda405b7", "git_parents": ["1ae1efbbb4f940d01491eb74eda6a750698f782d"], "node": "1708df0c3da513441ca50c439b530777450f8c6a", "parents": ["186f03abcf705123370c082c2d896b27894dbace"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067934 [wpt PR 62297] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62297\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-bevel-round-scoop-square-outset.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-notch-squircle-outset.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-superellipse-concave-outset.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-superellipse-convex-outset.html.ini"], "git_node": "e7213790b6da6400022d252c22fa53dd3d6169b6", "git_parents": ["fa26107d9afb46c19f444d268f38d691fda405b7"], "node": "97af96e44e51f525f725302a89135c974ef8c6cf", "parents": ["1708df0c3da513441ca50c439b530777450f8c6a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Amit Anilkumar \u003caanilkumar30@gatech.edu\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066666 [wpt PR 62205] - script: Invoke decodeAudioData error callback for detached buffers, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nwpt: Test decodeAudioData error callback on detached buffer\n\nPass the error callback and assert it is invoked with DataCloneError when the ArrayBuffer is detached.\n\nSigned-off-by: Amit Anilkumar \u003caanilkumar30@gatech.edu\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6efb1b12b95725c026cb1f5a451138345cfca937\nwpt-pr: 62205\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-audiocontext-interface/callback-detached-buffer.html"], "git_node": "5c8f841e82aeee6d22c2401ed533053eb76bcc81", "git_parents": ["e7213790b6da6400022d252c22fa53dd3d6169b6"], "node": "7ea520cdbfad160228abcccb78c4337cfc69c22e", "parents": ["97af96e44e51f525f725302a89135c974ef8c6cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067939 [wpt PR 62300] - Remove SharedWorkerGlobalScope onconnect test, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRemove SharedWorkerGlobalScope onconnect test\n\nIt cannot pass: it expects assigning a non-callable object to an event handler\nto yield null, but [LegacyTreatNonObjectAsNull] only nulls out non-objects, and\nit never calls done().\n\nEverything it covers is already tested, correctly. See\nworkers/interfaces/DedicatedWorkerGlobalScope/onmessage.worker.js for the event\nhandler attribute behavior in a worker global, and\nworkers/constructors/SharedWorker/connect-event.html for the connect event.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 81841cc6e29ed4d57173f8b6dd0b736096c0bb58\nwpt-pr: 62300\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/workers/interfaces/SharedWorkerGlobalScope/onconnect.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/workers/interfaces/SharedWorkerGlobalScope/onconnect.js"], "git_node": "e779603cd99b1e2e5f3ee9c41419973198e051f2", "git_parents": ["5c8f841e82aeee6d22c2401ed533053eb76bcc81"], "node": "3b0edd0985a5c9c402bdfaf8892cd1