/show_bug.cgi?id=291164, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=291164 (#62299)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7e755825e0b5c6f631cb862afd5fc451e6825441\nwpt-pr: 62299\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-contain/content-visibility/content-visibility-hidden-and-float-inside-skipped-subtree-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-contain/content-visibility/content-visibility-hidden-and-float-inside-skipped-subtree.html"], "git_node": "d5d4dbd8ba06768a82e0fef5ee2a25a30157359a", "git_parents": ["f4c8a9e4e02f1a2affe829087ecf4c8da93a611e"], "node": "a3842013136f9375ab3c61364604fdf1c6c3942a", "parents": ["027f7f6ee1c114f4a3ecfd70c81976ed011a63f0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067856 [wpt PR 62299] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62299\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-contain/content-visibility/content-visibility-with-top-layer-in-auto-subtree-removal.html.ini"], "git_node": "fcfed5bfc63f642e123687d4a1c16a29855d8341", "git_parents": ["d5d4dbd8ba06768a82e0fef5ee2a25a30157359a"], "node": "1367803d063d7bdac87c06d42771937d809e14f9", "parents": ["a3842013136f9375ab3c61364604fdf1c6c3942a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067983 [wpt PR 62281] - Add deprecation warning banner to all XSLT-transformed documents, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd deprecation warning banner to all XSLT-transformed documents\n\nPreviously, a visible deprecation warning banner was only injected for\nCommon Alerting Protocol (CAP) XML documents transformed via XSLT. This\nCL abstracts out the banner creation logic and displays a deprecation\nwarning banner on all XSLT-transformed documents, to improve visibility\nof the XSLT deprecation across all sites that use it. If the origin\ntrial *or* the enterprise policy are used to opt back in to XSLT, then\nthe banner is *not* shown.\n\nBug: 435623334\nChange-Id: I2cbbde3f20c0da66c69b13dd2e3fa2dde90127ec\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8299492\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688192}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 32118f63aa0cafbc450890512035ce18dedb032d\nwpt-pr: 62281\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/xml/xslt/document-function.window.js"], "git_node": "8a1611e2b055196e26cb0505ab04b31fe3874858", "git_parents": ["fcfed5bfc63f642e123687d4a1c16a29855d8341"], "node": "9cbf6c1de832129596bf3868ea0d8d9de12f3d7c", "parents": ["1367803d063d7bdac87c06d42771937d809e14f9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067983 [wpt PR 62281] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62281\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/xml/xslt/invalid-output-encoding-crash.html.ini"], "git_node": "7bfdbe29d3f8aabb97b8969bbb996bcf6709394c", "git_parents": ["8a1611e2b055196e26cb0505ab04b31fe3874858"], "node": "1a3584276d2b5aad9fc5199a27adee5986d9e224", "parents": ["9cbf6c1de832129596bf3868ea0d8d9de12f3d7c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067985 [wpt PR 62287] - TT: call createParserOptions before createHTML, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nTT: call createParserOptions before createHTML\n\nCalling createParserOptions first allows the policy to prefer the\nbuilt-in sanitizer, and only fall back to createHTML if the method\ndoes not support sanitizer (srcdoc/document.write), the browser does\nnot support createParserOptions, or createParserOptions is not specified by the policy/didn't return a sanitizer.\n\nBug: 491743369\nChange-Id: If71058beebc019f69f7fc1b58cb84e0db1b382c4\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8312789\nCommit-Queue: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Daniel Vogelheim \u003cvogelheim@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688226}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: bb5b8a99a4c391b0c56184c5e3a1d64206126dc7\nwpt-pr: 62287\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/sanitizer-api/sethtml-with-trustedtypes-createParserOptions.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/sanitizer-api/sethtml-with-trustedtypes.tentative.html"], "git_node": "d2a2157c1ba60308a73c96a25c887cf38e8ed084", "git_parents": ["7bfdbe29d3f8aabb97b8969bbb996bcf6709394c"], "node": "3402dc6b77b5bdf7844c45788ed81e4fdd9b4eb8", "parents": ["1a3584276d2b5aad9fc5199a27adee5986d9e224"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067985 [wpt PR 62287] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62287\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/sethtml-with-trustedtypes-createParserOptions.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/sethtml-with-trustedtypes.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "07c1b553612fda65963b447d0122a98f8f2ee178", "git_parents": ["d2a2157c1ba60308a73c96a25c887cf38e8ed084"], "node": "da93ef8a0a119c3a7c30e949e76a97ff05ea5a15", "parents": ["3402dc6b77b5bdf7844c45788ed81e4fdd9b4eb8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067988 [wpt PR 62293] - Change ::interest-button to use proposed anchor positioning, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nChange ::interest-button to use proposed anchor positioning\n\nSee\n\nhttps://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13981#issuecomment-4651351171\n\nThis CL makes Chromium follow that proposal.\n\nBug: 453705247\nChange-Id: I78f27b5bb9ac80d24bc4f1a12179b51d081925a3\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8298380\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688357}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f520e6dadd0074d1e2b7beb2b8b533f2bbe967a9\nwpt-pr: 62293\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/interestfor-pseudo-element-appearance-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/interestfor-pseudo-element-crash.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/interestfor-pseudo-element.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/resources/interest-button-styles.css"], "git_node": "e780984742062abfd615f25fcb29f73b1b14aff8", "git_parents": ["07c1b553612fda65963b447d0122a98f8f2ee178"], "node": "40096778542651b3f406fd06a2ec6cb00e579884", "parents": ["da93ef8a0a119c3a7c30e949e76a97ff05ea5a15"], "tags": []}, {"author": "SeungJun Lee \u003cmps756@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067990 [wpt PR 62284] - [Blink] Preserve FormData File identity, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Blink] Preserve FormData File identity\n\nFormData stored Blob values and applied Blob-to-File conversion and\nfilename overrides whenever a value was retrieved. Repeated get(),\ngetAll(), and iteration therefore returned different File objects, and\nsynthesized lastModified values changed between calls.\n\nNormalize Blob and File values once when creating the entry, matching\nthe HTML create-an-entry algorithm. Retain the filename override used by\nmultipart serialization and preserve backing-file metadata when cloning\na named File.\n\nExpand WPT coverage across set(), append(), custom filenames, getAll(),\nand iteration, and remove the obsolete failure expectations.\n\nBug: 40765469\nTest: xhr/formdata WPT (27 tests)\nTest: form_data.o, form_data_test.o, and libblink_core.so build\nChange-Id: I85bb25f3d647d2e63129244ebf1bb2c540b00f2d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8276954\nCommit-Queue: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688362}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a884161c1c38f9928bb8216ce3646803815269af\nwpt-pr: 62284\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/xhr/formdata/set-blob.any.js"], "git_node": "018f5dce01660ae85edbca64705abb11af1ffbe9", "git_parents": ["e780984742062abfd615f25fcb29f73b1b14aff8"], "node": "cc29e81aa36f7633f315f122e2d5793bb57e36b1", "parents": ["40096778542651b3f406fd06a2ec6cb00e579884"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Monica Chintala \u003cmonicach@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067993 [wpt PR 62286] - WebTransport: Implement Datagram writable streams, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebTransport: Implement Datagram writable streams\n\nAdd WebTransportDatagramDuplexStream.createWritable() and the\nWebTransportDatagramsWritable interface. Each call creates an\nindependent writable stream backed by the session's Datagram transport,\nwith sendGroup/sendOrder attributes, pre-connection buffering, cleanup\nhandling, and outgoing buffer-limit backpressure.\n\nGate the API behind an experimental runtime feature. This CL stores and\nvalidates sendGroup/sendOrder; plumbing those priorities through Mojo\nand the network service is intentionally left to a follow-up CL.\n\nPreserve the behavior of the legacy datagrams.writable stream and use\nweak sink registration so abandoned writable streams can be collected.\n\nThe maximum-size WPT remains expected to fail because this CL retains\nthe conservative 1024-byte maxDatagramSize value after connection.\nFollow-up CL https://crrev.com/c/8252325 plumbs the negotiated maximum\nand silently discards oversized writes.\n\nSpec -\nhttps://www.w3.org/TR/webtransport/#dom-webtransportdatagramduplexstream-createwritable\n\nhttps://www.w3.org/TR/webtransport/#webtransportdatagramswritable\n\nChrome entry - https://chromestatus.com/feature/5183354944225280\n\nBug: 547572475\nChange-Id: I307080981c4bd1e5321c890c504b3356f3f45032\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8254958\nReviewed-by: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Nidhi Jaju \u003cnidhijaju@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Monica Chintala \u003cmonicach@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688446}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 268e748de9c1ed2b306ba4261a36844cc3022bc3\nwpt-pr: 62286\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webtransport/datagrams-writable.https.any.js"], "git_node": "666be0311336b2a6870f4e811fd92b43e1930ac2", "git_parents": ["018f5dce01660ae85edbca64705abb11af1ffbe9"], "node": "fcb152217ed900e472f7f39b434529a2ee0f055e", "parents": ["cc29e81aa36f7633f315f122e2d5793bb57e36b1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrey Kosyakov \u003ccaseq@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067995 [wpt PR 62294] - Expect ServiceWorkerRegistration may have its ExecutionContext detached, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nExpect ServiceWorkerRegistration may have its ExecutionContext detached\n\nI pointed out to Gemini that service worker registration may have its\nExecutionContext return null and asked to locate and fix all call sites\nwhere this may cause a problem.\n\nFixed: 552461801, 332290373\nChange-Id: Id6be35ed3f66067c50949a8f51e923215d9a83eb\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8300597\nCommit-Queue: Andrey Kosyakov \u003ccaseq@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Peter Beverloo \u003cpeter@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688477}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d19d45c8899c7cbf9030dbb2aa45c8693d0bc7da\nwpt-pr: 62294\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/background-sync/crashtests/detached-frame.https.html"], "git_node": "4c9caa2428d601456674cd6f8b12707e18c34dbb", "git_parents": ["666be0311336b2a6870f4e811fd92b43e1930ac2"], "node": "0729d360e3f3cd5a467a6374742c51558587ebce", "parents": ["fcb152217ed900e472f7f39b434529a2ee0f055e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067998 [wpt PR 62295] - [html-in-canvas] Remove the DOMMatrix return type of drawElementImage, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[html-in-canvas] Remove the DOMMatrix return type of drawElementImage\n\nThis patch removes the DOMMatrix return type of drawElementImage and\nupdates the tests accordingly. The change has been put behind the\nElementCanvasTransform feature flag and a basic test has been added to\nthe \"element-canvas-transform-disabled\" virtual test suite to ensure\nusers are not broken.\n\nBug: 532229486\nChange-Id: I81f59043fd776b945fb1f370d5a2874c90dda81a\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8313150\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688489}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 068c4cfd796f745b302d5a3e9f97189c285b3df8\nwpt-pr: 62295\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/anchor-positioning.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/canvas-transform-update.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/draw-element-image-returned-matrix.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/manual/draw-element-image/drawElementImage-returned-matrix-worker.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/manual/draw-element-image/getElementTransform-worker.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/manual/draw-element-image/offscreenCanvas-drawElementImage.tentative.html"], "git_node": "b22333d7a4028c0c1f44b1c8a7a776ad948c0893", "git_parents": ["4c9caa2428d601456674cd6f8b12707e18c34dbb"], "node": "20103c8a8b354e4606edb1685cd541776f5405bf", "parents": ["0729d360e3f3cd5a467a6374742c51558587ebce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Aran Donohue \u003caran.donohue@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066640 [wpt PR 62196] - Let echo-request-headers.py report repeated header names, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nLet echo-request-headers.py report repeated header names\n\necho-request-headers.py keys its JSON payload by header name, so a request that\nuses the same header key more than once loses earlier values.  Add an\nopt-in ?format=list query parameter that reports every header value as a\nlist, in arrival order.\n\nBackward-compatible so no existing tests need to change.\n\nThis is intended for use in WPT tests with duplicate header keys.\n\nChange-Id: I09cb44c10e7674466fa40945865997101a774b43\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8258920\nReviewed-by: Adam Rice \u003cricea@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Robert Flack \u003cflackr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Adam Rice \u003cricea@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688918}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7f294759ec066d6bd7d5094783135c03125f012e\nwpt-pr: 62196\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webtransport/handlers/echo-request-headers.py"], "git_node": "9a11dcc54158a8c50c54ca4167c8173ea8b63951", "git_parents": ["b22333d7a4028c0c1f44b1c8a7a776ad948c0893"], "node": "bd3b374e6b309d78ce67d9939eb67524a02b3be3", "parents": ["20103c8a8b354e4606edb1685cd541776f5405bf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Eldar Pulatov \u003cepulatov.dev@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068003 [wpt PR 62292] - [wpt] Wait for rendering before checking moveBefore() focus fixup, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[wpt] Wait for rendering before checking moveBefore() focus fixup\n\nmoveBefore() preserves focus synchronously. If a move leaves the focused\nelement in an inert or hidden subtree, the focus fixup rule runs during\na rendering update.\n\nThe test waited for a blur event with a one-second timer. The timer was\nnot synchronized with rendering and rejected without a value. When it\nfired first, testharness reported \"Unhandled rejection with value:\nundefined\".\n\nReplace the blur wait with waitForAtLeastOneFrame() before checking\ndocument.activeElement. Give each subtest its own connected fixture and\nverify that moveBefore() moved the node. In the focusable case, check\nthat focus remains after a rendering update.\n\nChange-Id: If9ce8bc838403089c2cb9907af897e6d8fca30ee\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8306396\nReviewed-by: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688423}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3e1155aecaa16d66025c8d1a9ba400fbdef90b59\nwpt-pr: 62292\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/moveBefore/focus-preserve.html"], "git_node": "14ed4d488a6596d412ee6c541e9f69f3f71d5640", "git_parents": ["9a11dcc54158a8c50c54ca4167c8173ea8b63951"], "node": "01374a4433a9bed3c073d3591800fd998c00b539", "parents": ["bd3b374e6b309d78ce67d9939eb67524a02b3be3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Grogan \u003cdgrogan@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068004 [wpt PR 62289] - [menu a11y] Propagate dialog role through entire menu hierarchy, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[menu a11y] Propagate dialog role through entire menu hierarchy\n\nWhen any submenu in a menu hierarchy has forbidden content, every\nmenulist under the same top-level menu, and the top-level menubar\nitself, now gets a dialog aria role.\n\nPreviously, only the specific menu containing the violation would switch\nto a dialog role. This caused strange keyboard behavior, where the user\nwould have to switch between tab and arrow keys inside the same\n(logical) menu.\n\nThe change to \"dialog-everywhere\" behavior enables a top-level-only\narchitecture:\n1. Only the top-most menu element instantiates a MenuMutationObserver.\n2. This observer monitors the DOM subtree; it does not filter mutation\n   records or track detached root ownership, which was hairy. (We do\n   still have to track detached roots on child removal though, to see if\n   a violation was removed.)\n3. We do not observe detached menus. Instead, violations are checked for\n   on attachment.\n4. When content-model-violating elements are added or removed, we defer\n   the menu tree's dialog-mode update to a microtask. Because scripts\n   can insert or remove multiple violating elements in a single\n   synchronous block, delaying the update allows us to walk the menu\n   tree exactly once per JS turn.\n5. If a dialog-mode menu tree has a conforming submenu attached, we\n   update the conforming submenu's role to dialog immediately.\n\nAlternative designs considered:\n1. Each submenu has its own MenuMutationObserver and keeps track of its\n   own local violations. This required updating the root menu's global\n   counter, which was a few hundred lines more code with brittle logic.\n   It also required filtering observations to not double count submenu\n   violations. Initial hack at https://crrev.com/c/8275830\n2. Single root MenuMutationObserver (same as this CL) but synchronous\n   tree updates instead of via a microtask. This approach was slightly\n   less code but the logic to avoid a storm of redundant tree walks was\n   hard to follow.\n\nNote: as mentioned above, this CL changes the top-level menubar ARIA\nrole to dialog in the presence of a content model violation. We may\nchange that behavior upon further screen-reader testing.\n\nBug: 513637242\nChange-Id: I0cbfeab5cd3275e41dfc944d482be869c4899eb0\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8277920\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: David Grogan \u003cdgrogan@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688534}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e7d368cc9d4c87e805a025724a6a828306f4ca81\nwpt-pr: 62289\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/menu-content-model-violation.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/menu-dialog-mode-focus.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/reparent-with-pending-dialog-microtask.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/valid-submenu-invalid-root.html"], "git_node": "96d036eb5910352a5f94c3d9112c8675e10fa29a", "git_parents": ["14ed4d488a6596d412ee6c541e9f69f3f71d5640"], "node": "8c5223b5bb358b9fac85ca0412dfd6c1702b2693", "parents": ["01374a4433a9bed3c073d3591800fd998c00b539"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vaibhav Srivastava \u003cvaibhavsri1712@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068098 [wpt PR 62298] - docs: fix typo arbitary -\u003e arbitrary, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\ndocs: fix typo arbitary -\u003e arbitrary (#62298)\n\nSigned-off-by: Vaibhav Srivastava \u003cvaibhavsri1712@gmail.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 2ccd2cbf88ff710ff1ca5786da13aac0b1e07a59\nwpt-pr: 62298\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/docs/config.rst"], "git_node": "1321d3375ba74b406dbe1b158fe3041cb68382cf", "git_parents": ["96d036eb5910352a5f94c3d9112c8675e10fa29a"], "node": "9224969265fd5b26c83042cc47ecb08b087a006a", "parents": ["8c5223b5bb358b9fac85ca0412dfd6c1702b2693"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriel Brito \u003cgabrielbrito@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068101 [wpt PR 62283] - Fix visibility propagation to frames created hidden, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix visibility propagation to frames created hidden\n\nThis CL fixes the visibility data propagation to iframes that were\ncreated in an already hidden subtree. Without these changes, an iframe\ncreated hidden (display: none; visibility:hidden; zero-area) and not\nallowed to play audio by the `media-playback-while-not-visible`\npermission policy, could start playing audio when it shouldn't.\n\nA cross-origin iframe initially exists as an `about:blank` `LocalFrame`\nin the parent renderer. The parent can correctly compute and deliver the\nhidden media state to this initial frame. When the cross-origin\nnavigation commits, that `LocalFrame` is replaced by a `RemoteFrame` in\nthe parent renderer, while the destination renderer creates the real\n`LocalFrame`. The media visibility state from the initial frame is not\ntransferred during this swap, so the destination frame initially\nreceives the default `is_hidden_for_media_playback = false` value.\n\nNormally, a later viewport-intersection update corrects the value.\nHowever, a `display:none` iframe has no layout object, so no geometry or\nlifecycle event re-arms the parent intersection update. The OOPIF\ntherefore keeps the incorrect visible state.\n\nThere is a related ordering issue for nested same-process frames. If a\nchild is created after its hidden parent has already propagated its\nmedia visibility state, the new child misses that update. Because the\nhidden parent is render-throttled, another lifecycle pass may not run to\ncorrect it.\n\nThis change closes both propagation gaps:\n\n- When a `RemoteFrameView` is created, re-arm the embedding `LocalFrameView`'s intersection observation and schedule a lifecycle update. This recomputes the new remote frame's media visibility state after the process swap, even when the iframe has no layout object.\n- When a `LocalFrame` is initialized under an already-hidden same-process parent, inherit the parent's hidden media state. This covers descendants created after the parent's earlier intersection pass.\n\nBug: 351354996\nChange-Id: I572793f584be3b784a73ea49b1ee74cca6086294\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8128064\nCommit-Queue: Gabriel Brito \u003cgabrielbrito@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688249}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f99609f5d005595fbeb882b46c5dbea190d22bc2\nwpt-pr: 62283\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/media-playback-while-not-visible-permission-policy/cant-play-when-created-hidden.tentative.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/media-playback-while-not-visible-permission-policy/resources/media-playback-while-not-visible-utils.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webaudio/the-audio-api/media-playback-while-not-visible-permission-policy/interrupt-when-created-hidden.tentative.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webaudio/the-audio-api/media-playback-while-not-visible-permission-policy/resources/media-playback-while-not-visible-utils.js"], "git_node": "961fe656bba73ad5fd34efd23c6a288ad986895a", "git_parents": ["1321d3375ba74b406dbe1b158fe3041cb68382cf"], "node": "aa9327fb619a6ed121fa8d9f506ca330e2c1990c", "parents": ["9224969265fd5b26c83042cc47ecb08b087a006a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068101 [wpt PR 62283] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62283\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/media-playback-while-not-visible-permission-policy/cant-play-when-created-hidden.tentative.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webaudio/the-audio-api/media-playback-while-not-visible-permission-policy/interrupt-when-created-hidden.tentative.sub.html.ini"], "git_node": "2bb0c1359583fdf4e9ce2fe96a95a533f8808ccf", "git_parents": ["961fe656bba73ad5fd34efd23c6a288ad986895a"], "node": "bd2bcb81b35fd57e494973a6df71e6fa4d7c09f2", "parents": ["aa9327fb619a6ed121fa8d9f506ca330e2c1990c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Johannes Odland \u003cjohannes.odland@nrk.no\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067935 [wpt PR 51361] - Test all punctiation and whitespace categories that should be included in ::first-letter, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nCSS: test punctuation and whitespace categories that should be included in ::first-letter\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5e59630a71561d44b62309ab97e6849a81a48f1d\nwpt-pr: 51361\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/first-letter-punctuation-and-space-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/first-letter-punctuation-and-space.html"], "git_node": "c3ca926fa143c1a299ea43b5aa66c2410f97edfa", "git_parents": ["2bb0c1359583fdf4e9ce2fe96a95a533f8808ccf"], "node": "fe4a99c1c32c4f9c4de40f867c0ca1fd809dfff2", "parents": ["bd2bcb81b35fd57e494973a6df71e6fa4d7c09f2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067935 [wpt PR 51361] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 51361\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-pseudo/chrome-bug-1299142-crash.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-pseudo/chrome-first-letter-container-query-crash.html.ini"], "git_node": "19aeb886559b4f3de004d4f0714e32424ab08ae3", "git_parents": ["c3ca926fa143c1a299ea43b5aa66c2410f97edfa"], "node": "610e1dac95134e9c6b78f18862232964088e6014", "parents": ["fe4a99c1c32c4f9c4de40f867c0ca1fd809dfff2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003c52317531+Ahmad-S792@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068115 [wpt PR 62340] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322950, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322950 (#62340)\n\nCo-authored-by: Ahmad Saleem \u003cahmadsaleem@Ahmads-MacBook-Pro.local\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 10d18c6d8c6dee09a2209eff9117121bfafb2d24\nwpt-pr: 62340\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/animations/additive-color-precision-animation.html"], "git_node": "9a71bfb329993c292f12e0f593c2bed1339d3200", "git_parents": ["19aeb886559b4f3de004d4f0714e32424ab08ae3"], "node": "227e610fc4b21c7bbd7fecd489aa9d85f366ed9e", "parents": ["610e1dac95134e9c6b78f18862232964088e6014"], "tags": []}, {"author": "taher \u003c8665427+nullhook@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068118 [wpt PR 62338] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323017, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323017 (#62338)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3b9b0ed543915133fb2ed35e8d71058e98a98120\nwpt-pr: 62338\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-background-image-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-background-image.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-basic-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-basic.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-duplicate-name-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-duplicate-name.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-dynamic-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-dynamic.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-fallback-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-fallback.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-geometry-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-geometry.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-none-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-none.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-per-container-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-per-container.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/resources/geometry.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/resources/solid.svg"], "git_node": "3ff2480c9bd6f612a9a3026fdb105d291d154dbb", "git_parents": ["9a71bfb329993c292f12e0f593c2bed1339d3200"], "node": "44b1dcbe52a6308ea618c76cf2b2aeb13ee7f574", "parents": ["227e610fc4b21c7bbd7fecd489aa9d85f366ed9e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068118 [wpt PR 62338] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62338\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-duplicate-name.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-geometry.html.ini"], "git_node": "1124ef4b63ba38f2b4f5018742b40de479eb352d", "git_parents": ["3ff2480c9bd6f612a9a3026fdb105d291d154dbb"], "node": "1fd82ca9d3743f9ddbae8e8cc8828b6b4a77eb50", "parents": ["44b1dcbe52a6308ea618c76cf2b2aeb13ee7f574"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Antti Koivisto \u003cantti@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067875 [wpt PR 62326] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322983, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322983 (#62326)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 384c6d4cc3eeaef056564c29446bdfe853991da8\nwpt-pr: 62326\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-mixins/functions/at-function-parsing.html"], "git_node": "aa479766301d3d91a2333a793beac2e8c8eb9676", "git_parents": ["1124ef4b63ba38f2b4f5018742b40de479eb352d"], "node": "afba4f4b41d351f09285e4a6add8783ce37d2e70", "parents": ["1fd82ca9d3743f9ddbae8e8cc8828b6b4a77eb50"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067875 [wpt PR 62326] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62326\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-mixins/functions/at-function-parsing.html.ini"], "git_node": "d77004b43673320d003764d0681cc3a54c916e5f", "git_parents": ["aa479766301d3d91a2333a793beac2e8c8eb9676"], "node": "b244f0bed8181ae249fffff0c469a2c3c5504790", "parents": ["afba4f4b41d351f09285e4a6add8783ce37d2e70"], "tags": []}, {"author": "jogibear9988 \u003cjochen.kuehner@gmx.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054528 [wpt PR 61254] - Refactor GeometryUtils coverage, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRefactor GeometryUtils coverage\n\nAlign the CSSOM View GeometryUtils tests with Chromium change 8039580, patch set 13.\n\nSplit the combined special-cases test into focused coverage for lifecycle behavior, connected callbacks, Text nodes, shadow DOM, fragmentation, same-origin iframe conversion, and cross-origin ancestor paths. Add the supporting nested cross-origin resources.\n\nExpand convertPointFromNode coverage for flattened 2D results and display:none nodes, cover SVG geometry under CSS zoom, and verify box edge handling for fragmented inline elements.\n\nThe imported Chromium test and resource files match the review byte-for-byte.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b957e6bb661cdbd0ee6e4f71d8b81d3681fef6d1\nwpt-pr: 61254\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom-view/cssom-geometryutils-special-cases.html"], "git_node": "5f7876aaa74c73545d447b50d9210bcda246c39a", "git_parents": ["d77004b43673320d003764d0681cc3a54c916e5f"], "node": "054b4f15aef485a1ab0107b9194cb21094a9980c", "parents": ["b244f0bed8181ae249fffff0c469a2c3c5504790"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067885 [wpt PR 62327] - custom-elements: test that setValidity() normalizes newlines, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\ncustom-elements: test that setValidity() normalizes newlines\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0d1ac26816ba7519fd56e798c45caa3d7bd91416\nwpt-pr: 62327\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/custom-elements/form-associated/ElementInternals-setValidity-normalize-newlines.html"], "git_node": "1ed30b4eb2e91893f11778b2a0b372166018195d", "git_parents": ["5f7876aaa74c73545d447b50d9210bcda246c39a"], "node": "6569ac5811f99a1f39d02e0f4f6ef889f77c54cc", "parents": ["054b4f15aef485a1ab0107b9194cb21094a9980c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067885 [wpt PR 62327] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62327\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/custom-elements/form-associated/ElementInternals-setValidity-normalize-newlines.html.ini"], "git_node": "d40bc96eda37d104622131444cc06ae037b21e8b", "git_parents": ["1ed30b4eb2e91893f11778b2a0b372166018195d"], "node": "e424c44dacb3d59cdb66560e6780cada66a124c4", "parents": ["6569ac5811f99a1f39d02e0f4f6ef889f77c54cc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068146 [wpt PR 62346] - HTML parsing: foster parenting when script moves the table, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nHTML parsing: foster parenting when script moves the table\n\nA single \"nobr\" start tag foster parents twice: once when reconstructing the\nactive formatting elements, and again after the adoption agency algorithm finds\nno furthest block and pops the stack of open elements back to the \u003ctr\u003e. The\n\u003cscript\u003e element holding the table is therefore the foster parent, so the\nparser's own insertion runs it, and it can move or remove the table before the\nsecond insertion happens.\n\nThe appropriate place for inserting a node is computed per insertion, so the\nsecond one has to account for that: into the table's new parent immediately\nbefore it, into a template element's contents, or, once the table has no parent,\ninto the element immediately above it in the stack of open elements.\n\nAlso checks that the tree stays well-formed in each case, which is what fails\nwhen an implementation inserts before a reference child that has moved away.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 22d886d32824cb22decf0de1493b6aaa36a042c7\nwpt-pr: 62346\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/syntax/parsing/foster-parenting-moved-table.window.js"], "git_node": "8a780e15227764c0ab2148f9eb9e509acae56b02", "git_parents": ["d40bc96eda37d104622131444cc06ae037b21e8b"], "node": "1a35ef5ab0f4ef25e1cdaa104e617f55ce744b4a", "parents": ["e424c44dacb3d59cdb66560e6780cada66a124c4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068146 [wpt PR 62346] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62346\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/syntax/parsing/foster-parenting-moved-table.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "ed23eb35c2b49e08ec631eed5b1d6d60a40133e3", "git_parents": ["8a780e15227764c0ab2148f9eb9e509acae56b02"], "node": "16243cf72491c7be022c28f5af0e387a8963aa85", "parents": ["1a35ef5ab0f4ef25e1cdaa104e617f55ce744b4a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068147 [wpt PR 62355] - Test that Document.parseHTMLUnsafe() uses the current global object, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nTest that Document.parseHTMLUnsafe() uses the current global object\n\nFor https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/11799\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5275752104c9aa78a6cf478ebbaef4991b37ac93\nwpt-pr: 62355\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/trusted-types/Document-parseHTMLUnsafe-respects-current-globals-CSP.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/trusted-types/support/parseHTMLUnsafe-without-trusted-types.html"], "git_node": "704cabe4c84d48ccd6c676328e38ead921809f65", "git_parents": ["ed23eb35c2b49e08ec631eed5b1d6d60a40133e3"], "node": "e8c706ee7bc71f69b84bda04633a6d0a5ab43127", "parents": ["16243cf72491c7be022c28f5af0e387a8963aa85"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068147 [wpt PR 62355] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62355\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/trusted-types/__dir__.ini"], "git_node": "5efab9033c167dbb0f63852aa9ab15c075bca679", "git_parents": ["704cabe4c84d48ccd6c676328e38ead921809f65"], "node": "f6778521fefd9ac9e45953832d8182398ce0d06c", "parents": ["e8c706ee7bc71f69b84bda04633a6d0a5ab43127"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Karl Dubost \u003ckarlcow@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068150 [wpt PR 62345] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=303073, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=303073 (#62345)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 84e05db1de2fa8cdb00b78550ddc2af9b4fef200\nwpt-pr: 62345\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/types/scripted/SVGAnimatedNumber-invalid-values.html"], "git_node": "a7f20e2378350683a43e75b90560d34b3ba6af40", "git_parents": ["5efab9033c167dbb0f63852aa9ab15c075bca679"], "node": "c28476b250ce30a640b5d5063fc5eb795276a0e2", "parents": ["f6778521fefd9ac9e45953832d8182398ce0d06c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "sb3nder \u003csb3nd3r@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060360 [wpt PR 61696] - Update corner-shape ref rendering to match new algo, and add test cases, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nUpdate corner-shape ref rendering to match new algo, and add test cases (#61696)\n\n* fix gallery title\n\n* update corner-shape ref rendering to match new algo\nsee w3c/csswg-drafts#14142\n- fix border-width use.\n- add clip-path to test non-uniform outsets.\n\n* tweak 2 test variant\n\n* add test cases\n\n* fix position when using margins\n\n* Add more test cases\n\n* test non-uniform insets\n\n* test tricky mixed inset-outset case\n\n* test \"blue area rule\"\n\n* editorial pass\n\n* tweak and add test case\n\n* fix issues\n- fix \"ripple\" issue for `0 \u003c k \u003c 1` by drawing a single curve without miter lines, ensuring C2 continuity.\n- fix C1 discontinuity for `-1 \u003c k \u003c 0` between the curve and miter lines by drawing an approximate superellipse that can be mapped to any case.\n- fix C0 discontinuity in self-intersections as a result of the C1 continuity fix.\n- respect \"blue area rule\" by avoiding the control point method.\n\n* lint\n\n* editorial, align with spec\n\n* fix sign typo\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1b3e31000536bc29ff232a8a620ef0e00b520c59\nwpt-pr: 61696\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-gallery.manual.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/render-corner-shape.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/resources/render-corner-shape.js"], "git_node": "9a9da1342fe9a121340f30fe2a8e0bedb1f8a09f", "git_parents": ["a7f20e2378350683a43e75b90560d34b3ba6af40"], "node": "b277c63ba2ccafb252abc3aad674f206e0fe7e71", "parents": ["c28476b250ce30a640b5d5063fc5eb795276a0e2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060360 [wpt PR 61696] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61696\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/render-corner-shape.html.ini"], "git_node": "5bac881ca41c6eb65ba7aff56dbd5637d793296d", "git_parents": ["9a9da1342fe9a121340f30fe2a8e0bedb1f8a09f"], "node": "395078139cc6f41ea15504100a894b90598088f1", "parents": ["b277c63ba2ccafb252abc3aad674f206e0fe7e71"], "tags": []}, {"author": "dependabot[bot] \u003c49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2027224 [wpt PR 58731] - Bump httpx from 0.27.2 to 0.28.1 in /tools, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nBump httpx from 0.27.2 to 0.28.1 in /tools\n\nBumps [httpx](https://github.com/encode/httpx) from 0.27.2 to 0.28.1.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/encode/httpx/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/encode/httpx/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/encode/httpx/compare/0.27.2...0.28.1)\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/tools/requirements_tests.txt"], "git_node": "166fdaa3df29175515dee53acf15549fb7005f62", "git_parents": ["5bac881ca41c6eb65ba7aff56dbd5637d793296d"], "node": "b07be80b5cf28c30885762f47f11abbb2cff502a", "parents": ["395078139cc6f41ea15504100a894b90598088f1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068183 [wpt PR 62350] - Test named access on the window object with non-HTML elements, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nTest named access on the window object with non-HTML elements\n\nAll engines expose elements from any namespace by their id, not just\nHTML elements, and only expose HTML embed, form, img, and object\nelements by their name.\n\nFor https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/9766\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3398bb1f184d3eed8ff5c69b5feac188e8f06078\nwpt-pr: 62350\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/the-window-object/named-access-on-the-window-object/id-non-html-elements.html"], "git_node": "4b267fae25ca7bcde0d2b39acb2c757b0af74bdf", "git_parents": ["166fdaa3df29175515dee53acf15549fb7005f62"], "node": "735feb35bdeb78bd67510267bf90a90837e30cd6", "parents": ["b07be80b5cf28c30885762f47f11abbb2cff502a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068183 [wpt PR 62350] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62350\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/the-window-object/named-access-on-the-window-object/id-non-html-elements.html.ini"], "git_node": "ad2f745ccc8a9be0d47287b53f61954527a15596", "git_parents": ["4b267fae25ca7bcde0d2b39acb2c757b0af74bdf"], "node": "23a8c5727e32f2d7b6c16089a597bbd78a210b0e", "parents": ["735feb35bdeb78bd67510267bf90a90837e30cd6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068493 [wpt PR 62336] - [html-in-canvas] Element.getCanvasTransform -\u003e Canvas.getElementTransform, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[html-in-canvas] Element.getCanvasTransform -\u003e Canvas.getElementTransform\n\nThis patch implements the new behavior of having getElementTransform on\nHTMLCanvasElement, where it can be updated via\n{update, clear}ElementGeometry. This patch removes the getters and\nsetters for the canvas transform on Element.\n\nBug: 532229486\nChange-Id: I6504e68010099c87f7f9f80ee84fa74ae460c8c0\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8310981\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688497}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 16c4d3344adb306dfd4da470fd8a0ee3257045f0\nwpt-pr: 62336\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/canvas-transform-get-bounding-client-rect.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/canvas-transform-get-set.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/canvas-transform-update.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/hit-test/elementsFromPoint.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint.tentative.html"], "git_node": "6f09dc93e938fc957ff8d0e6ba92522030aadcf1", "git_parents": ["ad2f745ccc8a9be0d47287b53f61954527a15596"], "node": "17376412afaa46a66e79f7f8f3b9902dabccf02e", "parents": ["23a8c5727e32f2d7b6c16089a597bbd78a210b0e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068493 [wpt PR 62336] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62336\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/canvas-transform-get-bounding-client-rect.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/canvas-transform-get-set.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/hit-test/z-index.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "cca621716e59c5709690ad3e32db3bc84b6564b1", "git_parents": ["6f09dc93e938fc957ff8d0e6ba92522030aadcf1"], "node": "dc6d6c31ee9506699767f7ecdddbee184b588e1f", "parents": ["17376412afaa46a66e79f7f8f3b9902dabccf02e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Aran Donohue \u003caran.donohue@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067698 [wpt PR 62312] - Strengthen the WebTransport headers web tests, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nStrengthen the WebTransport headers web tests\n\nThe sequence-of-sequences test only checked that the option was accepted.\nConnect to echo-request-headers.py instead and assert that both headers\narrive at the server.\n\nAdd additional test coverage.\n\nR=ricea@chromium.org\n\nChange-Id: Ib71bec04f448e59284de710a5186222bdf1376f3\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8257344\nReviewed-by: Nidhi Jaju \u003cnidhijaju@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Adam Rice \u003cricea@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Adam Rice \u003cricea@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688914}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f5ef39900447f9d6c65ed521a3659e7e3bad5a13\nwpt-pr: 62312\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webtransport/headers.https.any.js"], "git_node": "9fd4c7c7e610cadfcd7f1da99a032b93045ce285", "git_parents": ["cca621716e59c5709690ad3e32db3bc84b6564b1"], "node": "17f8ebf634291e0790541cd0881ebc7d7299399d", "parents": ["dc6d6c31ee9506699767f7ecdddbee184b588e1f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067698 [wpt PR 62312] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62312\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webtransport/bidirectional-cancel-crash.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webtransport/headers.https.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "a389e3737ba001a464a30519205967b218f74a63", "git_parents": ["9fd4c7c7e610cadfcd7f1da99a032b93045ce285"], "node": "e24ff6698c2b7d65a36fb35f4e58f6f6a2408314", "parents": ["17f8ebf634291e0790541cd0881ebc7d7299399d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068498 [wpt PR 62306] - [Masonry] Add initial row grid-lanes fragmentation, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Masonry] Add initial row grid-lanes fragmentation\n\nAdd initial item fragmentation for row grid-lanes containers, expanding\non a similar change for columns in CL:8175168.\n\nGeneralize the item iterator to process row items, as well, similarly to\nflexbox. Row tracks are sized independently of their items, so use\ntheir track offsets to decide whether an unstarted row belongs in the\ncurrent fragment while allowing content from an earlier row to overflow.\n\nConvert persisted offsets to fragment-relative coordinates, create\nfragmented child constraint spaces, and derive each fragment's intrinsic\nblock size from the remaining row track geometry.\n\nSpanners, dense-packed items, fragmented subgrids, break rules, row\nexpansion, margins, baselines, and cloned decorations remain follow-up\nwork.\n\nAdd single- and multi-row WPT coverage adapted from Flex.\n\nBug: 343257585\nChange-Id: If1b578d399faea98c1ef3535c0669ee18b90bd89\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8307632\nCommit-Queue: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1689129}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 59ee77086dc86b06722f0e6402d26e5e881c94ca\nwpt-pr: 62306\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/grid-lanes-fragmentation-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-004.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-005.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-006.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-single-lane-fragmentation-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-single-lane-fragmentation-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-single-lane-fragmentation-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-single-lane-fragmentation-004.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-single-lane-fragmentation-005.html"], "git_node": "2f72722b6f9c8faa5db6017a8aff2c646cb45d83", "git_parents": ["a389e3737ba001a464a30519205967b218f74a63"], "node": "7be2c4dc93526ab6af3948e6fd6c69d2bb7e14f4", "parents": ["e24ff6698c2b7d65a36fb35f4e58f6f6a2408314"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068498 [wpt PR 62306] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62306\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-004.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-005.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-006.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-single-lane-fragmentation-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-single-lane-fragmentation-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-single-lane-fragmentation-004.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-single-lane-fragmentation-005.html.ini"], "git_node": "f8e3e517c265fa1d4cbca82a93ce02ffbafbdd23", "git_parents": ["2f72722b6f9c8faa5db6017a8aff2c646cb45d83"], "node": "b6757ed6378918bd200b7d4855149b7387b64fc6", "parents": ["7be2c4dc93526ab6af3948e6fd6c69d2bb7e14f4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "J\u00falio Piubello \u003cjulio@gitstart.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068499 [wpt PR 62285] - DevTools: Honor desktop viewport overrides on Android, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDevTools: Honor desktop viewport overrides on Android\n\nEmulation.setDeviceMetricsOverride with mobile=false and an explicit\nwidth or height changes the emulated widget size on Android, but Blink\notherwise keeps the embedder's native mobile viewport profile. Pages\nwithout viewport metadata therefore retain the 980px layout viewport\ninstead of using the requested dimensions.\n\nRepresent those requests as a derived desktop-viewport mode in\nDevToolsEmulator. Apply ViewportStyle::kDefault and a minimum page scale\nof 1, while DPR-only and scale-only overrides retain the latest embedder\nviewport style and scale limits. Keep transitions in the existing\nsave/apply/restore model and restore the latest embedder settings when\ndimensions are removed, the mode changes, or emulation is cleared.\n\nA previous patchset routed both embedder setters through the full mode\napplicator. That allowed SetDefaultPageScaleLimits() to overwrite an\neffective viewport style installed directly by existing callers and\nregressed two focus-autozoom WebFrameSimTests. Keep stable-mode setter\nupdates property-local: scale changes update only scale limits, style\nchanges update only viewport style, and a style change runs the full\ntransition only when it changes the derived mode.\n\nSeparate effective-profile application from synchronous lifecycle\nownership. Complete device-emulation enable/disable operations retain\nthe conditional lifecycle update after the whole profile, including\nnon-viewport mobile settings, has been applied. Scalar WebSettings\nupdates may run while ApplyWebPreferences() is applying a batch, so\nthey update effective viewport state without forcing layout mid-batch.\n\nAdd renderer coverage for two-way property isolation, full, partial,\nrepeated, DPR-only, scale-only, mobile/desktop, embedder-update, clear,\nshared mobile-emulation ownership, non-flushing viewport-style updates,\nand synchronous platform-color processing on mobile enter/exit. Add\ndirect Android CDP coverage, remove the now-stale Android BiDi WPT\nexpectations, and mark the viewport WPT as long.\n\nOverview doc: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P3lQkK9jMVF3kBDSWApoCh5SXUTAwdUHGSAc7Ir7qGU/edit?usp=sharing\n\nBug: 536833620\nInclude-Ci-Only-Tests: chromium.android:android-15-x64-rel|android_webdriver_wpt_tests\nInclude-Ci-Only-Tests: chromium.android:android-16-x64-rel|android_webdriver_wpt_tests\nInclude-Ci-Only-Tests: chromium.android:android-15-x64-rel|content_browsertests\nInclude-Ci-Only-Tests: chromium.android:android-16-x64-rel|content_browsertests\nCq-Include-Trybots: luci.chromium.try\u200b:android-15-x64-rel;luci.chromium.try\u200b:android-16-x64-rel\nChange-Id: Iaeed7f66c80bea82005caadaadcf16c8582c2463\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8116935\nReviewed-by: Danil Somsikov \u003cdsv@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Julio Piubello \u003cjulio@gitstart.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Nate Chapin \u003cjaphet@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Alex Rudenko \u003calexrudenko@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1689135}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9cd0258382d9f6fdaf8b152642cdf8120689bcef\nwpt-pr: 62285\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/browsing_context/set_viewport/viewport.py"], "git_node": "f7276241f31d02751569d4dfe444a01ea1775888", "git_parents": ["f8e3e517c265fa1d4cbca82a93ce02ffbafbdd23"], "node": "ed0e0647a4dce77dc1c85d77e7ff900731143479", "parents": ["b6757ed6378918bd200b7d4855149b7387b64fc6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen McGruer \u003csmcgruer@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068502 [wpt PR 62331] - Add Payment Method Manifest WPTs for redirects, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd Payment Method Manifest WPTs for redirects\n\nThis adds tests covering various redirect scenarios for payment\nmethod manifests. Tests added:\n\n   - Same-site cross-origin redirects on initial HEAD request - allowed\n   - Cross-site redirects on initial HEAD request - disallowed\n   - Initial HEAD request undergoing 3 redirects - allowed\n   - Initial HEAD request undergoing 4 redirects - disallowed\n   - Redirect on Payment Method Manifest GET request - disallowed\n   - Relative Link header targets should be resolved against the final\n     post-redirect response URL\n\nBug: 552832440\nChange-Id: If71ea0f7ce04b4cb5cb5f5230dd94771ecdbbba2\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8295860\nReviewed-by: Xuehui Chen \u003cxuehuichen@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Stephen McGruer \u003csmcgruer@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1689160}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1340fbf85348038db1e4fda2ea78929fdf7091f1\nwpt-pr: 62331\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/payment-method-manifest/link-header-redirect-resolution.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/payment-method-manifest/pmi-redirect-limits.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/payment-method-manifest/pmi-redirect-origins.https.sub.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/payment-method-manifest/pmm-redirect-disallowed.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/payment-method-manifest/resources/helpers.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/payment-method-manifest/resources/payment-method-identifier.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/payment-method-manifest/resources/payment-method-manifest.py"], "git_node": "7793e56da2a6742e3e652417183e89e356b1ed92", "git_parents": ["f7276241f31d02751569d4dfe444a01ea1775888"], "node": "85f7aecbadca1422cfd268f7c06b160d38079a36", "parents": ["ed0e0647a4dce77dc1c85d77e7ff900731143479"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068502 [wpt PR 62331] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62331\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/payment-method-manifest/link-header-redirect-resolution.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/payment-method-manifest/pmi-redirect-limits.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/payment-method-manifest/pmi-redirect-origins.https.sub.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/payment-method-manifest/pmm-redirect-disallowed.https.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "a106327f98603073507c31307a7851ac76f76489", "git_parents": ["7793e56da2a6742e3e652417183e89e356b1ed92"], "node": "70edfb45180fd1aba5b5cca875dc9b0f9c581921", "parents": ["85f7aecbadca1422cfd268f7c06b160d38079a36"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Eldar Pulatov \u003cepulatov.dev@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068506 [wpt PR 62339] - Preserve selection when input type changes between text and password, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nPreserve selection when input type changes between text and password\n\nWhen a click handler changes a focused input between text and password,\nBlink recreates its UA shadow tree, including its inner editor element.\nThis can collapse the live DOM selection to offset 0 while the correct\nselection remains cached for restoration after layout. The remaining\nmouse-release handling calls SelectionChanged(), which replaces the\ncache with the collapsed selection because the input is still focused.\n\nWith PreserveUnfocusedSelectionCache enabled, use\nShouldApplySelectionCache() instead of focus alone to decide whether\nSelectionChanged() may refresh the cache. This keeps the cached\nselection intact while a post-layout restore is pending. Preserve the\nold behavior when the runtime feature is disabled.\n\nAdd WPT coverage for text-to-password and password-to-text changes.\nExtend the moveBefore() test to check that the same post-layout\nrestoration mechanism preserves a focused input's backward selection.\n\nUpdate the release window for the PreserveUnfocusedSelectionCache: say\nthat the killswitch ships in M154 and can be removed in M156.\n\nBug: 40807608\nChange-Id: I3c257ddfc28198771da14e8a07fefa892da1b9d9\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8287984\nCommit-Queue: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1689298}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b22e473a8ccfeb95fdc848f17d237fd44197ff04\nwpt-pr: 62339\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/moveBefore/focus-preserve.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/textfieldselection/selection-preserved-after-text-password-type-change.html"], "git_node": "9c27666f0e28ccbcac9e367c8dd2ca53a47a9ac6", "git_parents": ["a106327f98603073507c31307a7851ac76f76489"], "node": "c0652acc3fcbf8d8d7e6465e90dc07e55d93fd9f", "parents": ["70edfb45180fd1aba5b5cca875dc9b0f9c581921"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068506 [wpt PR 62339] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62339\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/dom/nodes/moveBefore/chrome-338071841-crash.html.ini"], "git_node": "9ab6cd459455bcdcaa222b405b4dafbee72017e5", "git_parents": ["9c27666f0e28ccbcac9e367c8dd2ca53a47a9ac6"], "node": "5ad8082d2a8981b8b7d2f95b0500658566a7b61f", "parents": ["c0652acc3fcbf8d8d7e6465e90dc07e55d93fd9f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068509 [wpt PR 62341] - [grid] Fix auto repeat bug with subgrids, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[grid] Fix auto repeat bug with subgrids\n\nThis change fixes a long-standing issue with auto-repeated line names\ninherited through subgrids. We were not accounting for positions before\nthe auto repeat insertion point.\n\nThis change adds accounting for this case, as well as a new WPT that\nfails without the fix.\n\nChange-Id: I03e1ab20461c741fbc5db80a233a5145d1ae1c33\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8307273\nCommit-Queue: Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1689355}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6ea7cd821245a617268cfe384754ba3125042316\nwpt-pr: 62341\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/subgrid/grid-subgridded-to-grid-lanes/line-names/column-line-names-018-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/subgrid/grid-subgridded-to-grid-lanes/line-names/column-line-names-018.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/subgrid/line-names-parent-auto-repeat-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/subgrid/line-names-parent-auto-repeat-001.html"], "git_node": "9d48b84abd92c748be06a491936b843ebf5f2bbc", "git_parents": ["9ab6cd459455bcdcaa222b405b4dafbee72017e5"], "node": "5c7a4bbed4b6b3ab817d9f184cedda536481dd8d", "parents": ["5ad8082d2a8981b8b7d2f95b0500658566a7b61f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Celeste Pan \u003ccelestepan@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068513 [wpt PR 62239] - [Masonry] Add tests to ensure margins do not affect track opening and stacking axis alignment space, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Masonry] Add tests to ensure margins do not affect track opening and stacking axis alignment space\n\nAccording to the spec, \"Items that visually intrude into preceding empty\nspaces (via negative margins, position: relative, transforms, etc.), do\nnot affect the size of those empty spaces\" [1]. We should add test to\nensure that margins do not end up affecting track openings or stacking\naxis alignment spaces.\n\n[1] https://drafts.csswg.org/css-grid-3/#grid-lanes-layout-algorithm\n\nBug: 343257585, 517967196\nChange-Id: If5d8d7cf1ee6b974c462e49163461161c38ffd1b\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8281147\nReviewed-by: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Celeste Pan \u003ccelestepan@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1689368}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 945eda62dfab43d834243bab834fab83d85dc801\nwpt-pr: 62239\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/column-align-self-004-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/column-align-self-004.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/row-justify-self-004-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/row-justify-self-004.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/column-dense-packing-multi-span-013-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/column-dense-packing-multi-span-013.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/row-dense-packing-multi-span-006-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/row-dense-packing-multi-span-006.html"], "git_node": "7b878e1835891503aec6616f1aa9bccbbcc540ad", "git_parents": ["9d48b84abd92c748be06a491936b843ebf5f2bbc"], "node": "6c79fbfe0c572e1bac1709f9d3d604c6ae26623f", "parents": ["5c7a4bbed4b6b3ab817d9f184cedda536481dd8d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068513 [wpt PR 62239] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62239\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/column-align-self-004.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/row-justify-self-004.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/column-dense-packing-multi-span-013.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/row-dense-packing-multi-span-006.html.ini"], "git_node": "00ba535ac7fb58c56f23fd1b73c53bac6711b728", "git_parents": ["7b878e1835891503aec6616f1aa9bccbbcc540ad"], "node": "b41138c1cd1877933acf82aabb3a9ecf05f894bc", "parents": ["6c79fbfe0c572e1bac1709f9d3d604c6ae26623f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Seokho Song \u003cseokho@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068519 [wpt PR 62343] - Implement change event dispatch for ContainerQueryList, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nImplement change event dispatch for ContainerQueryList\n\nThe spec said to \"evaluate container queries and report changes\" after\nstyle and layout have been updated as part of the rendering steps.\n\nAdd an onchange event handler to ContainerQueryList and fire\na change event when the match state has changed at that step.\n\nIntroduce ContainerQueryListController, a LocalDOMWindow supplement that\nregisters each ContainerQueryList created via matchContainer() by its\ntarget element. LocalFrameView invokes the controller during the\nlifecycle update as the spec mentioned, at the same timing as\nResizeObserver.\n\nSplit the match evaluation in ContainerQueryList into ComputeMatches,\nwhich evaluates the query set, and UpdateMatches, which stores the\nresult and reports whether it changed. Evaluation is deferred until the\nfirst rendering step or matches() read, so constructing a list does not\nforce a style and layout update and the initial evaluation does not fire\nan event.\n\nSpec PR: https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/pull/13551\n\nBug: 40887402\nChange-Id: I853c6e75cb97a003c94982b3ed598d1060d72dcd\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8260311\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Seokho Song \u003cseokho@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1689666}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ad82f615987e1998acd70e507be9915c40f564fc\nwpt-pr: 62343\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-conditional/match-container-change-event.tentative.html"], "git_node": "d8ef1725b809d7a7d18acc9a99d0af6846c8cb30", "git_parents": ["00ba535ac7fb58c56f23fd1b73c53bac6711b728"], "node": "bb15da85ad7a373ed08229663ab017c31c2265bb", "parents": ["b41138c1cd1877933acf82aabb3a9ecf05f894bc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068519 [wpt PR 62343] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62343\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-conditional/container-queries/whitespace-update-after-removal.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-conditional/match-container-change-event.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "f0eb842cdc0fd6719c7538e6daa29d2bbe23213a", "git_parents": ["d8ef1725b809d7a7d18acc9a99d0af6846c8cb30"], "node": "39be831748e09d48631b0c5b908e639e4750932d", "parents": ["bb15da85ad7a373ed08229663ab017c31c2265bb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068524 [wpt PR 62347] - Quoted generic font-family names need to keep quotes for all cases, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nQuoted generic font-family names need to keep quotes for all cases\n\nfont-family:\"serif\" kept quotes for serialization, while\nfont-family:\"Serif\" didn't.\n\nBug: 483689942\nChange-Id: I136c8746ca06ce7f9947d5cff9ebf00b59037941\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8320589\nReviewed-by: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1689710}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9da2d5c68a9adf18c257b3f93cc77e1564f54511\nwpt-pr: 62347\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/parsing/font-family-valid.html"], "git_node": "675aa4517a9b6116952fc921ff0b0e9595dfee87", "git_parents": ["f0eb842cdc0fd6719c7538e6daa29d2bbe23213a"], "node": "a15caad9d09271df6e9f1da4c5a20e96281aa97c", "parents": ["39be831748e09d48631b0c5b908e639e4750932d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068525 [wpt PR 62354] - Recalc slot assignments for :target-before/after, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRecalc slot assignments for :target-before/after\n\n:target-before and :target-after matches based on flat tree positions.\nThat means slot assignments need to be up-to-date for selector matching,\nalso for querySelector. The matching code was doing slot re-assignments\nduring traversal, which could move the current target or the queried\ntarget out of the flat tree, which caused crashes.\n\nFor query mode, make sure the flat tree is up-to-date before traversing.\n\nBug: 555280390\nChange-Id: I3dfd571e7efd06a9b3d3e6804841d19a73c57997\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8331848\nCommit-Queue: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1689757}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 53eff3226884dcbf478b15ea038f295d71235664\nwpt-pr: 62354\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scroll-markers/chrome-555280390-crash.html"], "git_node": "2f3b3f7eb14278eb8e593551a0823c1f353de15a", "git_parents": ["675aa4517a9b6116952fc921ff0b0e9595dfee87"], "node": "e16ad343951ef9809ea174e8352e38926fe3fbeb", "parents": ["a15caad9d09271df6e9f1da4c5a20e96281aa97c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068525 [wpt PR 62354] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62354\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/scroll-markers/chrome-555280390-crash.html.ini"], "git_node": "c05d5798764d29ae5dc5a5a2e6930d68d84d0e17", "git_parents": ["2f3b3f7eb14278eb8e593551a0823c1f353de15a"], "node": "ba7faecc89308971196b5682e3d2bb28c30d0513", "parents": ["e16ad343951ef9809ea174e8352e38926fe3fbeb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068528 [wpt PR 62342] - WPT: animationcancel/transitioncancel are not fired synchronously on removal, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWPT: animationcancel/transitioncancel are not fired synchronously on removal\n\nThis is per spec:\n- https://drafts.csswg.org/css-animations-2/#event-dispatch\n- https://drafts.csswg.org/css-transitions-2/#event-dispatch\n- https://drafts.csswg.org/web-animations-1/#pending-animation-event-queue\n\nThis is to ensure that all kinds of events don't run synchronously on\nremove.\n\nBug: 550626700\nChange-Id: I678eef979de9d049caeaa54e6e63ec4ef6cbd85b\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8295899\nCommit-Queue: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1689841}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4819af4e400db92743d6f07e3ed9ffda435af963\nwpt-pr: 62342\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-animations/cancel-events-on-remove.html"], "git_node": "7c5e459be2139981bd8c961c8dc9da9bc13b8efb", "git_parents": ["c05d5798764d29ae5dc5a5a2e6930d68d84d0e17"], "node": "46d55c6de331ed2a13175c387cd1d15676e75ad0", "parents": ["ba7faecc89308971196b5682e3d2bb28c30d0513"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068528 [wpt PR 62342] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62342\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-animations/cancel-events-on-remove.html.ini"], "git_node": "b004a26a3f084f4877be8bcc88001a1fba59a2ea", "git_parents": ["7c5e459be2139981bd8c961c8dc9da9bc13b8efb"], "node": "2c1c37558729fd6e4e34b1b99b4ea706311eb11d", "parents": ["46d55c6de331ed2a13175c387cd1d15676e75ad0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nina Satragno \u003cnsatragno@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064141 [wpt PR 61988] - Set Credential Properties WebDriver command, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSet Credential Properties WebDriver command\n\nAdd support for the WebAuthn WebDriver Set Credential Properties\ncommand.\n\nhttps://w3c.github.io/webauthn/#sctn-automation-set-credential-properties\n\nUpcoming Credential Manager Trust Group Keys tests will make use of this\ncommand.\n\nSee issue https://github.com/w3c/webauthn/issues/2338.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: cfd7fb0219c82be2c118eda89aa580973c3b49f9\nwpt-pr: 61988\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/infrastructure/metadata/infrastructure/testdriver/virtual_authenticator.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/infrastructure/testdriver/virtual_authenticator.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resources/testdriver.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/webdriver/webdriver/client.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/executors/actions.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/executors/executorwebdriver.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/executors/protocol.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/testdriver-extra.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/classic/external/webauthn/set_credential_properties/__init__.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/classic/external/webauthn/set_credential_properties/invalid.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/classic/external/webauthn/set_credential_properties/set.py"], "git_node": "c3bcf35805e844922492c45cd5deff056bb17310", "git_parents": ["b004a26a3f084f4877be8bcc88001a1fba59a2ea"], "node": "4da9f36a12fb8126da9caa791f649a96119709ef", "parents": ["2c1c37558729fd6e4e34b1b99b4ea706311eb11d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064141 [wpt PR 61988] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61988\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/infrastructure/testdriver/virtual_authenticator.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/external/webauthn/set_credential_properties/invalid.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/external/webauthn/set_credential_properties/set.py.ini"], "git_node": "24da53996fff5025845fe8037bbaab8f7c14e0d4", "git_parents": ["c3bcf35805e844922492c45cd5deff056bb17310"], "node": "841245ccfda61137a0c5c910e5349076e896c6b6", "parents": ["4da9f36a12fb8126da9caa791f649a96119709ef"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Martinez \u003c157772165+AndrewJMart@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068534 [wpt PR 62332] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=289633, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=289633 (#62332)\n\nCo-authored-by: Andrew Martinez \u003camartinez55@apple.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1664a2a8437ccfa0f1d0d185fd0bdb2c24e5b482\nwpt-pr: 62332\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-nesting/nested-declarations-cssom.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-page/parsing/size-invalid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/parsing/size-invalid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/parsing/size-shorthand.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/parsing/size-valid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom/page-descriptors.html"], "git_node": "166bce69faee9cb9b099fe2bb6b3795b54385646", "git_parents": ["24da53996fff5025845fe8037bbaab8f7c14e0d4"], "node": "5040d2e7828695e2f42930a3e94e75e8dfed850c", "parents": ["841245ccfda61137a0c5c910e5349076e896c6b6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068534 [wpt PR 62332] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62332\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-sizing/parsing/size-shorthand.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-sizing/parsing/size-valid.html.ini"], "git_node": "c1ae0c656f46459d09d1fbf5b97d4efcc782d901", "git_parents": ["166bce69faee9cb9b099fe2bb6b3795b54385646"], "node": "124e697f92ff58c7830ffcdac95cd3b6cc4fa8c7", "parents": ["5040d2e7828695e2f42930a3e94e75e8dfed850c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brent Fulgham \u003c44174109+brentfulgham@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068537 [wpt PR 62359] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322612, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322612 (#62359)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 09159dcb3b69bb76d63f9a16bc6b8a3a2ee0d3b6\nwpt-pr: 62359\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-position/position-absolute-replaced-minmax.html"], "git_node": "cd90fba96a8dd65a6b9a5e1e7966554a5020cd3d", "git_parents": ["c1ae0c656f46459d09d1fbf5b97d4efcc782d901"], "node": "4a3868d6d9d11f58a2624f6e7f94683c06bfe018", "parents": ["124e697f92ff58c7830ffcdac95cd3b6cc4fa8c7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sammy Gill \u003csammy.gill@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068539 [wpt PR 62370] - [css-grid] Wait for Ahem to load in grid-self-alignment-fit-content-001, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-grid] Wait for Ahem to load in grid-self-alignment-fit-content-001 (#62370)\n\nThe test measures fit-content sizes of grid items laid out with Ahem at\n20px, but ran its subtests as soon as the parser reached the script, i.e.\nbefore the webfont had loaded. Every engine measured the fallback font\nand failed.\n\nGate the subtests on document.fonts.ready via setup({explicit_done: true}),\nmatching css/css-grid/grid-items/grid-minimum-size-grid-items-024.html.\n\nFollow-up to https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/62138.\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7c4ec356aff5dd83cdf58d124a189cec3ac4aa63\nwpt-pr: 62370\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/alignment/grid-self-alignment-fit-content-001.html"], "git_node": "345888e39a64f4e4768f8fa6c1cec784c9378628", "git_parents": ["cd90fba96a8dd65a6b9a5e1e7966554a5020cd3d"], "node": "5d664e97c9903f0de8918a66830163c816d67634", "parents": ["4a3868d6d9d11f58a2624f6e7f94683c06bfe018"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068539 [wpt PR 62370] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62370\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/alignment/grid-self-alignment-fit-content-001.html.ini"], "git_node": "0c479b4fd01b31cc2e04f13b2868cef1fd5c637c", "git_parents": ["345888e39a64f4e4768f8fa6c1cec784c9378628"], "node": "a4e696a0261648fc66cdc282cb5605197f1cba10", "parents": ["5d664e97c9903f0de8918a66830163c816d67634"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Aran Donohue \u003caran.donohue@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068542 [wpt PR 62365] - Broaden the WebTransport headers web test coverage, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nBroaden the WebTransport headers web test coverage\n\nTwo tests only checked that duplicate header names were accepted,\nbecause echo-request-headers.py reported just the last value for a\nrepeated name. Use its ?format=list mode to assert that every value\narrives.\n\nAssert that a user-supplied Host is dropped alongside Cookie, and that\nan empty headers object is accepted.\n\nDrop constructAndClose, now unused.\n\nChange-Id: I2fc80eec78b22f5417db937635964675897c3c2e\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8258277\nReviewed-by: Adam Rice \u003cricea@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Nidhi Jaju \u003cnidhijaju@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Adam Rice \u003cricea@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688919}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 05cb24ed7b0e2a60468df6fa2e7ca38636fd665e\nwpt-pr: 62365\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webtransport/headers.https.any.js"], "git_node": "d5562a8902d68a6dd12c0693af35a6ba7a3164ac", "git_parents": ["0c479b4fd01b31cc2e04f13b2868cef1fd5c637c"], "node": "fb5f655426cf2906142e3ff419189a866e070918", "parents": ["a4e696a0261648fc66cdc282cb5605197f1cba10"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068542 [wpt PR 62365] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62365\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webtransport/headers.https.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "d342c2b53659492db8e37f40c5cb387e7533d349", "git_parents": ["d5562a8902d68a6dd12c0693af35a6ba7a3164ac"], "node": "adcba65a0d280a7b21f84b0169b318e829ee8b66", "parents": ["fb5f655426cf2906142e3ff419189a866e070918"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sangwhan Moon \u003csxm@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068551 [wpt PR 62335] - [webvtt] Fix missing semicolon in repaint reference file, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[webvtt] Fix missing semicolon in repaint reference file\n\n`text-align: center` in `repaint-ref.html` was missing a trailing\nsemicolon, causing both it and the subsequent `font-family` declaration\nto be dropped. As a result, the reference rendered left-aligned serif\ntext, whereas the test rendered the default centered sans-serif cue.\n\nFix the missing semicolon so the reference matches the test rendering.\n\nBug: 40652084\nChange-Id: If23fd8c67e0ae5dc2b2b6163bb7b51e7d56e63f9\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8300279\nReviewed-by: Mahesh Kannan \u003ckmaheshb@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Ted (Chromium) Meyer \u003ctmathmeyer@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Sangwhan Moon \u003csxm@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Ted (Chromium) Meyer \u003ctmathmeyer@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1689290}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9451539bd0e2cd493608433609a0d0bbd5a8e600\nwpt-pr: 62335\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/repaint-ref.html"], "git_node": "51ef9f21c065381ffa3208e800a8ae1f8dc5812f", "git_parents": ["d342c2b53659492db8e37f40c5cb387e7533d349"], "node": "1a8e49473b8421c85409a4fae2bef120cc630828", "parents": ["adcba65a0d280a7b21f84b0169b318e829ee8b66"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Vogelheim \u003cvogelheim@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068553 [wpt PR 62357] - Consistently set XML parser \"already started\" flag., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nConsistently set XML parser \"already started\" flag.\n\nThe HTML spec & friends ask for XML parsing with\n\"XML scripting support disabled\" in several instances, specifically for\nDOMParser.parseFromString and XMLHttpResponse.responseXML.\n\nPreviously, this was only done for DOMParser.parseFromString. This\nchange also sets \"already started\" for XMLHttpResponse.responseXML.\n\nIn addition to the behavioural change above, we also simplify and unify\nthose two mechanisms:\n\n- Move the decision into a separate method,\n   ShouldMarkScriptAlreadyStarted, analogous to HTMLConstructionSite.\n- Include spec links to justify their behaviour.\n- Set CreateElementFlags for all elements, since CreateElement will\n   read only the flag it needs, so there is no need to restrict it to\n   scripts.\n- We also add tests for the new cases.\n\nBug: 542115030, 540021703\nChange-Id: I1b5e16fc63733b023d21cc3b5fd37b2c6b18f532\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8314690\nReviewed-by: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Daniel Vogelheim \u003cvogelheim@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1689914}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8c722694a1acfeeb37c7aae7455f14781a7b1720\nwpt-pr: 62357\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/DOMParser-parseFromString-xml-scripting-support-disabled.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/xhr/responseXML-xml-scripting-support-disabled.html"], "git_node": "127ed8a4d23f874a8ed32da81bb9c9e21993d3fe", "git_parents": ["51ef9f21c065381ffa3208e800a8ae1f8dc5812f"], "node": "af3c74c336078a1087dca1962d5f5f827c66f336", "parents": ["1a8e49473b8421c85409a4fae2bef120cc630828"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephanie Zhang \u003cstephanie.zhang@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068557 [wpt PR 62356] - Fix stale file input label after reset, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix stale file input label after reset\n\nWhen two file inputs share a FileList, resetting the first input clears\nthe shared list. The second input then appears empty before its own\nreset, so it skips its view update and retains a stale filename.\n\nExplicitly refresh a file input's view during reset so its displayed\nfilename reflects the empty selection. This preserves the existing\nshared FileList behavior.\n\nFixed: 420413450\nChange-Id: I7eca1768e565810e796e44ba3210d60741b88643\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8300232\nReviewed-by: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Stephanie Zhang \u003cstephanie.zhang@microsoft.com\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Stephanie Zhang \u003cstephanie.zhang@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1689933}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 318cbb466b74608b4e4bcea8079a1ed9d2eddc2c\nwpt-pr: 62356\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-input-element/file-input-reset-shared-file-list-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-input-element/file-input-reset-shared-file-list.html"], "git_node": "e5db048f94e58d056edd43ac6370a41329369743", "git_parents": ["127ed8a4d23f874a8ed32da81bb9c9e21993d3fe"], "node": "24a76073a4494ea8b6d56c917b1401299b1a4d15", "parents": ["af3c74c336078a1087dca1962d5f5f827c66f336"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068560 [wpt PR 62358] - [Masonry] Support OOF fragmentation, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Masonry] Support OOF fragmentation\n\nOut-of-flow grid-lanes descendants were only collected during the\ninitial layout pass. An item whose static position belonged to a later\nfragment could therefore be added to the wrong fragment and laid out\nincorrectly.\n\nPersist pending OOF children in `GridLanesBreakTokenData` and restore\nthem for each continuation. Resolve static positions against the full\nstitched block size, translate them into fragment-local coordinates, and\ndefer candidates until their position belongs in the current fragment.\nThis follows the grid fragmentation approach for both row and column\ngrid-lanes.\n\nAdd WPT coverage for alignment, nested and external containing blocks,\nwriting modes, fill and track reversal, intrinsic sizing, and explicit\ngrid areas. Expected failures reflect the remaining break-rule and row\nexpansion limitations of grid lanes in general.\n\nBug: 343257585\nChange-Id: Id00a426e5965da01e48e0ea6ea2888823b1e12f6\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8327892\nCommit-Queue: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1689953}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3f62d41037fa20ce6d9b083b5d4c0deb8f831a09\nwpt-pr: 62358\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-004.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-005.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-006.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-007.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-008.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-009.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-010.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-011.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-012.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-005.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-004.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-005.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-006.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-007.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-008.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-009.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-010.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-011.html"], "git_node": "916d8b5985c27a207b9d30439344be859c1353ac", "git_parents": ["e5db048f94e58d056edd43ac6370a41329369743"], "node": "3eaf15bc7e7fb1271daed421f02c60b458d3832c", "parents": ["24a76073a4494ea8b6d56c917b1401299b1a4d15"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068560 [wpt PR 62358] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62358\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-004.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-005.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-007.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-008.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-009.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-010.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-011.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-012.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-005.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-002.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-005.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-006.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-007.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-008.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-009.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-010.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-011.html.ini"], "git_node": "76e5008018ebf51cf05930e9aa876aa2ef0fcfa2", "git_parents": ["916d8b5985c27a207b9d30439344be859c1353ac"], "node": "c1350222c53629d9f3c06310c2d5368db5630d31", "parents": ["3eaf15bc7e7fb1271daed421f02c60b458d3832c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Koji Ishii \u003ckojii@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068561 [wpt PR 62366] - Move `pseudo-first-line-border-width` test to WPT, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nMove `pseudo-first-line-border-width` test to WPT\n\nIn preparation to crbug.com/41362700, this patch converts the\nlegacy pixel test `pseudo-first-line-border-width` to a WPT\nref-test.\n\nIt avoids rebaselines by unrelated changes such as\ncrbug.com/41362700.\n\nBug: 41362700\nChange-Id: I60699318189cfb00fbed068334f9d4b85d1e49d1\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8336647\nCommit-Queue: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Koji Ishii \u003ckojii@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1689962}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ad51a18f92be4ff8beea0518ab1fcd2e5dea309a\nwpt-pr: 62366\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/first-line-font-relative-units-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/first-line-font-relative-units-001.html"], "git_node": "5960d77e7b78db06ec4c0a120c308e8e5448caff", "git_parents": ["76e5008018ebf51cf05930e9aa876aa2ef0fcfa2"], "node": "448a5a4cbed53fab1c6bd3a8cf86288f53a586ba", "parents": ["c1350222c53629d9f3c06310c2d5368db5630d31"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068561 [wpt PR 62366] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62366\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-pseudo/first-line-font-relative-units-001.html.ini"], "git_node": "483903c91a314311f8858cf65c39a09ae32145aa", "git_parents": ["5960d77e7b78db06ec4c0a120c308e8e5448caff"], "node": "bb2c6e7ae8cbfd5c30076e4b3659b433d0796c35", "parents": ["448a5a4cbed53fab1c6bd3a8cf86288f53a586ba"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068562 [wpt PR 62360] - [gap-decorations] Fix padding offset with fragmentation, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[gap-decorations] Fix padding offset with fragmentation\n\nFixes a bug in gap decorations where the code didn't match the comment.\nIn this case, the comment is correct, but offset_in_stitched_container\nwill be zero in the first fragment, and the code was using this path for\nsubsequent fragments.\n\nThis change removes the condition by generalizing the computation and\nadds a WPT that was rendering incorrectly before the fix.\n\nBug: 357648037\nChange-Id: Ifffc9de06bd13f5bb87dc09c7675b8de4ec1881d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8291896\nReviewed-by: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1690011}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0d3d36837bfad11c70e14e292960050a9c4396c5\nwpt-pr: 62360\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid/fragmentation/grid-gap-decorations-fragmentation-038-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid/fragmentation/grid-gap-decorations-fragmentation-038.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid/fragmentation/grid-gap-decorations-fragmentation-039-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid/fragmentation/grid-gap-decorations-fragmentation-039.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid/fragmentation/grid-gap-decorations-fragmentation-040-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid/fragmentation/grid-gap-decorations-fragmentation-040.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid/fragmentation/grid-gap-decorations-fragmentation-041-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid/fragmentation/grid-gap-decorations-fragmentation-041.html"], "git_node": "9013c58249652c4b1cb8019f1728f6f8f9737594", "git_parents": ["483903c91a314311f8858cf65c39a09ae32145aa"], "node": "bc17750a2707f63d26fe7260a57f98b0a13c34a4", "parents": ["bb2c6e7ae8cbfd5c30076e4b3659b433d0796c35"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068562 [wpt PR 62360] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62360\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid/fragmentation/grid-gap-decorations-fragmentation-018-crash.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid/fragmentation/grid-gap-decorations-fragmentation-019-crash.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid/fragmentation/grid-gap-decorations-fragmentation-038.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid/fragmentation/grid-gap-decorations-fragmentation-039.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid/fragmentation/grid-gap-decorations-fragmentation-040.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid/fragmentation/grid-gap-decorations-fragmentation-041.html.ini"], "git_node": "d7274afec44c0a75e2d4f609a914450103601600", "git_parents": ["9013c58249652c4b1cb8019f1728f6f8f9737594"], "node": "301f1ed283a24443fa9b9fb438c0b55a615fcf60", "parents": ["bc17750a2707f63d26fe7260a57f98b0a13c34a4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068564 [wpt PR 62361] - Ensure all CEReactions are called for streamHTML*, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nEnsure all CEReactions are called for streamHTML*\n\n- disconnectedCallback() should be called synchronously if the streaming\n  method synchronously removes existing nodes (set/replaceWith)\n- Add more tests for CEReactions during write/close\n- Also add [NewObject] to stream* methods.\n\nBug: 491743369\nChange-Id: I345ec5119d9bd6e43fa1a3fc7e0c7624acbd81f7\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8314109\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1690037}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b969aa2798724da282b8cae3eb76a24868f41f4a\nwpt-pr: 62361\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/stream-html-custom-element.html"], "git_node": "9e2981f03d5a769b498d355ba87254b46eb718a7", "git_parents": ["d7274afec44c0a75e2d4f609a914450103601600"], "node": "bf6dc1d5f8916bb4068282e098925a7d1a61fa45", "parents": ["301f1ed283a24443fa9b9fb438c0b55a615fcf60"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068564 [wpt PR 62361] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62361\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/domparsing/tentative/stream-html-custom-element.html.ini"], "git_node": "0ff8c345b7a6d35cb15bdc070561589bfcc83e89", "git_parents": ["9e2981f03d5a769b498d355ba87254b46eb718a7"], "node": "b9f8ccb49ced9dcc82f86742eab23533f4194ef4", "parents": ["bf6dc1d5f8916bb4068282e098925a7d1a61fa45"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Christopher Cameron \u003cccameron@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068568 [wpt PR 62367] - Canvas2D: Hook up toneMapping context creation attribute, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nCanvas2D: Hook up toneMapping context creation attribute\n\nThe 2D, WebGL, and WebGPU tone mapping APIs are being unified.\n\nMove the parsing code from one-off WebGPU code to common\nParseCanvasToneMapping and CanvasToneMappingToV8 functions, and have\nWebGPU call them (mirroring what is already done for\nPredefinedColorSpace).\n\nUse this function (behind feature flag) in 2D canvas context creation\n(ToCanvasContextCreationAttributes) and context attributes querying\n(ToCanvasRenderingContext2DSettings).\n\nWith this in place 2D canvas and WebGPU will maintain HDR tone mapping\nfeatures in lock-step (like how the common PredefinedColorSpace has\nenabled adding linear spaces to all APIs in one move).\n\nAdd WPT tests, to be pointed at when I send out the HTML spec changes\nfor review.\n\nAdd TODOs to remove the very very old HTMLCanvasElement-based HDR APIs.\n\nTAG=agy\nCONV=9f2c857b-3ae8-4048-ab49-db1109f50272\n\nBug: 448552449\nChange-Id: I7e044fc7bf34d8f29a7ad94b901e9c028a140c45\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8327547\nReviewed-by: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: ccameron chromium \u003cccameron@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1690193}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: df77989abecd295d86579b1702fc321de9507c56\nwpt-pr: 62367\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/context-attributes/getContextAttributes.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/manual/context-attributes/getContextAttributes.html"], "git_node": "d5a01fe9336eeca601d066e8dad348772f19e2e4", "git_parents": ["0ff8c345b7a6d35cb15bdc070561589bfcc83e89"], "node": "42716d320bf9f3d8f4e049061ae3694fe7878633", "parents": ["b9f8ccb49ced9dcc82f86742eab23533f4194ef4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068568 [wpt PR 62367] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62367\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/context-attributes/getContextAttributes.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/offscreen/manual/context-attributes/getContextAttributes.html.ini"], "git_node": "5ec26a28b7cdeec5aaa40169e494d4dc029341ef", "git_parents": ["d5a01fe9336eeca601d066e8dad348772f19e2e4"], "node": "3a9758e4c11c9853ba69ecb4b0db977980f272cc", "parents": ["42716d320bf9f3d8f4e049061ae3694fe7878633"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Javier Contreras Tenorio \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068571 [wpt PR 62371] - [masonry] Add missing WPTs for inset percentage and overlap-join cases, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[masonry] Add missing WPTs for inset percentage and overlap-join cases\n\nBug: 343257585\nChange-Id: I038862a7650e47d41e3982baba6f0dba24cc6e58\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8334686\nCommit-Queue: Javier Contreras \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1690234}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 98a70a0c581153895f3dd9212850e4df18593c98\nwpt-pr: 62371\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-inset-non-overlapping-gutter-percentage-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-inset-non-overlapping-gutter-percentage.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-inset-overlap-join-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-inset-overlap-join.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-inset-overlap-join-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-inset-overlap-join.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-inset-overlapping-gutters-percentage-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-inset-overlapping-gutters-percentage.html"], "git_node": "6c67a859131cab7ba5c2b69c8cb500acb45fa3d7", "git_parents": ["5ec26a28b7cdeec5aaa40169e494d4dc029341ef"], "node": "b28939345f6fc1653ea0730b1ee155ec1cdf121a", "parents": ["3a9758e4c11c9853ba69ecb4b0db977980f272cc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068571 [wpt PR 62371] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62371\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-inset-non-overlapping-gutter-percentage.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-inset-overlap-join.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-inset-overlap-join.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-inset-overlapping-gutters-percentage.html.ini"], "git_node": "bf1274f3ca07278764e8ee7a274af475d5a991fb", "git_parents": ["6c67a859131cab7ba5c2b69c8cb500acb45fa3d7"], "node": "6bc66600a84a0a86c620b8ae97de50afe9d3111c", "parents": ["b28939345f6fc1653ea0730b1ee155ec1cdf121a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068576 [wpt PR 62296] - [html-in-canvas] Rename DrawElementOptions to DrawElementImageOptions, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[html-in-canvas] Rename DrawElementOptions to DrawElementImageOptions\n\nThis patch renames DrawElementOptions to DrawElementImageOptions, and\nalso updates the boolean member from updateGeometry to\npreserveElementGeometry (and flips the logic as needed).\n\nBug: 532229486\nChange-Id: I4974f2a8c425fb639c829fb718ff35f024a49069\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8309615\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688529}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 71dfe0c58ab25603342c6d00df8991972618e518\nwpt-pr: 62296\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/canvas-transform-update.tentative.html"], "git_node": "2a8335dafcd82adde658a084effe30cf5ceba988", "git_parents": ["bf1274f3ca07278764e8ee7a274af475d5a991fb"], "node": "32d56786e865c2719849566beb9fb185840e4823", "parents": ["6bc66600a84a0a86c620b8ae97de50afe9d3111c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068576 [wpt PR 62296] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62296\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/canvas-transform-update.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "d7ac0f5e5f3045907e87b1d04333b8b41c050ede", "git_parents": ["2a8335dafcd82adde658a084effe30cf5ceba988"], "node": "813f495e3ee5d8d0c8e152b5c5d75e4b830270d2", "parents": ["32d56786e865c2719849566beb9fb185840e4823"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068582 [wpt PR 62310] - [css] Refresh media query flags after media mutations, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css] Refresh media query flags after media mutations\n\nThis change fixes a media-query dependency update missed when\nCompareActiveStyleSheets() reports no active sheet changes. A sheet can\nremain non-matching\u2014and therefore have a null RuleSet\u2014while its\nmedia-query dependencies change. The fix is to determine aggregate media\nquery changes in ApplyRuleSetChanges, even when no style rules change.\n\nThis adds a new WPT that passes in Firefox and fails in Chromium without\nthis change with the message: [FAIL] Changing style media accounts for\nthe new viewport dependency\n  assert_equals: The media query is evaluated against the updated subframe viewport expected \"rgb(0, 128, 0)\" but got \"rgb(0, 0, 255)\"\n\nBug: 545636895\nChange-Id: I0972c0b6d2bbbc30cc6d825ec350bd7203b97451\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8255724\nCommit-Queue: Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1690079}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b7c635bd548fa842c49c6a6f73095b893027b003\nwpt-pr: 62310\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/mediaqueries/style-media-attribute-change-in-iframe.html"], "git_node": "662764aa5fc6979033bed25fa706a77855a316e6", "git_parents": ["d7ac0f5e5f3045907e87b1d04333b8b41c050ede"], "node": "1083c0bc5c6f6fde995c6721c089efe7ae151435", "parents": ["813f495e3ee5d8d0c8e152b5c5d75e4b830270d2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068583 [wpt PR 62334] - [html-in-canvas] Fix inline hit testing, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[html-in-canvas] Fix inline hit testing\n\nWhen an inline element has a canvas element transform, the offset from\n`PhysicalLinesBoundingBox` needs to be removed so the inline's origin\ndoes not include the inline's offset from its containing block, see:\n`LayoutInline::QuadsForSelfInternal`. This patch applies the same\nadjustment for LayoutInline::NodeAtPoint.\n\nBug: 554586994\nChange-Id: I3cc68e70754e1fbac0b774426a8b26c3d9dafa54\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8324827\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1690128}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 480fdfcd85d043c23875665f464c35c0043dff52\nwpt-pr: 62334\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/hit-test/elementsFromPoint-update-element-geometry.tentative.html"], "git_node": "687a4ab5f7ab4310747de180ed63a5a3792c63ab", "git_parents": ["662764aa5fc6979033bed25fa706a77855a316e6"], "node": "d213a24b75f45a100941abce39e1afd8897ba2e4", "parents": ["1083c0bc5c6f6fde995c6721c089efe7ae151435"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068583 [wpt PR 62334] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62334\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/hit-test/elementsFromPoint-update-element-geometry.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "5fcb988fc4058ca32cad1d254bc770dac639232b", "git_parents": ["687a4ab5f7ab4310747de180ed63a5a3792c63ab"], "node": "9d78450072bfc9ebd429e1a05a50c381a2303c83", "parents": ["d213a24b75f45a100941abce39e1afd8897ba2e4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056331 [wpt PR 61420] - VT: Ensure that scope qualifies for layout containment., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nVT: Ensure that scope qualifies for layout containment.\n\nWe need layout containment for all the right reparenting later in the\npipeline, so if the scope doesn't qualify then we shouldn't run the\ntransition.\n\nSee https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/14179\n\nR=kevers@chromium.org\n\nBug: 532144043\nChange-Id: Ibc4478200db52a00e495e70623341adad7f37a68\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8099762\nCommit-Queue: Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kevin Ellis \u003ckevers@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1689216}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 2e3a142b0ad49affa7147d508414cef390ed0ea3\nwpt-pr: 61420\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/scoped/crashtests/element-scoped-multicol-crash.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/scoped/element-scoped-containment-invalid-state.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/scoped/scope-containment-during-capture.html"], "git_node": "986352bd56c54601f6f88c39b73a1db98d55a476", "git_parents": ["5fcb988fc4058ca32cad1d254bc770dac639232b"], "node": "d5da9343d8f2a5ab40a526b745f2309ac8136999", "parents": ["9d78450072bfc9ebd429e1a05a50c381a2303c83"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056331 [wpt PR 61420] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61420\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-view-transitions/scoped/element-scoped-containment-invalid-state.html.ini"], "git_node": "86882af328282d8f8b556411b67e33923369f70f", "git_parents": ["986352bd56c54601f6f88c39b73a1db98d55a476"], "node": "a77a33462f429d06a662739938b79c99f3cdb213", "parents": ["d5da9343d8f2a5ab40a526b745f2309ac8136999"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hoch Hochkeppel \u003cmhochk@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068593 [wpt PR 62373] - Reduce page-background-image-print.html flakiness, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nReduce page-background-image-print.html flakiness\n\nThis test is passing the vast majority of the time, but is still failing\nwith some regularity due to a race between the image being loaded and\nthe framework capturing the rendered pixels. This change eliminates that\nrace by adding a preload, which the test framework will wait for.\n\nVerified locally with private stress-case runs on Mac15 that were\nreliably failing ~50% of executions, and are passing 100% with this\nchange.\n\nBug: NoBug\nChange-Id: Id5464451aeb9a96fe4d80edbe116fb4f24cefb1c\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8334591\nReviewed-by: Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Hoch Hochkeppel \u003cmhochk@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1690240}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 77f2ae0e7f6585595d3ad5c91665018c182247d0\nwpt-pr: 62373\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-page/page-background-image-print.html"], "git_node": "1aa239a27695275bc0a1852c55d724806494f7b7", "git_parents": ["86882af328282d8f8b556411b67e33923369f70f"], "node": "1e9e4470f275b7a343aaf2363c12f8c657690fe8", "parents": ["a77a33462f429d06a662739938b79c99f3cdb213"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068593 [wpt PR 62373] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62373\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-page/crashtests/match-media-listener-relayout-contained-inline-subtree-print.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-page/crashtests/match-media-listener-relayout-contained-subtree-print.html.ini"], "git_node": "a484e3fe836c00fb55dc11311b9bf3f975aa3c7d", "git_parents": ["1aa239a27695275bc0a1852c55d724806494f7b7"], "node": "8f708f5754999f357bd62f469b1a81ee37ee86a3", "parents": ["1e9e4470f275b7a343aaf2363c12f8c657690fe8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Christopher Cameron \u003cccameron@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068597 [wpt PR 62369] - Add parameterized getImageData color conversion WPT test, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd parameterized getImageData color conversion WPT test\n\nUnify and parameterize 2D canvas color space conversions for\ngetImageData in color_space.yaml across srgb, srgb-linear, display-p3,\nand display-p3-linear canvas spaces and destination ImageData color\nspaces.\n\nTest 4 pixels in a 2x2 grid: black and white on one diagonal, and\ngamut-specific colors on the other diagonal.\n\nRemove individual redundant tests superseded by this unified test.\n\nTAG=agy\nCONV=3da4bac4-8ad7-46e9-969f-5aa84b7a5620\n\nBug: 454152417\nChange-Id: I9ef57e595995b61e0edb492d111e8293de484761\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8313909\nReviewed-by: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: ccameron chromium \u003cccameron@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1690325}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 397d01d8ee6d3e5dd7084c2462051d7882294760\nwpt-pr: 62369\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/wide-gamut-canvas/2d.color.space.display-p3-linear.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/wide-gamut-canvas/2d.color.space.getImageData.convert.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/wide-gamut-canvas/2d.color.space.p3.to.p3.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/wide-gamut-canvas/2d.color.space.p3.to.srgb.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/wide-gamut-canvas/2d.color.space.srgb-linear.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/wide-gamut-canvas/2d.color.space.display-p3-linear.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/wide-gamut-canvas/2d.color.space.display-p3-linear.worker.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/wide-gamut-canvas/2d.color.space.getImageData.convert.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/wide-gamut-canvas/2d.color.space.getImageData.convert.worker.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/wide-gamut-canvas/2d.color.space.p3.to.p3.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/wide-gamut-canvas/2d.color.space.p3.to.p3.worker.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/wide-gamut-canvas/2d.color.space.p3.to.srgb.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/wide-gamut-canvas/2d.color.space.p3.to.srgb.worker.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/wide-gamut-canvas/2d.color.space.srgb-linear.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/wide-gamut-canvas/2d.color.space.srgb-linear.worker.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/tools/yaml/color_space.yaml"], "git_node": "b3431aa906f13a63466274c23508a043ce9f1bff", "git_parents": ["a484e3fe836c00fb55dc11311b9bf3f975aa3c7d"], "node": "1f4856cf7058f2db0a164dfce260c4072ade6d40", "parents": ["8f708f5754999f357bd62f469b1a81ee37ee86a3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068597 [wpt PR 62369] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62369\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/wide-gamut-canvas/2d.color.space.display-p3-linear.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/wide-gamut-canvas/2d.color.space.getImageData.convert.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/wide-gamut-canvas/2d.color.space.p3.to.p3.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/wide-gamut-canvas/2d.color.space.p3.to.srgb.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/wide-gamut-canvas/2d.color.space.srgb-linear.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/offscreen/wide-gamut-canvas/2d.color.space.display-p3-linear.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/offscreen/wide-gamut-canvas/2d.color.space.display-p3-linear.worker.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/offscreen/wide-gamut-canvas/2d.color.space.getImageData.convert.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/offscreen/wide-gamut-canvas/2d.color.space.getImageData.convert.worker.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/offscreen/wide-gamut-canvas/2d.color.space.p3.to.p3.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/offscreen/wide-gamut-canvas/2d.color.space.p3.to.p3.worker.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/offscreen/wide-gamut-canvas/2d.color.space.srgb-linear.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/offscreen/wide-gamut-canvas/2d.color.space.srgb-linear.worker.js.ini"], "git_node": "25f2eacd505dd79742368cb45e61fa01f3bf1e27", "git_parents": ["b3431aa906f13a63466274c23508a043ce9f1bff"], "node": "00de772aab39b0a3fb7ec6bb589c7319e3a3490f", "parents": ["1f4856cf7058f2db0a164dfce260c4072ade6d40"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephanie Zhang \u003cstephanie.zhang@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068599 [wpt PR 62375] - [css-mixins] Require values in @private, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-mixins] Require values in @private\n\nThe @private rule uses a declaration list, so private custom property\ndeclarations must include a colon and value. In CL:8228248, we\npreviously accepted bare names and typed names without values, however\nthe spec now specifies that this is not correct [0].\n\nReject these invalid declarations while retaining valid declarations in\nthe same block. Updated unit tests and WPT.\n\n[0] https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/commit/27fd597de31a8c43234f99f58983e4af3d1f9282\n\nBug: 542651959\nLow-Coverage-Reason: COVERAGE_UNDERREPORTED\nChange-Id: I3fa65115e9bce9a3d51297b67563aa105d6d39b0\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8337617\nCommit-Queue: Stephanie Zhang \u003cstephanie.zhang@microsoft.com\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Stephanie Zhang \u003cstephanie.zhang@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kevin Babbitt \u003ckbabbitt@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1690357}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ae6982b121c5636392e003d839fd0eecb943db74\nwpt-pr: 62375\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-mixins/private/private-cssom-