 Tab Page address bar. r=mbeier\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323562\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-newtab/browser.toml", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-newtab/browser_undo_history.js"], "git_node": "9914e73f60e6c9f2cb3c00f68dda228fa9cb8ecc", "git_parents": ["8ee1b70fa09f1cf477fc8ea12502627a612f920c"], "node": "cd69e7e6c88f507c973871385901bbf6c9db0c76", "parents": ["b7e1dc7684053047c152a867ae89feb937570959"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069426 - Avoid useless atom refcount traffic when building invalidation maps. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nSee bug 1744102 for the last time we changed our hashmaps.\n\nIn these maps, it's not uncommon to have multiple entries per key (in\nfact that's kinda the point). This prevents refcount traffic due to\ncloning when the entry already exists.\n\nOriginally noticed from profiles for bug 2065622, but this applies more\nbroadly to all our invalidation maps.\n\nentry_ref is a nicer version of what you can do in nightly rust with\nraw_entry_mut(), and performance should be equivalent. Plus we vendor\nhashbrown already so...\n\nWhile at it, switch all hashmaps to hashbrown, since it's better not to\nhave to reason about different impls.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323688\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "servo/components/malloc_size_of/Cargo.toml", "servo/components/malloc_size_of/lib.rs", "servo/components/selectors/Cargo.toml", "servo/components/selectors/lib.rs", "servo/components/selectors/nth_index_cache.rs", "servo/components/selectors/relative_selector/cache.rs", "servo/components/selectors/relative_selector/filter.rs", "servo/components/style/Cargo.toml", "servo/components/style/context.rs", "servo/components/style/custom_properties.rs", "servo/components/style/dom.rs", "servo/components/style/gecko/wrapper.rs", "servo/components/style/gecko_string_cache/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/invalidation/element/invalidation_map.rs", "servo/components/style/invalidation/element/relative_selector.rs", "servo/components/style/invalidation/media_queries.rs", "servo/components/style/invalidation/stylesheets.rs", "servo/components/style/lib.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/cascade.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/declaration_block.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/helpers/animated_properties.mako.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/properties_and_values/value.rs", "servo/components/style/rule_cache.rs", "servo/components/style/rule_tree/core.rs", "servo/components/style/rule_tree/map.rs", "servo/components/style/selector_map.rs", "servo/components/style/servo/animation.rs", "servo/components/style/servo/selector_parser.rs", "servo/components/style/stylesheets/container_rule.rs", "servo/components/style/stylesheets/scope_rule.rs", "servo/components/style/stylesheets/stylesheet.rs", "servo/components/style/stylist.rs", "servo/components/style/traversal.rs", "servo/components/style/typed_om/sum_value.rs", "servo/components/style/url/gecko.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/position.rs", "servo/components/to_shmem/Cargo.toml", "servo/components/to_shmem/lib.rs"], "git_node": "bd0918b47bbb24dc6bd95da24ba58c2b661497ac", "git_parents": ["9914e73f60e6c9f2cb3c00f68dda228fa9cb8ecc"], "node": "e3ec913456b23fcfc0513740d7e4bbac967d9952", "parents": ["cd69e7e6c88f507c973871385901bbf6c9db0c76"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emily McMinn \u003cemcminn@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067843 - Update Kit illustration at wide newtab message breakpoint r=reemhamz\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322402\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/assets/firefox-mascot-prop-heart-dark.svg", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/assets/firefox-mascot-prop-heart-light.svg"], "git_node": "ccf669ac53a69151e20c2678013117a983f78e66", "git_parents": ["bd0918b47bbb24dc6bd95da24ba58c2b661497ac"], "node": "07b7e1170c3adc5599fc620be17d0329964d4481", "parents": ["e3ec913456b23fcfc0513740d7e4bbac967d9952"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alejandro Savransky \u003casavransky@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069099 - Land strings for lapsed-user Windows toast notification r=aminomancer,fluent-reviewers,omc-reviewers,bolsson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323422\n", "files": ["browser/locales/en-US/browser/newtab/asrouter.ftl"], "git_node": "80048fe990452bc25c4c55d1943b6852b8412a2a", "git_parents": ["ccf669ac53a69151e20c2678013117a983f78e66"], "node": "5989cfeae69572413d0c4b00470e8dd78e50c181", "parents": ["07b7e1170c3adc5599fc620be17d0329964d4481"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068488 - Keep every urlbar bounce in one parent-side store keyed by the tab. r=mbeier\n\nOne module-level weak map replaces the per-collector stores, so a trigger resolves the tab's bounce whichever input started it. Triggering is a module function taking the browser, which the chrome call sites reach directly rather than through a collector and, on the message path, the actor.\n\nThe direct path collects its snapshot before awaiting a prior bounce's trigger, where the engagement record that follows had already closed the view. URILoadingHelper's trigger fires again too, having passed a browser element to a browser-id parameter since bug 1624579, and the load flag it checks now covers every urlbar input rather than the address bar alone.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323123\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarParentController.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/actors/UrlbarParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarChildTelemetry.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarParentControllerProxy.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-engagementTelemetry/browser_glean_telemetry_bounce.js", "browser/modules/URILoadingHelper.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "cf787af4a51b6ce83129bbf4c385155b707528ac", "git_parents": ["80048fe990452bc25c4c55d1943b6852b8412a2a"], "node": "8557e244b0dc50f7bf156d2abeb87bbd79eceef4", "parents": ["5989cfeae69572413d0c4b00470e8dd78e50c181"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068488 - Record urlbar.bounce for the New Tab search bar. r=mbeier\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323124\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-newtab/browser_bounceTelemetry.js"], "git_node": "a5b199f24922b4ef069a73d9fea939b0ceb4ab4d", "git_parents": ["cf787af4a51b6ce83129bbf4c385155b707528ac"], "node": "6c883acea68cb8e17b5fa7163ca0fedd1df62fda", "parents": ["8557e244b0dc50f7bf156d2abeb87bbd79eceef4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dale Harvey \u003cdale@arandomurl.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038925 - Use specific headers in trustpanel blocker view. r=emz,urlbar-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321202\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-siteProtections.js", "browser/base/content/browser-trustPanel.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-trustPanel/browser_trust_panel.js"], "git_node": "48b2da1d7a5e9d87eb69e14794a7f2777a9e545c", "git_parents": ["a5b199f24922b4ef069a73d9fea939b0ceb4ab4d"], "node": "3bc1192c211fb42cdd214eb1dd897ee22e96dd7b", "parents": ["6c883acea68cb8e17b5fa7163ca0fedd1df62fda"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoshi Cheng-Hao Huang \u003callstars.chh@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068343 - Don't clear a module's SCRIPT_SLOT while its top-level-await generator is suspended. r=arai\n\nonTopLevelEvaluationFinished clears SCRIPT_SLOT so the BaseScript can be\ncollected, but a module's evaluation can finish while its top-level-await\ngenerator is still suspended. The pending await reaction resumes the generator\nafterwards and the assertion of script() fails because it has been cleared.\n\nKeep the slot in that case, and clear it once the generator is closed, so the\nscript is still released.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323627\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/ModuleObject.cpp", "js/src/jit-test/tests/modules/bug-2068343-1.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/modules/bug-2068343-2.js", "js/src/vm/GeneratorObject.cpp", "js/src/vm/GeneratorObject.h"], "git_node": "43768585bf273279a8714dbcd56a39687a7bff3c", "git_parents": ["48b2da1d7a5e9d87eb69e14794a7f2777a9e545c"], "node": "a0db8b9ef25f9a1c7aec52984b3d47c07f38217e", "parents": ["3bc1192c211fb42cdd214eb1dd897ee22e96dd7b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068128 - Improve generation of white-listed files for clang-tidy r=sylvestre\n\nCurrent algorithm for third party identification iterates over a list of\ndirectory and checks if any of them contains individual files.\n\nThis list is built from tools/rewriting/ThirdPartyPaths.txt, which also\ncontains many directories or files that do not contains any file that\nmatters for clang-tidy.\n\nRemoving those entries leads to much faster third party identification,\nsaving more than 200ms per file for some C++ sources. It saves 0.3% of\nbuild time on spidermonkey.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322642\n", "files": ["build/clang-plugin/ThirdPartyPaths.py", "tools/rewriting/ThirdPartyPaths.txt"], "git_node": "bc311620d2d332a1ecc08f78c84bd41018cc3dfb", "git_parents": ["43768585bf273279a8714dbcd56a39687a7bff3c"], "node": "52733dcfabca006745c5bffa3ce78410105ce3d3", "parents": ["a0db8b9ef25f9a1c7aec52984b3d47c07f38217e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nikki Sharpley \u003cnsharpley@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067848 - Add \"Other profiles\" header to profile subpanel in app menu r=niklas\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323018\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-profiles.js", "browser/components/profiles/tests/browser/browser_appmenu.js"], "git_node": "d5d258e1495d4a641ae2862418c106fd1129766a", "git_parents": ["bc311620d2d332a1ecc08f78c84bd41018cc3dfb"], "node": "36133a1fc60bf0dfc1bfe09fd2930671c3e888ae", "parents": ["52733dcfabca006745c5bffa3ce78410105ce3d3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Cristian Tuns \u003cctuns@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2068128 - Improve generation of white-listed files for clang-tidy r=sylvestre\" for causing build bustages in Time.h\n\nThis reverts commit bc311620d2d332a1ecc08f78c84bd41018cc3dfb.\n", "files": ["build/clang-plugin/ThirdPartyPaths.py", "tools/rewriting/ThirdPartyPaths.txt"], "git_node": "fe0de173dd35004bf279370ff70d3d23de47c207", "git_parents": ["d5d258e1495d4a641ae2862418c106fd1129766a"], "node": "5a881a68db6048853de7ff40e9ffc2aa14b05b19", "parents": ["36133a1fc60bf0dfc1bfe09fd2930671c3e888ae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2068488 - Record urlbar.bounce for the New Tab search bar. r=mbeier\" for causing failures at browser_glean_telemetry_bounce_sap.js.\n\nThis reverts commit a5b199f24922b4ef069a73d9fea939b0ceb4ab4d.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2068488 - Keep every urlbar bounce in one parent-side store keyed by the tab. r=mbeier\"\n\nThis reverts commit cf787af4a51b6ce83129bbf4c385155b707528ac.\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarParentController.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/actors/UrlbarParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarChildTelemetry.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarParentControllerProxy.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-engagementTelemetry/browser_glean_telemetry_bounce.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-newtab/browser_bounceTelemetry.js", "browser/modules/URILoadingHelper.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "29349bf94fd23f5b5da5759ebd0f3c1a3fedd84b", "git_parents": ["fe0de173dd35004bf279370ff70d3d23de47c207"], "node": "43ee5cbe2cb89707bc4b31fae004e36c55a1524c", "parents": ["5a881a68db6048853de7ff40e9ffc2aa14b05b19"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ollie Hensman-Crook \u003cohensmancrook@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067229 - Make browser.alarms.clearAll() resolve with undefined. r=robwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323589\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/web-extensions/resources/alarms/background.js", "toolkit/components/extensions/parent/ext-alarms.js", "toolkit/components/extensions/schemas/alarms.json", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_ext_alarms.js"], "git_node": "2787d18cda7d1623a80d15d192e3f34952d6c5e2", "git_parents": ["29349bf94fd23f5b5da5759ebd0f3c1a3fedd84b"], "node": "b7ea1aead507a92811a406e4faa3e80a05bfda5d", "parents": ["43ee5cbe2cb89707bc4b31fae004e36c55a1524c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Neeco Fabian \u003cneecofabian@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068774 - Update illustration on the Your new profile is good to go messaging r=emcminn,omc-reviewers\n\n- Add a light and dark mode version of the new illustration for the new profile confirmation message\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323416\n", "files": ["browser/components/asrouter/modules/FeatureCalloutMessages.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "481aaf8d47137579f59372aa083bd2630a85a1b0", "git_parents": ["2787d18cda7d1623a80d15d192e3f34952d6c5e2"], "node": "2ba93bbcc1182e716de7a6bb0d3e57b78a69310b", "parents": ["b7ea1aead507a92811a406e4faa3e80a05bfda5d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "andyh \u003candhuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1925289 - Add a totalVisitsCount counter to the openURL trigger. r=omc-reviewers,sachung\n\nThe openURL trigger's visitsCount is keyed by the full URL, so under a broad pattern like \"*://*/*\" it reads 1 on nearly every fire and only advances when the same URL is loaded again, making \"show this on the Nth page load\" impossible to express. This patch adds totalVisitsCount to the trigger context, which is a session counter incremented on every match regardless of URL.\n\nNote that visitsCount keeps its per-URL semantics so existing messages are unaffected.\nNote the openURL listener is shared by all active openURL messages, so totalVisitsCount counts against their combined params/patterns/regexPatterns.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321997\n", "files": ["browser/components/asrouter/modules/ASRouterTriggerListeners.sys.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/tests/browser/browser_trigger_listeners.js", "browser/components/asrouter/tests/unit/ASRouterTriggerListeners.test.js", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/schemas/TriggerActionSchemas/TriggerActionSchemas.json", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/schemas/TriggerActionSchemas/index.md"], "git_node": "26d0dbf6aa14486fbb46fc9fa8dd6fd54eb7c070", "git_parents": ["481aaf8d47137579f59372aa083bd2630a85a1b0"], "node": "5315dd09144f6e6097423dc1aa50497b1e5c0ab5", "parents": ["2ba93bbcc1182e716de7a6bb0d3e57b78a69310b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "longsonr \u003clongsonr@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069349 - Update handling of negative std.dev for feGaussianblur/feDropShadow r=emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323588\n", "files": ["dom/svg/SVGFEDropShadowElement.cpp", "dom/svg/SVGFEGaussianBlurElement.cpp", "layout/reftests/svg/filters/feDropShadow-01-ref.svg", "layout/reftests/svg/filters/feDropShadow-01.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/filter-effects/feDropShadow-negative-deviation.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/filter-effects/feGaussianBlur-negative-deviation.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/filter-effects/reference/feDropShadow-negative-deviation-ref.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/filter-effects/reference/feGaussianBlur-negative-deviation-ref.svg"], "git_node": "bc569036cf04160462041ecdf8186a4294d7d8e6", "git_parents": ["26d0dbf6aa14486fbb46fc9fa8dd6fd54eb7c070"], "node": "4e69f579c78577e76fb8cb479791db2030c944c3", "parents": ["5315dd09144f6e6097423dc1aa50497b1e5c0ab5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065294 - Update YUVBufferGenerator r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320299\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestYUVBufferGenerator.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/YUVBufferGenerator.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/YUVBufferGenerator.h"], "git_node": "7797995b89a2fd1a636a4f87364e4fd8fbafc0ed", "git_parents": ["bc569036cf04160462041ecdf8186a4294d7d8e6"], "node": "dd11af0d50f864ce1abef601fb780777fd447623", "parents": ["4e69f579c78577e76fb8cb479791db2030c944c3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Omar Gonzalez \u003cs9tpepper@apache.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066287 - integrate calls to AITabStore in about:aitab r=jlewis\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323001\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/actors/AITabParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aitab_store_integration.js"], "git_node": "9e866629d48984ac644dea4b72329fea75ed9f4c", "git_parents": ["7797995b89a2fd1a636a4f87364e4fd8fbafc0ed"], "node": "f91dedbb500067d2bcadf43e7cdf218654b661bd", "parents": ["dd11af0d50f864ce1abef601fb780777fd447623"], "tags": []}, {"author": "John Oberhauser \u003cj.git@obez.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060389 - Preventing media from playing while the user is driving the car r=android-reviewers,gmalekpour\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321384\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/automotive/build.gradle", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/automotive/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/automotive/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/automotive/CarUxRestrictionsFeature.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/automotive/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/automotive/CarUxRestrictionsFeatureTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/automotive/src/test/resources/robolectric.properties", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/Core.kt"], "git_node": "e57069c16bec3fc057f501b48847bb7c9f62ab42", "git_parents": ["9e866629d48984ac644dea4b72329fea75ed9f4c"], "node": "f71bd288fd305593bd38c63b4bf712dbe2542f92", "parents": ["f91dedbb500067d2bcadf43e7cdf218654b661bd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kenneth Langga \u003cklangga@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059329 - Migrate the portal alerts backend to the dbus proxy API. r=saschanaz\n\nNow that the vendored dbus crate is 0.9, replace the ffidisp\ncompatibility API with blocking::Connection and a Proxy method call.\nThe connection is created per call and dropped afterwards, removing the\ncached connection and its dead-connection handling. AddNotification\ngoes through with_proxy and a typed (s, a{sv}) argument list, dropping\nthe MessageItem construction and its unwrap. With the connection no\nlonger outliving the call, a fire-and-forget send would lose the\nwithdrawal, as the portal discards a request whose sender has already\ndisconnected; RemoveNotification therefore waits for its reply as\nwell, which also makes withdrawal failures observable. Callback order\nand the D-Bus signatures and values are unchanged; each call now pays\nthe connection setup, and CloseAlert blocks up to the call timeout, on\nthe main thread until the next patch moves the calls off it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322048\n", "files": ["toolkit/system/gnome/rust/src/portal_alerts_service.rs"], "git_node": "c590167fced68fd6e5e4260553cc4f39521d835c", "git_parents": ["e57069c16bec3fc057f501b48847bb7c9f62ab42"], "node": "8b5a5cbe105558186022783389864c3fb5a2e279", "parents": ["f71bd288fd305593bd38c63b4bf712dbe2542f92"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kelly Cochrane \u003ckcochrane@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050182 - Prevent default splitter background-color on Win/Linux for the sidebar tools/extensions splitter r=nsharpley\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323698\n", "files": ["browser/components/sidebar/sidebar-main.css"], "git_node": "e6a9a218795117aa7cae335e13a338f5ff9f0b7b", "git_parents": ["c590167fced68fd6e5e4260553cc4f39521d835c"], "node": "54fb1cf6d159cabf3a73846a407e77556ba3bc64", "parents": ["8b5a5cbe105558186022783389864c3fb5a2e279"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064750 - Add a nimbus-prefs agent skill documenting pref/Nimbus/telemetry co-declaration r=jlockhart,ai4dev-reviewers,suhaib DONTBUILD\n\nThere is currently no in-tree guidance on making a feature pref\nNimbus-controllable. toolkit/components/nimbus/docs/index.md is a six-line\npointer to experimenter.info, and modules/libpref/docs/index.md never mentions\nNimbus at all.\n\nThis adds an agent skill covering:\n - which mechanism to use (fallbackPref, setPref, Nimbus-only, plain pref),\n - where to declare the pref,\n - the FeatureManifest.yaml entry,\n - the JS and C++ read paths, including why C++ should use setPref onto a\n   StaticPrefList.yaml pref rather than the NimbusFeatures C++ API, which only\n   sees isEarlyStartup features,\n - exposure events and pairing the pref with Glean,\n - the getVariable() resolution order and its traps,\n - when NOT to make a pref Nimbus-controllable.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314871\n", "files": [".agents/skills/nimbus-prefs/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/nimbus-prefs/SKILL.md"], "git_node": "b213040d4cbc5c951873aea71176bb3d3bf6938a", "git_parents": ["e6a9a218795117aa7cae335e13a338f5ff9f0b7b"], "node": "e64a1e24326e1ff991286e24336851fcca8a6471", "parents": ["54fb1cf6d159cabf3a73846a407e77556ba3bc64"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2060389 - Preventing media from playing while the user is driving the car r=android-reviewers,gmalekpour\" for causing buildconfig bustages.\n\nThis reverts commit e57069c16bec3fc057f501b48847bb7c9f62ab42.\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/automotive/build.gradle", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/automotive/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/automotive/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/automotive/CarUxRestrictionsFeature.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/automotive/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/automotive/CarUxRestrictionsFeatureTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/automotive/src/test/resources/robolectric.properties", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/Core.kt"], "git_node": "3eebdbb430862dcf5c14cf88c1b2f1b630ab95ec", "git_parents": ["b213040d4cbc5c951873aea71176bb3d3bf6938a"], "node": "eed267b1e490cd392647269a2f20c1e41f6540b7", "parents": ["e64a1e24326e1ff991286e24336851fcca8a6471"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2065294 - Update YUVBufferGenerator r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\" for causing GTest failures.\n\nThis reverts commit 7797995b89a2fd1a636a4f87364e4fd8fbafc0ed.\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestYUVBufferGenerator.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/YUVBufferGenerator.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/YUVBufferGenerator.h"], "git_node": "ef574e322b55c65b13274937becd3ced52feff12", "git_parents": ["3eebdbb430862dcf5c14cf88c1b2f1b630ab95ec"], "node": "5f2eb13b392965141c16366114d2fdbadc00f17b", "parents": ["eed267b1e490cd392647269a2f20c1e41f6540b7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2066287 - integrate calls to AITabStore in about:aitab r=jlewis\" for causing failures at browser_all_files_referenced.js\n\nThis reverts commit 9e866629d48984ac644dea4b72329fea75ed9f4c.\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/actors/AITabParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aitab_store_integration.js"], "git_node": "68b60962002e111ef2f528b78b84ad522f337df9", "git_parents": ["ef574e322b55c65b13274937becd3ced52feff12"], "node": "b6766d9fb5945a743a271b130b079fa6c3239ffb", "parents": ["5f2eb13b392965141c16366114d2fdbadc00f17b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ayoub hedri \u003cahedri@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068035 - Renamed Feature-Policy to Permissions-Policy and switched to SFV parser r=simonf\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322576\n", "files": ["dom/base/Document.cpp", "dom/security/featurepolicy/FeaturePolicy.cpp", "dom/security/featurepolicy/FeaturePolicy.h", "dom/security/featurepolicy/FeaturePolicyParser.cpp", "dom/security/featurepolicy/FeaturePolicyParser.h"], "git_node": "9b7e68aac74909fbd1343075e79d384c4a326bc2", "git_parents": ["68b60962002e111ef2f528b78b84ad522f337df9"], "node": "5510eda4ddd0631272dbca74c674493457df5130", "parents": ["b6766d9fb5945a743a271b130b079fa6c3239ffb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ayoub hedri \u003cahedri@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068035 - Rename policy methods used for iframe allow attributes. r=simonf\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322646\n", "files": ["dom/html/HTMLIFrameElement.cpp", "dom/security/featurepolicy/FeaturePolicy.cpp", "dom/security/featurepolicy/FeaturePolicy.h", "dom/security/featurepolicy/FeaturePolicyParser.cpp", "dom/security/featurepolicy/FeaturePolicyParser.h", "dom/security/featurepolicy/fuzztest/fp_fuzzer.cpp", "dom/security/featurepolicy/test/gtest/TestFeaturePolicyParser.cpp"], "git_node": "c58d870636dc29a64c56938b1ac1bb953edb39fe", "git_parents": ["9b7e68aac74909fbd1343075e79d384c4a326bc2"], "node": "11358553011e76923f3b38aa71f1aa594cd3b9de", "parents": ["5510eda4ddd0631272dbca74c674493457df5130"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ayoub hedri \u003cahedri@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068035 - Update mochitests to use the correct headers and WPT expectations for Permissions-Policy.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323213\n", "files": ["dom/security/featurepolicy/test/mochitest/file_xslt.html^headers^", "dom/security/featurepolicy/test/mochitest/file_xslt.xml^headers^", "dom/security/featurepolicy/test/mochitest/file_xslt.xsl^headers^", "dom/security/featurepolicy/test/mochitest/file_xslt_outer.html^headers^", "dom/security/featurepolicy/test/mochitest/test_parser.html^headers^", "testing/web-platform/meta/mediacapture-streams/MediaDevices-enumerateDevices-not-allowed-camera.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/mediacapture-streams/MediaDevices-enumerateDevices-not-allowed-mic.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/serial/serial-disabled-by-permissions-policy.https.sub.html.ini"], "git_node": "e0a5a755cc0daeae55798c4f9616cc2b20f34ff3", "git_parents": ["c58d870636dc29a64c56938b1ac1bb953edb39fe"], "node": "0473835238222882409973a4b754cfff8e06dda1", "parents": ["11358553011e76923f3b38aa71f1aa594cd3b9de"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Finn Terdal \u003cfterdal@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063319 - FRO Template - Terms of Use Screen Control for Managing Diagnostic and Interaction Data r=omc-reviewers,emcminn\n\nAdds the template capabilities the consolidated Terms of Use screen needs to\npresent its data-collection controls behind an inline disclosure:\n\n- a \"text\" content tile, which renders a LinkParagraph so a paragraph can be\n  positioned in the tiles order rather than only in above_button_content;\n- header.linkStyle, which renders a collapsible tile header as a centred link\n  with a chevron instead of a bordered button;\n- multiSelectItemDesign \"grouped-card\", one card around a whole multiselect\n  group rather than one card per item;\n- a description line beneath the label in both card designs, with the checkbox\n  centred across the two rows.\n\nThe controls the disclosure reveals are the existing interaction-data and\ncrash-data checkboxes, so this closes the in-modal telemetry opt-out gap on\nthat screen.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319221\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/static/browser_all_files_referenced.js", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/assets/pic-cursor.svg", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/assets/pic-shield.svg", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/content/aboutwelcome.bundle.js", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/content/aboutwelcome.css", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/jar.mn", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/tests/browser/browser_aboutwelcome_multiselect.js", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/components/ContentTiles.jsx", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/styles/_multistage.scss", "browser/components/asrouter/content/components/asrouter-newtab-multistage/asrouter-newtab-multistage.bundle.js", "browser/components/asrouter/content/components/asrouter-newtab-multistage/asrouter-newtab-multistage.css", "browser/components/asrouter/docs/feature-callout.md", "browser/components/asrouter/tests/unit/content-src/components/ContentTiles.test.jsx", "browser/components/asrouter/tests/unit/content-src/components/MultiSelect.test.jsx"], "git_node": "4972d600bd1d8f6f1005079a49b59f6683c4f01f", "git_parents": ["e0a5a755cc0daeae55798c4f9616cc2b20f34ff3"], "node": "cb268c1fc828f79149b848321181e9bba87b1b89", "parents": ["0473835238222882409973a4b754cfff8e06dda1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Beth Rennie \u003cbeth@brennie.ca\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2018640 - Attempt to abort Nimbus updates during shutdown before changing enrollment state r=nimbus-reviewers,emcminn,jstutte,fchasen,hsohaney\n\nWe now aggressively try to abort updateRecipes during shutdown at\nseveral point before we make changes to enrollment state. Additionally,\nwe race all IO-bound promises (i.e., `RemoteSettingsClient.get()` and\n`NimbusEnrollments.loadUnenrolledSlugsFromOtherProfiles`) with promises\nthat reject once shutdown begins.\n\nUnfortunately, there is a cut-off point after which we can no longer\nabort. As soona as we've made any enrollment changes, they must be\nflushed to the database to ensure that we do not corrupt profiles (e.g.,\nwith applied prefFlips or setPrefs that are not persisted to the\ndatabase).\n\nIn the case where we trigger shutdown during the initialization of\n`ExperimentAPI`, we will halt applying migrations and making enrollment\nchanges after attempting to enable the `RemoteSettingsExperimentLoader`.\n\nShutdown unit tests have been added to ensure that we correctly\nrace promises and bail out early.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312737\n", "files": ["browser/components/backup/resources/PreferencesBackupResource.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/nimbus/ExperimentAPI.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/ExperimentManager.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/Migrations.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/RemoteSettingsExperimentLoader.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/SharedDataMap.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/nimbus/moz.build", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/unit/head.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/unit/shutdown/head.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/unit/shutdown/test_RSEL_updateRecipes_RemoteSettingsClient_get.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/unit/shutdown/test_RSEL_updateRecipes_before_update.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/unit/shutdown/test_RSEL_updateRecipes_load_unenrolled_slugs.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/unit/shutdown/test_RSEL_updateRecipes_timer.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/unit/shutdown/test_RSEL_updateRecipes_timer_lock_held.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/unit/shutdown/test_RSEL_withUpdateLock.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/unit/shutdown/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "8f7116e4b67b50b6bfa15d51caa2d1119678ca96", "git_parents": ["4972d600bd1d8f6f1005079a49b59f6683c4f01f"], "node": "d8f7db6673d47652989714a1783753b32a5d1a06", "parents": ["cb268c1fc828f79149b848321181e9bba87b1b89"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069194 - Type-check sessionstore against the tabbrowser's shared element declarations. r=sfoster\n\nThe `loadURI` check in `getInternalObjectState` becomes a presence test so the union narrows. It selects the same branch for every input.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323459\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/tsconfig.json", "browser/components/sessionstore/types/sessionstore.ts"], "git_node": "b8f01caa80e5ce47399b70455edada91763f1e1d", "git_parents": ["8f7116e4b67b50b6bfa15d51caa2d1119678ca96"], "node": "6603ea0758e11f69ec47fe9ca1e3d8ff7210a2e1", "parents": ["d8f7db6673d47652989714a1783753b32a5d1a06"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065813 - Name the schemelessInput enum through its interface's namespace. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,jswinarton\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323552\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/types/globals.ts"], "git_node": "a97c1a64b01b16af23b70ae42b1852cb14797961", "git_parents": ["b8f01caa80e5ce47399b70455edada91763f1e1d"], "node": "cbfae13e0dc47813e65fb2349108895c98c0113e", "parents": ["6603ea0758e11f69ec47fe9ca1e3d8ff7210a2e1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "@Giulia Cardieri \u003cgcardieri@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061059: Style SFF autocomplete row item r=omarg,fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,credential-management-reviewers,mkennedy,hjones,bolsson,mtigley\n\n- Update the SFF autocomplete with its Figma style\n- Make the summary pills (when we have more than 2 sources) and the edit button clickable and focusable via keyboard\n- Add a aria-label that changes depending on the status of the SFF trigger status (loading/fill/not able to find sources) - this is needed because the content from the richlistitem is not visible to screen readers (per my understanding)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318806\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/assets/sff-autofill-icon.svg", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/jar.mn", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/SmartFormFillAutocomplete.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_smartformfill_autocomplete.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/head_smartformfill_autocomplete.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/browser_autocomplete_footer.js", "browser/locales-preview/aiWindow.ftl", "browser/themes/shared/autocomplete.css", "toolkit/components/satchel/autocomplete-row-item/autocomplete-row-item.css", "toolkit/components/satchel/autocomplete-row-item/autocomplete-row-item.mjs", "toolkit/components/satchel/test/browser/browser_autocomplete.js", "toolkit/content/widgets/autocomplete-popup.js"], "git_node": "06f72018b091d51b1a92c13753e2f00b36072073", "git_parents": ["a97c1a64b01b16af23b70ae42b1852cb14797961"], "node": "84770c9ed1432a0455ff287267f47533e3931aa0", "parents": ["cbfae13e0dc47813e65fb2349108895c98c0113e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Giulia Cardieri \u003cgcardieri@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067217: Make ai-website-confirmation component have a responsive max-width r=ngrato\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322732\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-website-confirmation/ai-website-confirmation.css"], "git_node": "70ad9abfce27261232dfbcea60ecac63198af7c4", "git_parents": ["06f72018b091d51b1a92c13753e2f00b36072073"], "node": "f343373c8db5831703f87faef0691088884d423a", "parents": ["84770c9ed1432a0455ff287267f47533e3931aa0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Punam Dahiya \u003cpdahiya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063153 - Resume activity conversation should use resume prompt clicked chat_id r=echa,cmurray\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323140\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/ConversationSuggestions.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_conversation_starters.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-window/ai-window.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_prompts.js"], "git_node": "fbb9e2c7fed084f6c8516063973ffe0404b72658", "git_parents": ["70ad9abfce27261232dfbcea60ecac63198af7c4"], "node": "32c9774320bb072eefcbaedc69cb29f174dd51fb", "parents": ["f343373c8db5831703f87faef0691088884d423a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069495 - Update intellij-markdown to version 0.7.11. r=android-reviewers,adhingra\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323745\n", "files": ["gradle/libs.versions.toml"], "git_node