c": "Bug 2067963 - Test parsing temporal IDs from AV1 OBU extension headers r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322537\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestAOMDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/agnostic/AOMDecoder.h"], "git_node": "77680dba46ba8a163895308d9561a3263a3a5780", "git_parents": ["36594f5cef03ac2da763a6b755c4167c7b74dcde"], "node": "e56963cfa7e62d9809e98613a2a07d7ff7d298c3", "parents": ["36a8dffb2089f552db3bf5b4696ddbdc138b7821"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067963 - Read temporal IDs from AV1 OBU extension headers r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322538\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/agnostic/AOMDecoder.cpp"], "git_node": "a59ea4c9322f1edd188371aa30d1cf265b148b13", "git_parents": ["77680dba46ba8a163895308d9561a3263a3a5780"], "node": "0e0311db39e9dcecb3dfb2cad5b7c70ee759a0af", "parents": ["e56963cfa7e62d9809e98613a2a07d7ff7d298c3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067963 - Let encoder tests select hardware preference r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322017\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestMediaDataEncoder.cpp"], "git_node": "2eaf2b219677f1363d08bcf7422a0f145a1ce50e", "git_parents": ["a59ea4c9322f1edd188371aa30d1cf265b148b13"], "node": "86accf0c1cb19738f43adc2aaab67b7ba9876cae", "parents": ["0e0311db39e9dcecb3dfb2cad5b7c70ee759a0af"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067963 - Let encoder tests select bitrate mode r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322699\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestMediaDataEncoder.cpp"], "git_node": "1ec523b28016795d9bd592ad08da336d83c6aa24", "git_parents": ["2eaf2b219677f1363d08bcf7422a0f145a1ce50e"], "node": "c579e9f2b16a872b893f4a3121da4aac869725ce", "parents": ["86accf0c1cb19738f43adc2aaab67b7ba9876cae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067963 - Test AV1 SVC temporal IDs on automatic keyframes r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nVerify that the temporal layer reported with an encoder-generated keyframe matches the temporal ID encoded in its AV1 OBU header.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322539\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestMediaDataEncoder.cpp"], "git_node": "3baed183eb325ef20ce405cf5d77a1f3ae495985", "git_parents": ["1ec523b28016795d9bd592ad08da336d83c6aa24"], "node": "74d91ce00849da1eeb3b07fdaae4959485f1292e", "parents": ["c579e9f2b16a872b893f4a3121da4aac869725ce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067963 - Preserve encoded AV1 SVC temporal IDs r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nAV1 temporal IDs are assigned before encoding. Avoid resetting their output-side schedule when libaom independently emits a keyframe, so MediaRawData continues to report the ID carried by the encoded OBU.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322540\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoEncoder.cpp"], "git_node": "2c1510c5e7b3f23d372296618182c89c19d4160c", "git_parents": ["3baed183eb325ef20ce405cf5d77a1f3ae495985"], "node": "b2fc20f0e576e232fe0dc738c1543b536b151d92", "parents": ["74d91ce00849da1eeb3b07fdaae4959485f1292e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2067994 - Cleanup some webrender pref usage. r=nical,gfx-reviewers\" for causing failures at tscrollx.\n\nThis reverts commit 8ee1b70fa09f1cf477fc8ea12502627a612f920c.\n", "files": ["gfx/config/gfxConfigManager.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxPlatform.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "modules/libpref/init/all.js"], "git_node": "d7ff90d9d6323a5071ef8876aee8d4da98b660e3", "git_parents": ["2c1510c5e7b3f23d372296618182c89c19d4160c"], "node": "b9db273d7da90a81a6450d511c86efbeac7e2bbc", "parents": ["b2fc20f0e576e232fe0dc738c1543b536b151d92"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065753. Decode JXL images on a dedicated thread pool. r=saschanaz,jstutte\n\njxl-rs 0.6 will decode one image on several threads if we hand it a\nJxlParallelRunner: it calls us back with a count and a closure, and expects us to\ncall that closure once per index, in parallel if we want to, and not return until\nthey have all finished. This implements that on a thread pool created in this\npatch, and hands it to process() and flush_pixels() in place of None.\n\nThe pool is a SharedThreadPool, which gets us three things without writing them. It\nis a singleton: one thread pool shared per-process. It is shut down at\nxpcom-shutdown-threads, so nothing here has to observe shutdown. And it reaps its\nidle threads after a few seconds.\n\nThe calling thread that blocks and the threads it waits on belong to different pools,\nso a blocked decode can never be holding a thread that a helper needs. AVIF already\nworks this way, fanning a decode out to dav1d's own threads. The calling thread\ntakes a share of the work as well as waiting, so the work still gets done if no\nhelper can be queued at all.\n\nnsIThreadPool has Rust bindings, but nsThreadPool is not a registered component, so\nthere is no way to construct one from Rust. JxlDecodePool.cpp constructs the thread\npool in C++ side. Everything else is in rust.\n\nThe part worth reviewing carefully is the lifetime. The closure jxl-rs hands us\nborrows its decode state, so it is only valid for the duration of the call, but a\nhelper is an nsIRunnable and has to be 'static. Both can't be true, so the lifetime\nis transmuted away and the closure travels behind a raw pointer, which switches off\nborrow checking for that data.\n\nWhat puts the guarantee back is that the call does not return until every helper it\nqueued has been accounted for. Each helper's payload decrements a count from its\ndestructor, which runs whether the helper ran or was thrown away without running,\nand a guard blocks until that count is zero. The guard does its waiting from a\ndestructor rather than from a statement after the work, so it also covers the\ncalling thread's own invocation of the closure panicking: a plain call sited after\nthe work would be skipped by the unwind while helpers were still holding the\npointer. Gecko builds Rust with panic=abort so that unwind does not arise in\nFirefox, but rusttests builds with unwinding.\n\nHelpers are dispatched with DISPATCH_FALLIBLE, so a dispatch the pool cannot accept\nreleases the helper rather than leaking it.\n\nI had Claude model the algorithm outside the tree and run it under Miri, including\nwith strict provenance since the design rests on a raw pointer, and under shuttle,\nwhich swaps in its own threading primitives so a test can walk the possible\ninterleavings instead of hoping to hit the bad one. Three of those searches\nenumerate every interleaving rather than sampling: that the wait covers a helper,\nthat a helper discarded without running still releases its count, and that a\ndispatch the pool refuses leaves the count balanced rather than one short. Two\nhelpers both claiming indices is too big a space to enumerate, so that case is\nsampled instead.\n\nTwo things that does not cover. The model substitutes its own dispatcher for\nmoz_task, because Miri will not execute foreign functions, so what it checks is the\nalgorithm and not the C++ side. And it assumes the pool honours DISPATCH_FALLIBLE,\nwhich comes from reading nsThreadPool rather than from the model.\n\nStarting the pool's threads costs about 0.2ms on my machine. My rough guess is that\nimages under about 4ms of decode time will stay on one thread and never touch the\npool at all, so the most this can cost is 0.2ms on a 5ms decode, or about 4%.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320649\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "image/build/nsImageModule.cpp", "image/decoders/JxlDecodePool.cpp", "image/decoders/moz.build", "image/rust/jxl/Cargo.toml", "image/rust/jxl/src/decoder.rs", "image/rust/jxl/src/lib.rs", "image/rust/jxl/src/runner.rs", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "592619e3a8e64866db073e110b0f0a773a30e64e", "git_parents": ["d7ff90d9d6323a5071ef8876aee8d4da98b660e3"], "node": "df6c0367d306143ff148a0e2e40b763b5fb4cdf7", "parents": ["b9db273d7da90a81a6450d511c86efbeac7e2bbc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065753. Add gtests that parallel JXL decoding produces the same pixels as serial. r=saschanaz\n\nAdd tests that decoding jxl serially or in parallel produce the same result. Add a test that throwing much more work at the jxl decoding pool than it has threads works fine.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320780\n", "files": ["image/test/gtest/Common.cpp", "image/test/gtest/Common.h", "image/test/gtest/TestDecoders.cpp", "image/test/gtest/large-jxl-reference.webp", "image/test/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "f5de96f20b5ccf5dfb1d473a26fe22e88575ba3e", "git_parents": ["592619e3a8e64866db073e110b0f0a773a30e64e"], "node": "daa391b107caf25d8f07546b229687ce083b5090", "parents": ["df6c0367d306143ff148a0e2e40b763b5fb4cdf7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Omar Gonzalez \u003cs9tpepper@apache.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066287 - integrate calls to AITabStore in about:aitab r=jlewis\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323001\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/static/browser_all_files_referenced.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/actors/AITabParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aitab_store_integration.js"], "git_node": "486735fc0ef43fa0d6162a359a5f6ccb4411efef", "git_parents": ["f5de96f20b5ccf5dfb1d473a26fe22e88575ba3e"], "node": "ef6bfa6737e18bf057f3e110b30d09f338f95be6", "parents": ["daa391b107caf25d8f07546b229687ce083b5090"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069432 - Drop the vestigial transparent border on the urlbar view action button. r=adw\n\nThe button shrinks by the border width on each side. Under forced colors, where an author border-color reverts to currentColor whatever its alpha, it no longer paints a frame.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323779\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/urlbar/view-nova.css"], "git_node": "d9e227b80d90ff7c7632ce61c587eb05c3ac3aa2", "git_parents": ["486735fc0ef43fa0d6162a359a5f6ccb4411efef"], "node": "521559b80933412e55b1c91c8aa59da0c332c463", "parents": ["ef6bfa6737e18bf057f3e110b30d09f338f95be6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069432 - Extract the snapped 1px border width out of --urlbar-input-container-border-width (no functional change). r=adw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323780\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/urlbar.css"], "git_node": "deab091afb6468e1e5142cb9f58a3e29cbd167d5", "git_parents": ["d9e227b80d90ff7c7632ce61c587eb05c3ac3aa2"], "node": "7d6b8ce8fb89c9bdef03c3a4af5f262b287f932f", "parents": ["521559b80933412e55b1c91c8aa59da0c332c463"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069432 - Give the realtime image container a border only on the row types that want one. r=adw\n\nThe padding that stands in for the border snaps the way a border width does, so the container is the same size either way at every device pixel ratio (measured at 0.75, 1, 1.25 and 1.5).\n\nUnder forced colors, where an author border-color reverts to currentColor whatever its alpha, the market, flight status and sports containers keep their solid line and every other variant stops painting one.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323781\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/urlbar/view-nova.css"], "git_node": "934e99df7c4aabc85be00b472d53a5b4fa6f8575", "git_parents": ["deab091afb6468e1e5142cb9f58a3e29cbd167d5"], "node": "70d85ec2faac66d058bb7548e95da72570f5c5f0", "parents": ["7d6b8ce8fb89c9bdef03c3a4af5f262b287f932f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Boris Chiou \u003cboris.chiou@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068460 - Add more assertions to catch the unexpected behaviors and make the code clearer. r=layout-scroll-driven-animation-reviewers,dshin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323759\n", "files": ["dom/animation/CSSAnimation.cpp"], "git_node": "09b75a75b1e2fa73a4173403c96b7af10c69be52", "git_parents": ["934e99df7c4aabc85be00b472d53a5b4fa6f8575"], "node": "95d1af79a1a8736e1b70c8d6b70be60f949a7019", "parents": ["70d85ec2faac66d058bb7548e95da72570f5c5f0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Boris Chiou \u003cboris.chiou@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068460 - Simplify the update of mIgnoreKeyframesGeneration. r=layout-scroll-driven-animation-reviewers,dshin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323760\n", "files": ["dom/animation/CSSAnimation.cpp"], "git_node": "cd413f64a6d3173e90d447dbc95ac3678187b8ea", "git_parents": ["09b75a75b1e2fa73a4173403c96b7af10c69be52"], "node": "dd1a7124fb89a85fe177ee7e3c9c23708cea935b", "parents": ["95d1af79a1a8736e1b70c8d6b70be60f949a7019"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Omar Gonzalez \u003cs9tpepper@apache.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064907 - add a no changes state when form fill doesnt make any changes r=gcardieri,fluent-reviewers,bolsson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323431\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/actors/SmartFormFillParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/actors/SmartFormFillReviewChild.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-sff-form-review/ai-sff-form-review.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-sff-form-review/ai-sff-form-review.stories.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/SmartFormFillConstants.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/SmartFormFillDocument.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/SmartFormFillReviewSession.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartformfill_form_review_filling.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/head_smartformfill_form_review.js", "browser/locales-preview/aiWindow.ftl"], "git_node": "91589cf986b04af6864caec9bc7c007409c09e5d", "git_parents": ["cd413f64a6d3173e90d447dbc95ac3678187b8ea"], "node": "3dbd255b07572e42d4698660b647319e0a19c7b5", "parents": ["dd1a7124fb89a85fe177ee7e3c9c23708cea935b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063577 - Measure discarded expired HTTP/3 Alt-Svc mappings r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nAdd a Glean timing_distribution recording how far past expiry a\ndiscarded HTTP/3 Alt-Svc mapping was, at the point AltSvcCache::LookupMapping\nremoves it for being expired.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323731\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/AlternateServices.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "08412b89c8cca0bac468871f020b9e572b50307b", "git_parents": ["91589cf986b04af6864caec9bc7c007409c09e5d"], "node": "0e9e139fe505d87b83afc31caf6750d9b5275419", "parents": ["3dbd255b07572e42d4698660b647319e0a19c7b5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch"