rap() in servo get_attr and any_attr_ignore_ns functions. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nNot relevant to Firefox, but this is wanted by downstream servo consumers;\nsee https://github.com/servo/stylo/issues/449.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323851\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/servo/selector_parser.rs"], "git_node": "be0f84bea8e1ba353398af936d886c98d79c45f6", "git_parents": ["1134f6689b15f26fdfad90c7f89b1512052aa628"], "node": "9ee2253673f3fc4fb28a7c15cc96ee6650b59e25", "parents": ["150727cd33d355c962104020ea7f54857dc71b49"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2069577 - Avoid unwrap() in servo get_attr and any_attr_ignore_ns functions. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\" for causing bc tests failures at nsCSPContext.cpp\n\nThis reverts commit be0f84bea8e1ba353398af936d886c98d79c45f6.\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/servo/selector_parser.rs"], "git_node": "ba9fb2d5f43dcf7fa6dc5720111d160ff955aab0", "git_parents": ["be0f84bea8e1ba353398af936d886c98d79c45f6"], "node": "53d1de9fb825db14614939edd6ae7bc99c6b2a46", "parents": ["9ee2253673f3fc4fb28a7c15cc96ee6650b59e25"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069577 - Avoid unwrap() in servo get_attr and any_attr_ignore_ns functions. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nNot relevant to Firefox, but this is wanted by downstream servo consumers;\nsee https://github.com/servo/stylo/issues/449.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323851\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/servo/selector_parser.rs"], "git_node": "3f7fea2b7a7b12c3a62807b5b601feddc5db2cc7", "git_parents": ["ba9fb2d5f43dcf7fa6dc5720111d160ff955aab0"], "node": "8588e98cfb02fc891fa28eb36feaf3ac82add033", "parents": ["53d1de9fb825db14614939edd6ae7bc99c6b2a46"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2069235 - Update PDF.js to 716aff9d50c08b4bec3e350540a3f05aea89dedc r=fluent-reviewers,bolsson,marco\" for causing bc tests failures\n\nThis reverts commit a9f6a88d960a318eff66d00f35bfa897bafc07e8.\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/aboutpdf/content/pdfFeaturesNotification.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.scripting.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.worker.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/viewer-geckoview.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/viewer.css", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/viewer.html", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/viewer.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/jar.mn", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/moz.yaml", "toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/about/pdfFeaturesNotification.ftl"], "git_node": "d8be62da89cdb63212b7f57459af66e9630aa58a", "git_parents": ["3f7fea2b7a7b12c3a62807b5b601feddc5db2cc7"], "node": "c67c6096ac7562a9a8d2a8644194c747e5e8b04f", "parents": ["8588e98cfb02fc891fa28eb36feaf3ac82add033"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Logan Rosen \u003cloganrosen@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1892289 - Add --data command-line option for data URLs. r=firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,mossop\n\nAdd an explicit --data \u003cdata-URL\u003e command-line option while keeping ordinary external top-level data: URLs blocked. The option preserves external-load semantics and opts in using LOAD_FLAGS_FORCE_ALLOW_DATA_URI. Tests cover startup and remote invocation, invalid input, external blocking, and null-principal behavior.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322525\n", "files": ["browser/components/BrowserContentHandler.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tests/browser/browser_initial_tab_remoteType.js", "browser/modules/BrowserDOMWindow.sys.mjs", "dom/interfaces/base/nsIBrowserDOMWindow.idl"], "git_node": "c85343a33e45395e02ab68dd8d4e8f17e1523bad", "git_parents": ["d8be62da89cdb63212b7f57459af66e9630aa58a"], "node": "2b0ff0566ffa6c466d476b24870a24f7c1efcc61", "parents": ["c67c6096ac7562a9a8d2a8644194c747e5e8b04f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Import translations from https://github.com/mozilla-l10n/android-l10n CLOSED TREE\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-hr/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/res/values-gn/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/res/values-in/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/res/values-tg/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/app-links/src/main/res/values-hr/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/ipprotection/src/main/res/values-hr/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/media/src/main/res/values-hr/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/password-importer/src/main/res/values-hr/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/main/res/values-hr/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/protection-dashboard/src/main/res/values-hr/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/res/values-gn/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-gn/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-tg/strings.xml"], "git_node": "0ce17c68a6a1322dcb597f2ab873e470f835c912", "git_parents": ["c85343a33e45395e02ab68dd8d4e8f17e1523bad"], "node": "f326e4aab70d3730de7cb66795e0271d214b9058", "parents": ["2b0ff0566ffa6c466d476b24870a24f7c1efcc61"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069326. Flip the pref to turn on multithreaded jxl decoding. r=saschanaz\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323574\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "93222b3aae1f8632d42cd4dea1ce9b9ca6ddd9b6", "git_parents": ["0ce17c68a6a1322dcb597f2ab873e470f835c912"], "node": "659f8e5099180232f957bb7a74449e6127648290", "parents": ["f326e4aab70d3730de7cb66795e0271d214b9058"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069593. Use Optional[str] in protoc_wrapper so that it imports on Python 3.9. r=ahochheiden,firefox-build-system-reviewers\n\nprotoc_binary is annotated `revision: None | str`, which is Python 3.10 syntax. mach's\nminimum is 3.9 (MIN_PYTHON_VERSION in mach) and that is what CI runs, so importing the\nmodule throws there:\n\n  File \".../toolkit/components/protobuf/scripts/protoc_wrapper.py\", line 19, in \u003cmodule\u003e\n      def protoc_binary(revision: None | str = None) -\u003e Path:\n  TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for |: 'NoneType' and 'type'\n\nOptional[str] means the same thing and works on every version we support.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323834\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/protobuf/scripts/protoc_wrapper.py"], "git_node": "7a5020a485ac5a5a19e2192b4ef2caab9fc361e1", "git_parents": ["93222b3aae1f8632d42cd4dea1ce9b9ca6ddd9b6"], "node": "371e1806dadbc9b5938b06ab18b389177a5d9c47", "parents": ["659f8e5099180232f957bb7a74449e6127648290"], "tags": []}, {"author": "chloezhouny \u003cchloezhouny@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052369 - Avoid document-sized work per keystroke in the multiline editor and smartbar input. r=urlbar-reviewers,Mardak,mak\n\nWhile composing a prompt, a few things ran on every keystroke that did work scaling with the size of the whole document, so typing could feel slow on longer prompts. This patch cuts that down:\n\n- Cache the editor's serialized `value` and reuse it while the document hasn't changed, instead of re-serializing it on every read.\n- In #dispatchTransaction, only read `value` when the document actually changed, so caret and selection changes don't serialize it.\n- Resolve both selection offsets in a single pass (#posFromTextOffsets).\n- Cache Mentions.hasMention the same way (by document identity) so it no longer walks the whole document on every call.\n- Make _on_keyup synchronous and move the rare deferred-Enter handling into a fire-and-forget #finishDeferredEnter helper, with a guard so a second keyup can't re-enter it while it's still waiting. (also mirrored in UrlbarInputBase).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321755\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_smartbar_inline_mentions.js", "browser/components/multilineeditor/multiline-editor.mjs", "browser/components/multilineeditor/plugins/MentionsPlugin.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs"], "git_node": "02b6f5eb9525e137a5fd8b2b5b89987b4044b291", "git_parents": ["7a5020a485ac5a5a19e2192b4ef2caab9fc361e1"], "node": "c7da848f4b62a7577aa884d56bbbab2679d0ccf1", "parents": ["371e1806dadbc9b5938b06ab18b389177a5d9c47"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriel Luong \u003cgabriel.luong@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2013052 - Part 4: Select the content recommendations provider with a config flag r=android-reviewers,skhan\n\nThis uses the Merino client to fetch the content recommendations when useMerinoClient is enabled, and passes the crash reporter through to it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322156\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/service/pocket/src/main/java/mozilla/components/service/pocket/PocketStoriesConfig.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/pocket/src/main/java/mozilla/components/service/pocket/PocketStoriesService.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/pocket/src/main/java/mozilla/components/service/pocket/recommendations/ContentRecommendationsUseCases.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/pocket/src/test/java/mozilla/components/service/pocket/PocketStoriesConfigTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/pocket/src/test/java/mozilla/components/service/pocket/recommendations/ContentRecommendationsUseCasesTest.kt"], "git_node": "f1c5ada8da795620ba150e7f84d73b3cafacf788", "git_parents": ["02b6f5eb9525e137a5fd8b2b5b89987b4044b291"], "node": "be71a14b1d4bc7d82000d17d1a74f74fd6fc6698", "parents": ["c7da848f4b62a7577aa884d56bbbab2679d0ccf1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriel Luong \u003cgabriel.luong@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2013052 - Part 5: Fetch the content recommendations with the Merino client when enabled r=android-reviewers,skhan\n\n- This wires the Merino client secret setting from Bug 2013066 through to the content recommendations request config\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322157\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/Core.kt"], "git_node": "dcc79e41ef1e3fc813713bdb7769cf01520581d5", "git_parents": ["f1c5ada8da795620ba150e7f84d73b3cafacf788"], "node": "3e7c6ac7647777883d34eb70373877039d283008", "parents": ["be71a14b1d4bc7d82000d17d1a74f74fd6fc6698"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788686943, "git_changesets": ["a9f6a88d960a318eff66d00f35bfa897bafc07e8", "c09386e514243601ed61eae41c428494b2ee7dfd", "cb97ce80c3ff5b43d72d57901d076ee84e30f413", "1134f6689b15f26fdfad90c7f89b1512052aa628", "be0f84bea8e1ba353398af936d886c98d79c45f6", "ba9fb2d5f43dcf7fa6dc5720111d160ff955aab0", "3f7fea2b7a7b12c3a62807b5b601feddc5db2cc7", "d8be62da89cdb63212b7f57459af66e9630aa58a", "c85343a33e45395e02ab68dd8d4e8f17e1523bad", "0ce17c68a6a1322dcb597f2ab873e470f835c912", "93222b3aae1f8632d42cd4dea1ce9b9ca6ddd9b6", "7a5020a485ac5