: "default", "desc": "Bug 2069649 - Add telemetry to know how many users have file: URL cookies r=cookie-reviewers,valentin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323856\n", "files": ["netwerk/cookie/CookiePersistentStorage.cpp", "netwerk/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "19ac54863dd36008e855edf1471fb8dd66fd6a31", "git_parents": ["39490752aed6c7dda6d33fafa0ca5f560b2ed51a"], "node": "ec48f5d7ac19976825950b8269dc238cf395450c", "parents": ["6c0ae70ffb7b98a34fc36c38d482c1ee439c0444"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059620 - Pt 1 - Move the unsnapped prim rect back into the interning key and template r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nReverts the move onto PrimitiveInstance from the fractional snapping work, which\nturned out not to be needed, and gets us closer to dropping PrimitiveInstance in\nfavour of template plus draw instance(s).\n\nSafe because the display-list builder normalizes the external scroll offset away\nin whole app units, so the rect does not change when the scroll position does.\nThat has to stay exact: unlike the quarter-device-pixel raster corners beside it,\na uid compare during invalidation is bit-exact.\n\nRestores the two macOS wpt annotations this un-hides. font-applies-to-001 and\n-007 draw their second, inline-level \"Filler Text\" line one device pixel low on\nmacOS, and did so with the same 578 pixel diff long before this work. Bug 2050692\nrounds a non-snapped primitive's bounding rect outward, which coarsened the\nraster corners enough that a reftest's reference page stopped invalidating the\ntile its test page had just drawn: the reference capture reused the test's pixels\nand the pair matched by construction. A bit-exact uid compare invalidates that\ntile again, so the reference renders on its own and the long-standing difference\nis visible once more. Reinstating the annotations restores the state before\n2050692; the 1 px inline-baseline difference itself is untouched, and\nfont-applies-to-017 is still annotated for the same reason.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315510\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/example-compositor/compositor/src/main.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/invalidation/cached_surface.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/borders.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/gradient/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/image.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/line_dec.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/rectangle.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/text_run.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_backend.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_building.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/visibility.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/key_types.rs", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/CSS2/fonts/font-applies-to-001.xht.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/CSS2/fonts/font-applies-to-007.xht.ini"], "git_node": "3994c0b0e94ce5e2de6efba6882ee5de8f9b4ad5", "git_parents": ["19ac54863dd36008e855edf1471fb8dd66fd6a31"], "node": "87c85e2481bbb6b3b81964618bad53c2f785b1cd", "parents": ["ec48f5d7ac19976825950b8269dc238cf395450c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059620 - Pt 2 - Only run the app-unit round trip on an axis the scroll offset moves r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nThe zero-offset skip was per point, so a y-only scroll offset still rounded x\nonto the app-unit grid: the same unshifted coordinate stored one value in an\nunscrolled frame and another in a scrolled one. That is below the quarter-device-\npixel raster corners, but a uid compare is bit-exact, so with the rect in the key\nevery tile invalidated at every scroll offset.\n\nGecko's coordinates are whole app units, so the round trip was already\nbit-identical for them and nothing changes there. Guarded by offgrid_repaint_1/2.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316372\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/display_list.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/invalidation/invalidation.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/invalidation/offgrid_repaint_1.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/invalidation/offgrid_repaint_2.yaml"], "git_node": "8bdef41e9329a299543849f1b40a90a2f10a0717", "git_parents": ["3994c0b0e94ce5e2de6efba6882ee5de8f9b4ad5"], "node": "35c643e498a9f80cbfb41ea979c6e320ebb1c2c6", "parents": ["87c85e2481bbb6b3b81964618bad53c2f785b1cd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059620 - Pt 3 - Compute an over-thick border's interior split once r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nA rounded fill drawn as an over-thick border - how the non-native theme draws\nscrollbar thumbs, see ThemeDrawing::PaintRoundedRectWithRadius and bug 1694269 -\nis four corner segments with no edges, each clipped to its own quadrant and\nmeeting at the rect's midpoint. The clips spelled that midpoint two ways: min\nplus the leading non-overlapping width for one neighbour, max minus the trailing\none for the other. Equal mathematically, one ULP apart in f32.\n\nEach segment rounds its device bounds on its non-antialiased edges, and the\nshared quadrant edge is non-antialiased for both, so at a half-pixel midpoint the\nULP sends the two roundings opposite ways - 253.49998 to 253, 253.5 to 254 - and\na whole device pixel row drops out of the shape. Evaluate each split once, and\nonly where the widths overlap: elsewhere the two expressions are genuinely\ndifferent boundaries.\n\nThe reftest reference is a PNG because two yamls of the same shape at the same\ndevice position intern to one uid with identical raster corners, so the second\nrender reuses the first one's tile and the comparison passes vacuously.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316373\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/border.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/border/border-overlap-split.png", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/border/border-overlap-split.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/border/reftest.list"], "git_node": "0bf135913272a3e6d4c3c3dae12b49c07bb717df", "git_parents": ["8bdef41e9329a299543849f1b40a90a2f10a0717"], "node": "c7d1cea27db7ed0226c5be9d6f4b7710444289cf", "parents": ["35c643e498a9f80cbfb41ea979c6e320ebb1c2c6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064638 - Let the vertical tabs be reached in fullscreen r=kcochrane,sfoster,desktop-theme-reviewers,tabbrowser-reviewers\n\nBug 1927457 made the sidebar launcher hide along with the autohidden nav\ntoolbox in fullscreen. Only the top of the screen brings the chrome back\nthough, so vertical tabs ended up out of reach: moving to the edge where they\nsit does nothing.\n\nWatch for the pointer reaching the launcher's edge of the screen and bring the\nchrome back there too, so reaching for the tabs works like reaching for the\ntoolbar. This goes through MousePosTracker rather than a hover target at the\nedge: an element there would also catch a pointer that merely happens to rest\nat the edge when the chrome collapses and reveal it again the moment it\nappeared, and it would sit over the content while it did. The band is measured\non demand, since the launcher can be sent to the other edge - or turned off -\nfrom a sidebar panel, which stays on screen while the chrome is gone. Nothing\nis watched in DOM fullscreen, which leaves the nav toolbox collapsed on its\nway out.\n\nReaching the tabs also has to keep them. MousePosTracker hides the chrome again\nonce the pointer enters the content area, and showNavToolbox seeded that rect\nfrom the collapsed layout, where the launcher takes no space - so the strip it\nwas about to reveal into counted as content, and touching a tab could send\neverything away again. Capture the rect while the chrome is still expanded\ninstead, since showing it restores that layout.\n\nThe chrome then has to be able to go away again. Revealed with the pointer\nalready in the content - keyboard shortcuts, or the macOS menubar sliding down -\naddListener's synchronous enter bails out while still collapsed but leaves the\npointer recorded as inside, and the tracker only reports transitions, so nothing\ncould hide the chrome again. Forget that enter.\n\nThat menubar also sends a reveal update for every frame of its slide down.\nTaking each one as a reveal put the chrome straight back after the pointer\nreturning to the content sent it away, which reads as the content jumping, so\nonly the start of the reveal counts. Its shift now goes through one place as\nwell, because a collapsed toolbar that keeps it hangs that far over the\ncontent until the menubar goes back up.\n\nWhile it is down, the shifted toolbox floats over whatever is laid out below\nit. With horizontal tabs that is only web content, but the launcher sits there\ntoo, and the toolbox landed on the first vertical tabs. Give the tabstrip that\nmuch room for as long as the shift lasts.\n\nbrowser_f11_fullscreen_sidebar.js was skipped on macOS because the toolbars stay\nput there, but it turns browser.fullscreen.autohide on itself - and macOS is\nwhere this was reported.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321946\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-fullScreenAndPointerLock.js", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_f11_fullscreen_sidebar.js", "browser/themes/shared/tabbrowser/fullscreen-and-pointerlock.css"], "git_node": "a0a061b117bbca53f4041ba11324c8eca9a91aab", "git_parents": ["0bf135913272a3e6d4c3c3dae12b49c07bb717df"], "node": "cc04cf3d95fa1ec9d0d8ba23f6502a495a124ae1", "parents": ["c7d1cea27db7ed0226c5be9d6f4b7710444289cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Geoff Lankow \u003cgeoff@darktrojan.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067037 - Add mail message parts to Necko IPC handling. r=necko-reviewers,jesup\n\nThis is just a minimal stub which forwards things to Thunderbird code, but it needs to live here\nbecause other things are hard-wired to talk to Necko actors only.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321797\n", "files": ["netwerk/ipc/NeckoParent.cpp", "netwerk/ipc/NeckoParent.h", "netwerk/ipc/PNecko.ipdl"], "git_node": "21efd22f19c67396f506667f8e2d5428012cf84e", "git_parents": ["a0a061b117bbca53f4041ba11324c8eca9a91aab"], "node": "c6a96895ce34f7e14df2441423a21137031396ef", "parents": ["cc04cf3d95fa1ec9d0d8ba23f6502a495a124ae1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065120 - [efficiency] Add typed page readiness contracts. r=aaronmt\n\nReplace overloaded string selector groups with typed assertion groups and dedicated selector metadata for readiness, scrolling, lifecycle, and generated interaction relationships.\n\nDefine identified, navigation-ready, and interactive contracts using live selector probes. Expose identity-anchor and ready-content roles for ordinary selector authors while retaining the individual profiles for navigation internals and advanced rules.\n\nVerify starting, intermediate, waypoint, and destination pages before advancing tracked navigation state, and pass planned state and route context to conditional rules.\n\nDiscover concrete selector vals automatically through page selector catalogs, eliminating manually synchronized all lists while excluding parameterized selector factories. Validate explicit traversal order for assertion groups with multiple scrolling selectors.\n\nUse route-aware Settings readiness to wait for Sync Debug only before layout-sensitive direct row clicks. Keep navigation interactions just-in-time with bounded polling, and expand structured diagnostics and contract coverage.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323401\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/core/VerbContractTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/core/VerbHost.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/core/Verbs.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/devtools/InteractionCaseGenerator.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/devtools/NavigationGraphContractTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/devtools/PageReadinessContractTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/devtools/SelectorContainerContractTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/devtools/effview/README.md", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/devtools/effview/effviewdump-v2.py", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/docs/architecture.md", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/docs/converting-a-test.md", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/docs/gotchas.md", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/docs/guides/adding-navigation.md", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/docs/guides/authoring-selectors.md", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/docs/guides/creating-a-page-object.md", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/docs/guides/debugging-tests.md", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/docs/guides/discovering-selectors.md", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/docs/guides/extending-basepage.md", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/interaction/InteractionTestPlanner.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/interaction/SelectorCatalog.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/BasePage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/PageContext.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/PageReadiness.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/Selector.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/SelectorContainer.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/NavigationRegistry.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/NavigationState.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/AddToHomeScreenComponent.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/BookmarkSearchPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/BookmarksPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/BrowserPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/CollectionsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/CustomTabsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/DownloadsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/FindInPagePage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/GoogleLensPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/HistoryPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/HistorySearchGroupPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/HomePage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/MainMenuPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/MicrosurveysPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/NotificationPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/OnboardingPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/PWAPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/ReaderViewPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/RecentlyClosedTabsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SearchBarComponent.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsAboutPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsAccessibilityPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsAddonsManagerPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsAppIconPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsAutofillPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsCustomizePage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsDataCollectionPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/moz