i", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/track-sizing/row-track-sizing-004.html.ini"], "git_node": "0d04e60d213ab1ae7e08facaa4ebcbb24923fa51", "git_parents": ["9cbb8d10c69a8e43065153daeefbe561e16baa5f"], "node": "7dcbb9a29e5d8b9c3a3723d7a6c4d64512389635", "parents": ["40da41d07eb4bff69ee8984441ab720ae172eaf9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069915. Restore ScrollContainerFrame query frame fast path. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nWe attempt to implement a fast query frame for ScrollContainerFrame\nhttps://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/ae0bb53a873d228e4e61b796e184dc3c687ff82e/layout/generic/nsQueryFrame.h#116\nbut bug 2031757 made IsScrollContainerOrSubclass a circular reference to query frame. This doesn't actually loop because IsScrollContainerOrSubclass is a const method, so Dest is const ScrollContainerFrame in the IMPL_FAST_QUERYFRAME macro and the specialization is only declared for the non-const type so it doesn't match, so we fall back to the slow virtual QueryFrame.\n\n(The obvious const issues that this brings up are fixed in next patches.)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324031\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsIFrame.cpp"], "git_node": "71ff7f33abd8f42ebb8cc0010ae04ce434ff796d", "git_parents": ["0d04e60d213ab1ae7e08facaa4ebcbb24923fa51"], "node": "25175d5e55dcf4adec61dcabbf850743381be20f", "parents": ["7dcbb9a29e5d8b9c3a3723d7a6c4d64512389635"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dave Townsend \u003cdtownsend@oxymoronical.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068619: Don't allow external callers to set the isInitial parameter to init. r=niklas\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322933\n", "files": ["browser/components/profiles/SelectableProfileService.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "32431f8a82b4176d6be76dee446a7ee0b282b768", "git_parents": ["71ff7f33abd8f42ebb8cc0010ae04ce434ff796d"], "node": "d0cabb63c92df0538179a725b3fd6d1d41e720e1", "parents": ["25175d5e55dcf4adec61dcabbf850743381be20f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069586 - Fix typo in SSE4.2 configuration handling r=padenot\n\nThis re-enables some vectorized code in nsRect and AudioNodeEngine that\nused to be ignored.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324001\n", "files": ["dom/media/webaudio/AudioNodeEngine.cpp", "gfx/src/nsRect.cpp"], "git_node": "8ca0e5032f6a2a6477226ac9e6d05a0c5c8f7ece", "git_parents": ["32431f8a82b4176d6be76dee446a7ee0b282b768"], "node": "ee4304a3dab0142d1ec9c6c330fb27040f78e47d", "parents": ["d0cabb63c92df0538179a725b3fd6d1d41e720e1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Erich Gubler \u003cerichdongubler@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066728 - chore(rust): upgrade `scopeguard` 1.1.0 \u2192 1.2.0 r=webgpu-reviewers,supply-chain-reviewers,teoxoy\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321486\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "supply-chain/imports.lock", "third_party/rust/scopeguard/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/scopeguard/.cargo_vcs_info.json", "third_party/rust/scopeguard/.github/workflows/ci.yaml", "third_party/rust/scopeguard/.travis.yml", "third_party/rust/scopeguard/Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/scopeguard/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/scopeguard/Cargo.toml.orig", "third_party/rust/scopeguard/README.md", "third_party/rust/scopeguard/README.rst", "third_party/rust/scopeguard/examples/readme.rs", "third_party/rust/scopeguard/src/lib.rs"], "git_node": "7b1fd2649092caa19efd7c3e81e26c0684c90b05", "git_parents": ["8ca0e5032f6a2a6477226ac9e6d05a0c5c8f7ece"], "node": "c1a3d87423dc9edf7bf4f01a524f3439272d0f3b", "parents": ["ee4304a3dab0142d1ec9c6c330fb27040f78e47d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckagami@tb.pro\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1842455 - Part 1: Extract notification permission test into WPT r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nRemoving the pref breaks the test, and while fixing it is possible, it involves remote browser. So I decided to do WPT instead as testing web API in chrome test is weird after all.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323269\n", "files": ["dom/base/test/chrome/chrome.toml", "dom/base/test/chrome/test_permission_hasValidTransientUserActivation.xhtml", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/notifications/requestPermission-user-activation.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/notifications/requestPermission-user-activation.https.window.js", "tools/lint/rejected-words.yml"], "git_node": "9135a449dc8bac360f29254c34dae2f5601144e7", "git_parents": ["7b1fd2649092caa19efd7c3e81e26c0684c90b05"], "node": "a4d8a49b5ce89cd12c14e0c22e3818e7c7ca55dc", "parents": ["c1a3d87423dc9edf7bf4f01a524f3439272d0f3b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "calixteman \u003ccalixte.denizet@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069926 - Add pdfjs-reviewers to the review groups documentation. r=firefox-source-docs-reviewers,sylvestre DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324055\n", "files": ["docs/contributing/reviews.md"], "git_node": "95e0f5f155369d77a4839d5b48a574b8e3d0fdc8", "git_parents": ["9135a449dc8bac360f29254c34dae2f5601144e7"], "node": "2547b7902cfb475380c74d8c3a309cdfef80dd74", "parents": ["a4d8a49b5ce89cd12c14e0c22e3818e7c7ca55dc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Zia \u003cfzia@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054460 - Enable ActionsProviderTabGroups SAP smartbar r=desktop-theme-reviewers,mstriemer,yjamora,daleharvey\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318492\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_smartbar_tabgroups.js", "browser/components/urlbar/ActionsProvider.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/ActionsProviderTabGroups.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderGlobalActions.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProvidersManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarView.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-tabs/browser_action_tabgroups.js", "browser/themes/shared/smartbar.css"], "git_node": "8cc0e83a5aafd7acf911d514f181235ac4f61f03", "git_parents": ["95e0f5f155369d77a4839d5b48a574b8e3d0fdc8"], "node": "2d27eb5c9853a21eddfceaa7405ed01f06c0498c", "parents": ["2547b7902cfb475380c74d8c3a309cdfef80dd74"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vincent Tunru \u003cgit@vincenttunru.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2007590 - Use status code, not response text r=credential-management-reviewers,dimi\n\nThe `status` value is injected into the text string after \"HTTP\nerror code:\", so showing the response text there was probably\nunintentional.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D278779\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/satchel/integrations/FirefoxRelay.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "7d32de01aeed673509cb9964d45ee89ea3b94476", "git_parents": ["8cc0e83a5aafd7acf911d514f181235ac4f61f03"], "node": "dd9794882604a0d2ec964927720cee973fe4ab26", "parents": ["2d27eb5c9853a21eddfceaa7405ed01f06c0498c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069090 - Extend nova background under the sidebar. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,dao\n\nMuch like on non-nova.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323358\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_themes_dynamic_updates.js", "toolkit/modules/LightweightThemeConsumer.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "b2a4671da001c757295adfc1fcb559aa642bc164", "git_parents": ["7d32de01aeed673509cb9964d45ee89ea3b94476"], "node": "711a99f8d2432f64b3c9d78049a85c5d3aa0affa", "parents": ["dd9794882604a0d2ec964927720cee973fe4ab26"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Marco Castelluccio \u003cmcastelluccio@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1994717 - Avoid redundant filesystem metadata checks in FileFinder. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nUse os.scandir during recursive traversal so FileFinder can reuse entry\ntype and existence information instead of calling isdir and lexists for every path.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316271\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozpack/files.py", "python/mozbuild/mozpack/test/test_files.py", "toolkit/mozapps/installer/packager.py"], "git_node": "1f4361fa3f5a57cc4ff867f0eb648fefe37c6a36", "git_parents": ["b2a4671da001c757295adfc1fcb559aa642bc164"], "node": "e4b4dc5667ac245f185ac0e5297213c66b170712", "parents": ["711a99f8d2432f64b3c9d78049a85c5d3aa0affa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriele Svelto \u003cgsvelto@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068794 - Return proper thread IDs even when the crash reporter is disabled r=afranchuk\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323626\n", "files": ["toolkit/crashreporter/nsDummyExceptionHandler.cpp"], "git_node": "b126e53ae3a098d476dc837e7866d6b154be7ded", "git_parents": ["1f4361fa3f5a57cc4ff867f0eb648fefe37c6a36"], "node": "1edb3565204beace02a9b8c3400f346ee63472e6", "parents": ["e4b4dc5667ac245f185ac0e5297213c66b170712"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandre Poirot \u003cpoirot.alex@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064034 - [devtools] Improve handling of percent encoded URLs in Local Mode. r=devtools-reviewers,jdescottes\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319927\n", "files": ["devtools/shared/network-observer/NetworkLocalMode.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "952eb3bc0417b8826b3e198ff92fe0b6d0daa85f", "git_parents": ["b126e53ae3a098d476dc837e7866d6b154be7ded"], "node": "f8379eea940f12ced6a203c9193d393f3c8e5123", "parents": ["1edb3565204beace02a9b8c3400f346ee63472e6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069465 - Fix clang 23 unused warnings in js. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nMapMemoryAtFuzzy is only called on 64-bit, so guard it with JS_64BIT. The dump helper in\ntestCompileScript.cpp and StringFlagsForCharType in StringType.cpp have no callers, and xpcshell's\nreportWarnings flag has not been read in years; -W and -w are still accepted as no-ops.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323874\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/Memory.cpp", "js/src/jsapi-tests/testCompileScript.cpp", "js/src/vm/StringType.cpp", "js/xpconnect/src/XPCShellImpl.cpp"], "git_node": "554b03ecb461171865e5974dfda62c51124efb4f", "git_parents": ["952eb3bc0417b8826b3e198ff92fe0b6d0daa85f"], "node": "e5360383a487b4c64a8dcc52f0316834f28fcbed", "parents": ["f8379eea940f12ced6a203c9193d393f3c8e5123"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069468 - Fix clang 23 unused warnings in gfx. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nTestTreeTraversal.cpp's leftover microbenchmark helpers and WebGLFormats.cpp's FindPtrOrNull have no\ncallers. The BackgroundHangMonitor pointers in RenderThread.cpp and CanvasRenderThread.cpp are only stored\nto keep the monitors alive, and WebRenderCommandBuilder.cpp's sIndent is only read by disabled debug\noutput, so mark them maybe_unused.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323876\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGLFormats.cpp", "gfx/ipc/CanvasRenderThread.cpp", "gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderCommandBuilder.cpp", "gfx/tests/gtest/TestTreeTraversal.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderThread.cpp"], "git_node": "a4c95e23ba8395723c55469732010b0665dca37f", "git_parents": ["554b03ecb461171865e5974dfda62c51124efb4f"], "node": "7a0f77e7f6d0b00d7031d4937d6303c4ddbe4939", "parents": ["e5360383a487b4c64a8dcc52f0316834f28fcbed"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Calixte Denizet \u003ccalixte.denizet@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049760 - Display PDFs loaded from frame attributes in PDF.js. r=farre\n\nTreat unsandboxed PDF loads from frame attribute processing like object/embed loads. Link-targeted navigations, sandboxed frames, and attachments keep their existing handling.\n\nOnly the loads a frame element starts from its own attributes qualify, so a frame navigated by a link, a form or a script inside it keeps the configured handler. The new pdfjs.handleFrameAttributeLoads pref turns the frame part of this off, leaving object and embed elements alone.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320883\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/PdfStreamConverter.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/pdfjs.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/browser_pdfjs_frame_pdfs.js", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/file_pdfjs_attachment.sjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/file_pdfjs_frame_attachment.html", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/file_pdfjs_frame_attachment_cross_site.html", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/file_pdfjs_frame_sandboxed.html", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/file_pdfjs_frame_sandboxed_cross_site.html", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/file_pdfjs_frame_target.html", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/file_pdfjs_frame_target_cross_site.html", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/file_pdfjs_frames.html", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/file_pdfjs_frames_cross_site.html", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/file_pdfjs_frameset.html", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/file_pdfjs_frameset_cross_site.html", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/file_pdfjs_iframe_cross_site.html", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/test_pdf_file_in_object.html"], "git_node": "8fcb9765c065b0800a2bb6d3f66c21bd797261bd", "git_parents": ["a4c95e23ba8395723c55469732010b0665dca37f"], "node": "655f766cc9648b6822fb5f6714935c087ed87bdb", "parents": ["7a0f77e7f6d0b00d7031d4937d6303c4ddbe4939"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Calixte Denizet \u003ccalixte.denizet@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049760 - Show the fallback for PDFs loaded from frame attributes. r=farre,fluent-reviewers,flod\n\nWhen PDF.js is disabled, use the embedded-PDF fallback for these loads; its button retry still uses normal PDF handling. Constrain the parent-side retry to embedded browsing contexts whose embedder has an unprivileged principal.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320884\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/PdfEmbedFallbackParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/PdfEmbedFallbackStreamConverter.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/pdfjs.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/browser_pdfjs_embed_fallback.js", "toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/pdfviewer/embedFallback.ftl", "toolkit/modules/ActorManagerParent.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "8310e944a8fdb1dd0369a296a08bcc9d70c2f945", "git_parents": ["8fcb9765c065b0800a2bb6d3f66c21bd797261bd"], "node": "c7e779a5163afafb0ce031302ac41ad46472513e", "parents": ["655f766cc9648b6822fb5f6714935c087ed87bdb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gian-Carlo Pascutto \u003cgcp@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068960 - Accept the \"dek\" JSON key when reading Lockstore DEK metadata r=simonf,fiji\n\nBuilds between the Bug 2055631 clippy rename and its revert serialized\nWrappedDek with a \"dek\" key instead of \"wrapped_dek\". Profiles created\nwith those builds fail to load with a missing field `wrapped_dek` error.\n\nKeep writing \"wrapped_dek\" and add a serde alias so either key\ndeserializes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324056\n", "files": ["security/lockstore/lockstore_rs/src/keystore.rs"], "git_node": "397f37e023ff567626a5e213aa13504d73338924", "git_parents": ["8310e944a8fdb1dd0369a296a08bcc9d70c2f945"], "node": "ccca904b9cfae2d82c3fd3e39f427b7a9e26a7de", "parents": ["c7e779a5163afafb0ce031302ac41ad46472513e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matthew Tighe \u003cmatthewdtighe@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064818 - Synthesize text and play it with Exoplayer r=matt-tighe,android-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321110\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/.buildconfig.yml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/build.gradle", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/fakes/Listen.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/playback/AudioFileCache.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/playback/ListenPlayer.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/synthesis/SpeechSynthesizer.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ListenMiddlewareTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/playback/DirectoryAudioFileCacheTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/synthesis/AndroidTtsSpeechSynthesizerTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/Components.kt"], "git_node": "53a1d75a68c8f133a5a26ca21647569ac06af621", "git_parents": ["397f37e023ff567626a5e213aa13504d73338924"], "node": "d687d581be0e0d3ce8dabfdb8222f4fdf2ea8ea1", "parents": ["ccca904b9cfae2d82c3fd3e39f427b7a9e26a7de"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Moyin \u003cmadeyemi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064819 - Add the Media3 MediaSessionService so audio survives backgrounding r=android-reviewers,matt-tighe\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323549\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/build.gradle", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ListenAction.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ListenMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/fakes/Listen.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/playback/ListenMediaSessionService.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/playback/ListenPlaybackController.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/playback/ListenPlayer.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ListenMiddlewareTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/Components.kt"], "git_node": "d4204fef45f0c71d80b3b83d92c6bfb481d5334b", "git_parents": ["53a1d75a68c8f133a5a26ca21647569ac06af621"], "node": "ac5316913b38f945df0c56651e6c3c97d42bda98", "parents": ["d687d581be0e0d3ce8dabfdb8222f4fdf2ea8ea1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Moyin \u003cmadeyemi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064819 - Clean up listenToPage initialization in Components r=android-reviewers,matt-tighe\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323567\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/HomeActivity.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/BrowserFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/Components.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/FenixListenPageExtractor.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/listentopage/FenixListenPageExtractor.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/listentopage/ListenToPage.kt"], "git_node": "e62e40ec22bc275b47b28331b10e54deaaeca52a", "git_parents": ["d4204fef45f0c71d80b3b83d92c6bfb481d5334b"], "node": "f7517baa380bf8243733bd5fb5d8d9e6ee232f07", "parents": ["ac5316913b38f945df0c56651e6c3c97d42bda98"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sebastian Streich \u003csstreich@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068550 - Report the failing frames as the source of ipprotection.error r=ip-protection-reviewers,apopov\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323666\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/ipprotection/IPPProxyManager.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/tests/xpcshell/test_IPProxyManager.js"], "git_node": "079820a464dbf8c5f14fd802cc3af52ca10e8a85", "git_parents": ["e62e40ec22bc275b47b28331b10e54deaaeca52a"], "node": "4bc471d31414d6b9e40563742e8cdaa6e9d00cec", "parents": ["f7517baa380bf8243733bd5fb5d8d9e6ee232f07"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069291 - Keep popover open while new tab search bar is focused. r=mbeier\n\nShowing a modal dialog moves focus into it, which means the search bar will lose focus and leave the top layer before the dialog enters it, and so we don't regress bug 2068104.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323794\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-newtab/browser.toml", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-newtab/browser_selection.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-newtab/browser_topLayer.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-newtab/browser_undo_history.js"], "git_node": "3f71ea58f0293d33ecb034d32fb0321b58ccd0b7", "git_parents": ["079820a464dbf8c5f14fd802cc3af52ca10e8a85"], "node": "9dce63a49bf746f1e6b3b9e33428f40b57ab951d", "parents": ["4bc471d31414d6b9e40563742e8cdaa6e9d00cec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Calixte Denizet \u003ccalixte.denizet@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065133 - Give the download zone test a distinct target file per saver r=mak\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320115\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/downloads/test/unit/common_test_Download.js"], "git_node": "61c7b6d2fe5fc598e573df6528447ab48bc027b3", "git_parents": ["3f71ea58f0293d33ecb034d32fb0321b58ccd0b7"], "node": "dd1235e06ef73b4264f137c8ea6d36774936bf7c", "parents": ["9dce63a49bf746f1e6b3b9e33428f40b57ab951d"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788815272, "git_changesets": ["c169dc7e1c7e840dd3cc97f836870aecf0afa8eb", "57cf7b17dabc7377ad20a30d9a675ffd1facd49f", "9ba93b490778534bb60a9d5daaac0518f4d7584b", "88ebb3424b5768f42940c5bddee5b1a7647ef89e", "94975073e754a9c08f8bdf935210d58f65e9e5d0", "6bdec778209a8b99f417302a13d600edd7771e58", "f5018c1c0d72c08c0df4c0f052b0e28c5fd1a2a9", "5267448ad58340b83b2f4fcda1fcf2c26ae1b709", "8168fe2d5fc7fd2a020f29ef395cada361d50888", "53e2383aaa9a8299656e0c49d7de4c79c3a20438", "0e917dd6be707eb40a24af8524e8b4f17d2f10ff", "c6572663ab6263903664e0f45cedbd33d66f4865", "e3b48f29a630dcecf8defb3622ccdfc35c531110", "64be6beabb5ef2affc4d56136e25206683e57013", "ebfb27e51d66ceaf7d88a36d2f43499440b1ca77", "bae80389ba22439cbc58edba17913a6277c48522", "ab826d5ec06930c58f64169691687a577f91b7dd", "aba1e6b2507988f6411fd99d0588a11571894ee3", "de14c16b69efbc9bb89b17669a07500a5d0fa6d5", "28e5b605facd681679e0600c7fe591c78e1c0e70", "7b9f80d79a1ed6ba416fdc2b590387ffbd068a41", "cd74d48a9d187e36e2a5f924bae5a1987dfdca96", "37a5e73a3670500d8abc07e9bef2a2dfe94c74fe", "9360841b52061c17ef5621da600ff86dadbf517b", "5b146cdc4dbfb260518fa846d06a569f1b9b3848", "cee547537311591a159f806f6181cde82d4dcb81", "bc709a8704109c2282c80289c99a9e464c352016", "a58cff11691d8145d6d77009b6f61ab32f71a5e8", "9cbb8d10c69a8e43065153daeefbe561e16baa5f", "0d04e60d213ab1ae7e08facaa4ebcbb24923fa51", "71ff7f33abd8f42ebb8cc0010ae04ce434ff796d", "32431f8a82b4176d6be76dee446a7ee0b282b768", "8ca0e5032f6a2a6477226ac9e6d05a0c5c8f7ece", "7b1fd2649092caa19efd7c3e81e26c0684c90b05", "9135a449dc8bac360f29254c34dae2f5601144e7", "95e0f5f155369d77a4839d5b48a574b8e3d0fdc8", "8cc0e83a5aafd7acf911d514f181235ac4f61f03", "7d32de01aeed673509cb9964d45ee89ea3b94476", "b2a4671da001c757295adfc1fcb559aa642bc164", "1f4361fa3f5a57cc4ff867f0eb648fefe37c6a36", "b126e53ae3a098d476dc837e7866d6b154be7ded", "952eb3bc0417b8826b3e198ff92fe0b6d0daa85f", "554b03ecb461171865e5974dfda62c51124efb4f", "a4c95e23ba8395723c55469732010b0665dca37f", "8fcb9765c065b0800a2bb6d3f66c21bd797261bd", "8310e944a8fdb1dd0369a296a08bcc9d70c2f945", "397f37e023ff567626a5e213aa13504d73338924", "53a1d75a68c8f133a5a26ca21647569ac06af621", "d4204fef45f0c71d80b3b83d92c6bfb481d5334b", "e62e40ec22bc275b47b28331b10e54deaaeca52a", "079820a464dbf8c5f14fd802cc3af52ca10e8a85", "3f71ea58f0293d33ecb034d32fb0321b58ccd0b7", "61c7b6d2fe5fc598e573df6528447ab48bc027b3"], "user": "csabou@mozilla.com"}, "45271": {"changesets": [{"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065075 - Exempt the IPC I/O thread from the graph's tail dispatch track and port invariant. r=karlt\n\nipc::MessageChannel::PostErrorNotifyTask() and MessageTask::Post() dispatch to\nthe channel's worker thread from the IPC I/O thread. For an ipc::MessageChannel\nopened on the graph thread that worker thread is the graph, which the channel\nkeeps alive by refcount rather than through a main-thread track or port. The\nchannel is closed when the graph shuts down, necessarily after the main-thread\ntrack and port counts have reached zero, so the invariant asserted in\nTailDispatchMessage() cannot hold for it.\n\nExempt the IPC I/O thread there, as Dispatch() already does for the\ntail-dispatch requirement, and factor that check into OnIPCIOThread() so it\nalso tolerates ipc::IOThread::Get() being null before startup and after\nshutdown.\n\nNo behaviour change is needed below the assert: these runnables are cancelable,\nso the existing branch re-dispatches them to the main thread and discards them\nonce the graph no longer processes messages.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321163\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/TestAudioTrackGraph.cpp"], "git_node": "be3e60e99a9b4bc89c008c9e487af2fc7223e471", "git_parents": ["61c7b6d2fe5fc598e573df6528447ab48bc027b3"], "node": "e5b90b433838c62cf3058c067d908ef3ff1e33f3", "parents": ["dd1235e06ef73b4264f137c8ea6d36774936bf7c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2031458 - Stop rewriting cache2 entry files when nothing changed r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nBug 2049534 stopped frecency and lastFetched/fetchCount updates from arming the\nmetadata write timer, but two paths still rewrite an entry file on a read hit\nwhen nothing about the entry has changed. Each rewrite is pure IO and makes\non-access anti-malware software (Windows Defender) rescan the file.\n\n1. CacheFileMetadata::ParseMetadata() marked the freshly parsed metadata dirty\n   unconditionally. The in-memory metadata is an exact copy of what was just\n   read, so this made every load of an existing entry rewrite its whole metadata\n   block when the entry closed - a plain read-only hit on any entry that was not\n   already in the memory pool. It also bumped mLastModified, which made merely\n   reading an entry look like a modification to CacheFileContextEvictor and to\n   CacheIndex::UpdateIndex(). The only thing parsing actually changes is the\n   header version, which is upgraded in memory, so only mark dirty when the\n   on-disk version differs, and without touching mLastModified.\n\n   This is the missing half of bug 2049534: CacheFileMetadata::RestoreAccessStats()\n   already documents that read hits do not rewrite the entry file, but the\n   unconditional MarkDirty() defeated that as soon as the entry came off disk.\n\n2. CacheFileMetadata::SetElement() dirtied the metadata even when the element\n   already held that exact value. nsHttpChannel does precisely that on every\n   HTTPS cache hit: OpenCacheInputStream() reads security-info out of the entry,\n   ReadFromCache() adopts it, and CloseCacheEntry() stores it straight back.\n   Compare against the current value and return early - the key lookup was\n   already being done, so this only adds a strcmp - and only arm the metadata\n   write timer in CacheFile::SetElement() when the metadata actually became\n   dirty.\n\nAlso skip the security-info store-back in nsHttpChannel::CloseCacheEntry() when\nthe value is the one this entry itself handed us. Item 2 already keeps that off\nthe disk, but the call also re-serializes the whole certificate chain via\nnsITransportSecurityInfo::ToString() on every HTTPS cache hit. A 304 still gets\nits fresher info from the socket transport stored, so bug 1040086 is unaffected.\n\nCacheFile::OnMetadataRead() now marks the metadata dirty explicitly on the\ncorrupt-alt-data path; it truncates and invalidates the file, and previously\nrelied on the unconditional MarkDirty() removed in 1.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323968\n", "files": ["netwerk/cache2/CacheFile.cpp", "netwerk/cache2/CacheFileMetadata.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpChannel.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_cache2-44-no-rewrite-unchanged-metadata.js", "netwerk/test/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "0f473da98c4133d7aa593f2471204fab346a7a39", "git_parents": ["be3e60e99a9b4bc89c008c9e487af2fc7223e471"], "node": "0adcc7654d799733e4bab5d7781ae494ccf351b5", "parents": ["e5b90b433838c62cf3058c067d908ef3ff1e33f3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063577 - Measure discarded expired HTTP/3 Alt-Svc mappings r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nAdd a Glean timing_distribution recording how far past expiry a\ndiscarded HTTP/3 Alt-Svc mapping was, at the point AltSvcCache::LookupMapping\nremoves it for being expired.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323731\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/AlternateServices.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "dbc4ca2eff02ea81260564bb273e909ab15d035c", "git_parents": ["0f473da98c4133d7aa593f2471204fab346a7a39"], "node": "b734200bd4e028caf0b21f9461e14a962d7b7e05", "parents": ["0adcc7654d799733e4bab5d7781ae494ccf351b5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065319 - Retry HTTP/2 and HTTP/3 requests after an unclean session shutdown r=necko-reviewers,valentin,kershaw\n\nWhen an H2 or H3 session goes away without a clean GOAWAY-based shutdown\n(e.g. the server silently drops a pooled connection), streams that never\nreceived any response data were closed with NS_ERROR_ABORT, which is not\nretried. Chrome retries in this situation as long as the connection was\nreused and no response headers were received yet.\n\nIntroduce NS_ERROR_NET_UNCLEAN_SHUTDOWN for this case and treat it like\nNS_ERROR_NET_RESET in nsHttpTransaction::Close's stale-connection retry\nlogic, so the request is retried once on a new connection instead of\nfailing outright.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323730\n", "files": ["docshell/base/metrics.yaml", "docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp", "docshell/base/nsDocShellTelemetryUtils.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http2Session.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http3Session.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpTransaction.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_h2_unclean_shutdown_retry.js", "netwerk/test/unit/xpcshell.toml", "xpcom/base/ErrorList.py"], "git_node": "6c361a9eeee07bb9d991514f80fc8e70760f8fbe", "git_parents": ["dbc4ca2eff02ea81260564bb273e909ab15d035c"], "node": "abecb9aa2b12d7c1c52ff1ac3f556e833e265f01", "parents": ["b734200bd4e028caf0b21f9461e14a962d7b7e05"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2065075 - Exempt the IPC I/O thread from the graph's tail dispatch track and port invariant. r=karlt\" for causing Bpgo bustages failures at MediaTrackGraph.cpp\n\nThis reverts commit be3e60e99a9b4bc89c008c9e487af2fc7223e471.\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/TestAudioTrackGraph.cpp"], "git_node": "d67c1d8850d08c77e514b3bfb6e2a56c81b2d82a", "git_parents": ["6c361a9eeee07bb9d991514f80fc8e70760f8fbe"], "node": "2b7c5b272e62bc8ad807acf9df043df3702d534f", "parents": ["abecb9aa2b12d7c1c52ff1ac3f556e833e265f01"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2065319 - Retry HTTP/2 and HTTP/3 requests after an unclean session shutdown r=necko-reviewers,valentin,kershaw\" for causing python telemtry failures at testTelemetryMirrors\n\nThis reverts commit 6c361a9eeee07bb9d991514f80fc8e70760f8fbe.\n", "files": ["docshell/base/metrics.yaml", "docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp", "docshell/base/nsDocShellTelemetryUtils.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http2Session.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http3Session.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpTransaction.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_h2_unclean_shutdown_retry.js", "netwerk/test/unit/xpcshell.toml", "xpcom/base/ErrorList.py"], "git_node": "4d79fcae2b3b815991a84d96c81f219b61111148", "git_parents": ["d67c1d8850d08c77e514b3bfb6e2a56c81b2d82a"], "node": "8eb5c1f4bbfa3c76da2563e7ca15ef0a6d7b3c5b", "parents": ["2b7c5b272e62bc8ad807acf9df043df3702d534f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065041 - Replace the UrlbarQueryContext lifetime diagram image with an inline mermaid diagram. r=mak,urlbar-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320025\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/docs/assets/lifetime/lifetime.png", "browser/components/urlbar/docs/lifetime.md"], "git_node": "32f9213de56b77014a1e55d2844605a0e17d7b9b", "git_parents": ["4d79fcae2b3b815991a84d96c81f219b61111148"], "node": "ff81a71f48e2297ba86b5bb59c0f7b4571a32b0c", "parents": ["8eb5c1f4bbfa3c76da2563e7ca15ef0a6d7b3c5b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065041 - Fix stale links, the date stamp and a typo in the search lifecycle walkthrough. r=mak,urlbar-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320026\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/docs/lifetime.md"], "git_node": "dfb8e07d300555859e75ff6b09819d983170a237", "git_parents": ["32f9213de56b77014a1e55d2844605a0e17d7b9b"], "node": "148e807a90533424457dcc746afd96e81484f6d2", "parents": ["ff81a71f48e2297ba86b5bb59c0f7b4571a32b0c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065046 - Run beta and ESR tasks at autoland priority unless the push is shipping, r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nBeta and ESR tasks have been running at a higher priority than autoland to\noptimize shipping time for chemspill releases. For most uplifts this is not\nneeded, and it starves try and autoland of constrained resources, typically\nthe Mac worker pools.\n\nTreat beta and ESR as the integration branches they usually are, and only\nraise their priority when the commit message contains \"SHIPPING\", which\nrelease managers set through the Lando flag added in bug 2064629.\n\nAlso removes the mozilla-inbound entry, as that branch no longer exists.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320027\n", "files": ["taskcluster/config.yml", "taskcluster/docs/parameters.md", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/config.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/decision.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/parameters.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/test/test_transforms_task.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/task.py"], "git_node": "201aa0e5a1f59731d4229a2495689aca6b9f44a7", "git_parents": ["dfb8e07d300555859e75ff6b09819d983170a237"], "node": "76f454e6889ab345ed85850f78ea0fb9f82c2779", "parents": ["148e807a90533424457dcc746afd96e81484f6d2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069999: Remove Set-Cookie handling from the multipart/x-mixed-replace converter and de-XPCOM setCookieHeaders. r=cookie-reviewers,necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nThis is step 1 of the plan in comment 0 (\"remove multipart setHeaders call\").\n\n`nsMultiMixedConv::ProcessHeader()` handled `Set-Cookie` headers found in the\nindividual parts of a `multipart/x-mixed-replace` response by calling\n`nsIHttpChannelInternal::setCookieHeaders()` on the *outer* channel.\n\nThat code was already dead in every shipping configuration:\n`network.cookie.prevent_set_cookie_from_multipart` defaults to true, so the\ncall was never made. It was also the only consumer of `setCookieHeaders`\noutside `nsHttpChannel` itself.\n\nWhen enabled, it was wrong in two ways:\n\n - It bypassed the `CookieServiceParent::CookieProcessingGuard` /\n   `CookieObserver` wrapping that both `nsHttpChannel` call sites use, so the\n   resulting cookie changes were never propagated to the content process via\n   `HttpChannelParent::SetCookieChanges()`.\n\n - The converter also runs in content processes (image loads, see\n   `imgLoader::OnStartRequest`), where `SetCookieHeaders()` reaches\n   `CookieServiceChild::SetCookieStringFromHttp()` \u2014 a `MOZ_CRASH` stub.\n\nSo remove the multipart Set-Cookie handling together with its pref. `Set-Cookie`\nnow falls through the existing `HEADER_UNKNOWN` path, which skips unrecognized\npart headers.\n\nWith the converter gone, the only remaining callers of `setCookieHeaders` are\ninside `nsHttpChannel`, so it no longer needs to be on `nsIHttpChannelInternal`:\nit becomes a plain protected method on `HttpBaseChannel`. The two\n`NS_FORWARD_SAFE_NSIHTTPCHANNELINTERNAL` consumers (`nsViewSourceChannel`,\n`ObliviousHttpChannel`) need no change.\n\nNo web-platform-test depends on cookies being set from multipart parts.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324029\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpBaseChannel.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpBaseChannel.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsIHttpChannelInternal.idl", "netwerk/streamconv/converters/nsMultiMixedConv.cpp", "netwerk/streamconv/converters/nsMultiMixedConv.h", "netwerk/test/unit/test_multipart_set_cookie.js"], "git_node": "c00e13400254038be772a094a2d57b3c27dc8f59", "git_parents": ["201aa0e5a1f59731d4229a2495689aca6b9f44a7"], "node": "9f763a232d70b3c8b3ee06045d0964554d3cd287", "parents": ["76f454e6889ab345ed85850f78ea0fb9f82c2779"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Bumping Firefox l10n changesets r=release a=l10n-bump DONTBUILD CLOSED TREE\n\nach -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\naf -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\nan -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\nar -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\nast -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\naz -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\nbe -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\nbg -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\nbn -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\nbo -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9