3693e\npt-BR -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\npt-PT -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\nrm -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\nro -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\nru -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\nsk -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\nsl -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\nson -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\nsq -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\nsr -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\nsv-SE -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\nta -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\nte -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\nth -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\ntl -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\ntr -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\ntrs -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\nuk -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\nur -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\nuz -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\nvi -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\nwo -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\nxh -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\nzam -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\nzh-CN -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\nzh-TW -\u003e 44e2b3ab233d9c5626b2bc884266b283aeb3693e\n", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": "82584629a6005530e04c36773efebd9d583b3e0b", "git_parents": ["f7eb01d7f75e2dbbc86ba8eb1ead8d1b8f13e0be"], "node": "9ca3bc0e990f5d67856ac635e33968fbc450b1ae", "parents": ["2bb932420df6ff82f4b9803f81ca95faa5b72a81"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065075 - Exempt the IPC I/O thread from the graph's tail dispatch track and port invariant. r=karlt\n\nipc::MessageChannel::PostErrorNotifyTask() and MessageTask::Post() dispatch to\nthe channel's worker thread from the IPC I/O thread. For an ipc::MessageChannel\nopened on the graph thread that worker thread is the graph, which the channel\nkeeps alive by refcount rather than through a main-thread track or port. The\nchannel is closed when the graph shuts down, necessarily after the main-thread\ntrack and port counts have reached zero, so the invariant asserted in\nTailDispatchMessage() cannot hold for it.\n\nExempt the IPC I/O thread there, as Dispatch() already does for the\ntail-dispatch requirement, and factor that check into OnIPCIOThread() so it\nalso tolerates ipc::IOThread::Get() being null before startup and after\nshutdown.\n\nNo behaviour change is needed below the assert: these runnables are cancelable,\nso the existing branch re-dispatches them to the main thread and discards them\nonce the graph no longer processes messages.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321163\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/TestAudioTrackGraph.cpp"], "git_node": "6218c34e1f2238efc8ee7824af98be1708718744", "git_parents": ["82584629a6005530e04c36773efebd9d583b3e0b"], "node": "267114a5ba1039548500ef617370fcaa698e8555", "parents": ["9ca3bc0e990f5d67856ac635e33968fbc450b1ae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069823 [Wayland] Implement BufferSurface as an abstraction class for DMABufSurface r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\n\nMove general surface interface to BufferSurface. It's designed to allow to map surface as texture\nand blit/paint it to another surface with color properties.\n\nIt's going to be used for dmabuf/shm surfaces color conversions and blitting to HDR buffer.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324003\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/BufferSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/BufferSurface.h", "widget/gtk/DMABufSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/DMABufSurface.h"], "git_node": "0a4a8412e16b83022c210b6a707f5840c07d95b5", "git_parents": ["6218c34e1f2238efc8ee7824af98be1708718744"], "node": "8ac7e924348f23efe4611b10ff24086a0b50a59d", "parents": ["267114a5ba1039548500ef617370fcaa698e8555"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069823 [Wayland] Implement SHMBufSurface r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\n\nSHMBufSurface is DMABufSurface variant which uses shm memory.\nThe memory sharing/IPC transfer iself is not implemeneted as it's used\non top of existing SHM machinery to utilise existing code.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324004\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/SHMBufSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/SHMBufSurface.h"], "git_node": "b93015f9635cdf2d9d7e73c48d97bf8495aefe5f", "git_parents": ["0a4a8412e16b83022c210b6a707f5840c07d95b5"], "node": "0672746a6a935e4468d99a7b2eeb40cfb711cfd9", "parents": ["8ac7e924348f23efe4611b10ff24086a0b50a59d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069823 [Wayland] Update SW rendering path for SHMBufSurface r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\n\nImplement WaylandBufferSHM via. SHMBufSurface, remove WaylandShmPool and update related code.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324005\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/SurfacePoolWayland.cpp", "widget/gtk/WaylandBuffer.cpp", "widget/gtk/WaylandBuffer.h", "widget/gtk/WindowSurfaceWaylandMultiBuffer.cpp", "widget/gtk/moz.build"], "git_node": "2c35d87be32003bf705a88d3b194e3a01a2ed31c", "git_parents": ["b93015f9635cdf2d9d7e73c48d97bf8495aefe5f"], "node": "30f1f8e9068a4ec43aac6c746e8e13b406ef7be5", "parents": ["0672746a6a935e4468d99a7b2eeb40cfb711cfd9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Henrik Skupin \u003cmail@hskupin.info\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068563 - [taskcluster] Extend expiration of variant \"async-event-dispatching\" for webdriver tests. r=jgraham\n\nDONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324012\n", "files": ["taskcluster/test_configs/variants.yml"], "git_node": "bc4aca5f79763ab61b935a654f1f2936e3d44eeb", "git_parents": ["2c35d87be32003bf705a88d3b194e3a01a2ed31c"], "node": "31156de108565253efb8767c7eea7b03035691ae", "parents": ["30f1f8e9068a4ec43aac6c746e8e13b406ef7be5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Cosmin Sabou \u003ccsabou@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2069823 [Wayland] Update SW rendering path for SHMBufSurface r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\" for causing build bustages on SHMBufSurface.\n\nThis reverts commit 2c35d87be32003bf705a88d3b194e3a01a2ed31c.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2069823 [Wayland] Implement SHMBufSurface r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit b93015f9635cdf2d9d7e73c48d97bf8495aefe5f.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2069823 [Wayland] Implement BufferSurface as an abstraction class for DMABufSurface r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit 0a4a8412e16b83022c210b6a707f5840c07d95b5.\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/SurfacePoolWayland.cpp", "widget/gtk/BufferSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/BufferSurface.h", "widget/gtk/DMABufSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/DMABufSurface.h", "widget/gtk/SHMBufSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/SHMBufSurface.h", "widget/gtk/WaylandBuffer.cpp", "widget/gtk/WaylandBuffer.h", "widget/gtk/WindowSurfaceWaylandMultiBuffer.cpp", "widget/gtk/moz.build"], "git_node": "4bab639f1dd486bb14675b08893599a26d94abad", "git_parents": ["bc4aca5f79763ab61b935a654f1f2936e3d44eeb"], "node": "7fc6318824078b191246c0fb15e27fe17aef5113", "parents": ["31156de108565253efb8767c7eea7b03035691ae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoshi Cheng-Hao Huang \u003callstars.chh@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061782 - Use StableCellHasher for ObjectRealm::moduleScriptSources. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nmoduleScriptSources currently uses DefaultHasher, so when a compacting GC\nrelocates a ScriptSourceObject, lookup() can no longer find it. Fixed by using\nStableCellHasher instead.\n\nAlso check the table in GCRuntime::checkHashTablesAfterMovingGC so the\ninvariant is enforced on every compacting GC in debug builds.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323606\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/ModuleObject.cpp", "js/src/gc/GC.cpp", "js/src/jit-test/tests/debug/bug-2061782.js", "js/src/vm/Realm.cpp", "js/src/vm/Realm.h"], "git_node": "1f52c8e57fd4271e580440dc9bca11275420015f", "git_parents": ["4bab639f1dd486bb14675b08893599a26d94abad"], "node": "55e93644d3ab152c8fdec8e8a3d7f880b9fb53de", "parents": ["7fc6318824078b191246c0fb15e27fe17aef5113"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1985030 - Name the redirect target's scheme on the unknownProtocolFound error page. r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nWhen a server redirects to a protocol Firefox cannot handle (e.g. `Location: ftp://example.org`), the redirect target channel fails with NS_ERROR_UNKNOWN_PROTOCOL, but the channel that reaches nsDocShell::EndPageLoad is still the HTTP channel we were redirected away from. nsDocShell::DisplayLoadError therefore derives the scheme list for the `unknownProtocolFound` message from the HTTP URI, and the error page claims that *http* is the protocol which \"isn't associated with any program\".\n\nPrefer the redirect target when the failed channel carries a Location header pointing at a different scheme, so the message names the protocol we actually could not handle. Direct navigations to an unknown protocol are unaffected, since there is no redirect response on the channel.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323916\n", "files": ["docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp", "docshell/test/browser/browser.toml", "docshell/test/browser/browser_unknownProtocolFound_redirect.js", "docshell/test/browser/redirect_to_unknown_protocol.sjs"], "git_node": "8ac382cce3239b5cd610ab4c0464f6622dbefd07", "git_parents": ["1f52c8e57fd4271e580440dc9bca11275420015f"], "node": "67755ff0f21b5b22646d53729c32847677986e34", "parents": ["55e93644d3ab152c8fdec8e8a3d7f880b9fb53de"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069670 - Update double-conversion to f501091d. r=sergesanspaille\n\nPicks up upstream PR #312, which removes the BitSize helper template that clang 23 reports under\n-Wunused-template, along with the string-to-double parsing fixes since 3.3.0. The add-mfbt-api-markers and\nto-fixed-dbl-max patches are regenerated for upstream context changes; their content is unchanged.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323872\n", "files": ["mfbt/double-conversion/add-mfbt-api-markers.patch", "mfbt/double-conversion/double-conversion/README.md", "mfbt/double-conversion/double-conversion/bignum-dtoa.cc", "mfbt/double-conversion/double-conversion/bignum.cc", "mfbt/double-conversion/double-conversion/double-to-string.cc", "mfbt/double-conversion/double-conversion/double-to-string.h", "mfbt/double-conversion/double-conversion/string-to-double.cc", "mfbt/double-conversion/double-conversion/strtod.cc", "mfbt/double-conversion/moz.yaml", "mfbt/double-conversion/to-fixed-dbl-max.patch"], "git_node": "711b4fbdad9b47b470b8fc10a910437679d458f2", "git_parents": ["8ac382cce3239b5cd610ab4c0464f6622dbefd07"], "node": "e8db12a4ca63f8ea0f5110f5d3ae81ba4f29361c", "parents": ["67755ff0f21b5b22646d53729c32847677986e34"], "tags": []}, {"author": "akizu matsuo \u003cpettyblue@proton.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053212 - Don't clear the status bar just because the frame was reframed. r=smaug\n\nClearFrameRefs unconditionally cleared the status bar even if the\ncontent was still in the document (e.g. when a CSS change caused the\nframe to be reframed).\nInstead of clearing the status bar immediately, defer the check to after\nthe RefreshDriver tick.\n\nRegressed by: Bug 2023374\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310891\n", "files": ["dom/events/EventStateManager.cpp", "dom/events/EventStateManager.h"], "git_node": "a7705cde24365968ecdc39ca97606137d966da58", "git_parents": ["711b4fbdad9b47b470b8fc10a910437679d458f2"], "node": "c37b47aa3293466ad1055f5e113630f62a610d0c", "parents": ["e8db12a4ca63f8ea0f5110f5d3ae81ba4f29361c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069823 [Wayland] Implement BufferSurface as an abstraction class for DMABufSurface r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\n\nMove general surface interface to BufferSurface. It's designed to allow to map surface as texture\nand blit/paint it to another surface with color properties.\n\nIt's going to be used for dmabuf/shm surfaces color conversions and blitting to HDR buffer.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324003\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/BufferSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/BufferSurface.h", "widget/gtk/DMABufSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/DMABufSurface.h"], "git_node": "2dd7414d520b95b9e3c6e988f277c1c8cc1eddfa", "git_parents": ["a7705cde24365968ecdc39ca97606137d966da58"], "node": "53965517f8154ca4d58476fe79409c3868d442b1", "parents": ["c37b47aa3293466ad1055f5e113630f62a610d0c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069823 [Wayland] Implement SHMBufSurface r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\n\nSHMBufSurface is DMABufSurface variant which uses shm memory.\nThe memory sharing/IPC transfer iself is not implemeneted as it's used\non top of existing SHM machinery to utilise existing code.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324004\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/SHMBufSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/SHMBufSurface.h"], "git_node": "68e5f12fbdea6b9933199ece867268e0fd7b4f01", "git_parents": ["2dd7414d520b95b9e3c6e988f277c1c8cc1eddfa"], "node": "c3e349b17f3b0fe1b4d09950c815d6e6482beb9f", "parents": ["53965517f8154ca4d58476fe79409c3868d442b1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069823 [Wayland] Update SW rendering path for SHMBufSurface r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\n\nImplement WaylandBufferSHM via. SHMBufSurface, remove WaylandShmPool and update related code.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324005\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/SurfacePoolWayland.cpp", "widget/gtk/WaylandBuffer.cpp", "widget/gtk/WaylandBuffer.h", "widget/gtk/WindowSurfaceWaylandMultiBuffer.cpp", "widget/gtk/moz.build"], "git_node": "1b75dc7be8efdc7604c3e6bbf68f416eb90718c1", "git_parents": ["68e5f12fbdea6b9933199ece867268e0fd7b4f01"], "node": "cc7617e1901b0774e223a19203476b25b409d3e4", "parents": ["c3e349b17f3b0fe1b4d09950c815d6e6482beb9f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069823: apply code formatting via Lando\n\n# ignore-this-changeset\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/BufferSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/SHMBufSurface.cpp"], "git_node": "43c71046a26461509b3bd5b796b8024be2baf56c", "git_parents": ["1b75dc7be8efdc7604c3e6bbf68f416eb90718c1"], "node": "8f7b4be6287f4ae709d8de918b63da8f5bfefa0c", "parents": ["cc7617e1901b0774e223a19203476b25b409d3e4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069413 - Show the popover for the duration of the breakout extension. r=mbeier\n\nBug 2061633 reverted this along with the rest of Bug 2022527. The popover work below rests on the popover tracking the extension rather than the breakout, so restore that part.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320974\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-editing/browser_urlbar_contextmenu.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/searchbar/browser_searchbar_customizing_nobreakout.js"], "git_node": "722299f76e7163584e3052bd394bfffb4dc56b35", "git_parents": ["43c71046a26461509b3bd5b796b8024be2baf56c"], "node": "c664f852b486f93b4987145e331850eb98345b4f", "parents": ["8f7b4be6287f4ae709d8de918b63da8f5bfefa0c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069413 - Replace the breakout-extend attribute with :popover-open. r=daisuke,urlbar-reviewers\n\nFor a toolbar element the attribute was set and cleared exactly where the popover is shown and hidden, so the styles it gated are unchanged. An in-page one is a popover while focused (bug 2069291), so those styles take `[open]` there to stay tied to the view.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320873\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-UrlbarInput/browser_breakout_state.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-results/browser_retainedResultsOnFocus.js", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar.css", "browser/themes/windows/browser.css"], "git_node": "84ab68a98ffcc364581f176e9714dfde545c4900", "git_parents": ["722299f76e7163584e3052bd394bfffb4dc56b35"], "node": "d84aee4eb0fdf57a5b648d88cb709a2ec61c2f2a", "parents": ["c664f852b486f93b4987145e331850eb98345b4f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069413 - Remove the breakout attribute. r=daisuke,urlbar-reviewers\n\nThe popover and the container height the bar measures into its parent now carry the state the attribute mirrored. Stopping breakout hides the popover, so the bar leaves the top layer for a modal dialog or customize mode.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320882\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-UrlbarInput/browser_breakout_state.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-search/browser_add_search_engine.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/searchbar/browser_searchbar_customizing_nobreakout.js", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar.css", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/view-nova.css", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/view-proton.css"], "git_node": "8bf55ea5edae86acd423a4b3e0360c56c541ffd4", "git_parents": ["84ab68a98ffcc364581f176e9714dfde545c4900"], "node": "cb12860ca5ffefe985e16221436d33f84a876af6", "parents": ["d84aee4eb0fdf57a5b648d88cb709a2ec61c2f2a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069413 - Rename the breakout concept to popover (no functional change). r=daisuke,urlbar-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320891\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AIWindow.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarView.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-UrlbarInput/browser.toml", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-UrlbarInput/browser_breakout_state.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-UrlbarInput/browser_popover_state.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/searchbar/browser.toml", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/searchbar/browser_searchbar_customizing_nobreakout.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/searchbar/browser_searchbar_customizing_nopopover.js", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar.css"], "git_node": "575ba140a4041431c2c0f3ec4c2dcc4b6421f140", "git_parents": ["8bf55ea5edae86acd423a4b3e0360c56c541ffd4"], "node": "bc53cb70910b34a5fe2f926924212e756bcebeff", "parents": ["cb12860ca5ffefe985e16221436d33f84a876af6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2022527 - Put only the view in the popover, anchored to the input container. r=mbeier\n\nThe three bars' geometry is unchanged, measured across idle, focused and open, as is the open background's under Proton, where the input grows over the container's block padding and inline margins.\n\nThe joint background is now two boxes meeting at the input's border edge. Sampled beside the seam, the pair's shadow is identical to a single box.\n\nbrowser_searchbar_customizing_nopopover.js, the Smart Window reveal observer and the titlebar fade's top-layer case all go with the anchoring and the host's popover. The host takes `role=\"group\"` in place of the `grouping` that attribute supplied, and the input container turns presentational so the group holds the controls.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323911\n", "files": ["accessible/tests/browser/tree/browser_searchbar_new.js", "browser/base/content/navigator-toolbox.inc.xhtml", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarNewTabComponentRegistrant.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/NewtabSearchbarContentTestUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-UrlbarInput/browser_a11y.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-UrlbarInput/browser_popover_state.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-newtab/browser_topLayer.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-search/browser_add_search_engine.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/searchbar/browser.toml", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/searchbar/browser_searchbar_customizing_nopopover.js", "browser/themes/shared/browser-shared.css", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar.css", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/view-nova.css", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/view-proton.css", "browser/themes/windows/browser.css"], "git_node": "52844d3a0a96b2557f090f547fd5844000640660", "git_parents": ["575ba140a4041431c2c0f3ec4c2dcc4b6421f140"], "node": "0691e17381307873290e723e4ed4236eaffabd30", "parents": ["bc53cb70910b34a5fe2f926924212e756bcebeff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2022527 - Close the view for a window-modal dialog instead of suppressing the popover. r=mbeier\n\nThe bar used to be the popover itself, which could only be demoted and put back; now the popover is the view, so a modal dialog closes it like anything else does.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323918\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser.js", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs"], "git_node": "886236e576c6a5789fd9d79b4d05d054342d61f4", "git_parents": ["52844d3a0a96b2557f090f547fd5844000640660"], "node": "8a3e224512ec0cfd620ce2c8a7680e2a53d134f4", "parents": ["0691e17381307873290e723e4ed4236eaffabd30"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2022527 - Drop the open checks that popover-open already implies. r=mbeier\n\n`popover-open` is only ever set while the view is open, so `[open]` can't narrow a selector that already carries it, and the compact rule's `:not([open])` can never match.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323919\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/urlbar.css"], "git_node": "42d4adf4c3e256cccf68aca5407461f1a0be0bd6", "git_parents": ["886236e576c6a5789fd9d79b4d05d054342d61f4"], "node": "64083d73a227379dfdc0cfe5dfd529504530a02b", "parents": ["8a3e224512ec0cfd620ce2c8a7680e2a53d134f4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069367 - Preserve an input's undo history across value setters via a preserveundohistory attribute. r=emilio,mbeier\n\nThe XUL-parent heuristic goes away, so the findbar, searchbar and smartbar inputs take the attribute to keep the behavior they had. The searchbar's escape-to-revert calls editor.undoAll(), so it needs the value setters to be undoable, not just the history to survive.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324083\n", "files": ["browser/components/search/content/searchbar.js", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-editing/browser_undo_history.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-newtab/browser_undo_history.js", "dom/base/test/chrome/test_input_value_set_preserve_undo.xhtml", "dom/html/HTMLInputElement.cpp", "dom/html/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/html/test/test_input_value_set_preserve_undo.html", "editor/libeditor/tests/test_can_undo_after_setting_value.xhtml", "toolkit/content/tests/browser/browser_findbar.js", "toolkit/content/widgets/findbar.js", "xpcom/ds/StaticAtoms.py"], "git_node": "97002592a11d79e0df2f2516087bdf5ecff32a6d", "git_parents": ["42d4adf4c3e256cccf68aca5407461f1a0be0bd6"], "node": "15b6e6e206f240e31e8817a82461cb1ca1b78f7a", "parents": ["64083d73a227379dfdc0cfe5dfd529504530a02b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicholas Poon \u003cnpoon@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1980905 - Make Continue section on homepage display the most recent non homepage tab when homepage as new tab is enabled r=android-reviewers,gl\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322727\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ext/BrowserState.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ext/BrowserStateTest.kt"], "git_node": "934e0c7db194650224a96cd80dde133f44e6133f", "git_parents": ["97002592a11d79e0df2f2516087bdf5ecff32a6d"], "node": "635adee4418f3ea9d54c3d0fc81162cc705850af", "parents": ["15b6e6e206f240e31e8817a82461cb1ca1b78f7a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dale Harvey \u003cdale@arandomurl.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2047987 - Convert urlbar context menu to use panel-list. r=fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,urlbar-reviewers,hjones,daisuke,bolsson,dao\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310018\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/navigator-toolbox.inc.xhtml", "browser/base/content/utilityOverlay.js", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarPrefs.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarChildController.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarView.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-editing/browser_urlbar_contextmenu.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/browser.ftl", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/view-nova.css", "python/l10n/fluent_migrations/bug_2047987_container_panel_item_labels.py", "toolkit/content/tests/widgets/chrome.toml", "toolkit/content/tests/widgets/test_panel_list_contextmenu.html", "toolkit/content/tests/widgets/test_panel_list_submenu_click.html", "toolkit/content/widgets/panel-list/README.stories.md", "toolkit/content/widgets/panel-list/panel-item.css", "toolkit/content/widgets/panel-list/panel-item.tokens.css", "toolkit/content/widgets/panel-list/panel-item.tokens.json", "toolkit/content/widgets/panel-list/panel-list.mjs", "toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/global/contextual-identity.ftl", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/semantic-categories.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-figma-theme.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-table.mjs"], "git_node": "4dc7afe23eba14a2d802841a877ba1c49a5e4f1b", "git_parents": ["934e0c7db194650224a96cd80dde133f44e6133f"], "node": "25b94b90b342837545d7787f3c43af3a596fd6f5", "parents": ["635adee4418f3ea9d54c3d0fc81162cc705850af"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2069823: apply code formatting via Lando\" for causing gtests failures at BufferSurface.cpp\n\nThis reverts commit 43c71046a26461509b3bd5b796b8024be2baf56c.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2069823 [Wayland] Update SW rendering path for SHMBufSurface r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit 1b75dc7be8efdc7604c3e6bbf68f416eb90718c1.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2069823 [Wayland] Implement SHMBufSurface r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit 68e5f12fbdea6b9933199ece867268e0fd7b4f01.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2069823 [Wayland] Implement BufferSurface as an abstraction class for DMABufSurface r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit 2dd7414d520b95b9e3c6e988f277c1c8cc1eddfa.\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/SurfacePoolWayland.cpp", "widget/gtk/BufferSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/BufferSurface.h", "widget/gtk/DMABufSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/DMABufSurface.h", "widget/gtk/SHMBufSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/SHMBufSurface.h", "widget/gtk/WaylandBuffer.cpp", "widget/gtk/WaylandBuffer.h", "widget/gtk/WindowSurfaceWaylandMultiBuffer.cpp", "widget/gtk/moz.build"], "git_node": "e7950da792e2ec543f0a6077f341dff3c9d11dff", "git_parents": ["4dc7afe23eba14a2d802841a877ba1c49a5e4f1b"], "node": "fa05c0afc772e6e7a72c50d602fc763af3993a79", "parents": ["25b94b90b342837545d7787f3c43af3a596fd6f5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Import translations from https://github.com/mozilla-l10n/android-l10n CLOSED TREE\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-hi-rIN/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-lv/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/menu/src/main/res/values-hi-rIN/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/toolbar/src/main/res/values-hi-rIN/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/res/values-es/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/res/values-fi/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/res/values-hi-rIN/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/res/values-hu/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/res/values-pt-rBR/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/res/values-ug/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/res/values-zh-rCN/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/base/src/main/res/values-hi-rIN/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/browser-toolbar/src/main/res/values-hi-rIN/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/cfr/src/main/res/values-hi-rIN/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/addons/src/main/res/values-hi-rIN/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/addons/src/main/res/values-lv/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/app-links/src/main/res/values-hi-rIN/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/res/values-lv/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/res/values-zh-rCN/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-cy/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-de/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-es-rAR/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-es/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-fi/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-hu/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-in/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-lv/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-pl/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-pt-rBR/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-sl/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-tg/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-ug/strings.xml"], "git_node": "82452e37a2e4590ff421b06e5fd8584b813b6eb8", "git_parents": ["e7950da792e2ec543f0a6077f341dff3c9d11dff"], "node": "2691396896eb5bebaf2c4f722f74f23d0d156a14", "parents": ["fa05c0afc772e6e7a72c50d602fc763af3993a79"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nina Pypchenko \u003cnpypchenko@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066037 - Stocks widget drop down and menu not visible with HCM r=reemhamz\n\nNova has no ghost-selected text token, so in High Contrast Mode the Stocks\ndropdown and context menu buttons disappear while their menu is open and\nturn blue on hover. Paint the inner button with the plain hover and active\nbackgrounds instead of the ghost ones, so both stay white with a black icon,\nas widget/topic section context menus already do.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324162\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Stocks/_Stocks.scss"], "git_node": "6762e79efb6111d51bb58951c1ebdbac886526e7", "git_parents": ["82452e37a2e4590ff421b06e5fd8584b813b6eb8"], "node": "eea728e4f6f7ab1adb57a53019cec0d5bf8a22a5", "parents": ["2691396896eb5bebaf2c4f722f74f23d0d156a14"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788841299, "git_changesets": ["be3e60e99a9b4bc89c008c9e487af2fc7223e471", "0f473da98c4133d7aa593f2471204fab346a7a39", "dbc4ca2eff02ea81260564bb273e909ab15d035c", "6c361a9eeee07bb9d991514f80fc8e70760f8fbe", "d67c1d8850d08c77e514b3bfb6e2a56c81b2d82a", "4d79fcae2b3b815991a84d96c81f219b61111148", "32f9213de56b77014a1e55d2844605a0e17d7b9b", "dfb8e07d300555859e75ff6b09819d983170a237", "201aa0e5a1f59731d4229a2495689aca6b9f44a7", "c00e13400254038be772a094a2d57b3c27dc8f59", "f7eb01d7f75e2dbbc86ba8eb1ead8d1b8f13e0be", "82584629a6005530e04c36773efebd9d583b3e0b", "6218c34e1f2238efc8ee7824af98be1708718744", "0a4a8412e16b83022c210b6a707f5840c07d95b5", "b93015f9635cdf2d9d7e73c48d97bf8495aefe5f", "2c35d87be32003bf705a88d3b194e3a01a2ed31c", "bc4aca5f79763ab61b935a654f1f2936e3d44eeb", "4bab639f1dd486bb14675b08893599a26d94abad", "1f52c8e57fd4271e580440dc9bca11275420015f", "8ac382cce3239b5cd610ab4c0464f6622dbefd07", "711b4fbdad9b47b470b8fc10a910437679d458f2", "a7705cde24365968ecdc39ca97606137d966da58", "2dd7414d520b95b9e3c6e988f277c1c8cc1eddfa", "68e5f12fbdea6b9933199ece867268e0fd7b4f01", "1b75dc7be8efdc7604c3e6bbf68f416eb90718c1", "43c71046a26461509b3bd5b796b8024be2baf56c", "722299f76e7163584e3052bd394bfffb4dc56b35", "84ab68a98ffcc364581f176e9714dfde545c4900", "8bf55ea5edae86acd423a4b3e0360c56c541ffd4", "575ba140a4041431c2c0f3ec4c2dcc4b6421f140", "52844d3a0a96b2557f090f547fd5844000640660", "886236e576c6a5789fd9d79b4d05d054342d61f4", "42d4adf4c3e256cccf68aca5407461f1a0be0bd6", "97002592a11d79e0df2f2516087bdf5ecff32a6d", "934e0c7db194650224a96cd80dde133f44e6133f", "4dc7afe23eba14a2d802841a877ba1c49a5e4f1b", "e7950da792e2ec543f0a6077f341dff3c9d11dff", "82452e37a2e4590ff421b06e5fd8584b813b6eb8", "6762e79efb6111d51bb58951c1ebdbac886526e7"], "user": "asilaghi@mozilla.com"}, "45272": {"changesets": [{"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069190 - Check target feature flags enabling instruction sets actually work. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nThere's a gap between compiler support for those flags and them actually\nworking... with GCC. Because GCC produces assembly and calls GAS to\ngenerate the machine code, actual support for the corresponding\ninstructions depend on what GAS supports, and the GCC and GAS versions\nare not necessarily lined up properly for that.\n\nGCC does disable support at build time when it detects GAS doesn't\nsupport the flags at GCC build time, but the GAS used at GCC build time\nand Firefox build time can be different. And thus we can end up in a\nsituation where configure says we can use e.g. -mavxvnni, but the build fails\nbecause GAS doesn't understand the operands produced by GCC.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323541\n", "files": ["build/moz.configure/toolchain.configure"], "git_node": "da3f96042f3811cc5cfe3cac8b528c6b7d11f443", "git_parents": ["6762e79efb6111d51bb58951c1ebdbac886526e7"], "node": "740716cdb8dd6d10bf316eb7f297306879f01646", "parents": ["eea728e4f6f7ab1adb57a53019cec0d5bf8a22a5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069190 - Don't build neon i8mm code when the corresponding compiler flag is not supported. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323544\n", "files": ["js/src/intgemm/moz.build"], "git_node": "38922f5e93d53f2d1c8087fcad3bfd1e129b232d", "git_parents": ["da3f96042f3811cc5cfe3cac8b528c6b7d11f443"], "node": "7d97c162e9be5620803d33790616b14812693b41", "parents": ["740716cdb8dd6d10bf316eb7f297306879f01646"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069463 - Make the widget/android JNI helper templates inline to fix -Wunused-template with clang 23. r=geckoview-reviewers,m_kato\n\nclang 23.1.0 puts -Wunused-template under -Wall, which flags internal-linkage templates a\ntranslation unit never instantiates. NullHandle/NullWeakPtr in Natives.h are static templates in\na header, so every TU that includes it without a weak-pointer native class trips on NullWeakPtr;\nmake them inline like the rest of the header. The CallAttachNative overloads in nsWindow.cpp have\nhad no callers since bug 1651705, so remove them.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323873\n", "files": ["widget/android/jni/Natives.h", "widget/android/nsWindow.cpp"], "git_node": "8ca447d1f670534cde8a77dc4e01ca1d19efa1fd", "git_parents": ["38922f5e93d53f2d1c8087fcad3bfd1e129b232d"], "node": "5b147f3ec460bed6559a874e6447ffb9aae2d302", "parents": ["7d97c162e9be5620803d33790616b14812693b41"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069193 - Fix syntax error that slipped in through bug 2028605. r=fluent-reviewers,flod\n\nPython formatting has mistakenly stopped applying to many files since\nthe switch to ruff instead of black, and bug 2028605 introduced a syntax\nerror that wasn't caught because of it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323533\n", "files": ["python/l10n/fluent_migrations/bug_2028605_report_broken_site_design_refresh_migration.py"], "git_node": "50fe51e0f91cd566816639abd98b79797071529d", "git_parents": ["8ca447d1f670534cde8a77dc4e01ca1d19efa1fd"], "node": "77db3bac2a60db0bb80eac6036e0d22fe38996ea", "parents": ["5b147f3ec460bed6559a874e6447ffb9aae2d302"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069193 - Reformat Python files that lost `ruff-format` coverage. r=linter-reviewers,perftest-reviewers,geckoview-reviewers,devtools-reviewers,firefox-style-system-reviewers,layout-reviewers,whimboo,sergesanspaille,dshin,sparky,m_kato\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323534\n", "files": ["build/moz.configure/android-ndk.configure", "build/moz.configure/android-sdk.configure", "build/moz.configure/bindgen.configure", "build/moz.configure/clang_plugin.configure", "build/moz.configure/compile-checks.configure", "build/moz.configure/flags.configure", "build/moz.configure/init.configure", "build/moz.configure/keyfiles.configure", "build/moz.configure/lto-pgo.configure", "build/moz.configure/nss.configure", "build/moz.configure/rust.configure", "build/moz.configure/toolchain.configure", "build/moz.configure/update-programs.configure", "build/moz.configure/util.configure", "build/moz.configure/windows-toolchain.configure", "build/moz.configure/windows.configure", "devtools/shared/inspector/moz.build", "devtools/shared/webconsole/GenerateDataFromWebIdls.py", "dom/bindings/Codegen.py", "dom/bindings/parser/WebIDL.py", "js/moz.configure", "layout/base/tests/marionette/selection.py", "layout/style/GenerateCSSProperties.py", "layout/style/GeneratePseudoStyleTypeList.py", "layout/style/test/gtest/generate_example_stylesheet.py", "mobile/android/gradle.configure", "mobile/android/moz.configure", "python/l10n/fluent_migrations/bug_2020067_about_translations_message_bar_headings.py", "python/l10n/fluent_migrations/bug_2023050_newtab_customization_panel_wallpapers_toggle_label.py", "python/l10n/fluent_migrations/bug_2029225_send_tab_firefox_view.py", "python/l10n/fluent_migrations/bug_2031472_send_tab_menupopup.py", "python/l10n/fluent_migrations/bug_2031711_toolboxoptions.py", "python/l10n/fluent_migrations/bug_2032640_send_tab_account_menu.py", "python/l10n/fluent_migrations/bug_2034596_address_doorhanger_nova.py", "python/l10n/fluent_migrations/bug_2039292_menuitem_to_panellist.py", "python/l10n/fluent_migrations/bug_2049610_devtools_mdn_icon_tooltips.py", "python/l10n/fluent_migrations/bug_2064925_referrals_share_firefox.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/action/tooltool.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/configure/data/subprocess.configure", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/sign_app.py", "servo/components/style/gecko/regen_pseudo_elements.py", "servo/components/style/properties/build.py", "servo/components/style/properties/data.py", "testing/condprofile/condprof/android.py", "testing/condprofile/condprof/creator.py", "testing/condprofile/condprof/helpers.py", "testing/condprofile/condprof/runner.py", "testing/jsshell/benchmark.py", "testing/marionette/harness/marionette_harness/tests/harness_unit/test_marionette_runner.py", "testing/marionette/harness/marionette_harness/tests/unit/test_accessibility_properties.py", "testing/marionette/harness/marionette_harness/tests/unit/test_element_state.py", "testing/marionette/harness/marionette_harness/tests/unit/test_errors.py", "testing/marionette/harness/marionette_harness/tests/unit/test_execute_async_script.py", "testing/marionette/harness/marionette_harness/tests/unit/test_execute_isolate.py", "testing/marionette/harness/marionette_harness/tests/unit/test_execute_script.py", "testing/marionette/harness/marionette_harness/tests/unit/test_file_upload.py", "testing/marionette/harness/marionette_harness/tests/unit/test_findelement.py", "testing/marionette/harness/marionette_harness/tests/unit/test_get_shadow_root.py", "testing/marionette/harness/marionette_harness/tests/unit/test_marionette.py", "testing/marionette/harness/marionette_harness/tests/unit/test_prefs.py", "testing/marionette/harness/marionette_harness/tests/unit/test_profile_management.py", "testing/marionette/harness/marionette_harness/tests/unit/test_proxy.py", "testing/marionette/harness/marionette_harness/tests/unit/test_visibility.py", "testing/marionette/harness/marionette_harness/tests/unit/test_window_rect.py", "testing/marionette/mach_commands.py", "testing/mozharness/examples/silent_script.py", "testing/mozharness/external_tools/robustcheckout.py", "testing/parse_build_tests_ccov.py", "testing/tools/iceserver/iceserver.py", "toolkit/components/protobuf/moz.build", "toolkit/moz.configure", "toolkit/mozapps/dmgInstallHelper/moz.build", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/browser/moz.build", "toolkit/mozapps/installer/find-dupes.py", "toolkit/mozapps/installer/informulate.py", "toolkit/mozapps/installer/l10n-repack.py", "toolkit/mozapps/macos-frameworks/ChannelPrefs-localbuild/moz.build", "toolkit/mozapps/macos-frameworks/ChannelPrefs/moz.build", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/gtest/moz.build", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/moz.build", "toolkit/mozapps/update/updater/macos-frameworks/UpdateSettings-localbuild/moz.build", "toolkit/mozapps/update/updater/moz.build", "toolkit/mozapps/update/updater/updater-common.build"], "git_node": "38946f6f1f52073220fff3aa0d1e738720362c59", "git_parents": ["50fe51e0f91cd566816639abd98b79797071529d"], "node": "d153b2f93b6aa48f23c1903c3981e02f619e03b0", "parents": ["77db3bac2a60db0bb80eac6036e0d22fe38996ea"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069193 - Move the `ruff` check exclusions to `lint.exclude`. r=linter-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nThe `exclude` list in derives from the one bug 1811850 converted from\n`.flake8`. Its entries were added to suppress *lint* diagnostics, but\napplies equally to both `rust check` and `rust format`, and that is how\nmany files stopped being formatted when `ruff format` replaced `black`\nin bug 2006716.\n\nMove the list to `lint.exclude`, which only `ruff check` reads, leaving\nin `exclude` just the entries that have to prune the tree walk: two that\noverride ruff's built-in defaults (one of which is `build`, a real\nsource directory here), and testing/web-platform/tests.  ruff config.\n\n`lint.exclude` is matched as a glob against each file path rather than\npruned during directory traversal, so every directory in it has to be\nspelled `\u003cdir\u003e/**`; a bare `\u003cdir\u003e` silently matches nothing and lints\neverything underneath. That is easy to get wrong, so\ntest_ruff.py::test_pyproject_section_exclude_uses_directory_globs\nenforces it, for `format.exclude` too should one ever be added (spoiler\nalert, it will be).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323535\n", "files": ["pyproject.toml", "tools/lint/test/test_ruff.py"], "git_node": "1b47c105ed17299cde1ec38b72b10237001da6bd", "git_parents": ["38946f6f1f52073220fff3aa0d1e738720362c59"], "node": "a74755a74a6c6d27119b4cb1cd40f34d445dabc6", "parents": ["d153b2f93b6aa48f23c1903c3981e02f619e03b0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069193 - Let `ruff-format` discover `mozbuild` files. r=linter-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323536\n", "files": ["pyproject.toml"], "git_node": "5d2e35192de5a26ef6135ba12bdee2c18f29edd9", "git_parents": ["1b47c105ed17299cde1ec38b72b10237001da6bd"], "node": "702d86c1310415ce2bb6ce641ccbbc31b18b41ca", "parents": ["a74755a74a6c6d27119b4cb1cd40f34d445dabc6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069193 - Use `--extend-exclude` for `ruff format`. r=linter-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\n`ruff format --exclude` replaces the `exclude` list ruff read from\npyproject.toml instead of adding to it, so `format()` compensates by parsing\npyproject.toml itself and re-passing that list alongside mozlint's. `ruff\nformat` does accept `--extend-exclude`, even though it is missing from its\n`--help` output, and `lint()` right above has been using it all along. Use it\nhere too, and the compensation is no longer needed.\n\nThis is a simplification rather than a fix: the preceding patches work without\nit. What it does buy is one less way to get the exclusions wrong.\n`get_pyproject_excludes()` reads `\u003clintargs[\"root\"]\u003e/pyproject.toml`, so it\nsilently returns nothing whenever `root` is not topsrcdir, and then `--exclude`\ndrops ruff's own `exclude` with nothing put back in its place.\n\nThat is not hypothetical: it is why the ruff-format test fixtures have been\nformatted at all. tools/lint/test/conftest.py points `root` at the fixture\ndirectory, so the global `tools/lint/test/files` exclusion was being discarded\non every run of the linter's own tests. Give those fixtures the same empty\nruff.toml the ruff ones already have, and declare `ruff.toml` in the linter's\nsupport-files, since its output depends on them.\n\nNote, the lint() and format() methods could probably be merged in the\nfuture.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323537\n", "files": ["tools/lint/python/ruff.py", "tools/lint/ruff-format.yml", "tools/lint/test/files/ruff-format/ruff.toml"], "git_node": "2a30b9c557090cc9fbe52c73e1bf55ee5e014a71", "git_parents": ["5d2e35192de5a26ef6135ba12bdee2c18f29edd9"], "node": "3fac269f4afb1c616a100ca4e341bb4ad3a907af", "parents": ["702d86c1310415ce2bb6ce641ccbbc31b18b41ca"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069193 - Move the `ruff-format` exclusions to `format.exclude`. r=linter-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nUnlike the yaml list, which mozlint applied before invoking the formatter,\nthese are resolved by ruff against the project root, so they no longer depend\non the directory `mach lint` happens to be run from.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323538\n", "files": ["pyproject.toml", "tools/lint/ruff-format.yml"], "git_node": "5853e9e9f3439ec3d63560b687548ead73348c9e", "git_parents": ["2a30b9c557090cc9fbe52c73e1bf55ee5e014a71"], "node": "01c5a5e7ae8d74a0200903af6c8ef6874e51c4d9", "parents": ["3fac269f4afb1c616a100ca4e341bb4ad3a907af"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069175 - Upgrade gcc 11 toolchain to 11.5.0. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323440\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/fetch/toolchains.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/toolchain/gcc.yml"], "git_node": "07502aa2f678fcd1a52cbad65955bc46b7f3c9eb", "git_parents": ["5853e9e9f3439ec3d63560b687548ead73348c9e"], "node": "362f21b54e259b61a2b71f2204fb8b35e4b0cc92", "parents": ["01c5a5e7ae8d74a0200903af6c8ef6874e51c4d9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069248 - Make the GCC 11 toolchain work with older binutils. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323505\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/toolchain/gcc.yml"], "git_node": "314b2ec8a3073a28feda4397600d089d5f04a4b5", "git_parents": ["07502aa2f678fcd1a52cbad65955bc46b7f3c9eb"], "node": "28142406754f2b9e7d6336a2b68287c2becf339f", "parents": ["362f21b54e259b61a2b71f2204fb8b35e4b0cc92"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069187 - Add missing include. r=xpcom-reviewers,jstutte\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323452\n", "files": ["xpcom/threads/Queue.h"], "git_node": "9c45b5e4d54ebf792d76c5653609404aa4c9e124", "git_parents": ["314b2ec8a3073a28feda4397600d089d5f04a4b5"], "node": "2da894ac0ac3e30f4a1fddafea07f53e72fde81a", "parents": ["28142406754f2b9e7d6336a2b68287c2becf339f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069185 - Use constinit fallback with libstdc++ 11. r=sergesanspaille\n\nThe STL in libstdc++ 11 doesn't have constexpr initializers for base\ntypes yet. The existing test was also relying on a date, which is not\nmonotonically increasing across versions. Instead rely on specific\nindicators that specific types have a given constexpr support level,\nwhich also indirectly takes into account _GLIBCXX_USE_CXX11_ABI.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323450\n", "files": ["mfbt/Attributes.h", "tools/power/rapl.cpp"], "git_node": "e39ac366d37c4d6632fd5cc8fd0d8024ce2f2323", "git_parents": ["9c45b5e4d54ebf792d76c5653609404aa4c9e124"], "node": "6ad10d40706e074e26e3cce659f35acbd8fa5285", "parents": ["2da894ac0ac3e30f4a1fddafea07f53e72fde81a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069823 [Wayland] Implement BufferSurface as an abstraction class for DMABufSurface r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\n\nMove general surface interface to BufferSurface. It's designed to allow to map surface as texture\nand blit/paint it to another surface with color properties.\n\nIt's going to be used for dmabuf/shm surfaces color conversions and blitting to HDR buffer.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324003\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/BufferSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/BufferSurface.h", "widget/gtk/DMABufSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/DMABufSurface.h", "widget/tests/gtest/TestDMABufSurface.cpp"], "git_node": "7fad901712e8779c69fc36185289e28d287049cd", "git_parents": ["e39ac366d37c4d6632fd5cc8fd0d8024ce2f2323"], "node": "18fb6d6a9c2105ca5323c28ce908c076514716c1", "parents": ["6ad10d40706e074e26e3cce659f35acbd8fa5285"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069823 [Wayland] Implement SHMBufSurface r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\n\nSHMBufSurface is DMABufSurface variant which uses shm memory.\nThe memory sharing/IPC transfer iself is not implemeneted as it's used\non top of existing SHM machinery to utilise existing code.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324004\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/SHMBufSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/SHMBufSurface.h"], "git_node": "60390dbfa6ac46bc533c00874ee94cafee0e30e3", "git_parents": ["7fad901712e8779c69fc36185289e28d287049cd"], "node": "b660c2ae5ae160de1015d00d0717c496fae474bf", "parents": ["18fb6d6a9c2105ca5323c28ce908c076514716c1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069823 [Wayland] Update SW rendering path for SHMBufSurface r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\n\nImplement WaylandBufferSHM via. SHMBufSurface, remove WaylandShmPool and update related code.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324005\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/SurfacePoolWayland.cpp", "widget/gtk/WaylandBuffer.cpp", "widget/gtk/WaylandBuffer.h", "widget/gtk/WindowSurfaceWaylandMultiBuffer.cpp", "widget/gtk/moz.build"], "git_node": "8088a22281302fe6a1b9c01bee306c72aa98a09f", "git_parents": ["60390dbfa6ac46bc533c00874ee94cafee0e30e3"], "node": "8d719faa610e70edc9eb0909fccf0068575c7307", "parents": ["b660c2ae5ae160de1015d00d0717c496fae474bf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069823: apply code formatting via Lando\n\n# ignore-this-changeset\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/BufferSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/SHMBufSurface.cpp", "widget/tests/gtest/TestDMABufSurface.cpp"], "git_node": "30d8f4dc48fe817ca0384a8a9d8e15b9962fc276", "git_parents": ["8088a22281302fe6a1b9c01bee306c72aa98a09f"], "node": "79552ec2848769c3a82a30ac2b34fc37f74bdd44", "parents": ["8d719faa610e70edc9eb0909fccf0068575c7307"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2069823: apply code formatting via Lando\" for causing build bustages in TestDMABufSurface.cpp.\n\nThis reverts commit 30d8f4dc48fe817ca0384a8a9d8e15b9962fc276.\n\nThis reverts commit 8088a22281302fe6a1b9c01bee306c72aa98a09f.\n\nThis reverts commit 60390dbfa6ac46bc533c00874ee94cafee0e30e3.\n\nThis reverts commit 7fad901712e8779c69fc36185289e28d287049cd.\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/SurfacePoolWayland.cpp", "widget/gtk/BufferSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/BufferSurface.h", "widget/gtk/DMABufSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/DMABufSurface.h", "widget/gtk/SHMBufSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/SHMBufSurface.h", "widget/gtk/WaylandBuffer.cpp", "widget/gtk/WaylandBuffer.h", "widget/gtk/WindowSurfaceWaylandMultiBuffer.cpp", "widget/gtk/moz.build", "widget/tests/gtest/TestDMABufSurface.cpp"], "git_node": "41e3b8e1d7c53dfc6666f90236f22595c5031825", "git_parents": ["30d8f4dc48fe817ca0384a8a9d8e15b9962fc276"], "node": "e643d7519989a745e2ddcc948da0e2df883aeaa9", "parents": ["79552ec2848769c3a82a30ac2b34fc37f74bdd44"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Aaron Ma \u003cmapengyu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069569 - widget/gtk: Notify the IM context of fallback focus r=gtk-reviewers,stransky\n\nOn native Wayland, OnContainerFocusInEvent() may finish without the\nGecko focus manager selecting a child window. It then assigns the\ncontainer to gFocusWindow as a fallback but does not notify its\nIMContextWrapper.\n\nThis leaves mLastFocusedWindow null, so IME key events and context\nupdates are rejected with:\n\n    OnKeyEvent(), FAILED, the caller isn't focused window,\n    mLastFocusedWindow=0x0\n\nNotify the IM context when installing the fallback focus window.\n\nThis restores IME key handling on native Wayland while preserving the\nexisting checks that reject calls from a non-focused window.\n\nSigned-off-by: Aaron Ma \u003cmapengyu@gmail.com\u003e\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323826\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/nsWindow.cpp"], "git_node": "a79aa0b1825704689ab2dca4a8173c1e82eaff81", "git_parents": ["41e3b8e1d7c53dfc6666f90236f22595c5031825"], "node": "ab113694293aa7df210d689f4513b30096709ffc", "parents": ["e643d7519989a745e2ddcc948da0e2df883aeaa9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Farre \u003cfarre@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1922677 - Rate limit every navigation. r=smaug,zcorpan,firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D300744\n", "files": ["docshell/base/BrowsingContext.cpp", "docshell/base/BrowsingContext.h", "docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp", "docshell/base/nsDocShell.h", "docshell/base/nsIDocShell.idl", "docshell/test/navigation/mochitest.toml", "docshell/test/navigation/test_rate_limit_location_change.html", "docshell/test/navigation/test_rate_limit_same_document_navigation.html", "dom/base/Location.cpp", "dom/base/nsHistory.cpp", "dom/base/test/mochitest-bug1.toml", "dom/html/test/mochitest-bug1.toml", "dom/html/test/mochitest-bug2.toml", "dom/locales/en-US/chrome/dom/dom.properties", "dom/tests/mochitest/dom-level1-core/mochitest-node.toml", "dom/tests/mochitest/dom-level1-core/mochitest.toml", "dom/tests/mochitest/dom-level2-core/mochitest.toml", "dom/tests/mochitest/dom-level2-html/mochitest-element.toml", "dom/tests/mochitest/dom-level2-html/mochitest-form.toml", "dom/tests/mochitest/dom-level2-html/mochitest-table.toml", "dom/tests/mochitest/dom-level2-html/mochitest.toml", "editor/libeditor/tests/mochitest.toml", "layout/style/test/mochitest.toml", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "parser/htmlparser/tests/mochitest/mochitest.toml", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/navigating-across-documents/navigate_too_many_calls.optional.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/history/the-history-interface/history_go_too_many_calls.optional.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/history/the-history-interface/history_pushstate_too_many_calls.optional.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/history/the-history-interface/history_pushstate_too_many_calls_ordering.optional.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/history/the-history-interface/history_replacestate_too_many_calls.optional.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/history/the-history-interface/history_replacestate_too_many_calls_ordering.optional.html.ini"], "git_node": "3e4bb75e2b5fd78c1fd29b4ab7811d59c37a6135", "git_parents": ["a79aa0b1825704689ab2dca4a8173c1e82eaff81"], "node": "6a88d849626a4ff5517451009e36e2d54f46301e", "parents": ["ab113694293aa7df210d689f4513b30096709ffc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Gaul \u003candrew@gaul.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068844 - jit: allow a memory operand on the compare lhs for Ion int32 compares. r=jandem\n\nIon's int32 compare and test lowering forced the lhs into a register\neven though the rhs already had an any policy, so a spilled value\nreloaded just before a compare against a constant cost an extra\nMoveGroup load: movl -0x1c(%rbp), %ecx followed by cmpl $0x8, %ecx.\nGive LCompare, LCompareAndBranch and LTestIAndBranch an any policy on\nthe input when the other operand is a constant (or for the test, which\nhas no rhs), and teach the shared codegen to emit cmp32/branch32 with\nan Address lhs, so the register allocator can fold the spill slot into\nthe compare: cmpl $0x8, -0x1c(%rbp).\n\nThe rhs keeps its existing memory arm; the constant-rhs gate keeps the\ninstruction encodable, since one compare cannot take two memory\noperands. Other architectures are unaffected because useAny degrades\nto useRegister everywhere but x86/x64.\n\nMeasured with x86lint on an x86-64 JetStream 3 codegen corpus: all\n1,153 spill-reload load-foldable-into-compare findings are gone\n(2,710 to 1,896 overall; the remainder are loads produced by the\nvalue-defining LIR itself, which need load-compare fusion instead).\nOctane is neutral within noise on Zen 5.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323157\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/ion/compare-spilled-lhs.js", "js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp", "js/src/jit/Lowering.cpp"], "git_node": "df269845284d08822222afd1ccbbd2649cbffde8", "git_parents": ["3e4bb75e2b5fd78c1fd29b4ab7811d59c37a6135"], "node": "5eb602c6e60770ec2cbd0c82458a77c6ab57260a", "parents": ["6a88d849626a4ff5517451009e36e2d54f46301e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Gaul \u003candrew@gaul.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070045 - jit/arm64: load the saved stack pointer directly in callWithABIPost. r=jandem\n\nFor a dynamically-aligned ABI call, callWithABIPost restored the stack\npointer saved by setupUnalignedABICall via initPseudoStackPtr(),\nfreeStack(stackAdjust), and a load through the PSP:\n\n  mov x20, sp\n  add x20, x20, #stackAdjust   (when nonzero)\n  ldr x20, [x20]\n\nSP is authoritative at the call boundary, so the saved value can be\nloaded in one instruction as ldr x20, [sp, #stackAdjust], folding the\nPSP resync and the outgoing-argument pop into the load's base and\noffset. The freeStack bookkeeping moves to implicitPop. The non-dynamic\npath keeps the resync unchanged, and wasm never uses dynamic alignment\n(asserted in setupUnalignedABICall).\n\nEvery unaligned ABI call return emits this sequence, and it is the\nwhole 'ADD + LDR foldable to immediate-offset LDR' armlint category:\non a JetStream 3 run all 19,378 findings (Ion 12,340 / Baseline 5,326\n/ RegExp 1,532 / trampolines 180, in 53.5M JIT instructions) are this\nshape, with stackAdjust zero at every site. With the patch the\ncategory drops to a single straggler of a different shape, removing\nroughly 76 KB of JIT code per run. The removed instruction sits on the\nserialized sp-restore chain of every such return (mov -\u003e ldr -\u003e sync\nbecomes ldr -\u003e sync), but a 12-run interleaved Octane A/B of this\npatch alone was flat on an M4 (total-score medians within 0.2%), so\ntreat it as a code-size and instruction-count win.\n\nFound via armlint.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324171\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/arm64/MacroAssembler-arm64.cpp"], "git_node": "d16948e34bd33d6b68aac640ddd28e372afc029b", "git_parents": ["df269845284d08822222afd1ccbbd2649cbffde8"], "node": "75746e49dba2775701fa6cd788c4833d471e5396", "parents": ["5eb602c6e60770ec2cbd0c82458a77c6ab57260a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069823 [Wayland] Implement BufferSurface as an abstraction class for DMABufSurface r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\n\nMove general surface interface to BufferSurface. It's designed to allow to map surface as texture\nand blit/paint it to another surface with color properties.\n\nIt's going to be used for dmabuf/shm surfaces color conversions and blitting to HDR buffer.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324003\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/BufferSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/BufferSurface.h", "widget/gtk/DMABufSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/DMABufSurface.h", "widget/tests/gtest/TestDMABufSurface.cpp", "widget/tests/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "a5258a22c535329835428c7e93b296ed48a082a3", "git_parents": ["d16948e34bd33d6b68aac640ddd28e372afc029b"], "node": "25d900f1e736e9bfa7a3500c262c7c3d8bc4d7fa", "parents": ["75746e49dba2775701fa6cd788c4833d471e5396"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069823 [Wayland] Implement SHMBufSurface r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\n\nSHMBufSurface is DMABufSurface variant which uses shm memory.\nThe memory sharing/IPC transfer iself is not implemeneted as it's used\non top of existing SHM machinery to utilise existing code.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324004\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/SHMBufSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/SHMBufSurface.h"], "git_node": "078e31d2261ead78b05b306fdd48f0a5cc779c86", "git_parents": ["a5258a22c535329835428c7e93b296ed48a082a3"], "node": "c8752e2b2b616914f6ed02a9e9a5057616722e36", "parents": ["25d900f1e736e9bfa7a3500c262c7c3d8bc4d7fa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069823 [Wayland] Update SW rendering path for SHMBufSurface r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\n\nImplement WaylandBufferSHM via. SHMBufSurface, remove WaylandShmPool and update related code.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324005\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/SurfacePoolWayland.cpp", "widget/gtk/WaylandBuffer.cpp", "widget/gtk/WaylandBuffer.h", "widget/gtk/WindowSurfaceWaylandMultiBuffer.cpp", "widget/gtk/moz.build"], "git_node": "3b4c8650f988230db962bf6a1b4be124406310bd", "git_parents": ["078e31d2261ead78b05b306fdd48f0a5cc779c86"], "node": "69a14dd8ed8d2fcdbf8ca6b511d600f109ef8949", "parents": ["c8752e2b2b616914f6ed02a9e9a5057616722e36"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069823: apply code formatting via Lando\n\n# ignore-this-changeset\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/BufferSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/SHMBufSurface.cpp", "widget/tests/gtest/TestDMABufSurface.cpp"], "git_node": "12bbf0581f452742422de9899da6b8b2ca0c9314", "git_parents": ["3b4c8650f988230db962bf6a1b4be124406310bd"], "node": "c2b7420a5b763b8602d5e22425b84ac3a9fe84ba", "parents": ["69a14dd8ed8d2fcdbf8ca6b511d600f109ef8949"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Bumping Firefox l10n changesets r=release a=l10n-bump DONTBUILD CLOSED TREE\n\nach -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\naf -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\nan -\u003e 48d8f02