\nnb-NO -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\nne-NP -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\nnl -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\nnn-NO -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\noc -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\npa-IN -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\npl -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\npt-BR -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\npt-PT -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\nrm -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\nro -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\nru -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\nsk -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\nsl -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\nson -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\nsq -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\nsr -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\nsv-SE -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\nta -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\nte -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\nth -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\ntl -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\ntr -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\ntrs -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\nuk -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\nur -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\nuz -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\nvi -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\nwo -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\nxh -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\nzam -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\nzh-CN -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\nzh-TW -\u003e 48d8f02ef0196e62ec2c1994b7a0bd12ee787046\n", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": "d1387411980cc0d8f62de1c620e5e9d03434c09b", "git_parents": ["f096cac13bb54e760d4b27a48d857f064f8b8901"], "node": "7141d78150ad504bb7ff098473730b29c1733f0b", "parents": ["649810cc61312fc9773a4caccb8ec966f07bbaf1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gopalarathnam Venkatesan \u003cgopal@g13n.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2042434 - fix clippy warnings in security/manager/ssl/abridged_certs/src/cert_storage.rs r=sylvestre\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322377\n", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/abridged_certs/src/cert_storage.rs"], "git_node": "c0aa2a5f6f489729cde493e4a4e8ab4105e404bd", "git_parents": ["d1387411980cc0d8f62de1c620e5e9d03434c09b"], "node": "4f73825355bbfd2e0a3e3d37f4c13168ddc92712", "parents": ["7141d78150ad504bb7ff098473730b29c1733f0b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Magnus Melin \u003cmkmelin+mozilla@iki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069988 - Add a mozlint linter_paths lintarg for payloads outside the linter directory r=linter-reviewers,sylvestre\n\nBug 2069661 made findobject load a linter's payload module from the file next to\nits .yml rather than importing it by name. That assumes the definition and the\nmodule it names sit in the same directory, which does not hold for comm-central.\n\nTake a linter_paths lintarg, listing extra directories to search after the\ndefinition's own. A payload is still loaded from a known linter directory and\nnot from sys.path.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324197\n", "files": ["docs/code-quality/lint/create.md", "python/mozlint/mozlint/pathutils.py", "python/mozlint/mozlint/roller.py", "python/mozlint/mozlint/types.py", "python/mozlint/test/test_pathutils.py"], "git_node": "3381809b31e4c696b49993a02f5d0552c75fd041", "git_parents": ["c0aa2a5f6f489729cde493e4a4e8ab4105e404bd"], "node": "7d4bd0921e2580c24d1e69c591e0973f6773883f", "parents": ["4f73825355bbfd2e0a3e3d37f4c13168ddc92712"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056050 - Don't let logins storage prompt for the primary password on top of requestReauth()'s own prompt, r=credential-management-reviewers,joschmidt.\n\nrequestReauth() logs the internal key token out before prompting for the primary\npassword, so a logins-store operation racing with it needs the key too. Since the\nRust backend became the default in bug 2053724, getPrimaryPassword() then opens a\nsecond modal prompt on top of NSS's, and each spins its own nested event loop, so\ndismissing one leaves the caller stuck behind the other. That is what\nbrowser_osAuthDialog.js hangs on until the harness force-kills the browser, which\nis why the bug is annotated as ShutdownLeaks rather than as a timeout.\n\nThe existing Services.logins.uiBusy early return only guards the opposite order:\nthe Rust store has not started prompting yet when it runs. Decline instead --\nwhat the JSON backend has always done here, since NSS's own\nPK11PasswordPromptRunnable::mRunning bails the same way.\n\nDeclining is a workaround for re-auth relocking the token, so every piece of it\nis commented with bug 2067167 and greppable by that number: the counter, its\ngetter, the try/finally in requestReauth(), the check in getPrimaryPassword() and\nthe test assertions that stop meaning anything once it lands.\n\nDeclining also fails the racing store operation, so extract the NS_ERROR_ABORT\ntranslation getAllLogins and searchLoginsAsync already had into one helper and\napply it to the six store methods that were missing it. Without that, a declined\nwrite left LoginManagerPrompter.persistData rejecting on a raw Rust \"Encryption\nkey is missing\", i.e. a password the user asked to save was silently not saved.\nThat translation is not part of the workaround -- a user cancelling the prompt\nneeds it just as much -- so it carries no bug number.\n\nThis fixes the hang, not the whole intermittent: the test still fails at a lower\nrate on the assertion race it was originally filed for, which is bug 2067167.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321925\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/passwordmgr/LoginHelper.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/passwordmgr/storage-rust.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/passwordmgr/test/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/passwordmgr/test/browser/browser_primary_password_reauth.js"], "git_node": "0118bbbaac6597f4ab610f948d9fe6501a910659", "git_parents": ["3381809b31e4c696b49993a02f5d0552c75fd041"], "node": "8a8a2e17b40156895d43fe269483f503817f62fd", "parents": ["7d4bd0921e2580c24d1e69c591e0973f6773883f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 1922677 - Rate limit every navigation. r=smaug,zcorpan,firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\" for causing mochitests-plain failures in test_bug694754.xhtml.\n\nThis reverts commit 3e4bb75e2b5fd78c1fd29b4ab7811d59c37a6135.\n", "files": ["docshell/base/BrowsingContext.cpp", "docshell/base/BrowsingContext.h", "docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp", "docshell/base/nsDocShell.h", "docshell/base/nsIDocShell.idl", "docshell/test/navigation/mochitest.toml", "docshell/test/navigation/test_rate_limit_location_change.html", "docshell/test/navigation/test_rate_limit_same_document_navigation.html", "dom/base/Location.cpp", "dom/base/nsHistory.cpp", "dom/base/test/mochitest-bug1.toml", "dom/html/test/mochitest-bug1.toml", "dom/html/test/mochitest-bug2.toml", "dom/locales/en-US/chrome/dom/dom.properties", "dom/tests/mochitest/dom-level1-core/mochitest-node.toml", "dom/tests/mochitest/dom-level1-core/mochitest.toml", "dom/tests/mochitest/dom-level2-core/mochitest.toml", "dom/tests/mochitest/dom-level2-html/mochitest-element.toml", "dom/tests/mochitest/dom-level2-html/mochitest-form.toml", "dom/tests/mochitest/dom-level2-html/mochitest-table.toml", "dom/tests/mochitest/dom-level2-html/mochitest.toml", "editor/libeditor/tests/mochitest.toml", "layout/style/test/mochitest.toml", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "parser/htmlparser/tests/mochitest/mochitest.toml", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/navigating-across-documents/navigate_too_many_calls.optional.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/history/the-history-interface/history_go_too_many_calls.optional.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/history/the-history-interface/history_pushstate_too_many_calls.optional.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/history/the-history-interface/history_pushstate_too_many_calls_ordering.optional.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/history/the-history-interface/history_replacestate_too_many_calls.optional.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/history/the-history-interface/history_replacestate_too_many_calls_ordering.optional.html.ini"], "git_node": "8822ed9cff390183a7bed0c8edaea1d7c75919ae", "git_parents": ["0118bbbaac6597f4ab610f948d9fe6501a910659"], "node": "020816d8913a5831bb7ff7ee9019da717a6b5fc2", "parents": ["8a8a2e17b40156895d43fe269483f503817f62fd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069951 - Fix wrshell build. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nwrshell had its own standalone [workspace], so it didn't inherit the\ngleam patch declared in gfx/wr/Cargo.toml. That patch redirects gleam\nto a fork with draw_elements_instanced_base_instance, which webrender\nneeds. Without it, wrshell pulled plain gleam from crates.io and\nwebrender failed to build as a dependency.\n\nAdd wrshell as a member of the gfx/wr workspace instead of giving it\nits own workspace, so it picks up the same patches as wrench.\n\nAlso remove two DisplayItem match arms in wrshell for PopAllShadows\nand PushShadow, which no longer exist in webrender_api.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324087\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/Cargo.lock", "gfx/wr/Cargo.toml", "gfx/wr/wrshell/Cargo.lock", "gfx/wr/wrshell/Cargo.toml", "gfx/wr/wrshell/src/wrench.rs"], "git_node": "09d3233a7e8e76a4434cc3b81f7c86b7203eb2b0", "git_parents": ["8822ed9cff390183a7bed0c8edaea1d7c75919ae"], "node": "d0ff48a48d1f7a8b4c979c398e7d5a8df174e3f2", "parents": ["020816d8913a5831bb7ff7ee9019da717a6b5fc2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069951 - Build wrshell in the Linux debug WebRender CI job. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nwrshell is a workspace member but had no dedicated build step in CI,\nso compile breaks in it would go unnoticed until someone built it\nlocally. Build it alongside webrender, wrench and examples in\nlinux-debug-tests.sh, which runs as part of the linux64-debug\nWebRender CI job (WR(wrench) debug) on every push that touches\ngfx/wr/**.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324088\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/ci-scripts/linux-debug-tests.sh"], "git_node": "161ecf4e3985f4d8afe9e3e556847591c02c5d71", "git_parents": ["09d3233a7e8e76a4434cc3b81f7c86b7203eb2b0"], "node": "6c3f173f6399f74cb41b84de9c173eac2be548ea", "parents": ["d0ff48a48d1f7a8b4c979c398e7d5a8df174e3f2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "R\u00e9mi Papilli\u00e9 \u003crpapillie@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069956 - Improve reporting of GLSL compile errors. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nThe current reporting of GLSL errors dumps the whole shader blob annotated with\nline numbers plus the actual error. While functional, this adds friction to shader\ndevelopment and prevents other tools from working correctly with it (IDEs, most notably).\n\nThis patch implements a simple source map for shaders, allowing the correct remapping\nof errors to the input source files and line numbers.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324095\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "gfx/wr/Cargo.lock", "gfx/wr/webrender/build.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/gl.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/tests/angle_shader_validation.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_build/Cargo.toml", "gfx/wr/webrender_build/src/shader.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/test_shaders.rs"], "git_node": "747d088b0ec850f94fd868730c0baccf194555b3", "git_parents": ["161ecf4e3985f4d8afe9e3e556847591c02c5d71"], "node": "b73d97c47ba98710a46c6acd12b7b41dd42e528c", "parents": ["6c3f173f6399f74cb41b84de9c173eac2be548ea"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Geoff Lankow \u003cgeoff@darktrojan.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070025 - Stop Thunderbird trying to access CustomizableUI.sys.mjs from DevTools. r=devtools-reviewers,ochameau\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324163\n", "files": ["devtools/startup/DevToolsStartup.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "64af51f66132dd0a8ec894564e21af47d9d7d2e6", "git_parents": ["747d088b0ec850f94fd868730c0baccf194555b3"], "node": "12cf29b5c1a3d78ade1e2c44f566f4e7f5047aa5", "parents": ["b73d97c47ba98710a46c6acd12b7b41dd42e528c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068585 - Get rid of collections.OrderedDict r=ahochheiden,firefox-build-system-reviewers\n\ndict is ordered since 3.6\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322946\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/action/fat_aar.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/artifact_commands.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/configenvironment.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/codecoverage/lcov_rewriter.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/compilation/database.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/configure/__init__.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/configure/constants.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/configure/options.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/controller/building.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/frontend/context.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/frontend/data.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/frontend/emitter.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/frontend/reader.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_containers.py", "python/mozbuild/mozpack/chrome/flags.py", "python/mozbuild/mozpack/copier.py", "python/mozbuild/mozpack/files.py", "python/mozbuild/mozpack/mozjar.py", "python/mozbuild/mozpack/test/test_mozjar.py", "python/mozbuild/mozpack/unify.py"], "git_node": "df44e7a55d65c554d5e9354be16f64a075c04f87", "git_parents": ["64af51f66132dd0a8ec894564e21af47d9d7d2e6"], "node": "1bca07c0d396fb8c9e729f235719fd390abba47f", "parents": ["12cf29b5c1a3d78ade1e2c44f566f4e7f5047aa5"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788882013, "git_changesets": ["da3f96042f3811cc5cfe3cac8b528c6b7d11f443", "38922f5e93d53f2d1c8087fcad3bfd1e129b232d", "8ca447d1f670534cde8a77dc4e01ca1d19efa1fd", "50fe51e0f91cd566816639abd98b79797071529d", "38946f6f1f52073220fff3aa0d1e738720362c59", "1b47c105ed17299cde1ec38b72b10237001da6bd", "5d2e35192de5a26ef6135ba12bdee2c18f29edd9", "2a30b9c557090cc9fbe52c73e1bf55ee5e014a71", "5853e9e9f3439ec3d63560b687548ead73348c9e", "07502aa2f678fcd1a52cbad65955bc46b7f3c9eb", "314b2ec8a3073a28feda4397600d089d5f04a4b5", "9c45b5e4d54ebf792d76c5653609404aa4c9e124", "e39ac366d37c4d6632fd5cc8fd0d8024ce2f2323", "7fad901712e8779c69fc36185289e28d287049cd", "60390dbfa6ac46bc533c00874ee94cafee0e30e3", "8088a22281302fe6a1b9c01bee306c72aa98a09f", "30d8f4dc48fe817ca0384a8a9d8e15b9962fc276", "41e3b8e1d7c53dfc6666f90236f22595c5031825", "a79aa0b1825704689ab2dca4a8173c1e82eaff81", "3e4bb75e2b5fd78c1fd29b4ab7811d59c37a6135", "df269845284d08822222afd1ccbbd2649cbffde8", "d16948e34bd33d6b68aac640ddd28e372afc029b", "a5258a22c535329835428c7e93b296ed48a082a3", "078e31d2261ead78b05b306fdd48f0a5cc779c86", "3b4c8650f988230db962bf6a1b4be124406310bd", "12bbf0581f452742422de9899da6b8b2ca0c9314", "f096cac13bb54e760d4b27a48d857f064f8b8901", "d1387411980cc0d8f62de1c620e5e9d03434c09b", "c0aa2a5f6f489729cde493e4a4e8ab4105e404bd", "3381809b31e4c696b49993a02f5d0552c75fd041", "0118bbbaac6597f4ab610f948d9fe6501a910659", "8822ed9cff390183a7bed0c8edaea1d7c75919ae", "09d3233a7e8e76a4434cc3b81f7c86b7203eb2b0", "161ecf4e3985f4d8afe9e3e556847591c02c5d71", "747d088b0ec850f94fd868730c0baccf194555b3", "64af51f66132dd0a8ec894564e21af47d9d7d2e6", "df44e7a55d65c554d5e9354be16f64a075c04f87"], "user": "amarc@mozilla.com"}, "45273": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 3b49a44994fb7ff6902f7df5a3bd5f689a4fb4e9 with FIREFOX_153_3_0esr_BUILD1 a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "5d01b41b531d7d26c79cdc408f4faa383caab924", "git_parents": ["3bf8c40c86a15419b3e56feec6823903da8ecd58"], "node": "7f4efbc453788d5efe70b8d76b9f7391c6ad1883", "parents": ["103f8c26fe098e3a3295951d034e62057653d7fe"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788893583, "git_changesets": ["5d01b41b531d7d26c79cdc408f4faa383caab924"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45274": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging af3b068ff4548a6d6818a7aca8d03f432e50b296 with FIREFOX_115_41_0esr_BUILD1 a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "ee1f48209df890f93a2b8dffe2366f8e39aa9995", "git_parents": ["5d01b41b531d7d26c79cdc408f4faa383caab924"], "node": "fc219d06babd5ba90562b6322cdbed8bc038e06b", "parents": ["7f4efbc453788d5efe70b8d76b9f7391c6ad1883"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788894562, "git_changesets": ["ee1f48209df890f93a2b8dffe2366f8e39aa9995"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45275": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging d864999404b3032f682d74ccc60d1ce38c9ce609 with FIREFOX_140_16_0esr_BUILD1 a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "f098aef4c97c1668ff4a0b905d476080ae4155c5", "git_parents": ["ee1f48209df890f93a2b8dffe2366f8e39aa9995"], "node": "6af5d3cadd3539586005cab84edd374df7c673af", "parents": ["fc219d06babd5ba90562b6322cdbed8bc038e06b"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788898265, "git_changesets": ["f098aef4c97c1668ff4a0b905d476080ae4155c5"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45276": {"changesets": [{"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069198 - Give event extras their declared types in the generated TypeScript declarations. r=janerik\n\nThe typelib is regenerated output.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323463\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/glean/build_scripts/glean_parser_ext/typescript.py", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.glean.d.ts"], "git_node": "b4e75b7a59d5dc2f561bbd5b96202e7560e309e5", "git_parents": ["df44e7a55d65c554d5e9354be16f64a075c04f87"], "node": "043f07f27b6010c9527c5cfc221b888780a902f3", "parents": ["1bca07c0d396fb8c9e729f235719fd390abba47f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069199 - Declare the two browser element properties the tabbrowser sets. r=nsharpley\n\nDeclaring the fields without initializers keeps them undefined, which browser_tab_sharing_state.js asserts.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323464\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/widgets/browser-custom-element.mjs"], "git_node": "b3cd4bc9bb2bbcecfbd9c8fcd527e0b648fbc3bc", "git_parents": ["b4e75b7a59d5dc2f561bbd5b96202e7560e309e5"], "node": "dbc72c66f44d6136581195743dfb22dd1bcc8f41", "parents": ["043f07f27b6010c9527c5cfc221b888780a902f3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069199 - Drop the isDistinctProductPageVisit carry-over, dead since the Review Checker's removal. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,nsharpley\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323465\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "d2fe2790eb82896daaa602dd6169a224ae052bbf", "git_parents": ["b3cd4bc9bb2bbcecfbd9c8fcd527e0b648fbc3bc"], "node": "fcad88e0a91dd25c6e665300fdf72d81431e2fb9", "parents": ["dbc72c66f44d6136581195743dfb22dd1bcc8f41"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069199 - Say which element the dropped-link handler is called on. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,nsharpley\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323466\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "e0a5a0d1ff56faf6147bf791a9cf1b14dd1c9265", "git_parents": ["d2fe2790eb82896daaa602dd6169a224ae052bbf"], "node": "91d71afdde99ba1e42c18523bbaa4c42f00cd6cf", "parents": ["fcad88e0a91dd25c6e665300fdf72d81431e2fb9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069200 - Move the tab strip's shared prefs to a static prefs object. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,nsharpley\n\nNothing outside browser/components/tabbrowser read either pref off the instance.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323467\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/drag-and-drop.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tab-context-menu.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tab-hover-preview.mjs"], "git_node": "b0eec7d4b57b7d11a3eb7d813056e409694d0cd5", "git_parents": ["e0a5a0d1ff56faf6147bf791a9cf1b14dd1c9265"], "node": "0a0acbacd7620d5032321152f7702ce4fcb4936d", "parents": ["91d71afdde99ba1e42c18523bbaa4c42f00cd6cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069199 - Type-check the tabbrowser class. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,nsharpley\n\nThe class is only at zero with bug 2069198's generated extra types.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323468\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/tsconfig.json"], "git_node": "f48426778632b8df1326dc0bc601e7215cbd6294", "git_parents": ["b0eec7d4b57b7d11a3eb7d813056e409694d0cd5"], "node": "546c0b5ed4cfb9039fd8f9756df6d04bdcf105f4", "parents": ["0a0acbacd7620d5032321152f7702ce4fcb4936d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Mehic \u003cdmehic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1610809 - Test clearing the disk cache by origin and base domain through the context evictor r=necko-reviewers,jesup\n\nClearing the cache for an origin or a base domain is served by two separate\npaths: CacheFileIOManager::EvictByContextInternal() dooms the entries that\nstill have an active handle, and CacheFileContextEvictor::EvictEntries() walks\nthe index and filters the rest. test_cache2-32 and -33 only reach the first\npath, because their entries are still in the memory pools when the clear\nhappens, so the filtering in the evictor - where bug 1591362's inverted origin\ncomparison lived - has no coverage.\n\nRestarting the cache in-process leaves the entries on disk with no active\nhandles, so a clear is then served entirely by the context evictor. The base\ndomain test also covers matching by partitionKey, which the evictor gained\nlater in bug 1863250.\n\nReintroducing the inverted comparison makes both tests fail with the original\nsymptom: the entries of the cleared origin survive and the unrelated ones are\ndeleted.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317304\n", "files": ["netwerk/test/unit/head_cache2.js", "netwerk/test/unit/test_cache2-44-clear-origin-context-evictor.js", "netwerk/test/unit/test_cache2-45-clear-base-domain-context-evictor.js", "netwerk/test/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "6be095170bdcf6a1985958e48ac85447ea1e2c88", "git_parents": ["f48426778632b8df1326dc0bc601e7215cbd6294"], "node": "d3981c8ef409952e819a898d413b4e7868ff80e7", "parents": ["546c0b5ed4cfb9039fd8f9756df6d04bdcf105f4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Chevobbe \u003cnchevobbe@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068162 - [devtools] Remove unnecessary margin on .ruleview-reveal-panel. r=jdescottes,devtools-reviewers.\n\nBecause this removes some space, we need to adjust the outline offset for the\ncls panel input, otherwise it would looked clipped.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324027\n", "files": ["devtools/client/themes/rules.css"], "git_node": "047a12f190ac7cf798c8c7250a447810c6a9b4f7", "git_parents": ["6be095170bdcf6a1985958e48ac85447ea1e2c88"], "node": "e4a3b2a204caf22092bae912b3b8ac124ca20e5c", "parents": ["d3981c8ef409952e819a898d413b4e7868ff80e7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "delan azabani \u003cdazabani@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068830 - Element array getters reflect host even if reference target is invalid. r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nper discussion in [webcomponents#1114], make the getters for `FrozenArray\u003cElement\u003e?`-typed IDL attributes reflect the host element regardless of whether the reference target is valid. this improves shadow DOM encapsulation, and makes getters more consistent with setters.\n\nthis is covered by updates to [html#10995], and fixes 1350 of the subtest regressions in [wpt#60283].\n\n[webcomponents#1114]: \u003chttps://github.com/WICG/webcomponents/issues/1114\u003e\n[html#10995]: \u003chttps://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/10995\u003e\n[wpt#60283]: \u003chttps://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/60283\u003e\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323151\n", "files": ["dom/base/Element.cpp", "dom/base/Element.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/shadow-dom/reference-target/tentative/property-reflection-idl-setters.html.ini"], "git_node": "ba997ad41b1bf496f74951d119118d10354989e4", "git_parents": ["047a12f190ac7cf798c8c7250a447810c6a9b4f7"], "node": "240e0014f34a3a62eeb6abc2543a7432191590fd", "parents": ["e4a3b2a204caf22092bae912b3b8ac124ca20e5c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070008 - Don't ignore XUL window position on GTK. r=stransky\n\nThis ifdef has been there basically since forever (bug 49802). But\nsession-restore will just call moveTo anyways as appropriate, and we\nhaven't seen major issues with that, so we should probably be fine.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324127\n", "files": ["xpfe/appshell/AppWindow.cpp", "xpfe/appshell/test/chrome.toml", "xpfe/appshell/test/test_bug2070008_independent_window_position.xhtml", "xpfe/appshell/test/window_bug2070008.xhtml"], "git_node": "7fb2bbfc8936daa710d438b2420cb3fd262861db", "git_parents": ["ba997ad41b1bf496f74951d119118d10354989e4"], "node": "323f148b04cf49058f6e5eee47aaf1f7bd1585e4", "parents": ["240e0014f34a3a62eeb6abc2543a7432191590fd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Calixte Denizet \u003ccalixte.denizet@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069995 - Wait until the short embedded PDF fallback is hidden. r=marco\n\nThe fallback load event can fire before its viewport is updated to the embed size. Wait for its computed display to become \"none\" rather than checking immediately.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324243\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/browser_pdfjs_embed_fallback.js"], "git_node": "f7410bb9aa21c073d4d14542c24dcef488cbd668", "git_parents": ["7fb2bbfc8936daa710d438b2420cb3fd262861db"], "node": "b305fa8cbc5c297b2c9f26f7786f4f907956ede4", "parents": ["323f148b04cf49058f6e5eee47aaf1f7bd1585e4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Corentin Bect \u003ccbect@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069211 - Discard onboarding cards that have an unexpected type r=android-reviewers,twhite\n\n`card-type` used to default to `default-browser` in `onboarding.fml.yaml`. When a configuration has a card type that can't be resolved, Nimbus builds a new card with the default value (`default-browser`). So a configuration still referring one of the card types removed in Bug 2060802 would add an extra card with the default browser type.\n\nThe `HorizontalPager` in `OnboardingScreen` keys each page by card type. So those extra cards with the same `default-browser` type makes Jetpack Compose compose the same key multiple times, which lead to a crash (Key \"DEFAULT_BROWSER\" was already used).\n\nThis patch makes `card-type` optional with a null default value. Cards without a type are discarded when mapping them to pages. So a misconfigured card is hidden instead of being treated as another type of card.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323634\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/onboarding.fml.yaml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/onboarding/view/OnboardingMapperTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/onboarding/OnboardingFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/onboarding/view/OnboardingMapper.kt"], "git_node": "0ac379c00d830a7514b0dba483eb968e56c4a6e5", "git_parents": ["f7410bb9aa21c073d4d14542c24dcef488cbd668"], "node": "47820ce120a48bc29e524a1caf206c6be674001c", "parents": ["b305fa8cbc5c297b2c9f26f7786f4f907956ede4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068585 - Get rid of collections.OrderedDict r=xpcom-reviewers,mccr8\n\ndict is ordered since 3.6\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322947\n", "files": ["xpcom/base/ErrorList.py", "xpcom/reflect/xptinfo/xptcodegen.py"], "git_node": "122a2634c3f51ead2e53dae32d360511be3fa036", "git_parents": ["0ac379c00d830a7514b0dba483eb968e56c4a6e5"], "node": "f89491cc1134e758841f1985b6a1d6bfbd8b2291", "parents": ["47820ce120a48bc29e524a1caf206c6be674001c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070015 - Fix an off-by-one in double-conversion's ToFixed DBL_MAX digit count. r=sergesanspaille\n\nDBL_MAX has 309 integer digits, not 308, so ToFixed(DBL_MAX, 100) overflows the stack buffer our\nto-fixed-dbl-max.patch sizes from kMaxFixedDigitsBeforePoint. Reachable via mozilla::Smprintf.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324152\n", "files": ["mfbt/double-conversion/double-conversion/double-to-string.h", "mfbt/double-conversion/to-fixed-dbl-max.patch", "mozglue/tests/TestPrintf.cpp"], "git_node": "741855c2f006c5fd56d192f12c39f2368f49b5ed", "git_parents": ["122a2634c3f51ead2e53dae32d360511be3fa036"], "node": "0c14e3b596cb1f2d8f810b8589a722d846fcfb48", "parents": ["f89491cc1134e758841f1985b6a1d6bfbd8b2291"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Marco Castelluccio \u003cmcastelluccio@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1994717 - Don't re-walk the tree multiple times (once per extension), but only once. r=linter-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nWith the eslint extensions, on my local machine the execution time improves by more than 8x from 37.1 to 4.5 seconds.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316243\n", "files": ["python/mozlint/mozlint/pathutils.py"], "git_node": "f6f09a42564853c8f01c3282410d403a2ab9f039", "git_parents": ["741855c2f006c5fd56d192f12c39f2368f49b5ed"], "node": "ac0a5a398c81f5d2caed4ee2691f9cdb8e4655bf", "parents": ["0c14e3b596cb1f2d8f810b8589a722d846fcfb48"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070085 - Update android nightly application-services version bump to e1f6fe836d1df033e1fda13a0f3face77e9247c0 r=release-managers,pascalc\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324198\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/plugins/dependencies/src/main/java/ApplicationServices.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/plugins/dependencies/src/main/java/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "c1710959a70365ea470fcbe0b8ecae9804b658a2", "git_parents": ["f6f09a42564853c8f01c3282410d403a2ab9f039"], "node": "ed693519186ab5eb8629a0a9d0327eb6a25cd16a", "parents": ["ac0a5a398c81f5d2caed4ee2691f9cdb8e4655bf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "lilly \u003c173393835+cupidsity@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065723 [wpt PR 62123] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322215, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export: corner-shape: square and notch corners are built as round and scoop on outlines and box-shadow spread (#62123)\n\nhttps://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322215\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a2dc05da185270baf676cfbd1c440949d270f9ac\nwpt-pr: 62123\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-bevel-round-scoop-square-outset-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-bevel-round-scoop-square-outset.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-notch-squircle-outset-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-notch-squircle-outset.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-superellipse-concave-outset-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-superellipse-concave-outset.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-superellipse-convex-outset-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-superellipse-convex-outset.html"], "git_node": "81dd06483101bddd2b1d9a4c3144b5a4a21b0bc4", "git_parents": ["c1710959a70365ea470fcbe0b8ecae9804b658a2"], "node": "5ee442575493baec79086d4c2ef74626296756a8", "parents": ["ed693519186ab5eb8629a0a9d0327eb6a25cd16a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brandon Walderman \u003cbrwalder@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065717 [wpt PR 62119] - [css-mixins] Give each effective MixinMap a unique identity, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-mixins] Give each effective MixinMap a unique identity\n\n@apply is flattened into the RuleSet built for a stylesheet, so a\nRuleSet is only valid for the exact set of mixins it was flattened\nagainst. That set is per tree scope, but StyleSheetContents caches a\nsingle RuleSet and is shared between tree scopes (inline \u003cstyle\u003e text\ncache, adopted stylesheets) and between Documents (the parsed stylesheet\ncache on CSSStyleSheetResource). A RuleSet therefore records the\nidentity of the mixin map it was built against; see\nRuleSet::DependingOnOutdatedMixins().\n\nThat identity used to be a counter owned by StyleSheetCollection, so two\nscopes could hand out the same value for different sets of mixins and\nreuse each other's flattened RuleSet, leaving the winning mixin\ndependent on which scope built its RuleSet first. It is now allocated by\nMixinMap::AllocateMapIdentifier(), unique across every scope and\nDocument on the renderer main thread, and renamed from \"generation\" to\n\"map_identifier\" to reflect that it is an opaque identity.\n\nThis also fixes a second bug: RuleSet recorded a dependency on the mixin\nmap only when an @apply resolved to a mixin, so a RuleSet flattened\nwhere the mixin is undefined looked mixin-independent and leaked into\nscopes that do define it. The identity is now recorded for every @apply,\nand AddRulesFromSheet() no longer clears it, as it recurses for @import.\n\nBug: 496807669\nTest: external/wpt/css/css-mixins/mixins/mixin-shadow-dom.html\nTest: external/wpt/css/css-mixins/mixins/mixin-shared-across-documents.html\nChange-Id: Id4ad99b6bbd717a82a86ba3b98cdb27b6b2be4c3\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8252237\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Brandon Walderman \u003cbrwalder@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1684976}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: bc957dbac9045c22fdd0fa61d0608a55f63f6c3c\nwpt-pr: 62119\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-mixins/mixins/mixin-shadow-dom.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-mixins/mixins/mixin-shared-across-documents.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-mixins/mixins/mixin-shared-sheet-no-mixins-in-scope.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-mixins/mixins/support/mixin-shared-across-documents-frame.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-mixins/mixins/support/mixin-shared-across-documents.css", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-mixins/mixins/support/mixin-shared-across-documents.css.headers"], "git_node": "98eca5517cc31237c758388df196176a9c30c1e7", "git_parents": ["81dd06483101bddd2b1d9a4c3144b5a4a21b0bc4"], "node": "063857a9016bd189ecf50087981f7c427c9cb70c", "parents": ["5ee442575493baec79086d4c2ef74626296756a8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065717 [wpt PR 62119] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62119\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-mixins/mixins/mixin-shadow-dom.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-mixins/mixins/mixin-shared-across-documents.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-mixins/mixins/mixin-shared-sheet-no-mixins-in-scope.html.ini"], "git_node": "a762b4361b42d5a9307920ba06e96e038afb7b69", "git_parents": ["98eca5517cc31237c758388df196176a9c30c1e7"], "node": "6d9a90b39f6fcc743ecfe68babb37cd10710a18e", "parents": ["063857a9016bd189ecf50087981f7c427c9cb70c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067911 [wpt PR 62264] - Fix \u003clink\u003e stylesheet cascade and refetch with moveBefore, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix \u003clink\u003e stylesheet cascade and refetch with moveBefore\n\nThis fixes two bugs during state-preserving atomic moves on \u003clink\u003e\nelements, one where we weren't invaliding the stylesheet properly and\nanother where we were incorrectly re-fetching the resource.\n\nThe first bug is during RemovedFrom - we need to update the cascade\norder via RemoveStyleSheetCandidateNode.\n\nThe refetch bug initiates in InsertedInto, where we need to early-exit\nin LinkStyle::Process to avoid re-fetching.\n\nThis adds two WPT's that both pass in Gecko and fail in Blink without\nthis change.\n\nstylesheet-cascade-order.html fails with:\n\nThis is a testharness.js-based test. [FAIL] Moving loaded link\nstylesheets updates their cascade order\n  assert_equals: removing the purple stylesheet makes blue win again expected \"rgb(0, 0, 255)\" but got \"rgb(0, 0, 0)\"\n\nstylesheet-no-refetch.html fails with: [FAIL] Moving a loaded link\nstylesheet preserves its resource\n  assert_equals: moving the stylesheet does not fetch it again expected 1 but got 2\n\nHarness: the test ran to completion.\nChange-Id: Ie94630259a09fd6d4ae84e4b3b1be152c8158222\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8236492\nReviewed-by: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688119}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4bb4984b67940cde4c18bbeb9d2b2cd54eb6b3df\nwpt-pr: 62264\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/moveBefore/resources/stylesheet-cascade-blue.css", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/moveBefore/resources/stylesheet-cascade-blue.css.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/moveBefore/resources/stylesheet-cascade-purple.css", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/moveBefore/resources/stylesheet-cascade-purple.css.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/moveBefore/stylesheet-cascade-order.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/moveBefore/stylesheet-no-refetch.html"], "git_node": "62c213616c0d20f86b61d0e9dd97615bdbe46d97", "git_parents": ["a762b4361b42d5a9307920ba06e96e038afb7b69"], "node": "8b583baca71eefb65487b2339505d9f2d59a5115", "parents": ["6d9a90b39f6fcc743ecfe68babb37cd10710a18e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Joanne Pan \u003c71951015+J0pan@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067917 [wpt PR 62288] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319919, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319919 (#62288)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: fb24b8bbf32ce4dffb00bc79e4a5e1f386b2d373\nwpt-pr: 62288\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-values/random-item-computed.html"], "git_node": "bc8068e4bbddffc560a4b8b36ba59420e6103369", "git_parents": ["62c213616c0d20f86b61d0e9dd97615bdbe46d97"], "node": "e812d2b978dd2b6f0bc326ee11c5f9cc51ac2cd0", "parents": ["8b583baca71eefb65487b2339505d9f2d59a5115"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067917 [wpt PR 62288] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62288\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-values/animations/scale-interpolation-crash.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-values/random-item-computed.html.ini"], "git_node": "c89be7caed3e9a4245a3939efb3e825a0ffcea43", "git_parents": ["bc8068e4bbddffc560a4b8b36ba59420e6103369"], "node": "0e098801d9e11247db07867978ce6e82e1c54c1c", "parents": ["e812d2b978dd2b6f0bc326ee11c5f9cc51ac2cd0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066904 [wpt PR 62222] - Avoid cyclic insertion in adoption agency, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAvoid cyclic insertion in adoption agency\n\nCyclic insertion can happen due to iframe pagehide, when the iframe\nis removed during the adoption agency algorithm.\n\nSeparate the removal from the insertion, and check for cyclic\nreferences *after* the removal.\n\nSee https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10194\nand https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12708\n\nBug: 547963403\nChange-Id: Ib37ca63359ecfc9f8bce86a69be6eada62d8abb7\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8261279\nCommit-Queue: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688198}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e07b5f38