Lauro Moura \u003clmoura@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066974 [wpt PR 62227] - [wdspec] Add tests on releasing actions with modifiers, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[wdspec] Add tests on releasing actions with modifiers (#62227)\n\n* [wdspec] Add tests on releasing actions with modifiers\n\nAdd an extra test for both bidi and classic with a modifier in the\nmiddle of the sequence to be released, to check whether the input cancel\nlist is treating both regular keys and modifiers in reversed order.\n\n* Fixing whitespace between tests\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 2cd714381f58fce90855c5ab88db06f364c3af73\nwpt-pr: 62227\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/input/release_actions/sequence.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/classic/release_actions/sequence.py"], "git_node": "4d61770d67be32afdf0b13012fec30896e3b4179", "git_parents": ["e9b54a2fc1a93cfe8c1750c054a4dd158ad14f12"], "node": "8d64b290a3eaa91f58f3bd67742d22393c699a25", "parents": ["d2be5f2e5291f6925bafd057b095b5bcd6dccec2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066974 [wpt PR 62227] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62227\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/input/release_actions/context.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/input/release_actions/invalid.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/input/release_actions/queue.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/release_actions/release.py.ini"], "git_node": "4bcfae61f122a74ce23c6e699b487feed860b10b", "git_parents": ["4d61770d67be32afdf0b13012fec30896e3b4179"], "node": "85895c2bb2a675a5ec12fb21f4caa54a89f81be0", "parents": ["8d64b290a3eaa91f58f3bd67742d22393c699a25"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Antti Koivisto \u003cantti@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067673 [wpt PR 62308] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321592, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321592 (#62308)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: fc50769c3f2c3cd3b1c7723467b199fdcf0616d9\nwpt-pr: 62308\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-mixins/functions/dashed-function-cycles.html"], "git_node": "5e3d4a87b9cfd9688f8afecbb6d8e4ff63ddb2ce", "git_parents": ["4bcfae61f122a74ce23c6e699b487feed860b10b"], "node": "32c9dca423ec9c1b6b599ed77187f7dbbb2123d5", "parents": ["85895c2bb2a675a5ec12fb21f4caa54a89f81be0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067673 [wpt PR 62308] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62308\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-mixins/functions/dashed-function-cycles.html.ini"], "git_node": "74f91a3b2e412d629d37f38e70f6bc58b6e94cb1", "git_parents": ["5e3d4a87b9cfd9688f8afecbb6d8e4ff63ddb2ce"], "node": "966ffc997be2abfdd97cbb4f56600e8f324fef2c", "parents": ["32c9dca423ec9c1b6b599ed77187f7dbbb2123d5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064831 [wpt PR 62062] - sanitizer-api: Add edge case tests for javascript URIs, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nsanitizer-api: Add edge case tests for javascript URIs (#62062)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9656d33f73b9d5b92265702641b6bc5f1b9f4c4d\nwpt-pr: 62062\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-javascript-url.html"], "git_node": "87d2df361610f83330dbcfe10689446fa817736e", "git_parents": ["74f91a3b2e412d629d37f38e70f6bc58b6e94cb1"], "node": "3db802e44bf90290772d1c11f5a9f1a2f088ca15", "parents": ["966ffc997be2abfdd97cbb4f56600e8f324fef2c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Antti Koivisto \u003cantti@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067676 [wpt PR 62309] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321585, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321585 (#62309)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 995f066702483c390022650fd91dfed1f871f7bd\nwpt-pr: 62309\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-mixins/functions/function-parameter-types.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-mixins/functions/local-if-substitution.html"], "git_node": "16bc9e289c4243081f5a7f5c756db638a7c62231", "git_parents": ["87d2df361610f83330dbcfe10689446fa817736e"], "node": "f820460ce3e67a3e2c8f630ec74eaba1abc62e33", "parents": ["3db802e44bf90290772d1c11f5a9f1a2f088ca15"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067676 [wpt PR 62309] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62309\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-mixins/functions/function-parameter-types.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-mixins/functions/local-if-substitution.html.ini"], "git_node": "522cc3a4a2406b1de940a5e615bbb5fbc30bcbfb", "git_parents": ["16bc9e289c4243081f5a7f5c756db638a7c62231"], "node": "8cff7f0e3f8d8bc4675fd6ce39f1eac4497dbd3b", "parents": ["f820460ce3e67a3e2c8f630ec74eaba1abc62e33"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003c52317531+Ahmad-S792@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067856 [wpt PR 62299] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=291164, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=291164 (#62299)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7e755825e0b5c6f631cb862afd5fc451e6825441\nwpt-pr: 62299\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-contain/content-visibility/content-visibility-hidden-and-float-inside-skipped-subtree-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-contain/content-visibility/content-visibility-hidden-and-float-inside-skipped-subtree.html"], "git_node": "b28f68b5df3e877a86951dbb4337d4a35b49d8c7", "git_parents": ["522cc3a4a2406b1de940a5e615bbb5fbc30bcbfb"], "node": "8b37ad0fbc6a01be10d755c4f887f6355b9cc083", "parents": ["8cff7f0e3f8d8bc4675fd6ce39f1eac4497dbd3b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067856 [wpt PR 62299] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62299\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-contain/content-visibility/content-visibility-with-top-layer-in-auto-subtree-removal.html.ini"], "git_node": "b8fe2922ca90b190380c304ea06d29a345fbca76", "git_parents": ["b28f68b5df3e877a86951dbb4337d4a35b49d8c7"], "node": "91bc94abea55be532ea8b57d9bdff1f0594ca376", "parents": ["8b37ad0fbc6a01be10d755c4f887f6355b9cc083"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067983 [wpt PR 62281] - Add deprecation warning banner to all XSLT-transformed documents, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd deprecation warning banner to all XSLT-transformed documents\n\nPreviously, a visible deprecation warning banner was only injected for\nCommon Alerting Protocol (CAP) XML documents transformed via XSLT. This\nCL abstracts out the banner creation logic and displays a deprecation\nwarning banner on all XSLT-transformed documents, to improve visibility\nof the XSLT deprecation across all sites that use it. If the origin\ntrial *or* the enterprise policy are used to opt back in to XSLT, then\nthe banner is *not* shown.\n\nBug: 435623334\nChange-Id: I2cbbde3f20c0da66c69b13dd2e3fa2dde90127ec\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8299492\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688192}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 32118f63aa0cafbc450890512035ce18dedb032d\nwpt-pr: 62281\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/xml/xslt/document-function.window.js"], "git_node": "3fb1f0e2b4ebc8c8610b39da601bcb2c1dbf8cdf", "git_parents": ["b8fe2922ca90b190380c304ea06d29a345fbca76"], "node": "32a09fbdf2b8f5638cd023bf4d505f5e7c0df70d", "parents": ["91bc94abea55be532ea8b57d9bdff1f0594ca376"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067983 [wpt PR 62281] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62281\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/xml/xslt/invalid-output-encoding-crash.html.ini"], "git_node": "cc4a6616421df95e5f0b83acbe1fc774bfebec8d", "git_parents": ["3fb1f0e2b4ebc8c8610b39da601bcb2c1dbf8cdf"], "node": "30c62939cca1c66745f08bc43449ec1ccfc737f1", "parents": ["32a09fbdf2b8f5638cd023bf4d505f5e7c0df70d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067985 [wpt PR 62287] - TT: call createParserOptions before createHTML, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nTT: call createParserOptions before createHTML\n\nCalling createParserOptions first allows the policy to prefer the\nbuilt-in sanitizer, and only fall back to createHTML if the method\ndoes not support sanitizer (srcdoc/document.write), the browser does\nnot support createParserOptions, or createParserOptions is not specified by the policy/didn't return a sanitizer.\n\nBug: 491743369\nChange-Id: If71058beebc019f69f7fc1b58cb84e0db1b382c4\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8312789\nCommit-Queue: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Daniel Vogelheim \u003cvogelheim@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688226}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: bb5b8a99a4c391b0c56184c5e3a1d64206126dc7\nwpt-pr: 62287\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/sanitizer-api/sethtml-with-trustedtypes-createParserOptions.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/sanitizer-api/sethtml-with-trustedtypes.tentative.html"], "git_node": "226388c481e7b70ecee2fdd1d4e896d62bca8006", "git_parents": ["cc4a6616421df95e5f0b83acbe1fc774bfebec8d"], "node": "82fa75a3afb40cf2856ca36ffb081086a0276f85", "parents": ["30c62939cca1c66745f08bc43449ec1ccfc737f1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067985 [wpt PR 62287] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62287\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/sethtml-with-trustedtypes-createParserOptions.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/sethtml-with-trustedtypes.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "40fc1e4c0c4150dcc712d37468370e539aef6f99", "git_parents": ["226388c481e7b70ecee2fdd1d4e896d62bca8006"], "node": "203d0c563b5d5925ec15359dc4d7440e302b63c7", "parents": ["82fa75a3afb40cf2856ca36ffb081086a0276f85"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067988 [wpt PR 62293] - Change ::interest-button to use proposed anchor positioning, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nChange ::interest-button to use proposed anchor positioning\n\nSee\n\nhttps://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13981#issuecomment-4651351171\n\nThis CL makes Chromium follow that proposal.\n\nBug: 453705247\nChange-Id: I78f27b5bb9ac80d24bc4f1a12179b51d081925a3\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8298380\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688357}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f520e6dadd0074d1e2b7beb2b8b533f2bbe967a9\nwpt-pr: 62293\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/interestfor-pseudo-element-appearance-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/interestfor-pseudo-element-crash.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/interestfor-pseudo-element.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interestfor/resources/interest-button-styles.css"], "git_node": "5c24570ed8fca9361e9506caf992ee1205b65c33", "git_parents": ["40fc1e4c0c4150dcc712d37468370e539aef6f99"], "node": "bb4d8c2c6908b82b4e8b16fab0903187af0662e7", "parents": ["203d0c563b5d5925ec15359dc4d7440e302b63c7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "SeungJun Lee \u003cmps756@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067990 [wpt PR 62284] - [Blink] Preserve FormData File identity, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Blink] Preserve FormData File identity\n\nFormData stored Blob values and applied Blob-to-File conversion and\nfilename overrides whenever a value was retrieved. Repeated get(),\ngetAll(), and iteration therefore returned different File objects, and\nsynthesized lastModified values changed between calls.\n\nNormalize Blob and File values once when creating the entry, matching\nthe HTML create-an-entry algorithm. Retain the filename override used by\nmultipart serialization and preserve backing-file metadata when cloning\na named File.\n\nExpand WPT coverage across set(), append(), custom filenames, getAll(),\nand iteration, and remove the obsolete failure expectations.\n\nBug: 40765469\nTest: xhr/formdata WPT (27 tests)\nTest: form_data.o, form_data_test.o, and libblink_core.so build\nChange-Id: I85bb25f3d647d2e63129244ebf1bb2c540b00f2d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8276954\nCommit-Queue: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688362}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a884161c1c38f9928bb8216ce3646803815269af\nwpt-pr: 62284\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/xhr/formdata/set-blob.any.js"], "git_node": "7a19d493dd19ca706afd297472785e49193eb8cf", "git_parents": ["5c24570ed8fca9361e9506caf992ee1205b65c33"], "node": "cff86ee7afe659df64b1bb0cebc6d472bfd27d15", "parents": ["bb4d8c2c6908b82b4e8b16fab0903187af0662e7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Monica Chintala \u003cmonicach@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067993 [wpt PR 62286] - WebTransport: Implement Datagram writable streams, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebTransport: Implement Datagram writable streams\n\nAdd WebTransportDatagramDuplexStream.createWritable() and the\nWebTransportDatagramsWritable interface. Each call creates an\nindependent writable stream backed by the session's Datagram transport,\nwith sendGroup/sendOrder attributes, pre-connection buffering, cleanup\nhandling, and outgoing buffer-limit backpressure.\n\nGate the API behind an experimental runtime feature. This CL stores and\nvalidates sendGroup/sendOrder; plumbing those priorities through Mojo\nand the network service is intentionally left to a follow-up CL.\n\nPreserve the behavior of the legacy datagrams.writable stream and use\nweak sink registration so abandoned writable streams can be collected.\n\nThe maximum-size WPT remains expected to fail because this CL retains\nthe conservative 1024-byte maxDatagramSize value after connection.\nFollow-up CL https://crrev.com/c/8252325 plumbs the negotiated maximum\nand silently discards oversized writes.\n\nSpec -\nhttps://www.w3.org/TR/webtransport/#dom-webtransportdatagramduplexstream-createwritable\n\nhttps://www.w3.org/TR/webtransport/#webtransportdatagramswritable\n\nChrome entry - https://chromestatus.com/feature/5183354944225280\n\nBug: 547572475\nChange-Id: I307080981c4bd1e5321c890c504b3356f3f45032\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8254958\nReviewed-by: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Nidhi Jaju \u003cnidhijaju@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Monica Chintala \u003cmonicach@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688446}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 268e748de9c1ed2b306ba4261a36844cc3022bc3\nwpt-pr: 62286\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webtransport/datagrams-writable.https.any.js"], "git_node": "d4be8fe1edc3483b11da9d99f76ed5aff3a686a1", "git_parents": ["7a19d493dd19ca706afd297472785e49193eb8cf"], "node": "9829e7682a5ff5f1f71faab96baf34646a1e866f", "parents": ["cff86ee7afe659df64b1bb0cebc6d472bfd27d15"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrey Kosyakov \u003ccaseq@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067995 [wpt PR 62294] - Expect ServiceWorkerRegistration may have its ExecutionContext detached, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nExpect ServiceWorkerRegistration may have its ExecutionContext detached\n\nI pointed out to Gemini that service worker registration may have its\nExecutionContext return null and asked to locate and fix all call sites\nwhere this may cause a problem.\n\nFixed: 552461801, 332290373\nChange-Id: Id6be35ed3f66067c50949a8f51e923215d9a83eb\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8300597\nCommit-Queue: Andrey Kosyakov \u003ccaseq@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Peter Beverloo \u003cpeter@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688477}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d19d45c8899c7cbf9030dbb2aa45c8693d0bc7da\nwpt-pr: 62294\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/background-sync/crashtests/detached-frame.https.html"], "git_node": "0ff5cad40c9f42594943d67273c79ecb2c2c7c58", "git_parents": ["d4be8fe1edc3483b11da9d99f76ed5aff3a686a1"], "node": "0b1ad11a6b9c39d5e427560b5af6a15fa276b3a3", "parents": ["9829e7682a5ff5f1f71faab96baf34646a1e866f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067998 [wpt PR 62295] - [html-in-canvas] Remove the DOMMatrix return type of drawElementImage, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[html-in-canvas] Remove the DOMMatrix return type of drawElementImage\n\nThis patch removes the DOMMatrix return type of drawElementImage and\nupdates the tests accordingly. The change has been put behind the\nElementCanvasTransform feature flag and a basic test has been added to\nthe \"element-canvas-transform-disabled\" virtual test suite to ensure\nusers are not broken.\n\nBug: 532229486\nChange-Id: I81f59043fd776b945fb1f370d5a2874c90dda81a\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8313150\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688489}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 068c4cfd796f745b302d5a3e9f97189c285b3df8\nwpt-pr: 62295\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/anchor-positioning.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/canvas-transform-update.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/draw-element-image-returned-matrix.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/manual/draw-element-image/drawElementImage-returned-matrix-worker.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/manual/draw-element-image/getElementTransform-worker.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/manual/draw-element-image/offscreenCanvas-drawElementImage.tentative.html"], "git_node": "202d5dfac657a90f4b1ab01f7376ccffae700187", "git_parents": ["0ff5cad40c9f42594943d67273c79ecb2c2c7c58"], "node": "030d9770b7929fc11a84b3f0a02fec8c47d39a8a", "parents": ["0b1ad11a6b9c39d5e427560b5af6a15fa276b3a3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Aran Donohue \u003caran.donohue@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066640 [wpt PR 62196] - Let echo-request-headers.py report repeated header names, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nLet echo-request-headers.py report repeated header names\n\necho-request-headers.py keys its JSON payload by header name, so a request that\nuses the same header key more than once loses earlier values.  Add an\nopt-in ?format=list query parameter that reports every header value as a\nlist, in arrival order.\n\nBackward-compatible so no existing tests need to change.\n\nThis is intended for use in WPT tests with duplicate header keys.\n\nChange-Id: I09cb44c10e7674466fa40945865997101a774b43\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8258920\nReviewed-by: Adam Rice \u003cricea@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Robert Flack \u003cflackr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Adam Rice \u003cricea@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688918}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7f294759ec066d6bd7d5094783135c03125f012e\nwpt-pr: 62196\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webtransport/handlers/echo-request-headers.py"], "git_node": "ffcdfbbbbb23430589aff3a38467e0db095a39a4", "git_parents": ["202d5dfac657a90f4b1ab01f7376ccffae700187"], "node": "57176214293b31e13f4ee1189647c56ef87cc868", "parents": ["030d9770b7929fc11a84b3f0a02fec8c47d39a8a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Eldar Pulatov \u003cepulatov.dev@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068003 [wpt PR 62292] - [wpt] Wait for rendering before checking moveBefore() focus fixup, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[wpt] Wait for rendering before checking moveBefore() focus fixup\n\nmoveBefore() preserves focus synchronously. If a move leaves the focused\nelement in an inert or hidden subtree, the focus fixup rule runs during\na rendering update.\n\nThe test waited for a blur event with a one-second timer. The timer was\nnot synchronized with rendering and rejected without a value. When it\nfired first, testharness reported \"Unhandled rejection with value:\nundefined\".\n\nReplace the blur wait with waitForAtLeastOneFrame() before checking\ndocument.activeElement. Give each subtest its own connected fixture and\nverify that moveBefore() moved the node. In the focusable case, check\nthat focus remains after a rendering update.\n\nChange-Id: If9ce8bc838403089c2cb9907af897e6d8fca30ee\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8306396\nReviewed-by: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688423}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3e1155aecaa16d66025c8d1a9ba400fbdef90b59\nwpt-pr: 62292\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/moveBefore/focus-preserve.html"], "git_node": "61462205a979eb5ae882fe4057ea26b5b04dec0f", "git_parents": ["ffcdfbbbbb23430589aff3a38467e0db095a39a4"], "node": "b65d64d8207741115a5af4b92e90159b72970754", "parents": ["57176214293b31e13f4ee1189647c56ef87cc868"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Grogan \u003cdgrogan@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068004 [wpt PR 62289] - [menu a11y] Propagate dialog role through entire menu hierarchy, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[menu a11y] Propagate dialog role through entire menu hierarchy\n\nWhen any submenu in a menu hierarchy has forbidden content, every\nmenulist under the same top-level menu, and the top-level menubar\nitself, now gets a dialog aria role.\n\nPreviously, only the specific menu containing the violation would switch\nto a dialog role. This caused strange keyboard behavior, where the user\nwould have to switch between tab and arrow keys inside the same\n(logical) menu.\n\nThe change to \"dialog-everywhere\" behavior enables a top-level-only\narchitecture:\n1. Only the top-most menu element instantiates a MenuMutationObserver.\n2. This observer monitors the DOM subtree; it does not filter mutation\n   records or track detached root ownership, which was hairy. (We do\n   still have to track detached roots on child removal though, to see if\n   a violation was removed.)\n3. We do not observe detached menus. Instead, violations are checked for\n   on attachment.\n4. When content-model-violating elements are added or removed, we defer\n   the menu tree's dialog-mode update to a microtask. Because scripts\n   can insert or remove multiple violating elements in a single\n   synchronous block, delaying the update allows us to walk the menu\n   tree exactly once per JS turn.\n5. If a dialog-mode menu tree has a conforming submenu attached, we\n   update the conforming submenu's role to dialog immediately.\n\nAlternative designs considered:\n1. Each submenu has its own MenuMutationObserver and keeps track of its\n   own local violations. This required updating the root menu's global\n   counter, which was a few hundred lines more code with brittle logic.\n   It also required filtering observations to not double count submenu\n   violations. Initial hack at https://crrev.com/c/8275830\n2. Single root MenuMutationObserver (same as this CL) but synchronous\n   tree updates instead of via a microtask. This approach was slightly\n   less code but the logic to avoid a storm of redundant tree walks was\n   hard to follow.\n\nNote: as mentioned above, this CL changes the top-level menubar ARIA\nrole to dialog in the presence of a content model violation. We may\nchange that behavior upon further screen-reader testing.\n\nBug: 513637242\nChange-Id: I0cbfeab5cd3275e41dfc944d482be869c4899eb0\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8277920\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: David Grogan \u003cdgrogan@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688534}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e7d368cc9d4c87e805a025724a6a828306f4ca81\nwpt-pr: 62289\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/menu-content-model-violation.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/menu-dialog-mode-focus.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/reparent-with-pending-dialog-microtask.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/valid-submenu-invalid-root.html"], "git_node": "75fd87ca9806241cbb1a2d07a13587c82e65a3da", "git_parents": ["61462205a979eb5ae882fe4057ea26b5b04dec0f"], "node": "e40a6e2dc600b743ed78a8b9eb96dc772bd88460", "parents": ["b65d64d8207741115a5af4b92e90159b72970754"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vaibhav Srivastava \u003cvaibhavsri1712@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068098 [wpt PR 62298] - docs: fix typo arbitary -\u003e arbitrary, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\ndocs: fix typo arbitary -\u003e arbitrary (#62298)\n\nSigned-off-by: Vaibhav Srivastava \u003cvaibhavsri1712@gmail.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 2ccd2cbf88ff710ff1ca5786da13aac0b1e07a59\nwpt-pr: 62298\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/docs/config.rst"], "git_node": "6afcae5604cc10b4fbdc941cd5811f0d5623a312", "git_parents": ["75fd87ca9806241cbb1a2d07a13587c82e65a3da"], "node": "510af6a515bbaa2f7fd001aaeb1c1574be036db1", "parents": ["e40a6e2dc600b743ed78a8b9eb96dc772bd88460"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriel Brito \u003cgabrielbrito@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068101 [wpt PR 62283] - Fix visibility propagation to frames created hidden, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix visibility propagation to frames created hidden\n\nThis CL fixes the visibility data propagation to iframes that were\ncreated in an already hidden subtree. Without these changes, an iframe\ncreated hidden (display: none; visibility:hidden; zero-area) and not\nallowed to play audio by the `media-playback-while-not-visible`\npermission policy, could start playing audio when it shouldn't.\n\nA cross-origin iframe initially exists as an `about:blank` `LocalFrame`\nin the parent renderer. The parent can correctly compute and deliver the\nhidden media state to this initial frame. When the cross-origin\nnavigation commits, that `LocalFrame` is replaced by a `RemoteFrame` in\nthe parent renderer, while the destination renderer creates the real\n`LocalFrame`. The media visibility state from the initial frame is not\ntransferred during this swap, so the destination frame initially\nreceives the default `is_hidden_for_media_playback = false` value.\n\nNormally, a later viewport-intersection update corrects the value.\nHowever, a `display:none` iframe has no layout object, so no geometry or\nlifecycle event re-arms the parent intersection update. The OOPIF\ntherefore keeps the incorrect visible state.\n\nThere is a related ordering issue for nested same-process frames. If a\nchild is created after its hidden parent has already propagated its\nmedia visibility state, the new child misses that update. Because the\nhidden parent is render-throttled, another lifecycle pass may not run to\ncorrect it.\n\nThis change closes both propagation gaps:\n\n- When a `RemoteFrameView` is created, re-arm the embedding `LocalFrameView`'s intersection observation and schedule a lifecycle update. This recomputes the new remote frame's media visibility state after the process swap, even when the iframe has no layout object.\n- When a `LocalFrame` is initialized under an already-hidden same-process parent, inherit the parent's hidden media state. This covers descendants created after the parent's earlier intersection pass.\n\nBug: 351354996\nChange-Id: I572793f584be3b784a73ea49b1ee74cca6086294\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8128064\nCommit-Queue: Gabriel Brito \u003cgabrielbrito@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1688249}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f99609f5d005595fbeb882b46c5dbea190d22bc2\nwpt-pr: 62283\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/media-playback-while-not-visible-permission-policy/cant-play-when-created-hidden.tentative.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/media-playback-while-not-visible-permission-policy/resources/media-playback-while-not-visible-utils.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webaudio/the-audio-api/media-playback-while-not-visible-permission-policy/interrupt-when-created-hidden.tentative.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webaudio/the-audio-api/media-playback-while-not-visible-permission-policy/resources/media-playback-while-not-visible-utils.js"], "git_node": "7231c91f01ba57c033180541e793039156f85fa4", "git_parents": ["6afcae5604cc10b4fbdc941cd5811f0d5623a312"], "node": "d317e40c2f44fe65fdb57efbd6155f7057a4419f", "parents": ["510af6a515bbaa2f7fd001aaeb1c1574be036db1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068101 [wpt PR 62283] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62283\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/media-playback-while-not-visible-permission-policy/cant-play-when-created-hidden.tentative.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webaudio/the-audio-api/media-playback-while-not-visible-permission-policy/interrupt-when-created-hidden.tentative.sub.html.ini"], "git_node": "a6c575c1f215ef77f7745b7e13ec904dfb15a5cd", "git_parents": ["7231c91f01ba57c033180541e793039156f85fa4"], "node": "b7dc332a98b3a635de1c11b65037aa9e923b608e", "parents": ["d317e40c2f44fe65fdb57efbd6155f7057a4419f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Johannes Odland \u003cjohannes.odland@nrk.no\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067935 [wpt PR 51361] - Test all punctiation and whitespace categories that should be included in ::first-letter, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nCSS: test punctuation and whitespace categories that should be included in ::first-letter\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5e59630a71561d44b62309ab97e6849a81a48f1d\nwpt-pr: 51361\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/first-letter-punctuation-and-space-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/first-letter-punctuation-