8328 - Add the Highlight to Search preferences and a new Nimbus variable under the search feature. r=search-reviewers,Standard8\n\nFor background on the new Highlight to Search project, here is [[ https://docs.google.com/document/d/1lpprhnIKYbXSNnVE-OSmVcE1Vpm9_vBBIKIOjW8_0lE/edit?tab=t.os3nbc21wjhe | the current spec ]].\n\nAnd one question where I'd appreciate reviewer feedback:\n  - Should these new prefs be prefixed with `\"browser.search\"` rather than just `\"browser\"`?\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323112\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/FeatureManifest.yaml"], "git_node": "17f5af33864b5c656f46c3f8c4894a322c0036f0", "git_parents": ["bc23defbcd3b3e47d54f8bedd9e30cfa7f0631d3"], "node": "507c7f5c821d35ba9970a4669ea486f6239be222", "parents": ["5bbef08b9ad589772d1443f302a858826ce018f8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan Varga \u003cjvarga@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057579 - Complete the CSSPerspective implementation; r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nComplete the remaining `CSSPerspective` functionality by implementing the\nmissing attribute setter and `ToMatrix()`, adding constructor and setter\nargument validation, and enabling the corresponding WPT coverage.\n\nExtend `DOMMatrix` with an internal `PerspectiveSelf()` helper and handle the\n`none` keyword as an identity transform.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314898\n", "files": ["dom/base/DOMMatrix.cpp", "dom/base/DOMMatrix.h", "layout/style/typedom/CSSKeywordValue.h", "layout/style/typedom/CSSPerspective.cpp", "layout/style/typedom/CSSPerspective.h", "layout/style/typedom/CSSTransformComponent.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-typed-om/stylevalue-subclasses/cssPerspective.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-typed-om/stylevalue-subclasses/cssTransformComponent-toMatrix-relative-units.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-typed-om/stylevalue-subclasses/cssTransformComponent-toMatrix.html.ini"], "git_node": "c0128c647a0406c7195a301f1a1a3b867c89c6c6", "git_parents": ["17f5af33864b5c656f46c3f8c4894a322c0036f0"], "node": "20a67337946c13c1c5a7c87f6a7048ae4036a4ce", "parents": ["507c7f5c821d35ba9970a4669ea486f6239be222"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rana Al-Khulaidi \u003cralkhulaidi@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065368 - Remove ext-normandyAddonStudy. r=nimbus-reviewers,extension-reviewers,rpl,android-reviewers,android-addons-reviewers,beth,tcampbell\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320970\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/ext-browser.json", "browser/components/extensions/jar.mn", "browser/components/extensions/parent/ext-normandyAddonStudy.js", "browser/components/extensions/schemas/jar.mn", "browser/components/extensions/schemas/normandyAddonStudy.json", "browser/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_ext_normandyAddonStudy.js", "browser/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/addons/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/addons/update/DefaultAddonUpdaterTest.kt", "toolkit/components/extensions/Extension.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_ext_permissions.js"], "git_node": "cf543a262296665e3d3c648e6c969504aad177ec", "git_parents": ["c0128c647a0406c7195a301f1a1a3b867c89c6c6"], "node": "94affa80cd597e22e1ade3e480b3e628e0e9afd6", "parents": ["20a67337946c13c1c5a7c87f6a7048ae4036a4ce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Antonio Borondo \u003caborondo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070147 - Use moz-src instead of resource urls in toolkit/components/push/moz.build r=saschanaz\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324273\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/push/components.conf", "toolkit/components/push/moz.build", "toolkit/components/push/test/browser/browser_receive_push_messages.js", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.modules.d.ts", "tools/@types/generated/tspaths.json"], "git_node": "ed630b9c1ec35ef3d309267e1c0ca041b72bed34", "git_parents": ["cf543a262296665e3d3c648e6c969504aad177ec"], "node": "732b6fc7acbfc1fb5c13ee98f7bea441c24054e5", "parents": ["94affa80cd597e22e1ade3e480b3e628e0e9afd6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Sudiaman \u003cjsudiaman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057860 - Fix browser_drag_horizontal_overflow.js failures by waiting until scroll button is enabled. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,jswinarton\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323375\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/dragdrop/browser.toml", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/dragdrop/browser_drag_horizontal_overflow.js"], "git_node": "7135b80766a3240bac67e5b31cb27d71c47734a6", "git_parents": ["ed630b9c1ec35ef3d309267e1c0ca041b72bed34"], "node": "1c003ff269198a65b2cd6cafb7462cdcccd88b64", "parents": ["732b6fc7acbfc1fb5c13ee98f7bea441c24054e5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ben Visness \u003cbvisness@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068315: Make MWasmLoadField::mightAlias phi-friendly. r=jseward\n\nLoop unrolling, it seems, can cause phis to pick up\nMIRType::WasmStructData, which annoyingly prevents us from cleverly\ngoing backwards to the base struct object for alias analysis.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323261\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/gc/bug2068315.js", "js/src/jit/MIR.cpp"], "git_node": "49867656536b0890d51d8f40c6bb2ab059581cb8", "git_parents": ["7135b80766a3240bac67e5b31cb27d71c47734a6"], "node": "c9a12c7ca9e32ce2e38339a9ce89fefcf649cc8d", "parents": ["1c003ff269198a65b2cd6cafb7462cdcccd88b64"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Gaul \u003candrew@gaul.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070044 - Fix fwrite return value check in disnative and open the dump file in binary mode. r=iain\n\nfwrite returns the number of items written, not bytes, so passing the\nwhole blob as size with nmemb 1 made a successful write return 1, which\nwas compared against the byte count and always failed. The bytes were\nwritten before the check, so the dump was complete, but the spurious\nerror skipped the disassembly and threw. Swapping size and nmemb makes\nthe return a byte count and also behaves correctly for zero-length code.\n\nAlso open the file with \"wb\" so Windows does not expand 0x0A to\n0x0D 0x0A in the raw binary dump.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324172\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/TestingFunctions.cpp"], "git_node": "4bf60c85ed8b7c99b09e6fed855ad3a76b1b5192", "git_parents": ["49867656536b0890d51d8f40c6bb2ab059581cb8"], "node": "421fdbe5a42a870293e73a974191fa25fbe43672", "parents": ["c9a12c7ca9e32ce2e38339a9ce89fefcf649cc8d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067272 - Don't override :active target in link mousedown handler r=emilio\n\nWe call SetActiveManager to replace active content during mousedown which\ncauses :active state to be reset. Activation happens on pointerdown since Bug\n1293741 (D308750).\n\nThis change removes this callsite, instead allowing it to propagate from its\ncall in EventStateManager::PreHandleEvent.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324296\n", "files": ["dom/base/Element.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/active-inside-link.html"], "git_node": "42a0c86070b9570a8a2d534e3f6b8095f08ded86", "git_parents": ["4bf60c85ed8b7c99b09e6fed855ad3a76b1b5192"], "node": "332b8575cebcae06edf627ebdc3b2df9a2330135", "parents": ["421fdbe5a42a870293e73a974191fa25fbe43672"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062652 - Part 4 - Sanitize while parsing r=dom-core-reviewers,hsivonen\n\nThis change passes the Sanitizer to nsHtml5TreeBuilder & co, allowing for\nconsumption of the Sanitizer during parsing, rather than iterating over the\nreified tree.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320597\n", "files": ["dom/base/Document.cpp", "dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp", "dom/base/nsContentUtils.h", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "parser/html/javasrc/TreeBuilder.java", "parser/html/nsHtml5StringParser.cpp", "parser/html/nsHtml5StringParser.h", "parser/html/nsHtml5TreeBuilder.cpp", "parser/html/nsHtml5TreeBuilder.h", "parser/html/nsHtml5TreeBuilderCppSupplement.h", "parser/html/nsHtml5TreeBuilderHSupplement.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/__dir__.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-basic-filtering.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-in-adoption-agency.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-parseHTML.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/sethtml-safety.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/sethtml-tree-construction.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-in-adoption-agency.sub.dat"], "git_node": "869e7cfd00ac543cdf6b39af28ecf4a4bc9432ec", "git_parents": ["42a0c86070b9570a8a2d534e3f6b8095f08ded86"], "node": "b28e9b9584985a4836f959f15d14ff6e259b3ceb", "parents": ["332b8575cebcae06edf627ebdc3b2df9a2330135"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070000 - selectors crate cleanup. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\n`mach cargo clippy --fix -p selectors` + some token cloning avoidance\nthat I noticed, plus other manual clippy allow() / fixes.\n\nThe OpaqueElement unsafety seems a bit unnecessary because well, you\nneed unsafe to cast and dereference the pointer, and the safety comment\nshould really be on the caller.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324114\n", "files": ["servo/components/selectors/builder.rs", "servo/components/selectors/context.rs", "servo/components/selectors/matching.rs", "servo/components/selectors/parser.rs", "servo/components/selectors/relative_selector/filter.rs", "servo/components/selectors/tree.rs", "servo/components/style/gecko/selector_parser.rs", "servo/components/style/gecko/wrapper.rs"], "git_node": "f91881d8fb9140a78c5f4cd0c0f87e432c5a9009", "git_parents": ["869e7cfd00ac543cdf6b39af28ecf4a4bc9432ec"], "node": "582c35760a829c744ce46b33b3c028166adf6e9a", "parents": ["b28e9b9584985a4836f959f15d14ff6e259b3ceb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070000 - to_shmem clippy fixes. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324265\n", "files": ["servo/components/to_shmem/lib.rs"], "git_node": "a464a54cb39215546429204e9f6c83590be519a6", "git_parents": ["f91881d8fb9140a78c5f4cd0c0f87e432c5a9009"], "node": "cd5a4087517180d51bcfe10864453977e7cb8d2f", "parents": ["582c35760a829c744ce46b33b3c028166adf6e9a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070000 - servo_arc clippy fixes. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324123\n", "files": ["servo/components/servo_arc/lib.rs"], "git_node": "0e926a23de4b7e8264bd565595e5514885440081", "git_parents": ["a464a54cb39215546429204e9f6c83590be519a6"], "node": "092498a6c7aaf395a57b59cde1cca44c5c080820", "parents": ["cd5a4087517180d51bcfe10864453977e7cb8d2f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070000 - style_traits clippy fixes. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324125\n", "files": ["servo/components/style_traits/arc_slice.rs", "servo/components/style_traits/owned_slice.rs", "servo/components/style_traits/owned_str.rs", "servo/components/style_traits/values.rs"], "git_node": "8fe60f05ecc67e331cdc440d63f1c735585cab98", "git_parents": ["0e926a23de4b7e8264bd565595e5514885440081"], "node": "f4736db38e8497cf05a40edeb8de65efbbf230c4", "parents": ["092498a6c7aaf395a57b59cde1cca44c5c080820"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060247 - Add a WPT for SpeechRecognition.available() with an invalid language tag. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nThe availability algorithm rejects with a SyntaxError in its step 3, which so\nfar only install() had coverage for.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322686\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/speech-api/SpeechRecognition-availableOnDevice.https.html"], "git_node": "01f30a74ce1c23132734c5f1a5d58be5df7e8b88", "git_parents": ["8fe60f05ecc67e331cdc440d63f1c735585cab98"], "node": "80bfc1286c585bf390292f57d8675cc3f7fe33cf", "parents": ["f4736db38e8497cf05a40edeb8de65efbbf230c4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060247 - Default SpeechRecognition.lang to the document's content language. r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nAn unset lang defaults to the language of the document root element, which is\nits lang attribute, else the pragma-set default language or the\nContent-Language header.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322687\n", "files": ["dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognition.cpp"], "git_node": "bb1d098ac6a1ab71316e3cc1490b3485093790fc", "git_parents": ["01f30a74ce1c23132734c5f1a5d58be5df7e8b88"], "node": "d266d43d40f3d8b372a17eeb8c41f62895efa399", "parents": ["80bfc1286c585bf390292f57d8675cc3f7fe33cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060247 - Select the speech recognition model from the locales it declares. r=media-playback-reviewers,ai-platform-reviewers,valentinp,alwu\n\nEach models.yaml entry now lists the locales its artifact recognizes, taken from\nthe artifact itself, and a request picks the first entry that recognizes it,\nnegotiated with LocaleService::NegotiateLanguages. That replaces the locale\nprefixes and the multilingual catch-all, so a language no model recognizes no\nlonger reaches one that would transcribe it as another language.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322688\n", "files": ["dom/media/docs/SpeechRecognition.md", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognitionModelMapping.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognitionModelMapping.h", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognitionParent.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognitionParent.h", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/gen_speech_models.py", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/models.yaml", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/test_parakeet_multilingual.html", "toolkit/components/ml/docs/HWInference.md"], "git_node": "937fa5578957cdad571eaf2e79fc2e03d0073319", "git_parents": ["bb1d098ac6a1ab71316e3cc1490b3485093790fc"], "node": "afbca69056dffcf6b5ad2a58c231adbd92ca72fd", "parents": ["d266d43d40f3d8b372a17eeb8c41f62895efa399"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060247 - Add a gtest for speech recognition locale negotiation. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nIt walks every locale every model declares, and checks that the model answering\nfor one declares the locale it hands back.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322689\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestSpeechModelMapping.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "784462ab6ff2ae02613baec5ee8ee2a06e07dc8c", "git_parents": ["937fa5578957cdad571eaf2e79fc2e03d0073319"], "node": "7b77eb562ea5b7ef23ea1fcfd0f97ec2e23a1840", "parents": ["afbca69056dffcf6b5ad2a58c231adbd92ca72fd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060247 - Refuse languages no speech recognition model recognizes. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\navailable() reports unavailable and install() resolves false without launching\nthe HWInference process or downloading anything, and start() fires\nservice-not-allowed, as its start session algorithm's step 4.1 requires.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322690\n", "files": ["dom/media/docs/SpeechRecognition.md", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognition.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/test_unsupported_language.html"], "git_node": "47a22389e1f475f5bdd58b291d823906c78fd7cc", "git_parents": ["784462ab6ff2ae02613baec5ee8ee2a06e07dc8c"], "node": "36f39ff1313b1af3e12c3f5f41e72e8ee36251da", "parents": ["7b77eb562ea5b7ef23ea1fcfd0f97ec2e23a1840"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060247 - Fall back to the user's language when the document declares none. r=eemeli\n\nHTML leaves the language of a node unknown for a document with neither a lang\nattribute nor a Content-Language, which is most of them, and recognition has to\nrun in some language regardless. Chrome answers that with the first of the\nuser's accepted languages; do the same.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324277\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsDocumentWarningList.inc", "dom/locales/en-US/chrome/dom/dom.properties", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognition.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/recognition/test/test_unsupported_language.html"], "git_node": "0d37e522d91e10263936c2b8b4ca482ad6e4cf47", "git_parents": ["47a22389e1f475f5bdd58b291d823906c78fd7cc"], "node": "a5d2d31e81d68850c1f7231cfb3dbbcacb316128", "parents": ["36f39ff1313b1af3e12c3f5f41e72e8ee36251da"], "tags": []}, {"author": "kevindoughty \u003ckvndy@protonmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066417 - [animation] Opacity clamping rollback r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323334\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/values/computed/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/mod.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/glue.rs", "testing/web-platform/meta/web-animations/animation-model/animation-types/clamping-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/web-animations/animation-model/animation-types/clamping-001.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/web-animations/animation-model/combining-effects/clamping-001.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/web-animations/animation-model/animation-types/clamping-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/web-animations/animation-model/animation-types/clamping-001.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/web-animations/animation-model/combining-effects/clamping-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/web-animations/animation-model/combining-effects/clamping-001.tentative.html"], "git_node": "0dd157f7f7188f6c8629bb5cc15fed31cd3d36ad", "git_parents": ["0d37e522d91e10263936c2b8b4ca482ad6e4cf47"], "node": "78bc7f72745161e705bde0d2f204697effef1caf", "parents": ["a5d2d31e81d68850c1f7231cfb3dbbcacb316128"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandra Borovova \u003caborovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068936 - Update more metadata for encoding/streams/decode-utf8.any.js.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324350\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/encoding/streams/decode-utf8.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "2a6321d87d8bfaa611ec870416eda48c87472c76", "git_parents": ["0dd157f7f7188f6c8629bb5cc15fed31cd3d36ad"], "node": "94682777a0bf89e755f18d5ff62d66e7b80cca92", "parents": ["78bc7f72745161e705bde0d2f204697effef1caf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060247 - Don't compile the new test on Android.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324364\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "6dfab33b32ae0d45bf8ba87ac3fc886c89061177", "git_parents": ["2a6321d87d8bfaa611ec870416eda48c87472c76"], "node": "7144d6815e89a300cf5709a7736543c0620cd014", "parents": ["94682777a0bf89e755f18d5ff62d66e7b80cca92"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandru Marc \u003camarc@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068936 - update more metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/clipboard-apis/clipboard-copy-selection-line-break.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/fetch/api/cors/cors-cookies.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/the-button-element/command-and-commandfor/on-video-behavior.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "bcad7949ee65a4bf19d8b27e0748882de733bae0", "git_parents": ["6dfab33b32ae0d45bf8ba87ac3fc886c89061177"], "node": "72b8abb37196eed103cdadb9ae3dc98ca124ebbb", "parents": ["7144d6815e89a300cf5709a7736543c0620cd014"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2066417 - [animation] Opacity clamping rollback r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\" for causing wpt failures in clamping-001.tentative.html.\n\nThis reverts commit 0dd157f7f7188f6c8629bb5cc15fed31cd3d36ad.\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/values/computed/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/mod.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/glue.rs", "testing/web-platform/meta/web-animations/animation-model/animation-types/clamping-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/web-animations/animation-model/animation-types/clamping-001.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/web-animations/animation-model/combining-effects/clamping-001.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/web-animations/animation-model/animation-types/clamping-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/web-animations/animation-model/animation-types/clamping-001.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/web-animations/animation-model/combining-effects/clamping-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/web-animations/animation-model/combining-effects/clamping-001.tentative.html"], "git_node": "35aac9c257a27c39c14d4caae7df78ffc8684398", "git_parents": ["bcad7949ee65a4bf19d8b27e0748882de733bae0"], "node": "7d107db3bd69e719e3b8b0920ebc4353d649a074", "parents": ["72b8abb37196eed103cdadb9ae3dc98ca124ebbb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "calu \u003ccalu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069464 - Add telemetry for tab groups onboarding impressions and dismissal r=android-reviewers,007\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323776\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/metrics.yaml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/TabsTrayTelemetryMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/TabsTrayTelemetryMiddlewareTest.kt"], "git_node": "abfc96ba0cd4a0b57a60d576b80e94245280c655", "git_parents": ["35aac9c257a27c39c14d4caae7df78ffc8684398"], "node": "b15f7ca5a10855d0fce879f4a18f1865e47179bd", "parents": ["7d107db3bd69e719e3b8b0920ebc4353d649a074"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2010541 - Stop exporting undefined disassembler symbols from clang 14's libLTO and libRemarks. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nBackport llvm-project c294bdd64768 and bf07de38b05e.\n\nLTODisassembler.cpp only forces the target disassembler registries into\nthe link; the LLVMCreateDisasm* entry points themselves live in\nLLVMMCDisassembler. With LLVM_LINK_LLVM_DYLIB, which we enable\neverywhere but Windows, they end up in libLLVM-14.so, so lto.exports\nnames six symbols libLTO.so.14 does not define. lld defaults to\n--no-undefined-version since llvm D135402 and rejects that.\n\nlibRemarks.so has the same problem, more so: Remarks.exports lists 25\nsymbols and libremarks.cpp defines exactly one.\n\nBoth upstream fixes landed for LLVM 16, so clang 19 and later already\nhave them.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320155\n", "files": ["build/build-clang/clang-14.json", "build/build-clang/llvmorg-17-init-946-gc294bdd64768_clang_14.patch", "build/build-clang/llvmorg-17-init-947-gbf07de38b05e_clang_14.patch"], "git_node": "c41f6ab34f0b247c19afd456a43cdf8f99aeb274", "git_parents": ["abfc96ba0cd4a0b57a60d576b80e94245280c655"], "node": "d5a1eddac54e3e8960280f9c61107115e0120f17", "parents": ["b15f7ca5a10855d0fce879f4a18f1865e47179bd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2010574 - Install libzstd-dev in the toolchain-build image, and don't autodetect zstd when building against a sysroot. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nlibcrypto in Debian 13 pulls in libzstd, so xar fails to link without\nlibzstd-dev in the image.\n\nInstalling it in turn makes LLVM and binutils pick up the system zstd,\nwhich isn't in the sysroots they link against, so turn it off explicitly.\nThis covers both build-clang.py and build-llvm-common.sh; the latter\nconfigures llvm proper for llvm-symbolizer. build-cctools-port.sh already\npasses -DLLVM_ENABLE_ZSTD=OFF for the same reason.\n\nLLVM_ENABLE_ZSTD=ON really means autodetect, so this only pins behaviour\nwe already had: no image shipped libzstd-dev until now.\n\nEventually we should either build xar against the sysroot or link\nstatically, but this is the smaller fix for now.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320156\n", "files": ["build/build-clang/build-clang.py", "build/unix/build-binutils/build-binutils.sh", "taskcluster/docker/toolchain-build/Dockerfile", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-llvm-common.sh"], "git_node": "b06f4b70348895945d65ef3a379f4412609e3108", "git_parents": ["c41f6ab34f0b247c19afd456a43cdf8f99aeb274"], "node": "a004076c082c25955252925746848d7d3116ec7d", "parents": ["d5a1eddac54e3e8960280f9c61107115e0120f17"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2010555 - Disable gcc's c++tools when building against a sysroot. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sylvestre\n\nlibcody is a bootstrapped host module, and POSTSTAGE1_CXX_EXPORT does not\npass the build sysroot's flags, so it is compiled against the image's\nheaders. c++tools is not bootstrapped and is built in the post-bootstrap\npass, where TARGET_FLAGS_TO_PASS sets CXX to the target compiler with\n--sysroot, so g++-mapper-server links against the sysroot's libc.\n\nWith glibc \u003e= 2.38 the image's stdlib.h redirects strtoul to\n__isoc23_strtoul, which the jessie sysroot's glibc 2.19 doesn't provide,\nand linking g++-mapper-server fails.\n\nNothing uses the standalone C++ module mapper server: gcc defaults to the\nin-process mapper. libcody itself is still built and linked into cc1plus,\nwhich is consistent since that link also happens without the sysroot.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320157\n", "files": ["build/unix/build-gcc/build-gcc.sh"], "git_node": "be52c036e2e7b6f7dc328147e92dd3c365d230ec", "git_parents": ["b06f4b70348895945d65ef3a379f4412609e3108"], "node": "276f49640795db37a4a9b50491e7900d04d810bf", "parents": ["a004076c082c25955252925746848d7d3116ec7d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2010489 - Switch toolchain tasks to Debian 13-based docker image. r=taskgraph-reviewers,ahal\n\nAdd gpgv to the toolchain-build image, required by build-sysroot.sh via\nthe gpgvnoexpkeysig script.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D279110\n", "files": ["build/build-clang/use-system-clang.json", "taskcluster/docker/toolchain-build/Dockerfile", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/job/toolchain.py"], "git_node": "41210f14a7d79a08a308a4891af024c072423bd9", "git_parents": ["be52c036e2e7b6f7dc328147e92dd3c365d230ec"], "node": "2d3260ae5f650f117c0942ed0bc9eb9ce72977e3", "parents": ["276f49640795db37a4a9b50491e7900d04d810bf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070120 - Build upx against the sysroot. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sylvestre,sergesanspaille\n\nupx was built with the docker image's headers and libraries, so the\nshipped binary's glibc floor followed the image: moving to Debian 13\ntook it from GLIBC_2.14 to GLIBC_2.38, which excludes Ubuntu 22.04,\nDebian 12 and Rocky 9. It is a local-toolchain, so mach bootstrap hands\nit to developers on arbitrary distributions.\n\nupx links nothing externally -- UCL and zlib are vendored and built\nstatic, and bzip2, zstd and threads are disabled in its CMakeLists --\nso pointing cmake at the sysroot is enough. Follows the same pattern as\nbuild-dmg-hfsplus.sh.\n\nwin64-upx shares the script and is unaffected: the new flags are in the\nnon-Msys branch.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324245\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/toolchain/upx.yml", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-upx.sh"], "git_node": "28b8040e2a8276b36e985a9a55900a7141d7948a", "git_parents": ["41210f14a7d79a08a308a4891af024c072423bd9"], "node": "179e4d446c09e2db7512e972eea63bfd1f625521", "parents": ["2d3260ae5f650f117c0942ed0bc9eb9ce72977e3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070120 - Build mkbom against the sysroot. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sylvestre,sergesanspaille\n\nmkbom was built with the docker image's compiler, so the shipped\nbinary's glibc floor followed the image: moving to Debian 13 took it\nfrom GLIBC_2.34 to GLIBC_2.38. It is a local-toolchain, so mach\nbootstrap hands it to developers on arbitrary distributions.\n\nbomutils assigns CXXFLAGS and LDFLAGS with = rather than ?= in its\nMakefile, so overriding them on the make command line would drop its\nown hardening flags. The sysroot flags go into CXX instead.\n\nThe task already fetched clang and the sysroot; it just wasn't using\nthem. Measured locally: GLIBC_2.38 -\u003e GLIBC_2.14.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324246\n", "files": ["taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-mkbom-linux.sh"], "git_node": "46399accbe5813c7a81bec1fb2a8d4719d1c1b45", "git_parents": ["28b8040e2a8276b36e985a9a55900a7141d7948a"], "node": "0799d4a17b5d370f3f82754e9cc9f8e317dcc083", "parents": ["179e4d446c09e2db7512e972eea63bfd1f625521"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070120 - Build winchecksec against the sysroot. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sylvestre,sergesanspaille\n\nwinchecksec was built with the docker image's headers and libraries, so\nthe shipped binary's glibc floor followed the image: moving to Debian 13\ntook it from GLIBC_2.14 to GLIBC_2.34. It is a local-toolchain, so mach\nbootstrap hands it to developers on arbitrary distributions.\n\nThe task fetched neither clang nor a sysroot, and build-winchecksec.sh\nhad no case for x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, so the linux build fell\nthrough with no cmake flags at all. Add the fetches and a linux case\nmirroring build-msix-packaging.sh.\n\nwin64-winchecksec shares the script and is unaffected. Measured locally:\nGLIBC_2.34 -\u003e GLIBC_2.14, and pe-parse's -Werror block still compiles\nclean under clang with the sysroot.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324247\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/toolchain/misc.yml", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-winchecksec.sh"], "git_node": "a45e8e65b478713a64b604fc1112c7cc379fa463", "git_parents": ["46399accbe5813c7a81bec1fb2a8d4719d1c1b45"], "node": "39c4a9096d74be91c2d2387db112d6a25aa39a58", "parents": ["0799d4a17b5d370f3f82754e9cc9f8e317dcc083"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070120 - Build gn against the sysroot. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sylvestre,sergesanspaille\n\ngn was built with the docker image's gcc, so the shipped binary's glibc\nfloor followed the image: moving to Debian 13 took it from GLIBC_2.18 to\nGLIBC_2.38. That broke source-test-vendor-verify-gfx, which runs gn to\nre-vendor gfx/angle on the static-analysis-build image; bug 2065412\nworked around it by moving that image to Debian 13, but the binary is\nalso a local-toolchain handed to developers on arbitrary distributions.\n\nThe symbols pulling in GLIBC_2.38 are the __isoc23_str* redirects glibc\napplies to strtol and friends for __cplusplus \u003e= 202302L, and gn is\nbuilt as C++23. Building against older headers removes the redirect\nrather than papering over it.\n\ngn needs linux64-toolchain-sysroot-gcc10 rather than\nlinux64-toolchain-sysroot: it uses \u003cconcepts\u003e and \u003cranges\u003e, which the\nlibstdc++ 8 in the latter does not have. cctools-port and node-22\nalready use the gcc10 sysroot for the same reason.\n\nbuild/gen.py bakes CXX, CFLAGS+CXXFLAGS and LDFLAGS into build.ninja at\ngeneration time and has no cxx-vs-cc distinction, so the environment\nvariables have to be set before it runs. The mac and win64 gn builds set\ntheir own and are unaffected; build-gn-common.sh is untouched.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324248\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/toolchain/gn.yml", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-gn-linux.sh"], "git_node": "a0dd954afbd53a4885a947e74e59809bd9dce78b", "git_parents": ["a45e8e65b478713a64b604fc1112c7cc379fa463"], "node": "62ccf0249627799c664095fda971d666d7ae4c00", "parents": ["39c4a9096d74be91c2d2387db112d6a25aa39a58"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070120 - Build xar against the sysroot. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sylvestre,sergesanspaille\n\nxar was built with the docker image's headers and libraries even though\nits task already fetched clang and a sysroot. Moving to Debian 13 took\nthe shipped binary from GLIBC_2.34 to GLIBC_2.38 and added a\nlibzstd.so.1 dependency, by way of deb13's openssl pulling zstd into\npkg-config --static --libs libcrypto. It is a local-toolchain, so mach\nbootstrap hands it to developers on arbitrary distributions.\n\nxar's configure can only locate libxml2 through xml2-config, which\nsysroots do not ship because they contain no /usr/bin. Left alone it\ncombines the host's libxml2 headers with the sysroot's library, so pass\na small shim backed by pkg-config.\n\nThe sysroot's openssl is 1.0.1t, which does not pull in zstd, so\nlibzstd-dev is no longer needed in the image; bug 2010574 only added it\nfor xar. Dropping it also stops gcc autodetecting zstd, which was\nsilently adding a libzstd.so.1 dependency to the gcc toolchains. The\nexplicit -DLLVM_ENABLE_ZSTD=OFF and --without-zstd stay: they pin\nautodetection that would otherwise vary with the image's contents.\n\nOther consequences worth knowing:\n - the statically linked libcrypto becomes the sysroot's openssl 1.0.1t.\n   xar only uses the EVP digest functions, no TLS or certificate code.\n - that libcrypto.a is not built PIC, so the binary can no longer be a\n   PIE.\n - the sysroot has lzma.h where the image did not, so xar gains lzma\n   support and a liblzma.so.5 dependency.\n\nMeasured locally: GLIBC_2.38 -\u003e GLIBC_2.14, configure resolves libxml\n2.9.1 with no host/sysroot split, and create/extract roundtrips pass for\nsha1, sha256 and md5 with gzip, bzip2 and no compression.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324249\n", "files": ["taskcluster/docker/toolchain-build/Dockerfile", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-xar-linux.sh"], "git_node": "49f78a104ff624a7b3d5fd769dfafb08b32a2e48", "git_parents": ["a0dd954afbd53a4885a947e74e59809bd9dce78b"], "node": "cf1f1ba27fadac5175d572eb55465476beb0c286", "parents": ["62ccf0249627799c664095fda971d666d7ae4c00"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070000 - malloc_size_of clippy fixes. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324126\n", "files": ["servo/components/malloc_size_of/lib.rs"], "git_node": "d3b4a46faf4436c3fa784c1debc8bbc7937f13cf", "git_parents": ["49f78a104ff624a7b3d5fd769dfafb08b32a2e48"], "node": "160bc33a7457acd303205c0758871c16bce32617", "parents": ["cf1f1ba27fadac5175d572eb55465476beb0c286"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bryan Johns \u003cbjohns@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2048659 - Added 'topics' argument to getOpenTabs to allow for topic-specific tab retrieval r=simonf,again\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D307639\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/Chat.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/Tools.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/test_Tools_GetOpenTabs.js"], "git_node": "57f6b8fe4cc0c9a3007f1b4c2948e09723e0bd2c", "git_parents": ["d3b4a46faf4436c3fa784c1debc8bbc7937f13cf"], "node": "8def7c42552946857fedebf2d911e2d97909d11f", "parents": ["160bc33a7457acd303205c0758871c16bce32617"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070000 - Clippy fixes for {style,to_shmem}_derive. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324340\n", "files": ["servo/components/style_derive/animate.rs", "servo/components/style_derive/cg.rs", "servo/components/style_derive/compute_squared_distance.rs", "servo/components/style_derive/specified_value_info.rs", "servo/components/style_derive/to_animated_value.rs", "servo/components/style_derive/to_animated_zero.rs", "servo/components/style_derive/to_computed_value.rs", "servo/component