huang@speediance.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069280 - Define --border-dead-row for dead rows in about:memory's Collector Log Analyzer r=dao,desktop-theme-reviewers DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324492\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/aboutmemory/content/aboutMemory.css"], "git_node": "7e1e37f5ef08ca4131da26ef455c670ebc53d0b4", "git_parents": ["7ca6b45b92e5f4c44cea5ff790af1bb3216ed990"], "node": "08f81cc253edbe26f0e9fd475c70b72a46b7171a", "parents": ["ea5b97aa3bab911267e0e7173e6e38dc4575d00d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066073 - Rename the tab group and split view element scripts to .mjs. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,jswinarton\n\nA pure move, ahead of the commit that makes them modules, so the rename stays visible to blame. The subscript loader does not read the extension, and dropping `\"use strict\"` only anticipates eslint parsing the file as a module.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323577\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-main.js", "browser/base/content/test/static/browser_parsable_css.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabgroup.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabgroup.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabsplitview.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabsplitview.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/jar.mn", "browser/components/tabbrowser/moz.build", "browser/components/tabbrowser/types/elements.ts"], "git_node": "04c45753bee1c2f31d659e78a61e93340163c26d", "git_parents": ["7e1e37f5ef08ca4131da26ef455c670ebc53d0b4"], "node": "ea1611c010dda8fe1214ed9cb748d6da5c01866b", "parents": ["08f81cc253edbe26f0e9fd475c70b72a46b7171a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066073 - Turn the tab group and split view elements into modules. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,sthompson\n\nDropping the block the subscript loader needed reindents both files, so `git diff -w` is the change and nothing in it is more than mechanical. `global: \"current\"` puts each module in the window's global, so the bare `gBrowser` and `SessionStore` references keep resolving.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323578\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-main.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabgroup.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabsplitview.mjs"], "git_node": "60ad9d1eb17a2b32acc4f9febbc3481b8ac5ff31", "git_parents": ["04c45753bee1c2f31d659e78a61e93340163c26d"], "node": "dcb5eb5efca7f18696c9e230370a12ac59af84ec", "parents": ["ea1611c010dda8fe1214ed9cb748d6da5c01866b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066073 - Type the tab group and split view elements from their classes. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,sthompson\n\nNothing checked the stand-in interfaces against the classes, so what only the interfaces said now has to be said in the classes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323579\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabgroup.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabsplitview.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/types/elements.ts"], "git_node": "c3d3e434db8e425d6d9d5219f24733a04acc79b4", "git_parents": ["60ad9d1eb17a2b32acc4f9febbc3481b8ac5ff31"], "node": "ed39ec09aaed2eaab3ad70877da695dcb637b6ba", "parents": ["dcb5eb5efca7f18696c9e230370a12ac59af84ec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064747 - Render the urlbar result menu's separators. r=daisuke\n\npanel-list styles `hr`, not the `separator` element the menu creates, so a result menu's separators have been invisible since it moved to panel-list.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324401\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarView.mjs"], "git_node": "80ae4003e55bad247a3191d0be54da2a674290c8", "git_parents": ["c3d3e434db8e425d6d9d5219f24733a04acc79b4"], "node": "b3e20294f19ec0ee1f30c8c1f76a321f16c2a037", "parents": ["ed39ec09aaed2eaab3ad70877da695dcb637b6ba"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2070131 - Add a context menu to the wrshell scene tree. r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\" for causing valgrind failures.\n\nThis reverts commit 3cfc84bdeb65adfed599f45b609252bc1deae016.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2070131 - Add a built scene inspector to the WebRender debugger and wrshell. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\"\n\nThis reverts commit c556ca6c731bc792697271be938ea3b4fc2a9918.\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/debugger.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/frame_builder.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/lib.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_api.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_backend.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_debug.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/visibility.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/debugger.rs", "gfx/wr/wrshell/README.md", "gfx/wr/wrshell/src/debug_commands.rs", "gfx/wr/wrshell/src/gui/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/wrshell/src/gui/scene_tree.rs"], "git_node": "7bf8d4ab193684fafe02114253b66369d2dac79b", "git_parents": ["80ae4003e55bad247a3191d0be54da2a674290c8"], "node": "636fc16cb5c6bb2d411ee8e49804cd0a3906675f", "parents": ["b3e20294f19ec0ee1f30c8c1f76a321f16c2a037"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mayankleoboy1 \u003cmayankleoboy1@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 661957 - Use PodCopy for same-type POD copyConstruct in Vector. r=sergesanspaille\n\nVectorImpl's POD specialization copies appended ranges with a per-element\nloop, on the grounds that append is usually given small ranges. It is also\nhow JSStringBuilder copies string segments: a samply profile of a\n60000-char str.replaceAll spends 57.9% of the call in copyConstruct at\nroughly 1.4 GB/s, against about 20 GB/s for the equivalent rope flatten.\n\nUse PodCopy when T and U are the same type, which is the patch proposed in\ncomment 2 of this bug in 2012. PodCopy already carries the size and platform\nheuristic measured in bug 933149 and bug 1967062, so ranges under 128\nelements on Linux keep the loop they have today.\n\nNo caller can pass overlapping ranges to PodCopy's new assertion: every\nmoveConstruct site targets a fresh allocation or the opposite of inline and\nheap storage, and an append whose source lies in the vector's own live range\nends at or before the destination, since the source must end by mLength and\nthe destination starts there.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323825\n", "files": ["mfbt/Vector.h"], "git_node": "33f7ca67aa71605087cbfe249f8ef333a6e51e72", "git_parents": ["7bf8d4ab193684fafe02114253b66369d2dac79b"], "node": "d82ace3dfb0d2ef2099458dc11edf8764aa8baf1", "parents": ["636fc16cb5c6bb2d411ee8e49804cd0a3906675f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Norisz Fay \u003cnfay@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 661957 - Use PodCopy for same-type POD copyConstruct in Vector. r=sergesanspaille\" for causing SM bustages\n\nThis reverts commit 33f7ca67aa71605087cbfe249f8ef333a6e51e72.\n", "files": ["mfbt/Vector.h"], "git_node": "814121cf025bff36a0471d8c1d30913d7e379f03", "git_parents": ["33f7ca67aa71605087cbfe249f8ef333a6e51e72"], "node": "21f06d48a9259ae9b413ae21f02990c8d7fb7c2e", "parents": ["d82ace3dfb0d2ef2099458dc11edf8764aa8baf1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Merge mozilla-central to autoland\n", "files": [], "git_node": "c16b6c2e6a57f3ae2b0d875d37cafa096dd3ded0", "git_parents": ["814121cf025bff36a0471d8c1d30913d7e379f03", "a641c7b27bb8a3fa8ffd47c312e1981456626ab2"], "node": "036eb81f1e1a1d5338e78953c5e93257e2497db8", "parents": ["21f06d48a9259ae9b413ae21f02990c8d7fb7c2e", "482ab468a7753e3a0c00eb718439ecdbfe28ceb9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Exploding-Joysticks \u003cExplodingJoysticks@proton.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1842469 - Remove the idle_period.cross_process_scheduling pref r=nimbus-reviewers,xpcom-reviewers,beth\n\nAmend: Removed some more code I had missed the first time around, I'm surprised it passed the tests.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322183\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "toolkit/components/nimbus/FeatureManifest.yaml", "tools/@types/subs/FeatureManifest.sys.d.mts", "xpcom/threads/IdlePeriodState.cpp"], "git_node": "4189aec2b4c926e31e1210c5cb98105829c6f6e4", "git_parents": ["c16b6c2e6a57f3ae2b0d875d37cafa096dd3ded0"], "node": "f64860526e26e8794114f340b2764e96c9c81193", "parents": ["036eb81f1e1a1d5338e78953c5e93257e2497db8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057759 - Test remote decoded color metadata transport r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321679\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestRemoteImageHolder.cpp"], "git_node": "38a8b7a877ab6aca6357811cfe9591afb7b34879", "git_parents": ["4189aec2b4c926e31e1210c5cb98105829c6f6e4"], "node": "76d5c1b9e927838dc27ecc510d2492c524f4ac68", "parents": ["f64860526e26e8794114f340b2764e96c9c81193"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057759 - Preserve decoded color metadata across remote image transport r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321680\n", "files": ["dom/media/ipc/RemoteImageHolder.cpp", "dom/media/ipc/RemoteVideoDecoder.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/SharedPlanarYCbCrImage.cpp"], "git_node": "53d18a533eed62d59096fc35e938ab1a9ade0441", "git_parents": ["38a8b7a877ab6aca6357811cfe9591afb7b34879"], "node": "15c3b7cb8132c2868b126e0755bcdc40edd1bdfc", "parents": ["76d5c1b9e927838dc27ecc510d2492c524f4ac68"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057759 - Test FFmpeg decoded frame color metadata r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nGenerate av1-color-metadata.mp4 with:\n  ./generate_color_metadata_video.py av1-color-metadata.mp4\n      --codec libaom-av1 --pixel-format yuv420p10le\n      --color-primaries bt2020 --color-transfer smpte2084\n      --color-matrix bt2020nc --color-range tv --movflags +faststart\n      --encoder-option cpu-used=8 --encoder-option still-picture=1\n      --encoder-option crf=30\n\nThe checked-in fixture was generated with FFmpeg 6.1.1-3ubuntu5.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321982\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestMediaDataDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/av1-color-metadata.mp4", "dom/media/gtest/generate_color_metadata_video.py", "dom/media/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "8f5ce1e423b0400e1d075a0a5b3648be3a026d61", "git_parents": ["53d18a533eed62d59096fc35e938ab1a9ade0441"], "node": "5636a563fe35f3ef3797358fb8b61f5dc33b81be", "parents": ["15c3b7cb8132c2868b126e0755bcdc40edd1bdfc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057759 - Preserve FFmpeg decoded frame color metadata r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321681\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.h"], "git_node": "d9ab7a4373b62f78e22f724e65ee88eeb67c4a3e", "git_parents": ["8f5ce1e423b0400e1d075a0a5b3648be3a026d61"], "node": "fd814ba50121f9323d6571229b2099eec16457f5", "parents": ["5636a563fe35f3ef3797358fb8b61f5dc33b81be"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057759 - Update draw-snapshot AV1 color-quads fuzziness r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nPreserving FFmpeg's decoded color metadata reduces the pixel differences for the full-range 8-bit and 10-bit AV1 cases. Update their draw-snapshot expectations to match the corrected output.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322710\n", "files": ["dom/media/test/reftest/color_quads/reftest.list"], "git_node": "dbcf03c2514fcd86461fb6240102932285e0e42c", "git_parents": ["d9ab7a4373b62f78e22f724e65ee88eeb67c4a3e"], "node": "d570eecf4efcc680d60b906cd8c151870b4312bd", "parents": ["fd814ba50121f9323d6571229b2099eec16457f5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057759 - Add debugging logs for PlanarYCbCrData r=media-playback-reviewers,gfx-reviewers,bradwerth,padenot\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323445\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.cpp", "gfx/2d/Types.cpp", "gfx/2d/Types.h", "gfx/layers/ImageContainer.cpp", "gfx/layers/ImageContainer.h"], "git_node": "3fea0e52800e61d0895ada227011c2a6e22f983a", "git_parents": ["dbcf03c2514fcd86461fb6240102932285e0e42c"], "node": "971821607876ce1ce2cb2b2b24485c3885c65068", "parents": ["d570eecf4efcc680d60b906cd8c151870b4312bd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057759 - Logging by gfx's logging convention r=media-playback-reviewers,gtk-reviewers,emilio,padenot\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323446\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/EncoderConfig.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/EncoderConfig.h", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/webcodecs/WebCodecsUtils.cpp", "gfx/layers/NativeLayerWayland.cpp", "widget/gtk/WaylandSurface.cpp"], "git_node": "318beee1c1b5f3039275d60c945136429b29e53e", "git_parents": ["3fea0e52800e61d0895ada227011c2a6e22f983a"], "node": "6797ffc9e6916e52baa1c5237676688b466a5186", "parents": ["971821607876ce1ce2cb2b2b24485c3885c65068"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057759 - Log colorspace in full-cycle path r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323447\n", "files": ["dom/media/ipc/RemoteImageHolder.cpp", "dom/media/ipc/RemoteImageHolder.h", "dom/media/ipc/RemoteVideoDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoEncoder.cpp", "dom/media/webcodecs/DecoderTemplate.cpp", "dom/media/webcodecs/EncoderAgent.cpp", "dom/media/webcodecs/EncoderTemplate.cpp", "dom/media/webcodecs/VideoDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/webcodecs/VideoFrame.cpp"], "git_node": "49dba1016062268e4e508297b17fc024915a9473", "git_parents": ["318beee1c1b5f3039275d60c945136429b29e53e"], "node": "ee6844cb440685bd051b3b3696dd304b3c2b4c41", "parents": ["6797ffc9e6916e52baa1c5237676688b466a5186"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057759 - Gate decoded frame color metadata behind a preference r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nKeep the existing behavior by default until encoder color-space signaling is complete. Enable the new behavior for the color-quads reftests.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323448\n", "files": ["dom/media/ipc/RemoteVideoDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/test/reftest/color_quads/reftest.list", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "3fe55e91796ba66fdc0f7d1235c92d5d34955182", "git_parents": ["49dba1016062268e4e508297b17fc024915a9473"], "node": "4125c7b72ad6133e51fd67086509368de4bd75b5", "parents": ["ee6844cb440685bd051b3b3696dd304b3c2b4c41"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057759: apply code formatting via Lando\n\n# ignore-this-changeset\n", "files": ["gfx/2d/Types.cpp", "gfx/2d/Types.h", "gfx/layers/ImageContainer.cpp"], "git_node": "d6ceec2da606eac1e94ecde0655a285f2fec799b", "git_parents": ["3fe55e91796ba66fdc0f7d1235c92d5d34955182"], "node": "e63ad1357f989ca73fa3dab8eee853c7cad22350", "parents": ["4125c7b72ad6133e51fd67086509368de4bd75b5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067277 - Always report APZ autoscroll rejection by message. r=hiro,botond\n\nStartAutoscroll returned whether APZ accepted the autoscroll, but that\nanswer only reached the caller when the compositor ran in the parent\nprocess. With a GPU process the request goes over an async message, so the\nreturn value only said the message was sent and the rejection came back\nvia message instead. This patch makes it report the rejection that way in\nboth cases.\n\nNotable details:\n\n- AutoScrollChild now registers its \"autoscroll-rejected-by-apz\" observer\n  before sending \"Autoscroll:Start\" rather than after the reply. Without a\n  GPU process, ChromeProcessController::NotifyAsyncAutoscrollRejected is\n  already on the UI thread and notifies synchronously, so the rejection\n  would otherwise always be delivered before the observer exists and be\n  dropped.\n\n- CanonicalBrowsingContext::StartApzAutoscroll keeps returning bool for its\n  own early-outs (no BrowserParent, no widget, APZ disabled) to prevent\n  a regression of main-thread scrolling. nsIWidget::StartAsyncAutoscroll no\n  longer has anything to report.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322015\n", "files": ["docshell/base/CanonicalBrowsingContext.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/public/IAPZCTreeManager.h", "gfx/layers/apz/src/APZCTreeManager.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/src/APZCTreeManager.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/APZCTreeManagerChild.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/APZCTreeManagerChild.h", "toolkit/actors/AutoScrollChild.sys.mjs", "widget/nsIWidget.cpp", "widget/nsIWidget.h"], "git_node": "57c647e76c75cb37fd6f274587b8d1e88b2a3a20", "git_parents": ["d6ceec2da606eac1e94ecde0655a285f2fec799b"], "node": "67936d6228a503849e3184055bfa4ce862b3c748", "parents": ["e63ad1357f989ca73fa3dab8eee853c7cad22350"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064211 - Move messages sent only from the parent process from PAPZCTreeManager to PAPZInputBridge. r=botond,geckoview-reviewers,hiro\n\nSetKeyboardMap, SetDPI, SetBrowserGestureResponse, StartAutoscroll,\nStopAutoscroll and SetLongTapEnabled are only ever sent from the UI\nprocess to the GPU process, so move them to PAPZInputBridge, a protocol\nwhich doesn't have an endpoint in the content process at all.\n\nNotable details:\n\n- PAPZInputBridge's child endpoint is bound to the APZ controller thread\n  rather than the main thread, so APZInputBridgeChild hops to it before\n  sending. Note that on Android, these calls can initially arrive on the\n  Java UI thread.\n\n- Originally, four of those methods are executed via APZUpdater queue by\n  RunOnUpdaterThread in APZCTreeManagerParent. But this patch doesn't use\n  the queue anymore, because the message doesn't need to be ordered with\n  respect to WR frame generation first of all.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319238\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/public/APZInputBridge.h", "gfx/layers/apz/public/IAPZCTreeManager.h", "gfx/layers/apz/src/APZCTreeManager.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/src/APZCTreeManager.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/APZCTreeManagerChild.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/APZCTreeManagerChild.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/APZCTreeManagerParent.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/APZCTreeManagerParent.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/APZInputBridgeChild.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/APZInputBridgeChild.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/APZInputBridgeParent.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/APZInputBridgeParent.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/PAPZCTreeManager.ipdl", "gfx/layers/ipc/PAPZInputBridge.ipdl", "widget/android/nsWindow.cpp", "widget/nsIWidget.cpp"], "git_node": "e65ec172ddcc7d51ba821607106e7c019a360d45", "git_parents": ["57c647e76c75cb37fd6f274587b8d1e88b2a3a20"], "node": "106ad3b8a82194220fd568942f5aaf9c45d6b408", "parents": ["67936d6228a503849e3184055bfa4ce862b3c748"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064211 - Move messages sent only to the parent process from PAPZCTreeManager to PAPZInputBridge. r=botond,hiro\n\nNotifyPinchGesture, CancelAutoscroll, NotifyScaleGestureComplete\nare only ever sent to the UI process from the GPU process, so move\nthem to PAPZInputBridge, a protocol which doesn't have an endpoint\nin the content process at all.\n\nNotable details:\n\n- In RemoteContentController.cpp, some non-trivial changes are added,\n  because APZInputBridgeParent is bound to the main thread while\n  APZCTreeManagerParent is bound to the compositor one.\n\n- In APZInputBridgeChild.cpp, APZInputBridgeChild is bound to the\n  controller thread, which on Android is the Java UI thread, so a\n  thread hop is needed before calling the implementations which need\n  to be on the main thread.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320331\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/ipc/APZCTreeManagerChild.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/APZCTreeManagerChild.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/APZInputBridgeChild.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/APZInputBridgeChild.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/CompositorBridgeParent.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/CompositorBridgeParent.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/PAPZCTreeManager.ipdl", "gfx/layers/ipc/PAPZInputBridge.ipdl", "gfx/layers/ipc/RemoteContentController.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/RemoteContentController.h"], "git_node": "8aa660504e43301b92b800ad1d39223d800bb503", "git_parents": ["e65ec172ddcc7d51ba821607106e7c019a360d45"], "node": "4327ed57d8ef11bdeaf079fc50133ab258fec574", "parents": ["106ad3b8a82194220fd568942f5aaf9c45d6b408"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064211 - Move messages sent only to the parent process from PAPZ to PAPZInputBridge. r=botond,hiro\n\nLayerTransforms, UpdateOverscrollVelocity, UpdateOverscrollOffset and\nHideDynamicToolbar are only ever sent to the UI process from the GPU\nprocess, so move them to PAPZInputBridge, a protocol which doesn't have\nan endpoint in the content process at all.\n\nAfter this patch, the remaining PAPZ methods are ones which can\ngenuinely reach a content process and accordingly have an implementation\nin ContentProcessController.\n\nNotable details:\n\n- APZInputBridgeParent is bound to the main thread and so\n  RemoteContentController hops to the main thread.\n\n- mCanSend check in RemoteContentController for these methods is\n  now not necessary, because APZInputBridge actors (parent/child) have\n  the same lifetime.\n\n- NotifyLayerTransforms has no ScrollableLayerGuid to select the target\n  window's input bridge with, so RemoteContentController now stores the\n  LayersId it was allocated for. For the actor that carries these messages\n  that is the window's root LayersId, which keeps the routing identical to\n  what sending on PAPZ did.\n\n- On the receiving side the four handlers hop to the main thread before\n  touching mCompositorSession, mirroring RecvHandleTap and\n  RecvNotifyPinchGesture. PAPZInputBridge's child endpoint is bound to the\n  APZ controller thread, which is not the main thread on Android, whereas\n  the compositor session and its content controller are only written on the\n  main thread.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320985\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/ipc/APZChild.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/APZChild.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/APZInputBridgeChild.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/APZInputBridgeChild.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/CompositorBridgeParent.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/ContentCompositorBridgeParent.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/PAPZ.ipdl", "gfx/layers/ipc/PAPZInputBridge.ipdl", "gfx/layers/ipc/RemoteContentController.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/RemoteContentController.h"], "git_node": "6a860f18759a57164826fc225c11e19f209bac89", "git_parents": ["8aa660504e43301b92b800ad1d39223d800bb503"], "node": "f00093b70e0d0b9ecb65da698e79ec08d8a83e0d", "parents": ["4327ed57d8ef11bdeaf079fc50133ab258fec574"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sotaro Ikeda \u003csotaro.ikeda.g@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068804 - Rename CompositeProcessD3D11FencesHolderMap to CompositeProcessFencesHolderMap r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nPreparation for Bug 2068875.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323161\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/CompositeProcessFencesHolderMap.cpp", "gfx/layers/CompositeProcessFencesHolderMap.h", "gfx/layers/d3d11/CompositeProcessD3D11FencesHolderMap.cpp", "gfx/layers/d3d11/CompositeProcessD3D11FencesHolderMap.h"], "git_node": "3fe2649f80b5d7097622f398d0d3f04de74dd2af", "git_parents": ["6a860f18759a57164826fc225c11e19f209bac89"], "node": "21939a36bae4c2700f2d525dfab6adb2b5e1195b", "parents": ["f00093b70e0d0b9ecb65da698e79ec08d8a83e0d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sotaro Ikeda \u003csotaro.ikeda.g@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068804 - Change CompositeProcessFencesHolderMap to platform independent r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323138\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/wmf/DXVA2Manager.cpp", "dom/webgpu/ExternalTexture.cpp", "dom/webgpu/SharedTextureD3D11.cpp", "gfx/gl/GLBlitHelperD3D.cpp", "gfx/gl/SharedSurfaceANGLE.cpp", "gfx/ipc/GPUParent.cpp", "gfx/layers/CompositeProcessFencesHolderMap.cpp", "gfx/layers/CompositeProcessFencesHolderMap.h", "gfx/layers/D3D11ShareHandleImage.cpp", "gfx/layers/IMFYCbCrImage.cpp", "gfx/layers/d3d11/FenceD3D11.cpp", "gfx/layers/d3d11/FenceD3D11.h", "gfx/layers/d3d11/TextureD3D11.cpp", "gfx/layers/moz.build", "gfx/thebes/gfxPlatform.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/DCLayerTree.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderD3D11TextureHost.cpp"], "git_node": "56b20259e55143f77f51af5d5920e1e030742eca", "git_parents": ["3fe2649f80b5d7097622f398d0d3f04de74dd2af"], "node": "30f03cd3045ba84113af1017a7a71e828e638bd3", "pare