rfaceTextureClientOGL.cpp", "gfx/layers/opengl/MacIOSurfaceTextureHostOGL.cpp", "gfx/layers/opengl/MacIOSurfaceTextureHostOGL.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxPlatform.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorLayerNative.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorLayerNative.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorNative.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorNative.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderMacIOSurfaceTextureHost.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderMacIOSurfaceTextureHost.h"], "git_node": "aefc0ccb6c88a58816ec23edbd6195bb26a49c4e", "git_parents": ["7ad9f990aa717231849ce09bacb13535f6a360ab"], "node": "4a6f16c6679e6540c345df89b7744739da66cad6", "parents": ["52226e85bf301708155dcdeb32bc721680655883"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2063178 - Differentiate default and disabled checkbox/radio more r=akulyk,emilio\" for causing wr failures @ield-sizing-input-number-relayout.html.\n\nThis reverts commit 926ffded1b617d3a84b7701c406d8a11d721a2c7.\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/test/test_bug232227.html", "widget/nsXPLookAndFeel.cpp"], "git_node": "9f21e148e96f3af716d4b464709846b00eab4850", "git_parents": ["aefc0ccb6c88a58816ec23edbd6195bb26a49c4e"], "node": "6c41e5b247f466bc8505b0788121d012a28a2737", "parents": ["4a6f16c6679e6540c345df89b7744739da66cad6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2067228: Add form fill outcomes test for SFF telemetry r=omarg\" for causing bc failures @browser_smartwindow_smartformfill_telemetry.js.\n\nThis reverts commit 0accc4119ad061f250b09551b2e6997a4e311c49.\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_smartformfill_telemetry.js"], "git_node": "9cb5b5b8e4ad756b49380a207d9fc4a94982d00d", "git_parents": ["9f21e148e96f3af716d4b464709846b00eab4850"], "node": "e9c0d83657fc9201a84356ab2c3d4b526b9d5bb7", "parents": ["6c41e5b247f466bc8505b0788121d012a28a2737"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan Varga \u003cjvarga@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057579 - Complete the CSSMatrixComponent and CSSTransformComponent implementations; r=emilio,firefox-style-system-reviewers\n\nComplete the remaining `CSSMatrixComponent` functionality by implementing the\nmissing `matrix` setter and `ToMatrix()`, including the required 2D flattening.\n\nThis completes `CSSTransformComponent::ToMatrix()` dispatch and enables the\nremaining WPT coverage for transform component objects.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314899\n", "files": ["layout/style/typedom/CSSMatrixComponent.cpp", "layout/style/typedom/CSSMatrixComponent.h", "layout/style/typedom/CSSTransformComponent.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-typed-om/stylevalue-subclasses/cssMatrixComponent.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-typed-om/stylevalue-subclasses/cssTransformComponent-2d-flattening.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-typed-om/stylevalue-subclasses/cssTransformComponent-toMatrix.html.ini"], "git_node": "e33f4ef93182255c95473b016293cc9d8649aa7b", "git_parents": ["9cb5b5b8e4ad756b49380a207d9fc4a94982d00d"], "node": "46e5d1c6dcf120dbda9be9ae133fee7819709bb2", "parents": ["e9c0d83657fc9201a84356ab2c3d4b526b9d5bb7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Striemer \u003cmstriemer@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070728 - Don't fire moz-segmented-control change events when unchanged r=akulyk\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324800\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/tests/widgets/test_segmented_control.html", "toolkit/content/widgets/lit-select-control.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-segmented-control/moz-segmented-control.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/browser/browser_html_themes_mode.js"], "git_node": "99bc5023d66106b2bd0a25476dc78989fab84cc1", "git_parents": ["e33f4ef93182255c95473b016293cc9d8649aa7b"], "node": "e725ad46d109743017fd4990e37d20d5a9bed384", "parents": ["46e5d1c6dcf120dbda9be9ae133fee7819709bb2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Drew Willcoxon \u003cadw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070771 - Send the urlbar-keyword-exposure ping over ohttp. r=daisuke,urlbar-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324829\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/pings.yaml"], "git_node": "173b469251b8207cde7306231bef9cf933d1c56d", "git_parents": ["99bc5023d66106b2bd0a25476dc78989fab84cc1"], "node": "84bbb60c4d2f0d00adc95a5c73a8acd16af64604", "parents": ["e725ad46d109743017fd4990e37d20d5a9bed384"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andr\u00e9 Bargull \u003candre.bargull@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057638 - Part 1: Change x86's convertUInt32ToDouble to not clobber its input. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nThis matches what Clang uses to convert from `uint32_t` to `double`.\n\nIt's also 2 bytes shorter and uses fewer cycles per iteration according to\n\u003chttps://uica.uops.info/\u003e.\n\nThis change helps to move lowering and codegen for `WasmUnsignedTo{Double,Float32}`\ninto shared code (part 2).\n\nThe new implementation uses `ScratchDoubleScope` as a scratch register, which is\na problem if `dest` is also `ScratchDoubleScope`. All except one caller can be\nupdated use a different float-register (part 8), but for the call from\n`MacroAssembler::boxUint32` I don't see an easy way to switch to a different\nfloat-register without ending up with worse code. That's why the old\nimplementation isn't completely removed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314071\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/x86/MacroAssembler-x86-inl.h", "js/src/jit/x86/MacroAssembler-x86.cpp", "js/src/jit/x86/MacroAssembler-x86.h"], "git_node": "ef1c4e799347ee3ae10d8f6043f184bb1cad38da", "git_parents": ["173b469251b8207cde7306231bef9cf933d1c56d"], "node": "25b05a6240f19953a0802812f988037e100f75a0", "parents": ["84bbb60c4d2f0d00adc95a5c73a8acd16af64604"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andr\u00e9 Bargull \u003candre.bargull@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057638 - Part 2: Move lowering and codegen for MWasmUnsignedTo{Double,Float32} into shared code. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nLowering and codegen is now the same for all architectures.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314072\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp", "js/src/jit/LIROps.yaml", "js/src/jit/Lowering.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm/CodeGenerator-arm.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm/Lowering-arm.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm64/CodeGenerator-arm64.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm64/Lowering-arm64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/CodeGenerator-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/Lowering-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/mips-shared/CodeGenerator-mips-shared.cpp", "js/src/jit/mips-shared/Lowering-mips-shared.cpp", "js/src/jit/riscv64/CodeGenerator-riscv64.cpp", "js/src/jit/riscv64/Lowering-riscv64.cpp", "js/src/jit/wasm32/CodeGenerator-wasm32.cpp", "js/src/jit/x64/CodeGenerator-x64.cpp", "js/src/jit/x64/Lowering-x64.cpp", "js/src/jit/x86/CodeGenerator-x86.cpp", "js/src/jit/x86/Lowering-x86.cpp"], "git_node": "920b5724471522f0194e551e8ed78dcee9abc55d", "git_parents": ["ef1c4e799347ee3ae10d8f6043f184bb1cad38da"], "node": "7f7e1004c730d2c0245080c4ded4f49fcd4e3d3c", "parents": ["25b05a6240f19953a0802812f988037e100f75a0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andr\u00e9 Bargull \u003candre.bargull@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057638 - Part 3: Rename MWasmUnsignedToDouble in preparation for using it outside of Wasm. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nPart 4 will use `MWasmUnsignedToDouble` outside of Wasm-specific code.\n\nAnd also rename `MWasmUnsignedToFloat32` for consistency.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314073\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp", "js/src/jit/LIROps.yaml", "js/src/jit/Lowering.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIR-wasm.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIR-wasm.h", "js/src/jit/MIR.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIR.h", "js/src/jit/MIROps.yaml", "js/src/wasm/WasmIonCompile.cpp"], "git_node": "0a01f00bf55e2b347e887b29c2b026cf80e3879b", "git_parents": ["920b5724471522f0194e551e8ed78dcee9abc55d"], "node": "22fd6bdee9b0f248f10440e071d483fd89cc55db", "parents": ["7f7e1004c730d2c0245080c4ded4f49fcd4e3d3c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andr\u00e9 Bargull \u003candre.bargull@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057638 - Part 4: Move Uint32 to Double conversion for Atomic operations into a separate instruction. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nPerform the Uint32 to Double conversion through a separate instruction, similar\nto how the Int64 to BigInt conversion works.\n\nThis allows to simplify the Atomics code, because now the output is always in a\n`Register`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314074\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/LIROps.yaml", "js/src/jit/MacroAssembler.h", "js/src/jit/WarpBuilderShared.cpp", "js/src/jit/WarpCacheIRTranspiler.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm/CodeGenerator-arm.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm/Lowering-arm.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm/MacroAssembler-arm.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm64/CodeGenerator-arm64.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm64/Lowering-arm64.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm64/MacroAssembler-arm64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/CodeGenerator-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/Lowering-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/mips-shared/CodeGenerator-mips-shared.cpp", "js/src/jit/mips-shared/Lowering-mips-shared.cpp", "js/src/jit/mips-shared/MacroAssembler-mips-shared.cpp", "js/src/jit/riscv64/CodeGenerator-riscv64.cpp", "js/src/jit/riscv64/Lowering-riscv64.cpp", "js/src/jit/riscv64/MacroAssembler-riscv64.cpp", "js/src/jit/x86-shared/CodeGenerator-x86-shared.cpp", "js/src/jit/x86-shared/Lowering-x86-shared.cpp", "js/src/jit/x86-shared/MacroAssembler-x86-shared.cpp"], "git_node": "fdfca4bb6b0e109f601cb61e4339614070bbe355", "git_parents": ["0a01f00bf55e2b347e887b29c2b026cf80e3879b"], "node": "695049fbe03a83961b7de9c916f4ef28d2423af5", "parents": ["22fd6bdee9b0f248f10440e071d483fd89cc55db"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andr\u00e9 Bargull \u003candre.bargull@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057638 - Part 5: Add recover support for MUnsignedToDouble. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nAtomic operations like `Atomics.exchange` on `Uint32Array` with an unused result\nnow no longer need to emit the code to convert from `Uint32` to `Double`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314075\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/ion/recover-unsignedtodouble.js", "js/src/jit/MIROps.yaml", "js/src/jit/Recover.cpp", "js/src/jit/Recover.h"], "git_node": "b5112eca5c0f450495af0a7b4c9862b99f47f522", "git_parents": ["fdfca4bb6b0e109f601cb61e4339614070bbe355"], "node": "e0542622ee8685ba42d57257f27d28948ba912aa", "parents": ["695049fbe03a83961b7de9c916f4ef28d2423af5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andr\u00e9 Bargull \u003candre.bargull@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057638 - Part 6: Retire JS-specific Atomic operations. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nNow that the JS-specific Atomic operations simply call the corresponding\nprimitive operations, it's easier if all caller directly call the primitive\noperations.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314076\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/MacroAssembler.h", "js/src/jit/arm/CodeGenerator-arm.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm/MacroAssembler-arm.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm64/CodeGenerator-arm64.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm64/MacroAssembler-arm64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/CodeGenerator-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/mips-shared/CodeGenerator-mips-shared.cpp", "js/src/jit/mips-shared/MacroAssembler-mips-shared.cpp", "js/src/jit/riscv64/CodeGenerator-riscv64.cpp", "js/src/jit/riscv64/MacroAssembler-riscv64.cpp", "js/src/jit/x86-shared/CodeGenerator-x86-shared.cpp", "js/src/jit/x86-shared/MacroAssembler-x86-shared.cpp"], "git_node": "5d5b0b5072a9a520711e1411f4bface02f5462ae", "git_parents": ["b5112eca5c0f450495af0a7b4c9862b99f47f522"], "node": "8a0d4d9e8034cfaa51e340cff01a5beabfe4dd33", "parents": ["e0542622ee8685ba42d57257f27d28948ba912aa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andr\u00e9 Bargull \u003candre.bargull@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057638 - Part 7: Rename atomicEffectOpJS to atomicEffectOp. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nThis moves `atomicEffectOp` into the \"primitive\" Atomic operations for\nconsistency after the changes from part 6.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314077\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/MacroAssembler.h", "js/src/jit/arm/CodeGenerator-arm.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm/MacroAssembler-arm.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm64/CodeGenerator-arm64.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm64/MacroAssembler-arm64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/CodeGenerator-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/mips-shared/CodeGenerator-mips-shared.cpp", "js/src/jit/mips-shared/MacroAssembler-mips-shared.cpp", "js/src/jit/riscv64/CodeGenerator-riscv64.cpp", "js/src/jit/riscv64/MacroAssembler-riscv64.cpp", "js/src/jit/x86-shared/CodeGenerator-x86-shared.cpp", "js/src/jit/x86-shared/MacroAssembler-x86-shared.cpp"], "git_node": "15f7d0944c8ae88ca3ca75eaad930a4d5e45dadf", "git_parents": ["5d5b0b5072a9a520711e1411f4bface02f5462ae"], "node": "da0056a33fe443d1d8c7a698b0082048b0d600f6", "parents": ["8a0d4d9e8034cfaa51e340cff01a5beabfe4dd33"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andr\u00e9 Bargull \u003candre.bargull@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057638 - Part 8: Switch most convertUInt32ToDouble calls to not use ScratchDoubleScope. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nNot using `ScratchDoubleScope` allows to use the new `convertUInt32ToDouble`\nfrom part 1.\n\nThe `convertUInt32ToDouble` method taking a `const ScratchDoubleScope&` is now\nonly called from `MacroAssembler::boxUint32`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314078\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/CacheIRCompiler.cpp"], "git_node": "343d8a76c0b14155e8a2e8ab25389f97e5ebe1e3", "git_parents": ["15f7d0944c8ae88ca3ca75eaad930a4d5e45dadf"], "node": "3fa4082a7c53c3d665bd3f0ff06ae3fdacaac22f", "parents": ["da0056a33fe443d1d8c7a698b0082048b0d600f6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068404. r=view-transitions-reviewers,nical\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324609\n", "files": ["dom/base/Document.cpp", "dom/base/Document.h"], "git_node": "5b891667c6851ce48eede6d695d3f749c01e70de", "git_parents": ["343d8a76c0b14155e8a2e8ab25389f97e5ebe1e3"], "node": "1d1f6c150beb29c1648a6ebb9ba2835f02161643", "parents": ["3fa4082a7c53c3d665bd3f0ff06ae3fdacaac22f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Seward \u003cjseward@acm.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049604 - fix missing debug stackmaps in baseline {F32,F64} -\u003e {I32,I64} checked conversions.  r=yury.\n\nFor wasm baseline {F32,F64} -\u003e {I32,I64} checked conversions, we generate code\nwhich will trap if the conversion goes bad (input = NaN or is out of integer\nrange).  Two different trap kinds are created, Trap::InvalidConversionToInteger\nfor NaNs and Trap::IntegerOverflow for the overflow case.\n\nIn principle this is simple: when we generate one of the above two traps, then\nalso generate a stackmap at the same time.  In practice it is difficult\nbecause:\n\n(1) The stackmap creation machinery lives at the BaseCompiler level (class);\n    but the traps are generated deep within the MacroAssembler level.  Only the\n    MacroAssembler knows the code offsets that stackmaps should use, but only\n    the BaseCompiler knows how to create the stackmaps and how to store them.\n\n(2) These traps are all in out-of-line code.  The associated stackmaps\n    therefore need to have keys (offsets) in the OOL code areas.  But the\n    stackmap itself describes the stack in a not-OOL area.  So we cannot wait\n    until the trapsite is created before computing the stack map; it will be\n    completely incorrect.\n\nTo solve (1), this patch introduces a new virtual class StackMapRegistry.  This\nmakes it possible to \"send into\" the MacroAssembler, any state we want; the\nMacroAssembler doesn't care what it is.  It only cares that it can call an\n`addMap` method on that object.\n\nThen, in baseline, we have a new class BaselineStackMapRegistry, which\nimplements the above interface.  This means that the MacroAssembler can add\nstackmaps for baseline without knowing any baseline internals.  It also means\n(later) we could make a implementation of the interface for Ion, so Ion can use\nthis scheme too.\n\nTo solve (2), code in baseline generates a StackMap at the \"right\" place in\nin-line code it generates.  It also creates a BaselineStackMapRegistry;\nimportantly, the latter is allocated on the C++ heap.  It sends (pointers to)\nboth objects into the MacroAssembler, including through various \"OOLCode\"\nsupporting classes.  When the assembler finally creates the trapsite, it can\nregister the stackmap in the Registry object, using the offset for the trap.\n\nHence what you see is, almost everywhere, a StackMap* and a\nBaselineStackMapRegistry* travelling together.\n\nIf there is no need to register a stackmap, then both the StackMap* and\nBaselineStackMapRegistry* can be nullptr.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313940\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/MacroAssembler.cpp", "js/src/jit/MacroAssembler.h", "js/src/jit/arm/CodeGenerator-arm.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm/MacroAssembler-arm.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm/MacroAssembler-arm.h", "js/src/jit/arm64/CodeGenerator-arm64.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm64/MacroAssembler-arm64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/mips-shared/MacroAssembler-mips-shared.cpp", "js/src/jit/riscv64/CodeGenerator-riscv64.cpp", "js/src/jit/riscv64/MacroAssembler-riscv64.cpp", "js/src/jit/wasm